\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 One of world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest windfarm developers to cut quarter of workforce\b0\par\par\uc2 Jillian Ambrose Energy correspondent \par \uc2 491 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 October 2025\par 11:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 \u216\'00\'D8rsted\uc2  plans to shrink company after Trump administration causes share price to plunge to all-time low\par \par \uc2 One of the world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest windfarm developers will cut its workforce by a quarter in the next two years after a series of setbacks for the industry.\par \par \uc2 The Danish wind giant \uc2 \u216\'00\'D8rsted\uc2  plans to remove about 2,000 positions from its 8,000-strong workforce by the end of 2027 through a combination of redundancies, natural attrition and selling off parts of its business.\par \par \uc2 The company, which is headquartered in Fredericia, Denmark, and employs more than 1,200 workers in the UK, plans to make 500 redundancies by the end of the year, including 235 in its home market.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2025/oct/05/donald-trump-hatred-renewables-us-falling-behind-world"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s hatred for renewables means the US is falling behind the rest of the world}}}\par \par \uc2 \u216\'00\'D8rsted boss \uc2 Rasmus Errboe\uc2  set out his plan to shrink the company weeks after the Trump administration caused its share price to plunge to an all-time low by ordering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2025/aug/25/rsted-shares-at-all-time-low-after-trump-halts-work-on-us-windfarm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an immediate halt to work}}}\uc2  on a near-complete windfarm off the coast of Rhode Island.\par \par \uc2 The developer, which is 50% owned by the Danish state, was forced to fundraise more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2025/aug/11/orsted-wind-generator-shares-sink-9bn-cash-call"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 than $9bn}}}\uc2  after the political hostility in the US made it more difficult to attract investors for its pipeline of projects.\par \par \uc2 The order to down tools dealt a blow to \u216\'00\'D8rsted, which earlier this year cancelled plans to build one of the UK\u8217\'20\'19s largest offshore windfarms, saying it no longer made economic sense due to high inflation and soaring costs in the industry\u8217\'20\'19s global supply chain.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2025/oct/07/global-renewable-energy-generation-surpasses-coal-first-time"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Global renewable energy generation surpasses coal for first time}}}\par \par \uc2 Although a US court last month allowed the company to restart work on the Revolution Wind project in Rhode Island, \u216\'00\'D8rsted intends to refocus its business on Europe\u8217\'20\'19s offshore wind sector \u8211\'20\'13 and select markets in Asia \u8211\'20\'13 once it has completed its existing pipeline of global projects.\par \par \uc2 Rasmus Errboe\uc2 , chief executive of \u216\'00\'D8rsted, said on Thursday that the group needed to be \u8220\'20\'1Cmore efficient and flexible\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a necessary consequence of our decision to focus our business and the fact that we\u8217\'20\'19ll be finalising our large construction portfolio in the coming years \u8211\'20\'13 which is why we\u8217\'20\'19ll need fewer employees.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the same time, we want to create a more efficient and flexible organisation and a more competitive \u216\'00\'D8rsted, ready to bid on new value-accretive offshore wind projects,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The company\u8217\'20\'19s market value has increased slightly since it fell to all-time lows of 99.54 Danish kroner in August, but remains 53% lower this time last year. Its share price fell to 119DKK (\u163\'00\'A313.8) on Thursday, down 2.6% from the day before.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 10 October 2025. An earlier version incorrectly said that \u216\'00\'D8rsted was headquartered in Oslo.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251009ela9005ha\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
