\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Entry-level workers face AI \u8216\'20\'18job-pocalypse\u8217\'20\'19; US probes \uc2 Tesla\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s self-driving system \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Graeme Wearden \par \uc2 3,418 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 October 2025\par 16:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Business leaders are prioritising automation through AI to fill skills gaps, rather than training junior employees, survey finds\par \par \uc2 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing post\par \par \uc2 Time to wrap up\u8230\'20\'26.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/oct/09/water-customers-bill-hike-winter-blackouts-risk-falls-stock-markets-pound-ftse-business-live-news?page=with%3Ablock-68e765838f0871610d006f5d#block-68e765838f0871610d006f5d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Entry-level workers are facing a \u8216\'20\'18job-pocalypse\u8217\'20\'19 due to companies favouring artificial intelligence systems over new hires}}}\uc2 , a new study of global business leaders shows.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/oct/09/water-customers-bill-hike-winter-blackouts-risk-falls-stock-markets-pound-ftse-business-live-news?page=with%3Ablock-68e786328f0871610d00707d#block-68e786328f0871610d00707d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The U.S. National Highway Traffic Safety Administration is opening an investigation into 2.88 million Tesla vehicles equipped with its Full Self-Driving system over traffic-safety violations after a series of crashes.}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/oct/09/water-customers-bill-hike-winter-blackouts-risk-falls-stock-markets-pound-ftse-business-live-news?page=with%3Ablock-68e774e78f08a99f04926bb5#block-68e774e78f08a99f04926bb5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The surge of UK inflation in the last few years has \u8220\'20\'1Cscarred\u8221\'20\'1D consumers, Bank of England policymaker Catherine Mann fears}}}\uc2 \u8230\'20\'26.\par \par \uc2 ..{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/oct/09/water-customers-bill-hike-winter-blackouts-risk-falls-stock-markets-pound-ftse-business-live-news?page=with%3Ablock-68e757368f08e1d65d2a5be1#block-68e757368f08e1d65d2a5be1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The boss of JP Morgan has warned that a stock market tumble may be approaching}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/oct/09/water-customers-bill-hike-winter-blackouts-risk-falls-stock-markets-pound-ftse-business-live-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-68e6c37e8f0871610d006ae1#block-68e6c37e8f0871610d006ae1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Water bills for millions of households in England are to increase by even more than expected}}}\par \par \uc2 after the competition regulator gave the green light for five water suppliers to raise charges to customers \u8211\'20\'13 but rejected most of the companies\u8217\'20\'19 demands.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/oct/09/water-customers-bill-hike-winter-blackouts-risk-falls-stock-markets-pound-ftse-business-live-news?page=with%3Ablock-68e74f678f0871610d006ee3#block-68e74f678f0871610d006ee3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Britain\u8217\'20\'19s risk of winter blackouts has fallen to its lowest level in five years, according to the energy system operator}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lloyds Banking Group\uc2  and \uc2 Close Brothers\uc2  have both warned that the motor finance scandal is likely to cost them materially more than they had already set aside.\par \par \uc2 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Silver price rises over $50/oz\par \par \uc2 The silver price has hit its highest level in decades, as the surge of money into precious metals continues.\par \par \uc2 Spot silver rose over $50 per ounce today for the first time in over 40 years.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  reports that it\u8217\'20\'19s the highest level since 1980 when the billionaire Hunt brothers attempted to corner the silver market, with disastrous results.\par \par \uc2 Nelson Bunker Hunt and William Herber Hunt inflated the price of silver by more than 700% after hoarding physical silver and purchasing silver futures contracts, using money accrued from the family oil business, and then borrowing more.\par \par \uc2 Eventually, they owned a third of all the silver in the world. But the trade turned sour after authorities restricted buying commodities with borrowed monet, prompting the silver price to collapse\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 The copper price has hit a 16-month high today, amid fears of shortage of a metal used widely in industry.\par \par \uc2 Copper rose to $11,000 per metric ton on Thursday, following a series of disruptions to mine supply\par \par \uc2 Benchmark three-month copper on the \uc2 London Metal Exchange\uc2  rose 3.1% to hit the $11,000 mark, near to its all-time peak of $11,104.50, set in May 2024.\par \par \uc2 Last month, producer \uc2 Freeport-McMoRan\uc2  declared force majeure at its Grasberg mine in Indonesia, after a large flow of wet material blocked access to parts of its underground mine, restricting evacuation routes for seven workers.\par \par \uc2 3.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jaguar Land Rover\uc2  has restarted Range Rover production lines in Solihull, with plans for all its manufacturing sites to be back up and running by the end of next week as it recovers from a major cyber attack.\par \par \uc2 The carmaker said employees went back to work at the Solihull site in the West Midlands today, following the phased restart of production on Wednesday after being suspended for more than a month due to the hack.\par \par \uc2 It said the remaining production lines in Solihull, which make the Range Rover Velar SUV and \uc2 Jaguar\uc2  F Pace models, will come back on stream next Monday, alongside vehicle manufacturing operations in Halewood, Merseyside, PA Media reports.\par \par \uc2 Overseas factories in Pune, India, and Brazil are set to follow suit later next week, marking the final sites to resume operations, according to the group.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a subdued start to trading on Wall Street today.\par \par \uc2 The DowJonesIndustrialAverage rose 20.5 points, or 0.04%, to 46,622.31 at the open, with the broader S&P 500 share index up 0.1%.\par \par \uc2 Investors hoping for a steer on monetary policy from \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  chair JeromePowell were disappointed \u8211\'20\'13 he opened a conference on community banking at the Fed an hour ago, but didn\u8217\'20\'19t commit any news.\par \par \uc2 2.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Surprising news of the day: Nearly a fifth of employees say they have secretly juggled two competing jobs, or know someone who has.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s according to a survey from fraud prevention service \uc2 Cifas\uc2 , which also found that 24 of staff think such \u8220\'20\'1Cpolygamous working\u8221\'20\'1D is justifiable.\par \par \uc2 The research published by \uc2 Cifas\uc2  involved research among 2,000 employees across different sectors, including HR, engineering, finance and IT.\par \par \uc2 Nearly 20% of people said they or someone they know had covered employment gaps with bogus references, according to the survey carried out by Opinion Matters in July.\par \par \uc2 Those who were surveyed were working in companies employing at least 1,000 people with UK operations.\par \par \uc2 Mike Haley, CEO of \uc2 Cifas\uc2 , said:\par \par \uc2 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u216\'00\'D8rsted to cut quarter of workforce\par \par \uc2 Offshore wind farm developer \u216\'00\'D8rsted is cutting its workforce by a quarter after running into setbacks in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u216\'00\'D8rsted\uc2  has announced it will cut about 2,000 jobs by the end of 2027, and focus more closely on the EU, having faced opposition to offshore wind projects from Donald Trump.\par \par \uc2 CEO RasmusErrboe said in a statement today that \u216\'00\'D8rsted needs to improve its competitiveness, explaining:\par \par \uc2 1.59pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ch.linkedin.com/in/burkhard-boeckem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Burkhard Boeckem}}}\uc2 , CTO of tech company{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://robotics.hexagon.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hexagon}}}\uc2 , which has developed an autonomous humanoid robot, argues that humans will be \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical in tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s job market\u8221\'20\'1D, despite the growth in artificial intelligence tools.\par \par \uc2 Following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/oct/09/water-customers-bill-hike-winter-blackouts-risk-falls-stock-markets-pound-ftse-business-live-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-68e765838f0871610d006f5d#block-68e765838f0871610d006f5d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the BSI\u8217\'20\'19s report today}}}\uc2  showing the \u8216\'20\'18job-pocalypse\u8217\'20\'19 being created by AI, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ch.linkedin.com/in/burkhard-boeckem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Boeckem}}}\uc2  says:\par \par \uc2 Updated at 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 1.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in the auto sector, shares in Ferrari have dropped sharply after it scaled back its electric car plans.\par \par \uc2 In the event at its headquarters in Maranello, Northern Italy, Ferrari revealed the production-ready chassis for its new EV vehicle, the Elettrica.\par \par \uc2 But it also revealed a less ambitious approach to electrification.\par \par \uc2 Ferrari is now aiming for a 2030 lineup made up of 40% internal combustion engine (ICE) models, 40% hybrids and 20% fully-electric. This marks a change from its 2022 plan, which had targeted 40% EVs, 40% hybrids and 20% ICE models in 2030, Reuters points out.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Citi\uc2  warned:\par \par \uc2 Ferrari is now planning to grow its revenues to \u8364\'20\'AC9bn by 2030, up from \u8364\'20\'AC7.1bn forecast for 2025, but lower than expected.\par \par \uc2 Shares in Ferrari have dropped 13% to their lowest levels since April.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 1.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 12.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Commission\uc2  has said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cconcerned\u8221\'20\'1D by China\u8217\'20\'19s announcement of new controls on the export of rare-earth technologies and items ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/oct/09/water-customers-bill-hike-winter-blackouts-risk-falls-stock-markets-pound-ftse-business-live-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-68e7908a8f08a99f04926d10#block-68e7908a8f08a99f04926d10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see earlier post}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 EU trade spokesman OlofGill told reporters:\par \par \uc2 12.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Close Brothers\uc2  warns motor finance scandal bill could rise\par \par \uc2 Newsflash: A second UK lender has warned shareholders that it may face a larger bill than expected from the motor finance scandal.\par \par \uc2 Close\par \par \uc2 Brothers has told the City that its existing provision, of \u163\'00\'A3165m, may not be sufficent following the compensation scheme announced earlier this week.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/oct/09/water-customers-bill-hike-winter-blackouts-risk-falls-stock-markets-pound-ftse-business-live-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-68e75e258f08a99f04926b2e#block-68e75e258f08a99f04926b2e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Following Lloyds\u8217\'20\'19 announcement this morning}}}\uc2 , CloseBrothers says:\par \par \uc2 Shares in CloseBrothers have tumbled; they\u8217\'20\'19re now down 10%.\par \par \uc2 11.42am BST\par \par \uc2 China tightens rare earths export controls again\par \par \uc2 China has again tightened export controls on rare earths and related technologies ahead of a possible meeting between Chinese leader Xi Jinping and Donald Trump.\par \par \uc2 Beijing said it would add several new rare earth elements to its list of goods with export restrictions including holmium, erbium, thulium, europium and ytterbium.\par \par \uc2 Previous export controls earlier this year hit the European car industry hard with shortages of magnets for door and boot openings hitting assembly lines among the consequences.\par \par \uc2 Political leaders in Europe say the fact that China can just impact industry through a \u8220\'20\'1Csnap of fingers\u8221\'20\'1D is alarming.\par \par \uc2 Kathleen\par \par \uc2 van\par \par \uc2 Brempt, vice president of the European social and democrats trade group in the \uc2 European Parliament\uc2 , says:\par \par \uc2 The move could also be seen as sabre-rattling in Europe as it comes two days after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/oct/07/eu-plan-to-match-trump-steel-tariffs-spurs-existential-threat-to-uk-steel-industry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the EU proposed 50% tariffs on foreign stee}}}\uc2 l.\par \par \uc2 In a further squeeze, the Chinese ministry has also added dozens of pieces of rare processing equipment, something that would limit development of processing outside China.\par \par \uc2 Foreign entities must now obtain a licence from Beijing to export any products containing more than 0.1% of rare earths, or manufactured using China\u8217\'20\'19s extraction, refining, magnet-making or recycling technology,\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.56am BST\par \par \uc2 10.57am BST\par \par \uc2 US opens probe into nearly 2.9 million \uc2 Tesla\uc2  vehicles over FSD traffic violations\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. National Highway Traffic Safety Administration\uc2  is opening an investigation into 2.88 million \uc2 Tesla\uc2  vehicles equipped with its Full Self-Driving system over traffic-safety violations after a series of crashes.\par \par \uc2 The auto safety agency said FSD - an assistance system that requires drivers to pay attention and intervene if needed - has \u8220\'20\'1Cinduced vehicle behavior that violated traffic safety laws\u8220\'20\'1C, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The agency said it has reports of \uc2 Tesla\uc2  vehicles driving through red traffic lights and driving against the proper direction of travel during a lane change, while using the system.\par \par \uc2 NHTSA\uc2  said it has six reports in which a \uc2 Tesla\uc2  vehicle, operating with FSD engaged, \u8220\'20\'1Capproached an intersection with a red traffic signal, continued to travel into the intersection against the red light and was subsequently involved in a crash with other motor vehicles in the intersection.\u8220\'20\'1C\par \par \uc2 NHTSA\uc2  said four crashes resulted in one or more injuries.\par \par \uc2 10.49am BST\par \par \uc2 DRC to start building gold reserve\par \par \uc2 The Democratic Republic of Congo is planning to join the dash into gold.\par \par \uc2 The DRC will start building gold reserves to bolster its currency and lift its economy, the central bank governor said today.\par \par \uc2 Andre\par \par \uc2 Wameso, who was appointed as head of the central bank in July, told Reuters:\par \par \uc2 Wameso\u8217\'20\'19s move comes as gold hit fresh record highs over $4,000/ounce this week, as investors drive the \u8216\'20\'18debasement trade\u8217\'20\'19":\par \par \uc2 10.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Wall Street futures are trading marginally in the red today amid growing warnings of bloated AI valuations.\par \par \uc2 Raffi Boyadjian, lead market analyst at TradingPoint, says:\par \par \uc2 10.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Compensation schemes for Post Office Horizon IT scandal victims \u8216\'20\'18to be improved\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Compensation schemes for victims of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/post-office-horizon-scandal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Post Office Horizon IT scandal}}}\uc2  will be improved, with a new appeals process and funded legal advice for post office operators, the government has announced.\par \par \uc2 Responding to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2025/jul/08/post-office-scandal-inquiry-horizon-it-scandal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first part of the findings}}}\uc2  from a two-year public inquiry into the Horizon IT scandal, regarded as one of the worst miscarriages of justice in UK legal history, the business secretary, Peter Kyle, said there would be anew appeals process for people who have accepted fixed-sum offers under the Horizon Shortfall Scheme, one of several compensation schemes.\par \par \uc2 Funded legal advice will also be offered. \uc2 The Post Office\uc2  will close this scheme on 31 January, to give post office operators who have not yet applied more time to put in applications.\par \par \uc2 More {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2025/oct/09/compensation-schemes-post-office-horizon-it-scandal-victims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 9.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Mann: high inflation has caused scarring, income uncertainty, and weak consumption growth\par \par \uc2 The surge of UK inflation in the last few years has \u8220\'20\'1Cscarred\u8221\'20\'1D consumers, \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  policymaker \uc2 Catherine Mann\uc2  fears.\par \par \uc2 Mann is warning in a speech that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe rapid increase in the price level has scarred consumers\u8221\'20\'1D, even as inflation has moderated, allowing incomes to rise faster than prices.\par \par \uc2 She explains that research shows that households who are more uncertain about future inflation become more uncertain about their future incomes. This leads them to save money, rather than spend it, which pulls down consumption.\par \par \uc2 Thus, she says, the Bank should keep interest rates high to bring inflation down and reassure consumers that price stability is intact, rather than lower borrowing costs to encourage consumption.\par \par \uc2 As Mann puts it:\par \par \uc2 Mann (among the majority of policymakers who voted to leave interest rates hold last month) also warns that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe are not there yet\u8221\'20\'1D in bringing down inflation expectations.\par \par \uc2 She explains:\par \par \uc2 Updated at 9.55am BST\par \par \uc2 9.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Business leaders may be \u8216\'20\'18pulling up the ladder\u8217\'20\'19 behind them, by focusing on AI tools rather than taking on new staff, warns Kate Field, global head human and social sustainability at the \uc2 BSI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Field explains:\par \par \uc2 9.06am BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BSI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s poll of global business leaders also found that large organizations are embracing AI more aggressively compared with SMEs.\par \par \uc2 It says:\par \par \uc2 8.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Entry-level workers face \u8216\'20\'18job-pocalypse\u8217\'20\'19 due to AI\par \par \uc2 Entry-level workers are facing a \u8216\'20\'18job-pocalypse\u8217\'20\'19 due to companies favouring artificial intelligence systems over new hires, a new study of global business leaders shows.\par \par \uc2 A new report by the \uc2 British Standards Institution (BSI)\uc2  has found that business leaders are prioritising automation through AI to fill skills gaps, in lieu of training for junior employees.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BSI\uc2  polled more than 850 bosses in Australia, China, France, Germany, Japan, the UK, and the US, and found that 41% said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/jul/13/could-ai-be-accelerating-slowdown-in-the-uk-job-market"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AI is enabling headcount reductions}}}\uc2 . Nearly a third of all respondents reported that their organization now explores AI solutions before considering hiring a human.\par \par \uc2 Two-fifths of leaders revealed that entry-level roles have already been reduced or cut due to efficiencies made by AI conducting research, admin and briefing tasks, and 43% expect this to happen in the next year.\par \par \uc2 Susan Taylor Martin, CEOof \uc2 BSI\uc2  says:\par \par \uc2 Worryingly for those trying to enter the jobs market, a quarter of business leaders said they believe most or all tasks done by an entry-level colleague could be performed by AI.\par \par \uc2 A third suspect their own first job would not exist today, due to the rise of artificial intelligence tools.\par \par \uc2 And\u8230\'20\'26 55% said they felt that the benefits of implementing AI in organizations would be worth the disruptions to workforces.\par \par \uc2 These findings will add to concerns that graduates face a workforce crisis as they battle AI in the labour market. A poll released in August found that half of UK adults fear AI will change, or eliminate, their jobs.\par \par \uc2 Telecoms firm BT is replacing about 10,000 jobs with AI systems, as part of a wider workforce reduction programme.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 9.21am BST\par \par \uc2 8.32am BST\par \par \uc2 HSBC\uc2  drags FTSE 100 down\par \par \uc2 The London stock market is in the red this morning, pulled down by banking giant \uc2 HSBC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The FTSE100 has dropped by 30 points, or 0.3%, to 9518, a day after hitting a record high.\par \par \uc2 HSBC\uc2  has dropped by 6%, after it announced plans to take full control of Hong Kong\u8217\'20\'19s HangSeng Bank, in which it already owns a controlling shareholding.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 9.17am BST\par \par \uc2 8.25am BST\par \par \uc2 ICAEW\uc2 : UK business confidence in freefall\par \par \uc2 UK business confidence has dropped to a three-year low as companies fret about higher taxes, a new poll has shown.\par \par \uc2 ICAEW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s business sentiment has dropped to -7.3 for the third quarter of 2025, down from -4.2 in April-June.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s the fifth consecutive quarterly fall in a row, and the lowest level since the last three months of 2022.\par \par \uc2 ICAEW\uc2  explains:\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.33am BST\par \par \uc2 8.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Lloyds\uc2  shares drop as additional motor finance costs loom\par \par \uc2 Shares in \uc2 Lloyds Bank\uc2  have dropped by 3.5% at the start of trading in London, after it warned shareholders it could face a larger financial hit from the UK motor finance scandal.\par \par \uc2 Lloyds\uc2  told the City this morning that it may need to take an \u8220\'20\'1Cadditional provision\u8221\'20\'1D to cover the cost of the issue.\par \par \uc2 This follows the unveiling of a compensation scheme for motorists who bought cars via discretionary commission deals from 2007 to 2024, which could lead to average payouts of \u163\'00\'A3700.\par \par \uc2 Lloyds\uc2  says:\par \par \uc2 Lloyds\uc2  shares have dropped to 84.5p.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.32am BST\par \par \uc2 7.38am BST\par \par \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 's Dimon warns about risks of US stock market fall\par \par \uc2 The boss of \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  has joined the choir of experts warning that a stock market tumble may be approaching.\par \par \uc2 Jamie\par \par \uc2 Dimon has revealed he is concerned that the US stock market is overheated, and cautioned there could be a serious market correction, which he said could come in the next six months to two years.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to the \uc2 BBC\uc2 , Dimon said a \u8220\'20\'1Clot of things out there\u8221\'20\'1D are creating an atmosphere of uncertainty, such as geopolitical risks, government spending, and the remilitarisation of the world.\par \par \uc2 Dimon says:\par \par \uc2 His comments come as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/bankofenglandgovernor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bank of England}}}\uc2  warned of a growing risk of a \u8220\'20\'1Csudden correction\u8221\'20\'1D in global markets, citing concerns about soaring valuations of leading AI tech companies.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.32am BST\par \par \uc2 7.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Table: How water bills will rise\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a table showing the increase to water bills signed off by the CMA, in its \u8220\'20\'1Cprovisional redeterminations on water price controls\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 7.31am BST\par \par \uc2 7.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Britain\u8217\'20\'19s risk of winter blackouts drops to five year low\par \par \uc2 From water to energy \u8230\'20\'26 and Britain\u8217\'20\'19s risk of winter blackouts has fallen to its lowest level in five years, according to the energy system operator \u8230\'20\'26 but it won\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily be affordable.\par \par \uc2 Forecasts by the NationalEnergySystemOperator (\uc2 Neso\uc2 ) show that electricity supply margins \u8211\'20\'13 the amount of generation available above the expected levels of demand \u8211\'20\'13 could reach 10% this winter. This would be the healthiest margins since the winter of 2019-2020.\par \par \uc2 However, the healthier supplies are down to an increase in energy imports, meaning they could be more expensive if international markets demand higher prices.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Neso\uc2  report expects margins to be healthier in part due to the start up of the Greenlink interconnector which runs from Pembrokeshire in Wales to County Wexford in Ireland and which will import power when prices are higher in the UK than in Ireland.\par \par \uc2 The UK\u8217\'20\'19s energy system also has a greater availability of gas plants this winter, after some returned from outage last winter, but this comes as the UK\u8217\'20\'19s gas supply margins shrink to their lowest in four years as the North Sea\u8217\'20\'19s production continues to dwindle.\par \par \uc2 Neso\uc2  warned that the UK will need to rely more heavily on imports of gas via liquified natural gas (LNG) tankers, which typically come from the US and Qatar. \uc2 National Gas\uc2 , which runs the UK\u8217\'20\'19s gas transmission network, expects the UK\u8217\'20\'19s overall gas demand to be slightly lower this winter but added that it can expect 6% less gas from the UK North Sea this winter compared with last year. Instead, it will increase LNG imports by 7%, it said.\par \par \uc2 This raises the chance of higher gas costs if the market price continues to rise. In Europe, gas storage levels are slightly lower than in previous winters meaning more LNG imports could be needed in neighbouring markets, too.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.31am BST\par \par \uc2 7.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Introduction: UK watchdog rejects 80% of water firms' price hike requests, but....\par \par \uc2 Good morning, and welcome to our rolling coverage of business, the financial markets and the world economy.\par \par \uc2 Millions of households in England are to be hit with even higher water bill increases than previously planned, under plans being unveiled by the competition regulator this morning.\par \par \uc2 But the pain isn\u8217\'20\'19t going to be as bad as the water companies had hoped.\par \par \uc2 The CompetitionsandMarketsAuthority has decided to approve around a fifth of spending increases proposed by water companies, on top of existing plans signed off by water regulator \uc2 Ofwat\uc2 , which will be funded by increases in bills.\par \par \uc2 And while it has \u8220\'20\'1Clargely rejected\u8221\'20\'1D companies\u8217\'20\'19 funding requests for new activities and projects, it is provisionally allowing 21% of the total \u163\'00\'A32.7bn requested by AnglianWater, NorthumbrianWater, SouthEastWater, SouthernWater, and WessexWater.\par \par \uc2 This means they can seek an extra \u163\'00\'A3556m in revenue, which is expected to mean an average increase of 3% in bills for customers of the disputing companies.\par \par \uc2 That is on top of the 24% increase in bills for customers of these companies under \uc2 Ofwat\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s original determination, which companies had complained was too stingy.\par \par \uc2 The CMA says this extra money will fund more resilient supply, reduce pollution and also reflect increased financing costs.\par \par \uc2 Kirstin Baker, who chaired the group which examined the issue, says:\par \par \uc2 The agenda\par \par \uc2 * 7am BST: German trade balance\par \par \uc2 * 9.30am BST: Economic activity and social change in the UK, real-time indicators from the ONS\par \par \uc2 * 9.30am BST: \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  policymaker \uc2 Catherine Mann\uc2  gives keynote speech at \uc2 Resolution Foundation\uc2  event\par \par \uc2 * 11am BST: \uc2 Financial Conduct Authority\uc2  annual public meeting\par \par \uc2 * 1.30pm BST: Federal Reserve chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  speaks\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251009ela9001md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
