\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 IRS\uc2  to furlough nearly half its workforce due to government shutdown\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 376 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 October 2025\par 21:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Move comes after White House memo suggests workers may not get back pay, despite law Trump signed in first term\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2  said it will furlough nearly half of its employees \u8211\'20\'13 about 34,000 workers \u8211\'20\'13 due to the government shutdown, making it significantly harder for US taxpayers to receive assistance.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/irs-employee-emergency-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on Wednesday, the \uc2 IRS\uc2  said that \u8220\'20\'1Cdue to the lapse in appropriations\u8221\'20\'1D, it would begin its furlough on 8 October for \u8220\'20\'1Ceveryone except already-identified excepted and exempt employees\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEmployee who are not exempt or excepted are furloughed and placed in a non-pay and non-duty status until further notice; however, all employees should plan to report to work for their next tour of duty,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 IRS\uc2  said, adding that employees would be given up to four hours to close out work requirements and receive formal furlough notification.\par \par \uc2 The furlough {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wtop.com/government/2025/10/irs-to-furlough-nearly-half-of-its-workforce-as-shutdown-enters-second-week/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will leave}}}\uc2  only 53.6%, or 39,870 IRS employees, working as the government remains shut down.\par \par \uc2 In the standard furlough {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.irs.gov/pub/foia/ig/cl/10-8-2025-furlough-decision-letter-fy26.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  provided to all affected employees, David Traynor, acting \uc2 IRS\uc2  human capital officer, confirmed that furloughed employees cannot work and will not be paid during the shutdown.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Treasury Employees Union\uc2 , which represents \uc2 IRS\uc2  employees, condemned the decision, with its president, Doreen Greenwald, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nteu.org/blog/2025/10/08/IRSShutdownStatement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  on Wednesday: \u8220\'20\'1CDue to the government shutdown the American people lost access to many vital services provided by the \uc2 IRS\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The statement continued: \u8220\'20\'1CExpect increased wait times, backlogs and delays implementing tax law changes as the shutdown continues. Taxpayers around the country will now have a much harder time getting the assistance they need, just as they get ready to file their extension returns due next week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IRS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to furlough its employees comes a day after a White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2025/10/07/trump-memo-furloughed-federal-workers-backpay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 memo}}}\uc2  suggested that furloughed workers may not receive back pay, despite the 2019 law Trump signed during his first term, during the last government shutdown; the Government Employee Fair Treatment Act of 2019 (Gefta) ensures government workers would be automatically paid after future shutdowns.\par \par \uc2 In his letter, Traynor said that \u8220\'20\'1Cemployees must be compensated on the earliest date possible after the lapse ends, regardless of scheduled pay dates\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251008ela8004xu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
