\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 US \u8216\'20\'18flying blind\u8217\'20\'19 at critical moment for economy, experts warn, with no jobs data amid shutdown\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 592 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2025\par 16:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Data was collected for closely-watched jobs report before shutdown, but Trump officials so far defy calls to publish it\par \par \uc2 Companies, consumers, policymakers and investors across the US are \u8220\'20\'1Cflying blind\u8221\'20\'1D at a crucial time for the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest economy, a former top official has warned, after Friday\u8217\'20\'19s closely-watched jobs report was not published as a result of the federal government shutdown.\par \par \uc2 The data for the release have already been collected, according to two former heads of the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  (\uc2 BLS\uc2 ). But the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  has so far defied calls to publish the report.\par \par \uc2 Employment growth has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/sep/05/us-jobs-report-august-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slowing for months}}}\uc2 . Donald Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/sep/17/labor-statistics-chief-trump-erika-mcentarfer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired the BLS commissioner}}}\uc2  in August, claiming without evidence that official data had been \u8220\'20\'1Cfaked\u8221\'20\'1D, as the labor market softened.\par \par \uc2 Erica Groshen\uc2 , who served as \uc2 BLS\uc2  commissioner during the Obama administration, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWithout today\u8217\'20\'19s jobs report and next week\u8217\'20\'19s scheduled inflation release (the data for which are already collected), the Federal Reserve, US treasury, financial markets, businesses and households will be flying blind.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey will be less certain of current conditions at what may or may not be the beginning of a recession \u8211\'20\'13 precisely when their decisions are most consequential.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week William Beach, who led the \uc2 BLS\uc2  for four years under Trump and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2 , also said the jobs data for September \u8220\'20\'1Chave been completely collected and processed\u8221\'20\'1D by the \uc2 BLS\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe jobs report is likely written in final draft,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fiscallab.org/financial-markets/qa-on-how-the-government-shutdown-will-affect-reports-from-the-bureau-of-labor-statistics/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to a private jobs report from the payroll processing company ADP, US firms lost {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/business/economy/companies-adp-lost-32000-jobs-rcna234880"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 32,000 jobs }}}\uc2 in the month of September, contrary to expectations from Wall Street of job growth of 45,000 for the month. ADP also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/business/economy/companies-adp-lost-32000-jobs-rcna234880"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revised}}}\uc2  its August job numbers from a growth of 54,000 jobs to a loss of 3,000 jobs.\par \par \uc2 Paul Schroeder, executive director of the Council of Professional Associations on Federal Statistics said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe monthly jobs report is a key economic indicator which is particularly critical at this moment as economists are trying to get a handle on how much the US labor market has cooled. Since the release is delayed, a big piece of the labor market puzzle is missing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Democratic senator Elizabeth Warren has called on the Trump administration to release the jobs report and upcoming inflation data despite the shutdown. \u8220\'20\'1CThe jobs data scheduled to come out this Friday has undoubtedly been collected and the President must release it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWithout it, the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  will not have the full picture it needs to make decisions this month about interest rates that will impact every family across the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDonald Trump has the power to make sure the federal government can continue producing and releasing this critical information on Friday and beyond during his shutdown.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Under the shutdown, the \uc2 BLS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s contingency plan calls for furloughing all employees but the acting commissioner at the agency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the event of a federal government shutdown, the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  (\uc2 BLS\uc2 ) will suspend data collection, processing, and dissemination,\u8221\'20\'1D an agency spokesperson said in an email. \u8220\'20\'1COnce funding is restored, \uc2 BLS\uc2  will resume normal operations and notify the public of any changes to the news release schedule on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/schedule/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BLS release calendar}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s nominee to lead the \uc2 BLS\uc2 , EJ Antoni, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/01/trump-administration-withdraws-ej-antoni-bureau-of-labor-statistics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withdrew}}}\uc2  his nomination earlier this week after his selection drew bipartisan criticism over his lack of qualifications and consensus he was too partisan for the role.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020251003ela3004pi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
