\par\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Heartbroken\u8217\'20\'19: staff laid off as California TV station abruptly closes newsroom\b0\par\par\uc2 Dani Anguiano \par \uc2 486 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 September 2025\par 21:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 KION-TV announces partnership with San Francisco CBS affiliate as workers condemn \u8216\'20\'18disservice to the community\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 This week KION-TV, a broadcast news outlet on California\u8217\'20\'19s central coast that\u8217\'20\'19s been on the air for more than 50 years, announced it was entering a \u8220\'20\'1Cnew chapter\u8221\'20\'1D with a San Francisco CBS affiliate to bring expanded coverage to its viewers.\par \par \uc2 But staff say the development has been devastating for the operation \u8211\'20\'13 the newsroom, which covers Salinas, Santa Cruz and Monterey, suddenly shuttered and more than a dozen people were laid off.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI still can\u8217\'20\'19t believe it. I ended my morning show by saying, \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19ll have more news at 5.\u8217\'20\'19 I had no idea,\u8221\'20\'1D Victor Guzman, the station\u8217\'20\'19s assistant news director, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lookout.co/as-kion-ends-local-news-ksbw-is-now-only-tv-broadcaster-serving-750k-on-the-central-coast/story"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lookout Santa Cruz}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 KION broadcast its last show on Tuesday morning and executives with the station\u8217\'20\'19s owner, the \uc2 News-Press & Gazette\uc2 , informed employees of the decision, while others learned of the development from co-workers, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2025-09-24/california-tv-news-station-shuts-down"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles Times}}}\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kioncentralcoast.com/news/top-stories/2025/09/23/kpix-news-launches-on-kion-expanding-statewide-coverage-for-the-central-coast/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  published on Tuesday and attributed to the KION546 news team, the station announced that beginning that afternoon it would \u8220\'20\'1Cno longer produce its own full local newscasts\u8221\'20\'1D. KION will instead partner with KPIX CBS San Francisco to bring viewers the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost significant stories\u8221\'20\'1D from northern and central California, \u8220\'20\'1Cwhile continuing to highlight local reporting, weather forecasts and community updates\u8221\'20\'1D, the statement said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur partnership with KPIX ensures that viewers across the Monterey, Salinas and Santa Cruz region continue to receive the high-quality local journalism they deserve,\u8221\'20\'1D Rall Bradley, an executive at the \uc2 News-Press & Gazette\uc2 , said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis collaboration brings together KION\u8217\'20\'19s deep roots in the community with the trusted reporting and innovative storytelling of CBS Bay Area \u8211\'20\'13 delivering a seamless experience for viewers during a time of change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, workers report that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lookout.co/telemundo-23-ends-its-local-news-leaving-central-coast-without-a-spanish-language-newscast/story"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Telemundo 23}}}\uc2 , which was housed at KION, is also shutting down, leaving an area with a majority-Latino population without a Spanish-language news show.\par \par \uc2 Local news has collapsed across the US in recent decades, with a 75% drop in local journalists since 2002, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rebuildlocalnews.org/new-report-reveals-alarming-and-widespread-shortage-of-local-journalists-across-the-u-s/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from Muck Rack and Rebuild Local News, which describes the decline as \u8220\'20\'1Calarming and widespread\u8221\'20\'1D. One in three US counties do not have the equivalent of one full-time local journalist, and an average of 2.5 newspapers shut down each week.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.montereycountynow.com/blogs/opinion_blog/kion-s-salinas-newsroom-is-dissolved-a-devastating-blow-to-the-local-news-landscape/article_f9e67be4-3874-4e94-b932-b09f266d552a.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Monterey County Now}}}\uc2  described the development as a \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating blow\u8221\'20\'1D to local journalism. Jeanette Bent, the station\u8217\'20\'19s managing editor, told the outlet: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a disservice to this community and we\u8217\'20\'19re all heartbroken.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The News-Press & Gazette has offered to pay staff for the remainder of their \u8220\'20\'1Ccontractual year\u8221\'20\'1D and help those interested in relocating to other \uc2 News-Press & Gazette\uc2  stations, Guzman told Lookout Santa Cruz.\par \par \uc2 The News-Press & Gazette did not immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250925el9p005xx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
