\par\par \b \uc2 What to know about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new $100,000 H-1B visa fee\b0\par\par\uc2 Coral Murphy Marcos \par \uc2 1,218 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 September 2025\par 16:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 White House proclamation announcing new visa fees has prompted questions and confusion \u8211\'20\'13 here\u8217\'20\'19s what to know\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration has announced an annual $100,000 fee on H-1B visa applications, a type of US visa that allows companies to hire foreign workers in skilled occupations such as IT, healthcare and engineering.\par \par \uc2 The new proclamation, signed on Friday, brought a mixed bag of emotions for hundreds of thousands of workers on H-1B visas, as well as many question. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what you need to know.\par \par \uc2 What is an H-1B visa?\par \par \uc2 The H-1B program dates back to 1990, when George HW Bush {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/statement-signing-the-immigration-act-1990"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a new bill into law}}}\uc2  in an effort to encourage the immigration of highly skilled workers, including scientists, engineers and educators, to address labor shortages in specialized fields.\par \par \uc2 This temporary visa category allows employers to petition for \u8220\'20\'1Chighly educated\u8221\'20\'1D foreign professionals to work in \u8220\'20\'1Cspecialty occupations\u8221\'20\'1D that require at least a bachelor\u8217\'20\'19s degree or the equivalent. The H-1B visa is typically granted for an initial period of three years and can be extended up to a maximum of six years.\par \par \uc2 There are as many as 730,000 H-1B holders in the US, and an additional 550,000 dependents, including spouses and children, who together make up nearly 1.3 million residents, according to a January 2025 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fwd.us/news/h1b-visa-program/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from fwd.us, an immigration and criminal justice advocacy group.\par \par \uc2 Previously, the cost for an H-1B ranged from about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://international.indianapolis.iu.edu/visas/departments/h1b-workers/h1b-fees.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1,700 to $4,500}}}\uc2 , depending on whether the visa was expedited. Each year, Congress caps H-1B visas at 85,000, awarded through a lottery system. To enter, companies pay a $215 registration fee, followed by the thousands of dollars more in application fees and legal costs if selected.\par \par \uc2 What changes did Trump announce?\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration increased the fee for skilled foreign workers applying for H-1B visas to $100,000, claiming the visas were being \u8220\'20\'1Cabused\u8221\'20\'1D to undercut American wages and outsource IT jobs. The new fee went into effect on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 The fees are intended to be paid by companies sponsoring the visas, rather than applicants themselves. The Trump administration implemented the fee in an effort to encourage companies to hire more American workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEither the person is very valuable to the company and America, or they are going to depart and the company is going to hire an American,\u8221\'20\'1D said US commerce secretary \uc2 Howard Lutnick\uc2  at Friday\u8217\'20\'19s briefing. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd that\u8217\'20\'19s the point of immigration. Hire Americans and make sure the people coming in are the top, top people. Stop the nonsense.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the Trump administration proposed a new process that would move away from the current random selection process to a weighted selection process, according to a Federal Register notice. The proposed process would give more weight to H-1B applications for roles with the highest wages if applications for the visas exceed the annual cap of 85,000.\par \par \uc2 Roles that meet or exceed the highest level of wages for the industry, as laid out by the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 , would be entered into the visa selection pool four times, roles that meet or exceed the second-highest level of wages would be entered three times and so on. DHS said that, if the proposal is finalized, the goal would be to incentivize \u8220\'20\'1Cemployers to offer higher wages, or to petition for positions requiring higher skills and higher skilled aliens, that are commensurate with higher wage levels\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe proposed process would favor the allocation of H-1B visas to higher skilled and higher paid aliens, while maintaining the opportunity for employers to secure H-1B workers at all wage levels,\u8221\'20\'1D the proposal reads.\par \par \uc2 Trump thoughts on H-1B have been anything but steady. Last year, the president told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2024/12/28/us-news/donald-trump-backs-h-1b-visa-program-supported-by-elon-musk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Post}}}\uc2  he supported the program, calling himself a \u8220\'20\'1Cbeliever\u8221\'20\'1D in the visas, and that he has used it \u8220\'20\'1Cmany times\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But, more recently, he said that adding such costly hurdles to the visa process will help protect American jobs. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a fantastic thing, and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to take that money and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to reduce taxes, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to reduce debt,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 What industries are affected?\par \par \uc2 Tech workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfchronicle.com/projects/2025/bay-area-h1b-visa-tracker/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 make up one of the largest groups}}}\uc2  of H-1B visa recipients, and the fee announcement sent the tech industry scrambling, with businesses in Silicon Valley urging staff not to travel outside the country amid early confusion over the new process.\par \par \uc2 Stem\uc2  (science, technology, engineering and mathematics) industries rely heavily on the H-1B program, with roughly two-thirds of H-1B jobs in computer-related roles. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uscis.gov/tools/reports-and-studies/h-1b-employer-data-hub"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to US Citizenship and Immigration Services}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Google\uc2 , \uc2 Meta\uc2 , \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and \uc2 Apple\uc2  were among the companies that employed the most H-1B visa holders last year.\par \par \uc2 Several prominent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/h-1b-visa-success-stories-elon-musk-sundar-pichai-and-other-h-1b-visa-holders-who-shape-the-future-of-the-us-tech-industry/articleshow/124037259.cms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tech industry leaders}}}\uc2 , including \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , \uc2 Alphabet\uc2  chief executive \uc2 Sundar Pichai\uc2  and \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  chief executive \uc2 Satya Nadella\uc2 , were at one point H-1B visa holders.\par \par \uc2 Employers also use the program to bring in educators and healthcare workers to the US.\par \par \uc2 What has the reaction been?\par \par \uc2 Economists have warned that the move could lead to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/sep/22/trump-h-1b-visa-fees-us-economy-tech-india"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weaker economic growth}}}\uc2 , since higher costs for employers will make it harder to attract foreign talent. They have also pointed to a potential \u8220\'20\'1Cbrain drain\u8221\'20\'1D as skilled international graduates are forced to leave the US.\par \par \uc2 In India, the largest beneficiary of H-1B visas last year, officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/22/trump-india-h1-b-visa-fee-hike-response-afraid-of-talent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said the fee}}}\uc2  would have humanitarian consequences \u8220\'20\'1Cby way of the disruption caused for families\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Indian government said it \u8220\'20\'1Chopes that these disruptions can be addressed suitably by the US authorities\u8221\'20\'1D and emphasised that the exchange of skilled workers had \u8220\'20\'1Ccontributed enormously\u8221\'20\'1D to both nations.\par \par \uc2 Other business leaders, however, have praised Trump\u8217\'20\'19s move, including \uc2 Netflix\uc2  co-founder \uc2 Reed Hastings\uc2 . In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/reedhastings/status/1969828972688248953?s=42"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post on X}}}\uc2 , Hastings said he had worked on H-1B politics for 30 years and said the added cost would allot visas for \u8220\'20\'1Cvery high-value jobs\u8221\'20\'1D. He said the move would eliminate the lottery and give employers more certainty.\par \par \uc2 Most major Silicon Valley companies have not publicly commented. Companies have sent internal memos to employees.\par \par \uc2 Before the new fee was announced, the visa had been contested across the political spectrum. The democratic socialist senator Bernie Sanders, for example, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/technology/5064132-sanders-criticizes-musk-h1b-visa/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been a longtime critic}}}\uc2  of the H-1B visa, arguing that the program replaces American jobs with cheaper international workers.\par \par \uc2 Do people who already hold an H-1B visa have to worry?\par \par \uc2 Lutnick said the fee would be paid annually, and would only apply to people seeking a new visa.\par \par \uc2 Amid initial confusion over the weekend, White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/PressSec/status/1969495900478488745"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clarified}}}\uc2  that the fee applies only to new applicants, and that those who already hold H-1B visas and are currently outside of the country would not be charged $100,000 to re-enter.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CH-1B visa holders can leave and re-enter the country to the same extent as they normally would; whatever ability they have to do that is not impacted by yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s proclamation,\u8221\'20\'1D Leavitt said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis applies only to new visas, not renewals, and not current visa holders.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250922el9m005eh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
