\par\par \b \uc2 Scams, silence, rejection: US job seekers describe \u8216\'20\'18depressing\u8217\'20\'19 work prospects\b0\par\par\uc2 Marina Dunbar \par \uc2 1,302 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 September 2025\par 11:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Qualified candidates struggle in a sluggish market due to Trump tariffs, AI screening and vanishing entry-level roles\par \par \uc2 When Philip Kowalski lost his job earlier this year as a \uc2 USAID\uc2  contractor working on aid to Ukraine due to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/01/musk-doge-usaid-firings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Doge cuts}}}\uc2 , he was confident in his credentials: a master\u8217\'20\'19s degree from the University of London and years of hands-on experience managing American foreign aid contracts that he thought would help him land on his feet.\par \par \uc2 Instead, he found himself adrift in what he calls \u8220\'20\'1Ca massive pool of unemployed people who are highly qualified all competing for the same tiny pool of available jobs\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve put out maybe 400 job applications in the last five months,\u8221\'20\'1D Kowalski said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve only gotten a handful of interviews. I think I\u8217\'20\'19ve interviewed with six different places. It\u8217\'20\'19s a really bleak situation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kowalski, 36, is far from alone. From the tech-centric coasts to the US deep south, job seekers describe a market where even advanced degrees, decades of experience and thousands of applications often yield little more than silence or, often, scam calls.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  (\uc2 BLS\uc2 ) announced on Tuesday that the US added {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/sep/09/us-created-fewer-jobs-march-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 911,000 fewer jobs}}}\uc2  than first estimated for the year to March 2025, highlighting already heightened concerns about the health of the labor market.\par \par \uc2 The news followed a lackluster August jobs report, with only 22,000 jobs added in the US. That report noted that 13,000 jobs were lost for the month of June 2025, the first negative jobs report survey since December 2020, the height of the Covid-19 pandemic. The unemployment rate increased to 4.3%, the highest rate since 2021.\par \par \uc2 Erika McEntarfer, commissioner of labor statistics, was fired by Trump after a weak job\u8217\'20\'19s report in July, which the president claimed, without evidence, was \u8220\'20\'1CRIGGED in order to make the Republicans, and ME, look bad\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Long-term unemployment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/opub/ted/2025/long-term-unemployed-accounted-for-25-7-percent-of-all-unemployed-people-in-august-2025.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has also climbed}}}\uc2 , with 1.9 million Americans out of work for at least 27 weeks as of August 2025, double the figure from early 2023. At the same time, underemployment is growing: more people are working part-time involuntarily, or accepting jobs far below their skill level simply to secure benefits or cover bills.\par \par \uc2 The sluggish market is due in part to the uncertainty added by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs, while automation and artificial intelligence are compounding these struggles. Hiring platforms and applicant tracking systems rely heavily on keyword filters, which can exclude qualified candidates who don\u8217\'20\'19t use the precise terms. Recent research has also linked AI adoption to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/ai-artificial-intelligence-jobs-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 higher unemployment}}}\uc2  in certain fields.\par \par \uc2 The gap between official statistics and lived experience is stark and growing. Taylor Napier, a 32-year-old from Kentucky, thought finishing her MBA would open new doors. Instead, she says she graduated \u8220\'20\'1Cin what is apparently the most difficult year to get a job with an MBA in the history of the degree\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Napier has sent \u8220\'20\'1Cover 2,000 applications over the last six months\u8221\'20\'1D, tailoring multiple resumes for roles in consulting, healthcare operations, HR and sales. Yet she says \u8220\'20\'1Cvery few people reach out for an interview anymore. It\u8217\'20\'19s mostly scams that contact me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She points to what she sees as systemic problems: AI-driven hiring tools that \u8220\'20\'1Caren\u8217\'20\'19t really catching actually qualified people\u8221\'20\'1D, a reliance on networking that collapses when \u8220\'20\'1Ccompanies are laying off thousands, tens of thousands of global employees\u8221\'20\'1D and entry-level roles vanishing under automation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe bottleneck is going to happen when, 15 to 20 years from now, your middle management is looking to retire, and you don\u8217\'20\'19t have any new fresh blood coming in,\u8221\'20\'1D Napier said.\par \par \uc2 For Hayden, a 46-year-old former software executive, the decline has been just as clear. He once served as chief operating officer of a tech company. Now, he works in a warehouse \u8220\'20\'1Cin order to have insurance for my family\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hayden has applied to \u8220\'20\'1Cnorth of 100 jobs in the past 18 months\u8221\'20\'1D, spending $1,000 on professional resume services optimized for AI filters. But he says employers\u8217\'20\'19 reliance on algorithms and inexperienced screeners often derails qualified candidates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of the primary concerns with screenings is that you have extremely under-qualified people doing the screenings and conducting the initial interviews,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI had an interview with a major bank a few weeks ago. I\u8217\'20\'19m a former COO of a software company, and the early 20s interviewer was asking me if I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever used technology in my previous positions. I asked her if she\u8217\'20\'19d actually read my resume.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He describes the market as \u8220\'20\'1Cheavily tilted towards employers\u8221\'20\'1D, where job postings sometimes serve more to build resume databases than to fill roles.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of the largest misconceptions and misdirections that has been done in the past year is to create the illusion that there isn\u8217\'20\'19t an employment crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D Hayden said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere absolutely is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amanda Bradshaw, a 44-year-old creeler from Georgia, describes the job market as \u8220\'20\'1Clike the dating scene only the recruiters are the ones swiping left\u8221\'20\'1D. She says she has applied to over 200 jobs but has not received a single call back. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I call them they tell me they aren\u8217\'20\'19t hiring. It\u8217\'20\'19s depressing,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Despite official unemployment rates hovering around 4\u8211\'20\'135%, job seekers overwhelmingly believe the statistics hide the reality. \u8220\'20\'1CI would speculate that it\u8217\'20\'19s at least double that,\u8221\'20\'1D Hayden said.\par \par \uc2 Kowalski echoed that sentiment, calling DC \u8220\'20\'1Cground zero\u8221\'20\'1D for the economic collapse: \u8220\'20\'1CI think that Washington DC has not bottomed out yet. There might not be a bottom because the federal government is hostile towards federal employees and contractors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that the Trump administration has turned DC even more so into a place where only the wealthiest can afford to live and make their way professionally,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, for an administration that fancies itself as big anti-elites, they\u8217\'20\'19ve turned DC into an elites-only place.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Napier, who currently works in nursing, says the instability has reshaped her life plans: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m at the age where I would like to start a family, but certainly can\u8217\'20\'19t afford one. It\u8217\'20\'19s become too difficult to save.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lexi, a 29-year-old copywriter from Oklahoma, said she was laid off in summer 2024. \u8220\'20\'1CIn the hundreds of jobs I applied for between the time I started looking casually and when I was laid off, I didn\u8217\'20\'19t get a single interview despite having over five years of experience,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CMy husband is in the same boat, he\u8217\'20\'19s been a manager at a movie theater for 14 years and can\u8217\'20\'19t find anything else. I\u8217\'20\'19m on a higher dose of anxiety medication than ever before because of how bad things have gotten politically in the US and even locally in Oklahoma.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The increasing prevalence of scams add another obstacle to the job search, including fake postings, misleading offers or predatory \u8220\'20\'1Copportunities.\u8221\'20\'1D Kowalski says he receives \u8220\'20\'1Cabout five a week minimum\u8221\'20\'1D. Napier said most of the rare contacts she gets are \u8220\'20\'1Cindependent contractor\u8221\'20\'1D roles with no benefits or security: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not sure who\u8217\'20\'19s taking that deal, but it seems to be sticking around.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Even legitimate offers come with caveats. Hayden described one company offering higher salaries if workers declined health benefits: \u8220\'20\'1CThey were going to give a substantial increase in salary if you turn down any benefits \u8230\'20\'26 $12,000 more a year if you did not use their medical, dental, vision,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 As Napier put it: \u8220\'20\'1CYou have a lot of people who are in the middle of their career applying for entry level roles, because, you know, any port in a storm.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250922el9m0028p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
