\par\par \b \uc2 Strikes and marches against budget cuts cause disruption across France, with 141 arrests \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Jakub Krupa \par \uc2 3,984 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 September 2025\par 16:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 At least 476 separate demonstrations are taking place over public services and wages, a week after the appointment of new PM S\u233\'00\'E9bastien LecornuPeople in France: share your views on the strikeFull report: France\u8217\'20\'19s biggest strike in years under way amid political crisis\par \par \uc2 4.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 and on that note, it\u8217\'20\'19s a wrap!\par \par \uc2 * Thousands of people have marched in demonstrations across France on a national day of strikes affecting schools, transport, pharmacies, and other industries ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/sep/18/france-strikes-lecornu-merz-sanchez-von-der-leyen-europe-live-latest-updates?page=with%3Ablock-68cbb2368f085b3ecec02f6e#block-68cbb2368f085b3ecec02f6e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 9:49}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 * More than 140 people had been arrested as of late afternoon, with major protests reported in Marseille, Nantes, Lyon, Paris and other cities ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/sep/18/france-strikes-lecornu-merz-sanchez-von-der-leyen-europe-live-latest-updates?page=with%3Ablock-68cbd6e28f08e4203c9a6bea#block-68cbd6e28f08e4203c9a6bea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 12:00}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/sep/18/france-strikes-lecornu-merz-sanchez-von-der-leyen-europe-live-latest-updates?page=with%3Ablock-68cbe7558f08e4203c9a6cf4#block-68cbe7558f08e4203c9a6cf4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 13:14}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/sep/18/france-strikes-lecornu-merz-sanchez-von-der-leyen-europe-live-latest-updates?page=with%3Ablock-68cbf6738f0816a4522bd281#block-68cbf6738f0816a4522bd281"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 14:11}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/sep/18/france-strikes-lecornu-merz-sanchez-von-der-leyen-europe-live-latest-updates?page=with%3Ablock-68cbf8188f08895801e078af#block-68cbf8188f08895801e078af"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 14:22}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/sep/18/france-strikes-lecornu-merz-sanchez-von-der-leyen-europe-live-latest-updates?page=with%3Ablock-68cc09528f0816a4522bd3aa#block-68cc09528f0816a4522bd3aa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 15:33}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/sep/18/france-strikes-lecornu-merz-sanchez-von-der-leyen-europe-live-latest-updates?page=with%3Ablock-68cc1c668f08895801e07acf#block-68cc1c668f08895801e07acf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 16:54}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 * Most demonstrations were peaceful, with some reports of isolated clashes and \u8220\'20\'1Cprovocations\u8221\'20\'1D at some of them, with tensions also reported at the main event in Paris this afternoon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/sep/18/france-strikes-lecornu-merz-sanchez-von-der-leyen-europe-live-latest-updates?page=with%3Ablock-68cc1fca8f0816a4522bd4e8#block-68cc1fca8f0816a4522bd4e8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 17:11}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 Separately,\par \par \uc2 * US president Donald Trumpsaid that Russian presidentVladimir Putin \u8220\'20\'1Clet him down\u8221\'20\'1D ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/sep/18/france-strikes-lecornu-merz-sanchez-von-der-leyen-europe-live-latest-updates?page=with%3Ablock-68cc15458f0816a4522bd452#block-68cc15458f0816a4522bd452"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 16:23}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/sep/18/france-strikes-lecornu-merz-sanchez-von-der-leyen-europe-live-latest-updates?page=with%3Ablock-68cc16788f08e4203c9a6fc6#block-68cc16788f08e4203c9a6fc6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 16:42}}}\uc2 ) as he spoke at a press conference alongside UK\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2  and repeated his demand for European allies to drop Russian oil supplies ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/sep/18/france-strikes-lecornu-merz-sanchez-von-der-leyen-europe-live-latest-updates?page=with%3Ablock-68cc1d618f08895801e07ada#block-68cc1d618f08895801e07ada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 16:58}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 * His comments came after Putin revealed that over 700,000 Russian soldiers were involved in the war against Ukraine, while Ukraine claimed it pushed back some of Russian recent advances. ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/sep/18/france-strikes-lecornu-merz-sanchez-von-der-leyen-europe-live-latest-updates?page=with%3Ablock-68cc112e8f08e4203c9a6f5f#block-68cc112e8f08e4203c9a6f5f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 16:11}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 * There was no update on the \uc2 EU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s latest, 19th, package of sanctions against Russia, with the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  saying only that it expected to \u8220\'20\'1Cpresent [them] soon\u8221\'20\'1D ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/sep/18/france-strikes-lecornu-merz-sanchez-von-der-leyen-europe-live-latest-updates?page=with%3Ablock-68cbdc9a8f08e4203c9a6c2b#block-68cbdc9a8f08e4203c9a6c2b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 12:22}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 And that\u8217\'20\'19s all from me, Jakub Krupa, for today. You can read our main report on the French marches and strikes here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/18/strike-action-across-france-as-hundreds-of-thousands-march-to-demand-pm-rethinks-budget-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Strike action across France as hundreds of thousands march to demand PM rethinks budget cuts}}}\par \par \uc2 If you have any tips, comments or suggestions, email me at jakub.krupa@theguardian.com.\par \par \uc2 I am also on Bluesky at @jakubkrupa.bsky.social and on X at @jakubkrupa.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 'Provocations' reported on margins of Paris demonstration\par \par \uc2 The French police is now reporting some isolated \u8220\'20\'1Cprovocations\u8221\'20\'1D on the margins of the main demonstration in Paris, including attempted attacks on banks, with some clashes between protesters and police, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.leparisien.fr/economie/direct-greve-du-18-septembre-800-000-manifestants-attendus-risques-de-troubles-blocages-les-policiers-deja-sur-le-front-18-09-2025-FHGIVK2BX5HVJACAZXI7SBPXRU.php#e08b10fe-dba4-43c8-a940-9c17329134f2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Le Figaro and Le Parisien reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the CGT union claimed that over million people took part in today\u8217\'20\'19s protests, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lemonde.fr/politique/live/2025/09/18/en-direct-mobilisation-du-18-septembre-suivez-les-greves-et-les-manifestations-a-l-appel-de-l-intersyndicale_6641656_823448.html?#id-2577794"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Le Monde said.}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 4.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 'If oil price comes down, Putin is going to drop out' of war with Ukraine, Trump says\par \par \uc2 Back to Chequers, on Russia, Trump also gives another hint at what he expects Europe to do next as he says that \u8220\'20\'1Cif the price of oil comes down, Putin is going to drop out, he\u8217\'20\'19s going to have no choice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He says he is willing \u8220\'20\'1Cto do other things\u8221\'20\'1D to help Europeans push back against Russia, but \u8220\'20\'1Cnot when the people that I\u8217\'20\'19m fighting for are buying oil from Russia\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t [do that], that\u8217\'20\'19s not playing fair with the United States, and we can\u8217\'20\'19t have that,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the oil price comes down, very simply, Russia will settle,\u8221\'20\'1D he insists.\par \par \uc2 And it ends the press conference.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 280,000 people took part in French protests excluding Paris, estimates suggest\par \par \uc2 We are getting more figures from France on the number of people arrested on the sidelines of today\u8217\'20\'19s protests.\par \par \uc2 By 4pm, 141 people had been arrested, including 21 in Paris, and 75 people remain in custody, the latest figures from the interior ministry showed.\par \par \uc2 The authorities say just over 280,000 people attended protests outside of Paris, but the numbers are still being checked, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lemonde.fr/politique/live/2025/09/18/en-direct-mobilisation-du-18-septembre-suivez-les-greves-et-les-manifestations-a-l-appel-de-l-intersyndicale_6641656_823448.html?#id-2577717"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Le Monde reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 3.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 My focus here is on broader European issues, but the two leaders also answered questions about their conversations on domestic migration, energy, and free speech.\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re interested, you can read the key lines over on the UK blog here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2025/sep/18/donald-trump-state-visit-uk-keir-starmer-labour-politics-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump suggests Starmer use military to cu\u8211\'20\'13 UK politics live}}}\par \par \uc2 3.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Russians 'being killed at higher rate than Ukrainian soldiers,' Trump says\par \par \uc2 Trump gets asked a follow-up question on Putin.\par \par \uc2 He repeats that Putin \u8220\'20\'1Chas let me down,\u8221\'20\'1D and he adds:\par \par \uc2 He then goes on about other conflicts he claims to have solved.\par \par \uc2 But eventually comes back to Ukraine and says he hopes \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re going to have some good news for you coming up\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He repeatedly says that the Russian invasion of Ukraine was potentially \u8220\'20\'1Cheading to a third world war\u8221\'20\'1D although \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think we\u8217\'20\'19re going to go there now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Starmer responds with a general line on the need to put more pressure on Putin, and he also notes last week\u8217\'20\'19s Russian drone incursion into Polish airspace.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 3.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 'He's really let me down,' Trump says about Putin\par \par \uc2 In his opening comments, Trump strikes a similar line, saying he will be working on ending the Russian invasion of Ukraine, repeating his usual line that he thought it \u8220\'20\'1Cwould be easiest [to end] because of my relationship with President Putin\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But, unusually, he goes a bit further and adds:\par \par \uc2 He then says \u8220\'20\'1Cwe will see how that turns out\u8221\'20\'1D, and that \u8220\'20\'1CRussia and Ukraine will get done, but \u8230\'20\'26 you never know in war, you know, war is a different thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThings happen that are very opposite of what you thought, you thought you were going to have an easy time or a hard time, and it turns out to be the reverse,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 3.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 3.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 In his opening comments, Starmer says the pair has \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscussed today how we can build our defences, further support Ukraine, and decisively increase the pressure on Putin to get him to agree a peace deal that will last.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s see what Trump says on that point. He\u8217\'20\'19s speaking now.\par \par \uc2 3.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Starmer, Trump give press conference at Chequers\par \par \uc2 Over in Britain, Starmer and Trump are now giving a press conference at the end of the US president\u8217\'20\'19s two-day state visit in the UK.\par \par \uc2 It could be a lively one.\par \par \uc2 You can watch along here:\par \par \uc2 I will bring you all major non-UK news lines here, but you can also check our UK live blog here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2025/sep/18/donald-trump-state-visit-uk-keir-starmer-labour-politics-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump and Starmer hold joint press conference after signing \u8216\'20\'18tech prosperity deal\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 UK politics live}}}\par \par \uc2 3.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Zelenskyy says Ukraine 'pushed back' some of Russia's advances as Putin reveals 700,000 soldiers are deployed on frontline\par \par \uc2 We are also getting some updates from Ukraine, where the country\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2 , met troops in the eastern Donetsk region and announced his army had pushed back some of the advances Russia made over the summer, AFP said.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian leader said his troops had reclaimed 160 sq km (62 sq miles) of land near the eastern coal mining town of Dobropillia, where Russia pierced Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s defences in August.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , said on Thursday that more than 700,000 Russian soldiers are now deployed on the Ukrainian frontline.\par \par \uc2 Putin made the comment during a televised meeting with top Russian lawmakers, Reuters said.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Main Paris demonstration under way \u8212\'20\'14 in pictures\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the main Paris demonstrations is now under way and we\u8217\'20\'19re getting first pictures of what\u8217\'20\'19s happening on the streets of the French capital.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 2.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Italy first in EU to pass comprehensive law regulating use of AI\par \par \uc2 in Rome\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, Italy has become the first country in the EU to approve a comprehensive law regulating the use of artificial intelligence, including imposing prison terms on those who use the technology to cause harm, such as generating deepfakes, and limiting child access.\par \par \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rightwing government said the legislation, which aligns with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/08/eu-agrees-historic-deal-with-worlds-first-laws-to-regulate-ai"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 EU\u8217\'20\'19s landmark AI Act}}}\uc2 , is a decisive move in influencing how AI is used across Italy.\par \par \uc2 The aim is to promote \u8220\'20\'1Chuman-centric, transparent and safe AI use\u8221\'20\'1D while emphasising \u8220\'20\'1Cinnovation, cybersecurity and privacy protections\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The bill introduces prison sentences of between one and five years for the illegal spreading of AI-generated or manipulated content if it causes harm.\par \par \uc2 There will also be harsher penalties for using the technology to commit crimes, including fraud and identity theft, and stricter transparency and human oversight rules governing how the technology is used in workplaces as well as in a range of sectors such as healthcare, education, justice and sport.\par \par \uc2 In addition, children under the age of 14 will need parental consent to access AI.\par \par \uc2 When it comes to copyright, the law stipulates that works created with AI assistance are protected if they originate from genuine intellectual effort, while AI-driven text and data mining will only be permitted for non-copyrighted content or scientific research by authorised institutions.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/18/italy-first-in-eu-to-pass-comprehensive-law-regulating-ai"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Italy first in EU to pass comprehensive law regulating use of AI}}}\par \par \uc2 1.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Starmer, Trump speaking at reception for business leaders\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2  and Donald Trumpare speaking at a reception for business leaders at Chequers.\par \par \uc2 You can follow all the key lines coming out of that meeting with Andrew Sparrow over on the UK blog here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2025/sep/18/donald-trump-state-visit-uk-keir-starmer-labour-politics-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump and Starmer hold talks at Chequers as UK businesses hope for tariff concessions \u8211\'20\'13 UK politics live}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 or watch their speeches live here:\par \par \uc2 Updated at 1.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 1.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Some clashes were reported on the margins of protest rallies in the western city of Nantes, with police firing teargas, and in Lyon, where French media said three people were injured, Reuters said.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 1.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 1.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Crowds gather in Paris as part of day of strikes and marches \u8212\'20\'14 in pictures\par \par \uc2 Updated at 2.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 12.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Are you in France? Tells us what you think.\par \par \uc2 Are you in France? How do you view of Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s strikes? Are you taking part?\par \par \uc2 Tell us what you think.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/18/people-in-france-share-your-views-of-thursdays-nationwide-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 People in France: share your views of Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s nationwide strike }}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 12.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 12.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Strikes and protests across France \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates\par \par \uc2 Back in France, we\u8217\'20\'19re getting more striking pictures from the day of strikes and protests across the country.\par \par \uc2 94 people\par \par \uc2 had been arrested by midday, including 15 in Paris, and 32 remain in custody, according to the latest government figures reported by the French media. At least 476 separate demonstrations are under way.\par \par \uc2 About 15,000 people took part in a demonstration in Marseille, according to the local police, with significantly higher numbers reported by the organisers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lefigaro.fr/social/blocage-18-septembre-en-direct-greve-transports-paris-ratp-manifestation-parcours-mouvement-social-20250918#18-09-2025-13-03-01"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Le Figaro said.}}}\par \par \uc2 Major demonstrations walked down the streets of Nantes and Lyon, too.\par \par \uc2 In Paris,\par \par \uc2 about 100 protesters managed to get to the economy ministry, \u8220\'20\'1Csetting off a few smoke bombs\u8221\'20\'1D as they move towards Place de la Bastille where the main demonstration of the day takes place later today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lemonde.fr/politique/live/2025/09/18/en-direct-mobilisation-du-18-septembre-suivez-les-greves-et-les-manifestations-a-l-appel-de-l-intersyndicale_6641656_823448.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Le Monde said.}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 12.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 11.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Poland agrees deal to learn from Ukraine on drone warfare\par \par \uc2 Poland\u8217\'20\'19s defence minister signed a partnership agreement with Ukraine today\par \par \uc2 , saying that the country hopes to benefit from Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s knowledge and skills regarding drone warfare.\par \par \uc2 The announcement comes a week after a Russian drone incursion into Polish airspace sparked a national debate about air defence and the country\u8217\'20\'19s readiness for any future attack of this sort.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to benefit from your knowledge and skills, and we want Polish companies, both public and private, to be able to participate in this together,\u8221\'20\'1D Poland\u8217\'20\'19s defence minister, W\u322\'01\'42adys\u322\'01\'42aw Kosiniak-Kamysz, said during a news conference in Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 His Ukrainian counterpart, \uc2 Denys Shmyhal\uc2 , said that Ukrainian troops and engineers will train their Polish counterparts, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are ready to ... share our experience in any conditions...but the key thing is air defence from Russian drones, (and) missiles,\u8221\'20\'1D Shmyhal said.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.58am BST\par \par \uc2 11.45am BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Commission\uc2  was also asked about the Polish-Belarusian border situation, after Poland had temporarily closed its border with Belarus in the buildup to the recent Russian-Belarusian military drills.\par \par \uc2 It has since extended the closure until further notice, risking disruption to EU-China trade by rail, estimated to be worth around \u8364\'20\'AC25-30bn (\u163\'00\'A322-26bn) per year.\par \par \uc2 The issue was reportedly discussed during Monday\u8217\'20\'19s meeting between Poland\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister, Rados\u322\'01\'42aw Sikorski, and his Chinese counterpart, Wang Yi.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 EU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s deputy chief spokesperson, Olof Gill, said:\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.49am BST\par \par \uc2 11.22am BST\par \par \uc2 EU\uc2  'expects to present' new sanctions on Russia 'soon'\par \par \uc2 I am keeping an eye on the \uc2 EU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s midday briefing just now, but there is no substantial update from the \uc2 EU\uc2  on the 19th package of sanctions against Russia.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Commission\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s deputy chief spokesperson, Olof Gill, repeated that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe expect to present \u8230\'20\'26 [them] soon\u8221\'20\'1D, as he asked journalists to \u8220\'20\'1Cplease bear with us on that\u8221\'20\'1D, without offering more detail.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-09-18/eu-set-to-propose-new-russia-sanctions-as-soon-as-this-week?srnd=homepage-uk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u163\'00\'A3}}}\uc2 ) is reporting that they are now expected to be presented to member states on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.28am BST\par \par \uc2 11.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Day of strikes and protests in France \u8211\'20\'13 in pictures\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.05am BST\par \par \uc2 10.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Spain to investigate human rights violations in Gaza as S\u225\'00\'E1nchez meets with Germany's Merz\par \par \uc2 in Madrid\par \par \uc2 Spain\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general has authorised the creation of a team to investigate human rights violations in Gaza after Spanish police and prosecutors found possible evidence that Israel had committed crimes \u8220\'20\'1Cagainst the international community\u8221\'20\'1D in the Gaza strip.\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Thursday, the attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office said the team would \u8220\'20\'1Ccollect and preserve evidence sources\u8221\'20\'1D to be handed over to the international criminal court as it investigates possible breaches of international human right law.\par \par \uc2 It added:\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the commission found that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/16/israel-committed-genocide-in-gaza-says-un-inquiry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 committing genocide in Gaza}}}\uc2 , citing tens of thousands of civilian deaths and massive destruction, and urged member countries to punish those responsible for it.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Cadena Ser radio on Thursday, Spain\u8217\'20\'19s human rights and democratic memory prosecutor, Dolores Delgado, said more and more evidence was pouring in as Israel continued its offensive in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen the possible committing of violation of international human rights law in real time,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to preserve this evidence. Imagine if we\u8217\'20\'19d had this real-time material in the case of the Holocaust.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s announcement comes as Spain\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Pedro S\u225\'00\'E1nchez\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who had been the most outspoken European critic of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s offensive in Gaza \u8211\'20\'13 prepares to meet the German chancellor, \uc2 Friedrich Merz\uc2 , in Madrid to discuss bilateral relations and investments.\par \par \uc2 Merz\u8217\'20\'19s first visit to Spain since he took office in May is likely to be overshadowed by his far more cautious stance on Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Last week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/08/spanish-pm-pedro-sanchez-israel-exterminating-defenceless-people-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 S\u225\'00\'E1nchez announced a raft of measures}}}\uc2  designed to increase the pressure on \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  to stop the military campaign, saying Israel was \u8220\'20\'1Cexterminating a defenceless people\u8221\'20\'1D by bombing hospitals and \u8220\'20\'1Ckilling innocent boys and girls with hunger\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Although Merz last month halted German military exports that could be used in Gaza, he has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/merz-germany-will-not-join-allies-initiative-recognise-palestinian-state-2025-08-26/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to join international efforts to recognise a Palestinian state}}}\uc2 , saying the requisite conditions had not yet been met.\par \par \uc2 Spain, along with Ireland and Norway, formally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/22/palestinian-state-recognition-ireland-spain-recognise-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recognised a Palestinian state}}}\uc2  in May 2024.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 10.48am BST\par \par \uc2 10.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Slash red tape to help us grow, German industry chiefs urge commission president von der Leyen\par \par \uc2 German industry chiefs have called on the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  chief, \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , to slash red tape and dump two laws for every new law\par \par \uc2 added to European statute books.\par \par \uc2 They said the \u8220\'20\'1Cone in, two out rule\u8221\'20\'1D, which has echoes of a \u8216\'20\'18one in, one out\u8217\'20\'19 policy pursued by \uc2 Tony Blair\uc2  when prime minister of the UK, is an essential part of any effort to accelerate competition conditions that will make it easier to take on rivals such as the Chinese.\par \par \uc2 They have also called for \u8220\'20\'1Csimplification\u8221\'20\'1D of environmental laws and demanded urgent action from the \uc2 German government\uc2  to cut energy costs, the highest in Europe, just pipping Denmark and Ireland,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEU legislation must become better and faster \u8211\'20\'13 with mandatory impact assessments and competitiveness checks for all economically relevant laws, stringent application of the \u8216\'20\'18one in, two out\u8217\'20\'19 principle, and the consistent elimination of regulatory duplication and disproportionate burdens,\u8221\'20\'1D said the four top business organisations.\par \par \uc2 They are the BDA, the \uc2 Confederation of German Employers\u8217\'20\'19 Associations\uc2 , BDI, the Federation of German Industries, DIHK, the German Chamber of Commerce and Industry and Commerce and ZDH, the German Confederation of Skilled Crafts.\par \par \uc2 They said the \uc2 German government\uc2  had heeded some of their calls to cut red tape but it was not enough.\par \par \uc2 Berlin needed to \u8220\'20\'1Creduce existing over-regulation through further omnibus packages and carry out regular reviews of laws in the long term\u8221\'20\'1D, the said.\par \par \uc2 The joint statement was released in response to a speech by von der Leyen at a conference in Berlin on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 10.39am BST\par \par \uc2 10.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump likely to get 'much more aggressive' on Russia, ally claims\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is likely to become \u8220\'20\'1Cmuch more aggressive\u8221\'20\'1D towards Russia in support of Ukraine, one of his allies has claimed.\par \par \uc2 Christopher Ruddy\uc2 , CEO of \uc2 Newsmax\uc2 , a rightwing news organisation in the US, was a guest at the state banquet last night.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with the Today programme, Ruddy, who has been a friend and informal adviser to the president for years, predicted that Trump would soon harden his stance against Russia.\par \par \uc2 He said:\par \par \uc2 Ruddy conceded that Trump was not in favour of sending US troops into action.\par \par \uc2 Instead, Trump sees this as \u8220\'20\'1Can economic battle\u8221\'20\'1D, Ruddy said.\par \par \uc2 Asked about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s views on \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , the Russian president, Ruddy said Trump viewed him as \u8220\'20\'1Ca bad guy, even though he won\u8217\'20\'19t say that publicly\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump thought it was worth trying to win Putin round, Ruddy said. But Trump has now decided that\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cnot going to work\u8221\'20\'1D, Ruddy claimed.\par \par \uc2 9.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump's schedule for day two of state visit in Britain\par \par \uc2 If you fancy following the latest on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s visit to Britain, here\u8217\'20\'19s today\u8217\'20\'19s schedule as per Andrew Sparrow on the UK blog.10am: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  leaves Windsor CastleMorning: Melania Trump and Queen Camilla visit Queen Mary\u8217\'20\'19s Dolls\u8217\'20\'19 House in Windsor and Frogmore Gardens.10.45am: Trump is due to arrive at Chequers, where he will hold bilateral talks with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/keir-starmer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Keir Starmer}}}\uc2 . The two leaders are also speaking at an event for business leaders, and viewing items from the Winston Churchill archive at the mansion, the official country residence of the PM. And there will be a parachute display by the Red Devils.Around 2.30pm: Starmer and Trump hold a press conference at Chequers.Follow for live updates:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2025/sep/18/donald-trump-state-visit-uk-keir-starmer-labour-politics-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starmer and Trump to hold talks as PM warned UK faces \u8216\'20\'18huge dilemma\u8217\'20\'19 over relationship with US \u8211\'20\'13 UK politics live}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 10.00am BST\par \par \uc2 9.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in France, more than 50 people have been arrested since this morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lefigaro.fr/social/blocage-18-septembre-en-direct-greve-transports-paris-ratp-manifestation-parcours-mouvement-social-20250918"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Le Figaro says}}}\uc2 . Seven in Paris, and 44 outside the capital.\par \par \uc2 According to the latest data as of 10am, there were 252 \u8216\'20\'18actions\u8217\'20\'19 outside largest cities, with about 30,000 people taking part, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lefigaro.fr/social/blocage-18-septembre-en-direct-greve-transports-paris-ratp-manifestation-parcours-mouvement-social-20250918#18-09-2025-10-19-57"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the paper said.}}}\par \par \uc2 But Sophie Binet, the leader of the CGT trade union, warned that the strong police presence demanded by the outgoing interior minister is \u8220\'20\'1Cadding fuel to fire\u8221\'20\'1D, as she criticised the police response so far this morning as heavy-handed, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lemonde.fr/politique/live/2025/09/18/en-direct-mobilisation-du-18-septembre-suivez-les-greves-et-les-manifestations-a-l-appel-de-l-intersyndicale_6641656_823448.html?#id-2576863"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Le Monde reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 In an interview with BFMTV, she also urged more people to join protests, underlining the new prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cfragility\u8221\'20\'1D and need to respond to social demands, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.leparisien.fr/economie/direct-greve-du-18-septembre-800-000-manifestants-attendus-risques-de-troubles-blocages-les-policiers-deja-sur-le-front-18-09-2025-FHGIVK2BX5HVJACAZXI7SBPXRU.php#b9ea121f-f095-4de9-9b2d-5aef293df1a6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Le Parisien added.}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 9.31am BST\par \par \uc2 9.15am BST\par \par \uc2 UK set to begin talks with \uc2 EU\uc2  about access to defence loans scheme\par \par \uc2 Brussels correspondent\par \par \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s government is expected to soon begin talks with the \uc2 EU\uc2  to negotiate Britain\u8217\'20\'19s entry into the EU\u8217\'20\'19s \u8364\'20\'AC150bn (\u163\'00\'A3130bn) defence loans scheme.\par \par \uc2 The negotiations can start because on Wednesday, \uc2 EU\uc2  member states agreed a negotiating mandate for the \uc2 European Commission\uc2 , but must conclude quickly if British companies are to be involved.\par \par \uc2 The scheme, called Security Action for Europe (Safe), provides EU member states with cheap, EU-backed loans to finance defence equipment, either for their armies or for Ukraine. The UK is not applying for a loan, but would like the biggest possible role for British companies in winning contacts.\par \par \uc2 The first loans are expected to be disbursed in early 2026, with member states due to submit spending plans to the commission by the end of November.\par \par \uc2 The UK\u8217\'20\'19s Europe minister \uc2 Nick Thomas-Symonds\uc2  made clear the deadline was on his mind when he spoke at a conference in Brussels on Wednesday. Asked by politics professor \uc2 Anand Menon\uc2  whether the UK could miss out on the first round, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CI profoundly hope not... But my sense on this is that you\u8217\'20\'19re absolutely right to emphasise the deadline.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  reported this week that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/sep/17/france-proposes-ceiling-on-value-of-uk-components-in-eu-defence-fund"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 France has called for a 50% ceiling on the value of UK components}}}\uc2  in projects financed by Safe. The final EU negotiating mandate leaves the point vague, giving \uc2 EU\uc2  negotiators flexibility.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 EU\uc2  and UK must also negotiate a British entry fee to cover administrative costs. \uc2 EU\uc2  sources have suggested the fee will be linked to the level of British participation\par \par \uc2 Asked about the French position, Thomas-Symonds said the UK and EU were in a live negotiation, without commenting on details:\par \par \uc2 Updated at 9.27am BST\par \par \uc2 9.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Hungary hasn't changed view on accelerating Russian oil phaseout amid concerns about energy security, minister says\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 EU\uc2  ministers are meeting at the environment council in Brussels to discuss energy and the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 The gathering takes place amid ongoing discussions about accelerating the bloc\u8217\'20\'19s plans to phase out Russian oil, bringing the current 2028 deadline forward.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Commission\uc2  president, \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , spoke about it with US president, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , earlier this week after he appeared to link the issue to further US sanctions on Russia. Poland, separately, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/17/eu-calls-for-closer-ties-with-india-despite-modi-ties-to-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also asked for a more ambitious 2026 target.}}}\par \par \uc2 But the Hungarian junior energy minister Anik\u243\'00\'F3 Raisz indicated that Hungary \u8211\'20\'13 one of the two countries most heavily relying on Russian imports, alongside Slovakia \u8211\'20\'13 is not particularly interested by any of that.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 9.07am BST\par \par \uc2 8.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Morning opening: France grinds to halt\par \par \uc2 France is expected to see one of the biggest strikes in recent years today, as trade unions throw a welcome party of sorts for the country\u8217\'20\'19s new prime minister, S\u233\'00\'E9bastien Lecornu,in hope of influencing his views on budget cuts set to affect public services and wages.\par \par \uc2 About 800,000 people are expected to join\par \par \uc2 approximately 250 marches across the country, according to police, affecting schools, rail and air transport. Up to 80,000 police officers will be deployed amid warnings about potential unrest.\par \par \uc2 I will keep an eye on this.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the US president, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , continues his state visit to the UK, with the political replacing the ceremonial as he meets the UK prime minister, \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 , at Chequers.\par \par \uc2 The pair will hold bilateral talks and meet business leaders, among others. I will look out for any news lines coming out from that.\par \par \uc2 In other high-level talks, Germany\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Friedrich Merz\uc2  is set to visit Madrid for talks with Spain\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Pedro S\u225\'00\'E1nchez\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a lively day.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s Thursday, 18 September 2025, it\u8217\'20\'19s Jakub Krupa here, and this is Europe Live.\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250918el9i0020a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
