\par\par \b \uc2 Sky\uc2  puts 900 roles at risk in shake-up to compete with US streaming services\b0\par\par\uc2 Mark Sweney \par \uc2 459 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 September 2025\par 13:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Company expects consultation process to result in about 600 roles being cut out of 23,000 UK staffBusiness live \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates\par \par \uc2 Sky\uc2  has put 900 roles at risk as the broadcaster continues to reshape its business in the streaming era.\par \par \uc2 The company, which employs about 23,000 staff in the UK, expects the consultation process to result in about 600 roles being cut, with 300 redeployed.\par \par \uc2 The latest round of cuts \u8211\'20\'13 the third in a little over 18 months \u8211\'20\'13 follows a series of product launches including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/may/01/sky-glass-gen-2-review-smart-streaming-tv-picture-sound-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 second iteration of the Sky Glass smart TV}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/sep/01/sky-glass-air-review-a-surprisingly-good-budget-smart-tv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 budget-friendly Sky Glass Air}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Comcast\uc2 -owned broadcaster is focused on improving existing services, and the cuts will hit \uc2 Sky\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s technology and product teams and related corporate functions.\par \par \uc2 Sky\uc2  has cut almost 3,500 roles since the beginning of last year as the broadcaster looks to move away from traditional satellite pay-TV to streaming-based services in the fight against US giants such as \uc2 Netflix\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The latest round of cuts brings \uc2 Sky UK\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s employee base back down to roughly the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://assets.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt4b099fa9cc3801a6/bltec7b428f27f4aa13/68b576f16f1cb91ea9ef49b8/Annual-report-2018.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 23,000 level at which it stood in 2018}}}\uc2 , when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2018/sep/23/comcast-30bn-bid-for-sky-what-does-it-mean#:~:text=Why%20has%20Comcast%20bid%20%C2%A3,and%20produces%20its%20own%20content.https://www.theguardian.com/business/2018/feb/27/comcast-boss-brian-roberts-london-cab-driver-role-sky-bid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Comcast acquired the business for \u163\'00\'A331bn}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sky\uc2  estimates that more than 90% of new subscriptions are via internet-based products such as Sky Glass and Sky Stream, a new streaming set-top box.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver the past few years, \uc2 Sky\uc2  has launched a set of market-leading products including Sky Glass, Sky Stream and our full fibre broadband service,\u8221\'20\'1D said a \uc2 Sky\uc2  spokesperson. \u8220\'20\'1CThese products are now firmly established and used by millions of customers, strengthening \uc2 Sky\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reputation for innovation and great service.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs we look ahead, we are shifting our approach to bring customers the next generation of experience by investing in digital-first service, unbeatable content, and even better performance from our products, powered by the best of global innovation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In March, \uc2 Sky\uc2  moved to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/mar/27/sky-to-cut-2000-jobs-at-customer-service-centres-and-close-three-sites-in-uk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut 2,000 jobs at its customer service centres}}}\uc2  and closed three sites.\par \par \uc2 The company said the closures would make it \u8220\'20\'1Cfuture-ready\u8221\'20\'1D as it shifted from dealing with customers over the phone to digital communications.\par \par \uc2 Last January, \uc2 Sky{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/jan/30/sky-cut-1000-jobs-customers-move-pay-tv-internet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut about 800 jobs}}}\uc2 , mainly from its army of workers that install equipment in households, as consumers stop taking traditional pay-TV equipment and shift to \u8220\'20\'1Cplug-and-go\u8221\'20\'1D internet-based products.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, \uc2 Sky{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/dec/09/sky-warner-bros-discovery-deal-hbo-max"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck a deal with Warner Bros Discovery}}}\uc2 , the owner of the film studio behind Barbie and \uc2 HBO\uc2  shows including Succession and The White Lotus, which led to it losing the right to exclusively broadcast programmes.\par \par \uc2 The deal will result in \uc2 WBD\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 HBO\uc2  Max streaming service being made available via \uc2 Sky\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250916el9g002p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
