\par\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Like working in a prison\u8217\'20\'19: cuts, fear and understaffing at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s labor department\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,467 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 September 2025\par 11:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Morale has plummeted as staff charged with protecting US workers feel their core mission is being undermined\par \par \uc2 A giant banner featuring a serious-looking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  now hangs down the front of the Department of Labor\u8217\'20\'19s Washington DC office. Covering the windows of nearly three floors, the poster reads: \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican Workers FIRST.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMr President, I invite you see your big beautiful face on a banner in front of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.the-independent.com/topic/department-of-labor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Department of Labor}}}\uc2  because you are really the transformational president of the American worker,\u8221\'20\'1D the labor secretary, Lori Chavez-DeReme, said last month at a cabinet meeting with the president.\par \par \uc2 Staff at the agency say they have other concerns. \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone thinks it\u8217\'20\'19s a joke because it is a joke. There are parts of the building that have not been fixed. We have closed bathrooms all over the place. The front door doesn\u8217\'20\'19t work, it\u8217\'20\'19s been broken for two months, but we have money for a stupid banner,\u8221\'20\'1D said one worker, who requested anonymity for fear of retribution.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSeeing her in that cabinet meeting where she begged Trump to look at it, it\u8217\'20\'19s embarrassing. Fawning over the president, regardless of who the president is, acting that way means she can\u8217\'20\'19t give him hard or bad news and you should be able to do that if you\u8217\'20\'19re a leader.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Employees at the department and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/DOEJf9sjR_l/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 labor advocates }}}\uc2 say the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  is undermining the agency\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/labor-department#:~:text=The%20Department%20of%20Labor%20(DOL,insurance;%20and%20other%20income%20support."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mission}}}\uc2  to foster and promote the welfare of job seekers, wage earners and retirees through drastic cuts, deregulations that include pay cuts for workers, and mistreatment of those employed at the agency.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/03/mass-resignations-at-labor-department-threaten-workers-in-us-and-overseas-warn-staff-as-more-cuts-loom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 About 20% }}}\uc2 of staff at the \uc2 US Department of Labor\uc2  have resigned or retired ahead of threatened cuts at the agency.\par \par \uc2 The agency has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/osec/osec20250904"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed}}}\uc2  nearly 150 deregulatory actions, including a proposal to eliminate minimum wage and overtime protections for 3.7 million domestic care workers, in addition to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/03/mass-resignations-at-labor-department-threaten-workers-in-us-and-overseas-warn-staff-as-more-cuts-loom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cuts}}}\uc2  undertaken by the so-called department of government efficiency (Doge) such as office lease cancellations, and cutting millions in international labor grants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey are gutting us. They are taking away everything that makes us helpful to the citizens of the states we work in,\u8221\'20\'1D said a current employee at the department\u8217\'20\'19s wage and hour division who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation. \u8220\'20\'1CThey say they\u8217\'20\'19re changing things for the American worker. I was born in the US and am a veteran. I\u8217\'20\'19m an American worker and they don\u8217\'20\'19t care about us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The secretary of labor\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff sent out a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/us-department-labor-leak-criminal-charges-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 memo}}}\uc2  in April 2025 to all department employees warning they could face \u8220\'20\'1Cserious legal consequences\u8221\'20\'1D if they speak to the media. Under the National Labor Relations Act, employees have a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.akerman.com/en/perspectives/hrdef-be-careful-about-restricting-employee-communications-with-media.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protected right}}}\uc2  to speak to the media about their working conditions and labor concerns.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA federal worker shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be scared to speak the truth. For me to even be concerned about speaking is ridiculous, it\u8217\'20\'19s how we stand up to protect ourselves and those around us,\u8221\'20\'1D they said.\par \par \uc2 The worker explained they now have to get any fieldwork approved beforehand, and it has to be tied to a pre-existing case. In the meantime, employers are being pushed to perform self-audits.\par \par \uc2 This, coupled with the drastic staffing cuts faced throughout the \uc2 US Department of Labor\uc2 , they argued, is undermining the department\u8217\'20\'19s ability to enforce wage and hour laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t have manning to do these enforcement, day-in-day-out, jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D they added. \u8220\'20\'1CThe department has tried to push these self-audits, where they are allowing bad actors to self-audit,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CThose bad actors are going to essentially get away with it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Department of Labor only provided comment on the maintenance and repairs, claiming they were working to improve the overall maintenance of the building, and claimed all 91 bathrooms had recently been repaired.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis fake news hit piece is exactly why public trust in the mainstream media is at historic lows,\u8221\'20\'1D said a labor department spokesperson, Courtney Parella.\par \par \uc2 Morale has plummeted as the national office amid all the cuts at the agency, threats, harassment and intimidation from the administration, and new policies, such as security bag screenings to get into the building every day, said workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s kind of like working in a prison,\u8221\'20\'1D they added. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very clear how they treat us is a bellwether for how they want other workers to be treated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Department of Labor is being deployed fully as one arm of this president\u8217\'20\'19s war on workers, which is even more painful given that the mission of the Department of Labor is to protect workers,\u8221\'20\'1D said Julie Su, who served as secretary of labor under the Biden administration. \u8220\'20\'1CThe way you treat your own workers is a sign of how you believe workers in general deserve to be treated. And this administration has taken a very destructive approach to its own workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Su also criticized the Department of Labor\u8217\'20\'19s adoption of rhetoric from the Trump administration, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/osec/osec20250904"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claiming }}}\uc2 to \u8220\'20\'1Cput American workers first\u8221\'20\'1D and usher in a \u8220\'20\'1Cgolden age\u8221\'20\'1D for \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican workers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis administration, they constantly talk about doing right by American workers. That\u8217\'20\'19s a pretty coded way of saying what they want to say, which is that they no longer believe that immigrant workers deserve protection and that\u8217\'20\'19s part of their overall war on workers,\u8221\'20\'1D Su said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s an anti-immigrant philosophy of the entire administration, but for the Department of Labor to adopt it is especially harmful, because so many workers who keep our economy going are immigrant workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She cited other examples of policies that harm workers being pursued by this administration, from{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://stopchildlabor.org/civil-society-groups-alarmed-by-cuts-to-ilab-grants-to-address-forced-labor-and-child-labor/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  cutting $500m}}}\uc2  in grants dedicated toward fighting child labor and forced labor abroad, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jordanbarab.com/confinedspace/2025/08/27/trump-republicans-continue-war-on-coal-miners/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delaying}}}\uc2  implementation of a rule to protect coalminers from silica dust exposure, pushing to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theregreview.org/2025/08/06/mcferran-proposed-osha-rule-is-dangerous-for-workers-and-the-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 create an exemption}}}\uc2  for employers to the general duty clause of the Occupational Safety and Health Act that obligates employers to keep workers safe on the job, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/policywatch/department-of-labor-halts-enforcement-of-expanded-labor-protections-for-migrant-farmworkers-on-h-2a-temporary-visas/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ceasing }}}\uc2 enforcement of expanded labor protections for immigrant farm workers on H-2A temporary visas.\par \par \uc2 Among the deregulations being pushed by the Department of Labor include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/the-trump-administration-is-quietly-gutting-minimum-wage-protections-for-millions-of-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposing a rule}}}\uc2  to exempt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2025/07/02/2025-12316/application-of-the-fair-labor-standards-act-to-domestic-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 3.7 million}}}\uc2  home health and personal care workers in the US from minimum wage and overtime protections.\par \par \uc2 These workers are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/medicaid/who-are-the-direct-care-workers-providing-long-term-services-and-supports-ltss/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 predominantly }}}\uc2 women and paid low wages, with immigrants comprising a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/medicaid/what-role-do-immigrants-play-in-the-direct-long-term-care-workforce/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significant }}}\uc2 and growing portion of the workforce.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat the \uc2 US Department of Labor\uc2  is proposing is the Trump administration reversing history, and saying, no, wait a minute, home care workers are not deserving of overtime protections, of minimum wage, and that just sets us back into a whole other era,\u8221\'20\'1D said Arnulfo De La Cruz, president of SEIU Local 2015, which represents {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seiu2015.org/statement-from-president-of-seiu-local-2015-arnulfo-de-la-cruz-on-texas-ruling-striking-down-federal-nursing-home-staffing-standards/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over half a million}}}\uc2  long-term care workers in California. \u8220\'20\'1CThis change would undo a decade of progress toward recognizing home care as real professional work, and this is yet another Trump administration attack on workers. This comes down to special interests who want to increase their profits by paying workers less.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Astrid Zuniga, a home care worker in Modesto, California, and president of United Domestic Workers of America, UDW/AFSCME Local 3930, said she would stand to lose about $1,200 a month if overtime protections are removed for care workers, which she relies on to cover the costs of medications her son needs, who has autism, epilepsy and other intellectual disabilities, and who she cares for 24/7.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo lose that much money a month, when most of us already live paycheck to paycheck as it is, would be damaging to many households,\u8221\'20\'1D said Zuniga. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you go and you implement these kinds of cuts to the low-wage workforce, that only hurts the workers and most of these workers are making right at about minimum wage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She emphasized home care workers were already bracing for the impact of Medicaid cuts to benefits and services that will also decrease their ability to provide services to clients.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHome care is the{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/healthcare/home-health-aides-and-personal-care-aides.htm#:~:text=Employment%20of%20home%20health%20and,on%20average%2C%20over%20the%20decade."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  fastest-growing sector}}}\uc2  of workers across the nation. It is the highest in demand. Nobody is getting any younger or any healthier,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CCuts should not be made to these types of services,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd if we\u8217\'20\'19re not making this a desirable workforce and not making investments into these kinds of home- and community-based services that our most vulnerable communities rely on, what are we doing?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the message is that they think workers have it too good, too many protections, too high of wages, too much security. Their view is that workers are too comfortable,\u8221\'20\'1D added Su.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250916el9g002mk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
