\par\par \b \uc2 Elizabeth Warren introduces bill to ban employers from running credit reports in hiring\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 465 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2025\par 16:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Exclusive: Massachusetts senator said credit checks in hiring disproportionately affect people of color and women\par \par \uc2 As the US labor market {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/sep/05/us-jobs-report-august-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comes under pressure}}}\uc2 , two senior figures in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/washington-dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington}}}\uc2  are pushing to end a practice that prevents large swaths of US workers from obtaining jobs.\par \par \uc2 A bill reintroduced today by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/elizabeth-warren"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elizabeth Warren}}}\uc2 , the senator from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/massachusetts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Massachusetts}}}\uc2 , and Steve Cohen, the representative from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tennessee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tennessee}}}\uc2 , bans employers from using credit checks to vet potential hires.\par \par \uc2 Denying jobs based on a candidate\u8217\'20\'19s financial history \u8220\'20\'1Cmakes no sense\u8221\'20\'1D, the prominent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  argue. It also disproportionately affects minorities.\par \par \uc2 The bill would amend the Fair Credit Reporting Act to stop employers from requiring job applicants to disclose their credit history, or suggesting they should, and from procuring consumer or investigative reports on applicants. It also would prohibit credit reporting agencies from providing reports to employers, and prevent employers from disqualifying job applicants based on credit information.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNobody should be discriminated against and miss out on a job opportunity because of their financial history,\u8221\'20\'1D Warren said in a statement to the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the Trump administration tanks the labor market, our bill prohibits employers from using credit scores in their hiring process so that everyone can have a fair chance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Versions of the legislation have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/111th-congress/house-bill/3149?q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22Equal+Employment+for+All+Act%22%7D&s=1&r=3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed}}}\uc2  since the aftermath of the 2008-09 economic recession, when Americans\u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/08/25/household-debt-is-at-an-all-time-high-but-2008-was-still-worse.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 consumer and credit debt swelled}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Credit reports in the hiring process are \u8220\'20\'1Cdisproportionately used to disqualifypeople of color from open positions\u8221\'20\'1D, according to Warren\u8217\'20\'19s office, which said that women are also more likely to have poor credit.\par \par \uc2 About half of employers use information from credit reports in their hiring processes, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.urban.org/research/publication/preemployment-credit-checks-employer-practices-worker-outcomes-and"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  published last year by the Urban Institute.\par \par \uc2 One in 10 respondents to a 2012 Demos {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.demos.org/research/discredited-how-employment-credit-checks-keep-qualified-workers-out-job"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey}}}\uc2  said they had been denied a job due to information in their credit report, despite a lack of correlation between credit history and job performance. Poor credit is most often associated with medical debt, or periods of unemployment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUsing a job applicant\u8217\'20\'19s credit history to deny employment is not just unfair, it also makes no sense. Credit scores are an inaccurate way to predict future job performance or ability,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cohen in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe should be making the job application process fairer so people can succeed with good jobs, not adding obstacles to prevent them from being hired.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Several states, including California, Colorado, Hawaii, Illinois, Nevada, Oregon and Washington, and municipalities have already enacted local laws that ban employers from using credit reports in hiring, albeit with some exemptions, such as national security roles or positions in financial services. New York City {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ogletree.com/insights-resources/blog-posts/new-york-city-passes-bill-prohibiting-employers-from-requesting-or-using-credit-history-in-employment-decisions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned}}}\uc2  the practice in 2015, and state legislators are currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nysenate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2025/james-sanders-jr/senator-sanders-credit-history-ban-bill-clears-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pursuing}}}\uc2  a statewide ban.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250915el9f002bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
