\par\par \b \uc2 Workplace safety issues at Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Hyundai plant may have led to Ice raid\b0\par\par\uc2 George Chidi \par \uc2 1,525 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2025\par 03:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Three people have died in two years at the South Korean Hyundai-LG battery plant in Ellabell\par \par \uc2 A week after a federal immigration raid on a South Korean battery plant under construction in Georgia, concerns over the economic fallout have reverberated between the United States and South Korea. The detention of more than 300 Korean workers at the Hyundai-LG worksite in Ellabell has created uncertainty both about the future of the project and those like it in Georgia, as well as the exact reasons for the aggressive and unusual workplace raid.\par \par \uc2 One reason that may have driven immigration officials to take actions that threaten an important trade relationship and a politically and economically sensitive development in one of the poorest parts of the US: workplace safety issues that led to three deaths in two years.\par \par \uc2 The investigation began in March, DHS officials said, a time that coincides with the second of three fatal workplace accidents at the site. It is conceivable that the presence of undocumented workers might have contributed to workplace safety culture issues, if people were not free to make complaints to the \uc2 Occupational Safety and Health Administration\uc2  out of fear of deportation.\par \par \uc2 In April 2023, 34-year-old construction worker Victor Javier Cajija Gamboa fell to his death at the HL-GA Battery Company site after his safety line was severed. In March, Sunbok You died there in a forklift accident. A Bryan county sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office report described You as \u8220\'20\'1Claying behind the forklift\u8221\'20\'1D with \u8220\'20\'1Ca blood trail approximately 10-15 feet long\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Two months later, Allen Kowalski, 27, was crushed to death by a load falling from a forklift.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/news/2025/06/construction-deaths-injuries-at-hyundais-georgia-ev-plant-draw-scrutiny/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from the Atlanta Journal-Constitution noted that construction injuries and deaths had far outpaced industry averages for a project of the size of the battery plant. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.savannahnow.com/story/news/local/2025/03/15/people-suffer-injuries-at-hyundai-plant-in-ellabell/82416535007/?gnt-cfr=1&gca-cat=p&gca-uir=true&gca-epti=z113836e008400v113836b0038xxd003865&gca-ft=167&gca-ds=sophi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 story}}}\uc2  by the Savannah Morning News noted that 91 ambulance calls had been made from the construction site over a 20-month period.\par \par \uc2 Hyundai and LG were asked whether workers at this or other sites owned by LG or Hyundai are free to report workplace safety issues without reprisal, and if they believe that workplace safety issues \u8211\'20\'13 specifically the deaths of three employees at the worksite over the last two years \u8211\'20\'13 contributed to the decision by Homeland Security Investigations to seek a search warrant and round up HL-GA site workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll of the personnel we directly hired for HL-GA Battery Company are legally employed, and we will work with our suppliers to apply the same standards,\u8221\'20\'1D replied Phil Lienert, a spokesperson for \uc2 LG Energy Solution\uc2 , a partner in the battery plant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe health and safety of everyone at our facilities and construction sites is our highest priority,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1COur direct employees as well as our subcontractors understand our commitment to safety and occupational industrial safety and health policies. Together with our subcontractors and relevant authorities, we have fully supported thorough investigations to determine the root cause of the incident and to help prevent such accidents in the future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Ice would not confirm but did not deny that safety issues contributed to the investigation. But he did express skepticism about claims made by Tori Branum, a Republican and former US marine running for Congress in Georgia, that her calls of complaint to Ice prompted the action.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know who that is,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Ice spokesperson, Lindsay Williams. \u8220\'20\'1CThe executive summary that I\u8217\'20\'19ve been briefed on doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have her name in it at all \u8230\'20\'26 it has nothing to do with our investigation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The raid by Homeland Security Investigations and other agencies ended with 475 people in detention, of whom 320 were Korean nationals, most of whom had a B-1 visa or entered with a visa waiver, said Charles Kuck, an immigration attorney representing four of the detained workers. With regard to other detainees, fear of reporting safety problems because of the possibility of deportation was \u8220\'20\'1Ca plausible\u8221\'20\'1D issue, he said.\par \par \uc2 When Ice made arrests, \u8220\'20\'1Cthere were a lot of Mexican, Guatemalan, Chilean, Colombian, Ecuadorian, Venezuelan people\u8221\'20\'1D, said Vanessa Contreras, a spokesperson for Migrant Equity Southeast. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd of course, a lot of these people were documented. A lot of these people did have valid work permits. A lot of these people were here legally. But of course, that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter, because regardless of you having documentation or not, we have seen prior that even if you follow the quote-unquote law, it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter, you\u8217\'20\'19re still going to be treated a certain way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Incentives provided by the Inflation Reduction Act spurred more than $55bn in private investments by Korea in the United States, according to the Korea Economic Institute of America, a Washington DC thinktank funded by the South Korean government. The country\u8217\'20\'19s US investments in recent years have fallen in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://keia.org/korean-ira-investments/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 band}}}\uc2  beginning around Detroit and ending around Savannah, Georgia, passing through America\u8217\'20\'19s Rust belt and the union-busting states of Tennessee, Alabama and Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Georgia has had a particularly strong relationship with South Korea over the years, a product of careful economic diplomacy and a wave of Korean immigration. The third-most-spoken language in most states is either Chinese, French or German. In Georgia, it\u8217\'20\'19s Korean.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGeorgia has always worked to maintain a strong relationship with the Republic of Korea and Korean partners like Hyundai, stretching back 40 years to the establishment of Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s trade office in Seoul,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Georgia governor, \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe are thankful they are reiterating their commitment to adhere to all state and federal laws, just as we remain committed to not allowing this unfortunate incident to undo the decades of mutually beneficial partnerships we\u8217\'20\'19ve built together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Georgia has drawn more than $21bn in South Korean manufacturing investment across 20 projects since the Inflation Reduction Act passed in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no relationship fallout,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Trip Tollison\uc2 , president and CEO of the Savannah Economic Development Authority. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is important to note, that those that were detained were not full-time, permanent employees and were here to install sophisticated equipment and train employees on that equipment. HL-GA Battery JV has told us they are committed to the Savannah facility and that they are focused on the release of the detainees.\u8221\'20\'1D Tollison emphasized the temporary nature of the employees because the terms of their visas did not allow them to have extended working trips.\par \par \uc2 The main Hyundai car plant had created more than 2,800 jobs, and the expected number of jobs between Hyundai and 21 suppliers was 15,716, on a capital investment of $10bn, Tollison said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat has not changed,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have not done an economic impact study yet but will complete one sometime in the near future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s political leaders insist that everything is going to be fine, even though \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s immigration policy is sharply at odds with the interests of foreign investors.\par \par \uc2 South Korea\u8217\'20\'19s political leaders insist everything is not fine, while largely eliding over worker safety issues and the employment practices of its subcontractors that may have prompted the raid in the first place.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday morning, the South Korean president, \uc2 Lee Jae Myung{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/south-korea-visa-us-trump-investments-immigration-raid-25f04d539eb2556f3ff2fad49db0f74e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  companies were likely to be hesitant about investing in the United States in future.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not like these are long-term workers. When you build a factory or install equipment at a factory, you need technicians, but the United States doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have that workforce and yet they won\u8217\'20\'19t issue visas to let our people stay and do the work,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf that\u8217\'20\'19s not possible, then establishing a local factory in the United States will either come with severe disadvantages or become very difficult for our companies. They will wonder whether they should even do it,\u8221\'20\'1D Lee added.\par \par \uc2 South Korean and US trade negotiators agreed in July to a 15% tariff on South Korean goods \u8211\'20\'13 in lieu of punitive tariffs that had been on the table \u8211\'20\'13 in return for a pledge to invest $350bn in new investments in the United States. South Korean business leaders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://english.hani.co.kr/arti/english_edition/e_business/1215550.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  plans to invest an additional $150bn in American enterprises after a summit in August. Hyundai alone {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hyundai.com/worldwide/en/newsroom/detail/hyundai-motor-group-increases-u.s.-investment-to-%252426-billion-to-accelerate-growth-and-innovation-0000001003"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  its intent to invest an additional $26bn in American manufacturing only three weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 The scope of those investments, from artificial intelligence to shipbuilding and nuclear energy, is vast. So is the scope of the interest South Korea\u8217\'20\'19s new president has aggressively pursued for American investment to light up South Korea\u8217\'20\'19s waning economy.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Hyundai\u8217\'20\'19s chief executive officer, \uc2 Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz\uc2 , said the detentions, and the departure of their joint venture\u8217\'20\'19s employees back to South Korea, would set back completion of the battery plant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is going to give us minimum two to three months\u8217\'20\'19 delay, because now all these people want to get back,\u8221\'20\'1D Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz told reporters in Detroit on Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1CThen you need to see how can you fill those positions. And for the most part, those people are not in the US.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250913el9d000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
