\par\par \b \uc2 Trump reportedly asks \uc2 EU\uc2  to levy 100% tariffs on India and China; Ozempic maker Novo to cut 9,000 jobs \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Julia Kollewe \par \uc2 4,827 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 September 2025\par 14:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US president wants to up pressure on Russia to end war in Ukraine\par \par \uc2 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The Danish maker of the weight-loss and diabetes drugs Wegovy and Ozempic is to cut 9,000 jobs as it slashed its profit forecast again, amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/business/2025/aug/06/sales-of-novo-nordisk-diabetes-drugs-including-ozempic-slow-sharply"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fierce competition}}}\uc2  from its US rival \uc2 Eli Lilly\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Novo Nordisk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s decision to cut 11% of its global workforce of 78,400 is an attempt by the new chief executive, Mike Doustdar, to revive its fortunes.\par \par \uc2 Sales of its blockbuster injection Wegovy have slowed sharply as it has lost ground to \uc2 Eli Lilly\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Mounjaro jabs, as well as cheaper versions by generic drugmakers, while the pharmaceutical sector faces the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/business/2025/aug/06/stocks-shares-european-drug-companies-three-month-low-trump-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threat of targeted US tariffs}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The drugmaker said that 5,000 of the job losses would be in its home country of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/world/denmark"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Denmark}}}\uc2 . The share price rose by 2.1% by Wednesday afternoon as investors were cheered by the cost savings\par \par \uc2 Booming sales of GLP-1 diabetes and obesity drugs in recent years had helped \uc2 Novo Nordisk\uc2  rise to become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/business/2023/sep/05/weight-loss-novo-nordisk-wegovy-uk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Europe\u8217\'20\'19s most valuable company}}}\uc2 , but it lost the title in March, only briefly regaining it in June.\par \par \uc2 Studies have shown that \uc2 Eli Lilly\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/commentisfree/2025/may/13/the-toxic-debate-about-obesity-rages-on-but-at-least-we-know-if-mounjaro-or-wegovy-is-better-for-weight-loss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mounjaro is more effective than Wegovy}}}\uc2  in reducing weight. Both can be prescribed by \uc2 NHS\uc2  doctors to patients with high clinical need. \uc2 Novo Nordisk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Ozempic injection is also available on the \uc2 NHS\uc2  , as a treatment for type 2 diabetes. It can be prescribed by private doctors \u8220\'20\'1Coff label\u8221\'20\'1D for weight loss.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has asked the \uc2 EU\uc2  to impose tariffs of up to 100% on India and China as part of an effort to force the Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  , to end the war in Ukraine, according to reports.\par \par \uc2 The US president made the demand during a meeting between US and EU officials discussing options to increase economic pressure on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  on Tuesday, according to the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  , \uc2 BBC\uc2  and Bloomberg, who cited sources familiar with the discussions.\par \par \uc2 One US official reportedly said that Trump administration was \u8220\'20\'1Cready to go, ready to go right now, but we are only going to do this if our European partners step up with us\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s proposal comes amid his frustration at brokering a peace deal, including at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/aug/17/vladimir-putin-donald-trump-alaska-anchorage-summit-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 high-profile summit with Putin in Alaska}}}\uc2 , and amid Russia\u8217\'20\'19s increasing drone attacks, including its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/07/child-among-three-people-killed-in-russian-attack-on-kyiv-that-also-sparked-fire-at-government-building"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largest ever air attack on Ukraine}}}\uc2  last week.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Commission\uc2  president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ursula-von-der-leyen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen}}}\uc2 , has called for a suspension of trade with Israel, as she spoke of Europe\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cpainful\u8221\'20\'1D inability to respond to the war on Gaza and ensuing humanitarian disaster.\par \par \uc2 In her most extended condemnation yet of the Israeli government, von der Leyen criticised plans for illegal settlements that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/aug/14/israel-appears-set-to-approve-controversial-settlement-of-3400-homes-in-west-bank"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would split the occupied West Bank in half}}}\uc2 , as well as incitement of violence by extremist Israeli ministers, as a \u8220\'20\'1Cclear attempt to undermine the two-state solution\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She made the remarks during her annual \u8220\'20\'1Cstate of the union\u8221\'20\'1D speech to the European parliament in Strasbourg, in which she depicted a turbulent world where battle lines \u8220\'20\'1Care being drawn\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdependencies are ruthlessly weaponised\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In response to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/sep/10/poland-pm-condemns-repeated-violation-of-airspace-amid-russian-attack-on-ukraine-follow-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-68c134748f084b00adb68002#block-68c134748f084b00adb68002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s overnight violations of Polish airspace}}}\uc2 , she said Europe \u8220\'20\'1Cstands in full solidarity with Poland\u8221\'20\'1D, a line prompting MEPs to their feet applauding in support. \uc2 Von der Leyen\uc2  continued, calling for Europe to exert more pressure on the Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  , to come to the negotiating table.\par \par \uc2 Our other main stories:Thank you for reading. We\u8217\'20\'19ll be back tomorrow with the latest news. Take care \u8211\'20\'13 JK\par \par \uc2 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Wall Street indices hit record highs after jump in \uc2 Oracle\uc2  shares, producer price data\par \par \uc2 Wall Street indices have hit record highs after a jump in \uc2 Oracle\uc2  shares, and weaker-than-expected producer price inflation data cemented expectations for a Federal Reserve interest rate cut next week.\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 index and the tech-heavy Nasdaq both rose to intra-day all-time highs.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Oracle\uc2  share price surged by 37% to a record high of $339.69, and was set for its biggest one-day percentage gain since 1992, after the company announced that it expected booked revenue at its \uc2 Oracle\uc2  Cloud Infrastructure business to exceed half a trillion dollars.\par \par \uc2 Some chipmakers also rose on the news, with \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  climbing by 3.8%, \uc2 Advanced Micro Devices\uc2  up 3.3% and \uc2 Broadcom\uc2  adding 8.9%.\par \par \uc2 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meta\uc2  and \uc2 TikTok\uc2  win legal challenge against regulatory fees\par \par \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Meta and \uc2 TikTok\uc2  have won a legal challenge against the regulatory fees they are charged under \uc2 European Union\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s digital content rules.\par \par \uc2 Big tech, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  , have chafed against the \uc2 EU\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s new tech regulations including the digital services act (DSA), which requires strict policing of their platforms.\par \par \uc2 Facebook\uc2  parent \uc2 Meta\uc2  and Chinese-owned \uc2 TikTok\uc2  have taken on the DSA by suing the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  , the \uc2 EU\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s executive arm, over their required contribution to the cost of complying with the act. They argued that the supervisory fee of 0.05% of their annual worldwide net income was based on a flawed calculation and resulted in disproportionate fees.\par \par \uc2 The Luxembourg-based General Court sided with Meta and TikTok, giving European Union regulators 12 months to fix their methodology using a different legal act. Judges said:\par \par \uc2 They said regulators need not repay the 2023 fees paid by the companies for now, while they come up with a new legal basis for the methodology used to determine the size of the fee.\par \par \uc2 The Commission said the court had confirmed that its fee methodology is sound and sees no issue with the principle of the fee nor the amount.\par \par \uc2 TikTok and Meta welcomed the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, with the US company saying it looked forward to \u8220\'20\'1Cthe flaws in the methodology being addressed\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 Zuckerberg, Meta \u8217\'20\'19s founder and chief executive, has criticised EU tech regulation this year, warning that Europe \u8220\'20\'1Chas an ever increasing number of laws institutionalising censorship and making it difficult to build anything innovative there\u8221\'20\'1D. The European Commission , the EU \u8217\'20\'19s executive arm, denied Zuckerberg\u8217\'20\'19s claim, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cwe absolutely refute any claims of censorship\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 AO chair Geoff Cooper named as new Channel 4 chair\par \par \uc2 Geoff Cooper , chair of electrical appliance retailer AO, has been named as the new chair of Channel 4, as the broadcaster faces huge head winds in a fast-changing media world.\par \par \uc2 His appointment comes at a time of huge change for Channel 4, which is already looking for a new chief executive after the departure of Alex Mahon . Cooper\u8217\'20\'19s first major task will be to find her replacement.\par \par \uc2 He will have to do so with Channel 4 having to battle huge changes in media consumption that has seen audiences move away from linear TV and towards both streaming services, like Netflix and Disney , and digital platforms like YouTube .\par \par \uc2 The upheaval has created serious challenges for Channel 4, which is reliant on an advertising market that has fragmented and turned its attention towards digital platforms. Channel 4 is publicly owned, while being commercially funded.\par \par \uc2 Cooper takes over from Sir Ian Cheshire , who stepped down this year. Channel 4 insiders had wanted to see the chair position go to Dawn Airey, who is currently acting as an interim chair.\par \par \uc2 However, she did not run for the post. Sources close to the company believe this was down to her previous clashes with Michael Grade , chair of media regulator Ofcom who drew up the shortlist of candidates.\par \par \uc2 Cooper does not have a background in television, but does have extensive boardroom experience. He is a former chief executive of builders\u8217\'20\'19 merchant Travis Perkins . He also held posts at the retailers Dunelm and Card Factory and the food wholesaler Brakes.\par \par \uc2 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 US producer price pressures weaker than expected in August\par \par \uc2 US producer prices unexpectedly fell last month, suggesting Donald Trump \u8217\'20\'19s trade tariff effects are \u8220\'20\'1Cfeeding through only slowly,\u8221\'20\'1D according to an economist.\par \par \uc2 The producer price index, which captures factory gate inflation before it hits consumers, showed that wholesale inflation dipped by 0.1% in August from July, after advancing 0.7% month-on-month in July, according to data from the US Labor Department .\par \par \uc2 The drop in producer prices makes it even more likely that the Federal Reserve will cut its benchmark interest rate next week for the first time this year.\par \par \uc2 Wholesale services prices fell on smaller profit margins at retailers and wholesalers, which might be a sign that those companies are absorbing the cost of Donald Trump \u8217\'20\'19s sweeping trade tariffs. Compared to a year earlier, producer prices were up by 2.6%.\par \par \uc2 The core measure, excluding food and energy which can be volatile, also fell by 0.1% in August from the previous month, while economists had expected a 0.3% gain.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Brown, deputy chief North America economist at Capita Economics, said:\par \par \uc2 12.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Peter Kyle in Beijing for UK's first trade talks with China in seven years\par \par \uc2 The newly appointed business secretary, Peter Kyle, is in Beijing for the UK\u8217\'20\'19s first trade talks with the country in seven years in an attempt to revitalise economic relations.\par \par \uc2 As part of a two day programme he held a bilateral with Li Lecheng, the minister of industry and information technology on Wednesday morning as part of a revived industrial cooperation dialogue, a Sino-British relationship format that has not sat since 2022.\par \par \uc2 The ministry is responsible for industrial policy but also telecoms and the internet, which is heavily censored in China.\par \par \uc2 Tomorow Kyle, who was only promoted to the post on Friday, will have a day long programme with China\u8217\'20\'19s long-standing commerce minister Wang Wentao including a bilateral in the morning, followed by a meeting of the UK-China Joint Economic and Trade Commission (Jetco) which has not sat for seven years.\par \par \uc2 It will end with a joint dinner where the ministers will be joined by Chinese and British businesses.\par \par \uc2 Kyle is the ninth government representative to visit China since Labour were elected to power last year with hopes that the trip will unlock an export market worth more than \u163\'00\'A31bn over five years, according to a statement from the department for business and trade.\par \par \uc2 Restarting trade talks with China was \u8220\'20\'1Can essential tool to put money into people\u8217\'20\'19s pockets,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kyle.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the Jetco meeting, the department for business and trade (DBT) unveiled {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/export-wins-to-china-2024-to-2025-confirmed-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new deals and market openings for British interests worth \u163\'00\'A32bn}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 These include a new three-season TV deal for the Premier League and marketing opportunities for companies ranging from Eve Lom cosmetics to Hayman\u8217\'20\'19s gin distillery and Aedas architecture firm which has previously been involved in buildings such as Kong Kong\u8217\'20\'19s West Kowloon rail station and the giant Sina Plaza science park in Beijing.\par \par \uc2 The department also pointed to China being a \u8220\'20\'1Chuge market\u8221\'20\'1D for British cars and for porcine genetics, a pig breeding programme, cattle hides and sheep skins.\par \par \uc2 The UK is looking to China to achieve much-needed economic growth but so far the trading relationship does not reflect the size of the country.\par \par \uc2 Sam Goodman, senior policy director at Chinese Strategic Risks Institute, said:\par \par \uc2 12.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Starmer tightens grip on economic policy by strengthening autumn \u8216\'20\'18budget board\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Keir Starmer is tightening his grip on economic policy by beefing up a committee that will help shape the 26 November budget.\par \par \uc2 Pensions minister Torsten Bell and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/aug/29/starmer-names-former-bank-of-england-deputy-governor-as-his-chief-economic-adviser"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starmer\u8217\'20\'19s new chief economic adviser, }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/aug/29/starmer-names-former-bank-of-england-deputy-governor-as-his-chief-economic-adviser"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minouche Shafik}}}\uc2 , will co-chair the \u8220\'20\'1Cbudget board\u8221\'20\'1D, that will meet weekly to discuss the details of the statement.\par \par \uc2 Government sources said the meetings were aimed at ensuring No 10 and No 11 were aligned and that there was not a repeat of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/nov/19/uk-retailers-rachel-reeves-budget-tax-rises-brc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backlash from businesses}}}\uc2  that followed Rachel Reeves \u8217\'20\'19s maiden budget.\par \par \uc2 Starmer has looked to increase his grip on economic policy in recent weeks, by appointing Shafiq, poaching Reeves\u8217\'20\'19s No 2, Darren Jones, and{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/aug/28/keir-starmer-replaces-key-aide-nin-pandit-no-10-more-changes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  appointing a longtime Treasury civil servant }}}\uc2 to be his principal private secretary.\par \par \uc2 12.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jaguar Land Rover says cyber-attack has affected \u8216\'20\'18some data\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The cyber-attack on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/jaguar-land-rover"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jaguar Land Rover}}}\uc2  has affected data held by the carmaker, it has said, as its factories in the UK and abroad face prolonged closure.\par \par \uc2 JLR , Britain\u8217\'20\'19s biggest carmaker, said on Wednesday that in its investigations into the{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/sep/02/jaguar-land-rover-cyber-incident-manufacturing-retail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  hack}}}\uc2 , which first emerged last week, it had now discovered data had been breached.\par \par \uc2 The manufacturer said it could not provide more details of which data was affected, or if customers\u8217\'20\'19 or suppliers\u8217\'20\'19 information was stolen, but said it would be contacting anyone affected.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson said all the relevant authorities had been notified, understood to include the Information Commissioner\u8217\'20\'19s Office , which had already been informed of the risk of a data breach.\par \par \uc2 11.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Oracle shares jump ahead of opening bell on cloud computing boost\par \par \uc2 Shares in Oracle have jumped by nearly 32% before the opening bell on Wall Street, after the business software company got a big boost from its cloud computing business.\par \par \uc2 The Austin, Texas-based company forecast that revenue from its core cloud division will exceed half a trillion dollars over the next few months.\par \par \uc2 Investors have been betting big on AI-driven cloud firms. Oracle \u8217\'20\'19s rivals are seeing rapid cloud growth as well, reflecting how rising enterprise demand for AI infrastructure is fuelling a broader lift across the industry. The results lifted shares of several US chipmakers in pre-market trading, with AMD up around 3% and Nvidia 2.2% higher.\par \par \uc2 Russ Mould, investment director at the stockbroker AJ Bell , said:\par \par \uc2 Oracle said on Tuesday that it had signed four multi-billion-dollar contracts with three customers in the first quarter, signalling booming demand for its low-cost cloud infrastructure services. Chief executive Safra Catz said:\par \par \uc2 The company forecast Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI ) revenue growth of 77% to $18bn this year, and $144bn in the following four years.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at the research firm Morningstar said:\par \par \uc2 The company has struck deals with Amazon , Google owner Alphabet and Microsoft to run OCI within their clouds, with revenue from these clients up 1,529% in the first quarter.\par \par \uc2 Oracle expects second-quarter revenue to rise by 12%-14%, including cloud revenue growth of between 32% and 36%.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.53am BST\par \par \uc2 11.17am BST\par \par \uc2 An estimated 64.5% of adult Brits are overweight or living with obesity, yet more than 71% (48 million people) say weight loss injections are out of reach.\par \par \uc2 Novo Nordisk \u8217\'20\'19s Wegovy and Eli Lilly \u8217\'20\'19s Mounjaro drugs are available on the NHS , but are limited to people with high clinical need.\par \par \uc2 Now, with Mounjaro prices surging by up to 170% in the UK, some patients, who buy the drug privately, will be paying nearly three times more for their treatment.\par \par \uc2 Mounjaro users reacted with dismay to when its manufacturer, Eli Lilly , announced a price increase {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/aug/14/eli-lilly-uk-price-weight-loss-jab-mounjaro-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the UK from September}}}\uc2 , as we reported last month. Many people are worried they will be unable to continue using the medication, raising concerns for their mental and physical health.\par \par \uc2 But even before the price hikes, affordability was an issue. A survey by the online pharmacy ZAVA showed that\par \par \uc2 * 49% of Brits (nearly 33 million people) can only afford to spend up to \u163\'00\'A380 a month, far below Mounjaro\u8217\'20\'19s new \u163\'00\'A3170\u8211\'20\'13\u163\'00\'A3310 range.\par \par \uc2 * With Wegovy\u8217\'20\'19s highest dose (2.4mg) now capped at \u163\'00\'A3189.99, a steep price but experts say it could offer a more accessible option for patients than Mounjaro\par \par \uc2 Dr. Crystal Wyllie, ZAVA doctor, said:\par \par \uc2 10.39am BST\par \par \uc2 Junk food leads to more children being obese than underweight globally\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s our full story on Wegovy and Ozempic maker Novo Nordisk making job cuts as it struggles against competition from Eli Lilly \u8217\'20\'19s Mounjaro jab and cheaper generic versions:\par \par \uc2 It comes as a UN report found that more children around the world are obese than underweight for the first time \u8211\'20\'13 a sad milestone. It warned that ultra-processed junk food is overwhelming childhood diets.\par \par \uc2 There are 188 million teenagers and school-age children with obesity \u8211\'20\'13 one in 10 \u8211\'20\'13 Unicef said, affecting health and development and bringing a risk of life-threatening diseases.\par \par \uc2 Catherine Russell , executive director of the UN agency for children, said:\par \par \uc2 While 9.2% of five to 19-year-olds worldwide are underweight, 9.4% are considered obese, the report found. In 2000, nearly 13% were underweight and just 3% were obese.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 10.46am BST\par \par \uc2 10.35am BST\par \par \uc2 Rise in energy prices leaves 1m UK households behind on bills\par \par \uc2 About 1m households are behind on their gas and electricity bills with no repayment plan amid a rise in energy debt over the past decade, according to a new report.\par \par \uc2 The Resolution Foundation thinktank found that the number of customers in energy debt has increased and the size of their debts has risen. It found that between 2012 and 2024 the average gas and electricity debts more than doubled to \u163\'00\'A31,400 and \u163\'00\'A31,600, respectively, from an average of approximately \u163\'00\'A3500.\par \par \uc2 The number of customers behind on their electricity bills, with no repayment plan, has more than tripled from 300,000 in 2012 to more than 1m at the end of last year, the report found. The number of customers who are behind on their gas bills also tripled from 300,000 to 900,000 over the same period.\par \par \uc2 10.33am BST\par \par \uc2 UK contactless payments could go above \u163\'00\'A3100 or become unlimited\par \par \uc2 Contactless card payments could go above \u163\'00\'A3100 and potentially become unlimited under proposals to allow banks and other providers to set their own limits for customers.\par \par \uc2 The Financial Conduct Authority (FCA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fca.org.uk/news/press-releases/proposed-contactless-changes-could-increase-convenience-consumers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said on Wednesday}}}\uc2  that the proposal to scrap the current limit would provide shoppers with more convenience and card providers \u8220\'20\'1Cthe flexibility to decide the right limit for them and customers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The UK financial watchdog has been consulting on giving banks the option of raising or removing the \u163\'00\'A3100 cap, which would mean shoppers no longer need to enter a four-digit pin to authorise big purchases, since March.\par \par \uc2 Customers are also currently unable to make more than \u163\'00\'A3300 of touch-free payments in a single day.\par \par \uc2 10.28am BST\par \par \uc2 European Green Party heartened by Ursula von der Leyen 's green remarks\par \par \uc2 Ciar\u225\'00\'E1n Cuffe , co chair of the European Green Party, said he was heartened to hear Ursula von der Leyen make an unexpected return to the narrative of the green deal.\par \par \uc2 After a year or more of pressure from centre right and far right political interests to abandon environmental targets, von der Leyen, president of the European Commission in Brussels, told MEPs:\par \par \uc2 Cuffe told the Guardian:\par \par \uc2 Luca de Meo , the former boss of car giant Stellantis , has previously called on Europe to follow the Japanese example to make what is known as \u8220\'20\'1CKei cars\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a distinct class of small cars which come with incentives such as reduced taxes and parking costs.\par \par \uc2 But yesterday the German chancellor Friederich Merz weighed in on the side of the Germany car industry, urging Brussels to consider \u8220\'20\'1Cflexibility\u8221\'20\'1D around the 2035 target for phasing out the sale of new petrol cars.\par \par \uc2 This set Germany up for a clash with Nordic brands Polestar and Volvo, which say they should not be punished just because the Germans have been slow to adopt to change.\par \par \uc2 10.18am BST\par \par \uc2 European stocks eke out modest gains; Russian rouble fells to five-month low\par \par \uc2 In financial markets, the FTSE 100 index of leading UK shares is broadly flat at 9,250, up by 8.7 points. The German and French stock markets edged by 0.1% higher, while the Italian borsa slipped by 0.17%.\par \par \uc2 The Russian rouble fell to a five-month low against the US dollar, crossing the 85 rouble mark, after drones from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/10/poland-shoots-down-drones-over-its-territory-amid-russian-attack-on-ukraine-says-military"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s attack in western Ukraine were shot down in Polish airspace}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rouble fell by 1.6% to 84 against the dollar at one stage. It has lost 5% against the dollar since the start of the week. Analysts pointed to an expected interest rate cut by the Russian central bank on 12 September, rising demand for imports and the threat of new western sanctions on Moscow.\par \par \uc2 Bank of St Petersburg analysts said:\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s attack on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  spread to Nato territory in the most significant way since the full-scale invasion more than three years ago. You can follow the latest on our Europe live blog here:\par \par \uc2 9.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Zara owner reports weaker-than-expected sales in 'complex' market\par \par \uc2 The fashion company behind Zara has reported weaker-than-expected sales after a slowdown in growth at the retail chain.\par \par \uc2 The boss of Inditex , the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest fashion retailer, insisted it reported a \u8220\'20\'1Csolid\u8221\'20\'1D performance in the face of \u8220\'20\'1Ccomplex\u8221\'20\'1D market conditions. Inditex said sales picked up in recent weeks after the launch of its autumn and winter collections, which were \u8220\'20\'1Cvery well received by our customers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Galicia-based retailer, which also owns the Pull & Bear and Bershka brands, said sales grew by 1.6% to \u8364\'20\'AC18.4bn (\u163\'00\'A315.9bn) in the six months to July. Sales were up 5.1% after adjusting for currency rates. Sales of \u8364\'20\'AC10.08bn in the second quarter came in below the \u8364\'20\'AC10.26bn expected by analysts.\par \par \uc2 Sales for the group\u8217\'20\'19s flagship Zara business grew slightly to \u8364\'20\'AC13.15bn, however this was a slowdown, amid pressure on household finances.\par \par \uc2 Inditex reported a pick up in sales more recently, with 9% growth across its stores and online between 1 August 1 and 7 September.\par \par \uc2 Oscar Garcia Maceiras , chief executive of Inditex , said:\par \par \uc2 Separately on Wednesday, Primark owner Associated British Foods said like-for-like sales in the second half would be 2% below the same period last year, amid \u8220\'20\'1Cconsumer caution\u8221\'20\'1D. It flagged a \u8220\'20\'1Cmore subdued consumer environment in Europe and trading was weaker, while performance in the US was strong\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Over the year as a whole, the company expects Primark \u8217\'20\'19s like-for-like sales growth to be around 1%, with its store rollout programme driving total sales growth of around 4%.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 9.48am BST\par \par \uc2 8.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Anthony Codling, housing analyst at RBC Europe , said:\par \par \uc2 8.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Vistry Group shares plunge 8% after profits halve\par \par \uc2 Shares in Vistry Group , one of Britain\u8217\'20\'19s biggest housebuilders, plunged after its first-half profits more than halved.\par \par \uc2 The company, which owns Bovis Homes , Countryside and Linden Homes, said its pre-tax profit in the first six months of the year fell to \u163\'00\'A340.9m from \u163\'00\'A391.2m a year earlier. On an adjusted basis, profits fell by a third to \u163\'00\'A380.6m.\par \par \uc2 It completed 6,889 homes, down 12% from the 7,792 completed a year earlier. Revenues fell by 5% to \u163\'00\'A31.6bn.\par \par \uc2 Vistry shares fell as much as 8% to 555p, and are now down 3.7%.\par \par \uc2 However, Vistry was upbeat, after forming a long-term joint venture with the UK\u8217\'20\'19s housing agency earlier this week. Homes England and the company have created a new vehicle, called Hestia, backed by a combined \u163\'00\'A3150m of capital investment. Last year, the government pledged to build 1.5m homes in this parliament, over five years, with a focus on social and affordable housing.\par \par \uc2 In June, then-housing secretary Angela Rayner announced a massive boost to the government\u8217\'20\'19s affordable housing programme, almost doubling funding to \u163\'00\'A339bn over the next decade.\par \par \uc2 Greg Fitzgerald , the Vistry chief executive, said:\par \par \uc2 Vistry now specialises in building social and affordable homes for its partners.{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vistrygroup.co.uk/our-partnerships-model/our-partnerships-model#:~:text=A%20UNIQUE%20STRATEGIC%20ADVANTAGE,that%20is%20what%20we%20receive.%E2%80%9D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  The company pre-sells at least 50% of new homes}}}\uc2  on its developments to housing associations, local authorities, and private rented sector providers.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 9.55am BST\par \par \uc2 8.17am BST\par \par \uc2 US supreme court to decide on legality of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s sweeping global tariffs\par \par \uc2 The news comes after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  agreed on Tuesday to decide the legality of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s sweeping global {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tariffs}}}\uc2 , setting up a major test of one of the Republican president\u8217\'20\'19s boldest assertions of executive power that has been central to his economic and trade agenda.\par \par \uc2 The justices took up the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s appeal of a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that Trump overstepped his authority in imposing most of his tariffs under a federal law meant for emergencies. The court acted swiftly after the administration last week asked it to review the case, which involves trillions of dollars in customs duties over the next decade.\par \par \uc2 The court, which begins its next nine-month term on 6 October, placed the case on a fast track, scheduling oral arguments for the first week of November.\par \par \uc2 The justices also agreed to hear a separate challenge to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs brought by a family-owned toy company, Learning Resources.\par \par \uc2 The US court of appeals for the federal circuit in Washington ruled on 29 August that Trump overreached in invoking a 1977 law known as the International Emergency Economic Powers Act (IEEPA) to impose the tariffs, undercutting a major priority for the president in his second term. The tariffs, however, remain in effect during the appeal to the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 8.11am BST\par \par \uc2 More on the proposed Trump tariffs on India and China.\par \par \uc2 According to the Financial Times , a second US official said Washington was prepared to \u8220\'20\'1Cmirror\u8221\'20\'1D any tariffs on China and India imposed by the EU, potentially leading to a further increase in US levies on imports from both countries.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s proposal comes as the White House is getting frustrated with its efforts at brokering a peace deal and Russia\u8217\'20\'19s recent heavy aerial attacks on Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president came on this morning and his view is that the obvious approach here is, let\u8217\'20\'19s all put on dramatic tariffs and keep the tariffs on until the Chinese agree to stop buying the oil. There really aren\u8217\'20\'19t many other places that oil can go,\u8221\'20\'1D the first US official said.\par \par \uc2 The US president later told reporters he expected to have a call with Russian president Vladimir Putin \u8220\'20\'1Cthis week or early next week\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 7.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Introduction: Trump reportedly asks EU to levy 100% tariffs on India and China; Novo Nordisk to cut 9,000 jobs\par \par \uc2 Good morning, and welcome to our rolling coverage of business, the financial markets and the world economy.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump has reportedly asked the EU to levy tariffs of up to 100% on India and China, in order to increase pressure on Russia to end its war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The US president made the demand after he dialled into a meeting on Tuesday between senior US and EU officials gathered in Washington, the Financial Times , Bloomberg News and other media reported. One US official said, according to the FT:\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Ozempic and Wegovy maker Novo Nordisk announced that it will cut 9,000 jobs and trimmed its profit forecast for this year, as it struggles against competition from US rival Eli Lilly \u8217\'20\'19s Mounjaro weight loss injection.\par \par \uc2 The job cuts amount to 11% of the drugmaker\u8217\'20\'19s workforce of 78,400. About 5,000 of the job losses will happen in Denmark.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.novonordisk.com/news-and-media/news-and-ir-materials/news-details.html?id=916424#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Novo Nordisk said the move would save 8bn Danish kroner}}}\uc2  (\u163\'00\'A3930m) a year, although it will also lead to one-off costs of 8bn kroner this year. As a result, it expects to deliver operating profit growth of 4% to 10% at constant exchange rates, down from 10%\u8212\'20\'1416%.\par \par \uc2 It is the first major move by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.novonordisk.com/news-and-media/latest-news/meet-mike-doustdar.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Doustdar}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.novonordisk.com/news-and-media/latest-news/meet-mike-doustdar.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 , an Iranian-born Austrian-American businessman}}}\uc2 , who took over as chief executive last month. Novo Nordisk \u8211\'20\'13 which had become Europe\u8217\'20\'19s most valuable company on the back of the weight loss drug boom \u8211\'20\'13 recently lost two thirds of its market value following disappointing drug trial results and slowing sales.\par \par \uc2 Doustdar said:\par \par \uc2 Studies have shown that Eli Lilly \u8217\'20\'19s Mounjaro is more effective than Wegovy in reducing weight. Novo\u8217\'20\'19s Ozempic injection is also available on the NHS , as a treatment for type 2 diabetes.\par \par \uc2 Asian stock markets rose while government bonds fell, after weaker US labour market data heightened expectations of a Federal Reserve interest rate cut of at least a quarter point next week.\par \par \uc2 Japan\u8217\'20\'19s Nikkei closed 0.87% higher while Hong Kong\u8217\'20\'19s Hang Seng climbed by 1.1% and South Korea\u8217\'20\'19s Kospi rose by 1.67%.\par \par \uc2 US government bonds fell for a second day on Wednesday, pushing yields higher. The yield, or interest rate, on the benchmark 10-year Treasury rose by 1 basis point to 4.088%, after climbing almost 3 basis points on Tuesday. The equivalent Japanese bond yield rose by 0.5 basis points to 1.565%.\par \par \uc2 The Agenda\par \par \uc2 * 8am BST: Spain Industrial production for July\par \par \uc2 * 9am BST: Italy Industrial production for July\par \par \uc2 * 10am BST: UK Treasury gilt 2031 auction\par \par \uc2 * 1.30pm BST: US producer prices for August\par \par \uc2 Updated at 9.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Document