\par\par \b \uc2 US job seekers: what is it like to be looking for work right now?\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian community team \par \uc2 196 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 September 2025\par 14:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19d like to hear from US job seekers how their search for a new position has been going, as well as from employees who decided to stay put, and why\par \par \uc2 The US added 911,000 fewer jobs than first estimated for the year through March 2025, the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  (\uc2 BLS\uc2 ) has announced, highlighting recent concerns about the health of America\u8217\'20\'19s labor market.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/sep/09/us-created-fewer-jobs-march-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The revision}}}\uc2  comes after a lackluster August jobs report, with only 22,000 jobs added in the US.\par \par \uc2 The largest revisions were in leisure and hospitality (down 176,000), professional and business services (down 158,000) and retail trade (down 126,200). Government jobs were adjusted down by 31,000 jobs.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19d like to hear from current job seekers in the US what their experience of looking for work right now has been like.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19d also like to hear from US employees who were considering leaving their jobs for new opportunities but have decided to stay put, and why. Do you have concerns about the US labor market? Tell us.\par \par \uc2 Callout\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250910el9a004bl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
