\par\par \b \uc2 Anglo American\uc2  agrees mining mega merger; Londoners face commuting struggles as tube strike enters second day \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Julia Kollewe \par \uc2 4,027 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 September 2025\par 15:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Deal will create $53bn mining giant but raises fears of job cuts as headquarters moves to Vancouver\par \par \uc2 4.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The London-listed miner {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/anglo-american"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anglo American}}}\uc2  has agreed to merge with its Canadian rival \uc2 Teck Resources\uc2  , in a deal that will create a $53bn (\u163\'00\'A339bn) global copper group after both companies saw off takeover attempts.\par \par \uc2 The merger to form one of the biggest copper producers in the world is expected to bring hundreds of job losses at Anglo\u8217\'20\'19s London office as the company prepares to move its headquarters to Vancouver, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/canada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Canada}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The new company will retain Anglo\u8217\'20\'19s primary listing on the \uc2 London Stock Exchange\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 held since 1999 - with secondary listings in Johannesburg, Vancouver and New York. But Anglo Teck\u8217\'20\'19s senior leadership team will be based in Vancouver after sweeping efforts by the \uc2 Canadian government\uc2  to protect the country\u8217\'20\'19s minerals sector.\par \par \uc2 In London, the tube network was brought to a standstill for a second day as RMT workers went on strike, in a dispute over pay and conditions.\par \par \uc2 Our other main stories today:Thank you for reading. We\u8217\'20\'19ll be back tomorrow. Take care \u8211\'20\'13 JK\par \par \uc2 Updated at 4.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 4.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 US economy created 911,000 fewer jobs than thought in year to March\par \par \uc2 The US economy created 911,000 fewer jobs in the 12 months through March than previously estimated, according to government figures, suggesting that job growth was already stalling before president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s aggressive trade tariffs.\par \par \uc2 This was towards the high end of expectations.\par \par \uc2 Bradley Saunders, North America economist at \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 3.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 More from Lisa O\u8217\'20\'19Carroll reporting on the Munich car show.\par \par \uc2 The chief executive of Nordic car brand Polestar has launched a scathing attack on German rivals claiming they are pushing for \u8220\'20\'1Cdelays\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Clifelines\u8221\'20\'1D from Brussels to rescue them from Chinese electric vehicle rivals.\par \par \uc2 Hours after the German chancellor \uc2 Friedrich Merz\uc2  called for more \u8220\'20\'1Cflexibility\u8221\'20\'1D from Brussels in relation to the phasing out of new petrol cars by 2035, \uc2 Michael Lohscheller\uc2  , condemned what he called the delay tactics warning that Europe does not need \u8220\'20\'1Ctech neutrality\u8221\'20\'1D but \u8220\'20\'1Cambition and action\u8221\'20\'1D from Brussels.\par \par \uc2 Calls for \u8220\'20\'1Ctechnology neutral\u8221\'20\'1D policy opens the door for synthetic fuels and continued investment in hybrid rather than fully electric cars, he said.\par \par \uc2 His remarks at the Munich car show come just days before the EU launches a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrategic dialogue\u8221\'20\'1D with the car industry over its future.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 3.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 2.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 French borrowing costs top Italy's in historic shift\par \par \uc2 With France in political crisis, French borrowing costs have risen above those in Italy for the first time in the eurozone\u8217\'20\'19s history.\par \par \uc2 The yield, or interest rate, on 10-year French government bonds rose to 3.48% at one stage, above Italy\u8217\'20\'19s 3.47%. It is the first time this has happened since 1998.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg News said the shift was due to technical reasons, as the French bond moved to a slighter later maturity than the Italian equivalent \u8211\'20\'13 but the trend towards convergence between the two nations\u8217\'20\'19 debt has been years in the making.\par \par \uc2 Europe\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest economy is without a government (again) after the centrist prime minister {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/dec/13/from-farmer-to-premier-who-is-francois-bayrou-the-new-french-prime-minister"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fran\u231\'00\'E7ois Bayrou}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s resignation today (he lost a confidence vote yesterday, which he had called himself, after only nine months as prime minister).\par \par \uc2 In a speech to lawmakers on Monday, Bayrou called France\u8217\'20\'19s debt level \u8220\'20\'1Clife-threatening\u8221\'20\'1D for the country, adding:\par \par \uc2 2.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Our economics correspondent Richard Partingon is at the TUC\u8217\'20\'19s annual congress in Brighton. He reports:\par \par \uc2 For union delegates gathering in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk/brighton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brighton}}}\uc2 , sunshine glimmered on the Channel outside the annual TUC conference but the focus for many inside was on stormy developments elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 After a tough first year in power for Labour, two big spectres dominated the meeting: disappointment with \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s government, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/sep/08/labour-must-do-more-to-tackle-populist-right-as-partys-support-leaks-to-reform-say-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and the march of }}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s government, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/sep/08/labour-must-do-more-to-tackle-populist-right-as-partys-support-leaks-to-reform-say-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nigel Farage}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s government, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/sep/08/labour-must-do-more-to-tackle-populist-right-as-partys-support-leaks-to-reform-say-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Reform UK}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s unexpectedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/sep/05/who-will-replace-angela-rayner-the-role-changes-in-labours-reshuffle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 far-reaching reshuffle}}}\uc2  had provoked union fears that Labour may temper its plan to boost workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights in yet another pro-growth reset.\par \par \uc2 Business leaders are already sensing an opportunity: Britain\u8217\'20\'19s economy is weak, inflation is rising, \uc2 Rachel Reeves\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s tax on employment in her first autumn budget has chilled the jobs market, and the prospect of further rises, in her second act on 26 November, are looming.\par \par \uc2 For many it was ironic that the union gathering was taking place while the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2025/sep/08/london-tube-strike-tfl-website-rmt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 London Underground was brought close to a standstill}}}\uc2  by striking RMT members. Meanwhile, Labour was entering a potentially fractious {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/sep/08/labour-mps-80-nominations-by-thursday-stand-deputy-leader-angela-rayner-resignation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deputy leadership battle}}}\uc2  of the kind Starmer promised was only really a feature of the last Tory government.\par \par \uc2 Businesses reckon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/sep/05/angela-rayner-stands-down-over-stamp-duty-row"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Angela Rayner}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/sep/05/angela-rayner-stands-down-over-stamp-duty-row"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s resignation}}}\uc2  and the sacking of Justin Madders, the junior minister responsible for the workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights legislation \u8211\'20\'13 both politicians have close links to the union movement \u8211\'20\'13 could remove obstacles, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/sep/07/uk-business-secretary-peter-kyle-visit-beijing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peter Kyle}}}\uc2  and the sacking of Justin Madders, the junior minister responsible for the workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights legislation \u8211\'20\'13 both politicians have close links to the union movement \u8211\'20\'13 could remove obstacles, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/sep/07/uk-business-secretary-peter-kyle-visit-beijing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 , the new business secretary}}}\uc2 , had a warm relationship with tech bosses in his old job.\par \par \uc2 For union leaders, however, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/labour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Labour}}}\uc2  watering down its workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights bill, after a string of measures in Starmer\u8217\'20\'19s first year hitting the poorest in society \u8211\'20\'13 not least cuts to winter fuel and proposed disability benefit cuts \u8211\'20\'13 would be a red line.\par \par \uc2 Sharon Graham, the Unite general secretary, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI do not understand how a Labour government has been attacking some of poorest in our society \u8230\'20\'26 pensioners, the disabled \u8230\'20\'26 whilst leaving the super-rich totally untouched.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat the hell are Labour doing?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 3.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Business minister: can't say if JLR cyber attack was state-sponsored\par \par \uc2 A business minister said he cannot confirm or deny whether a cyber attack on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/jaguar-land-rover"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jaguar Land Rover}}}\uc2  (JLR) was state-sponsored.\par \par \uc2 When pressed by the Conservatives to reveal who was behind the attack, Sir Chris Bryant said he will not \u8220\'20\'1Cjump to conclusions\u8221\'20\'1D, with investigations ongoing, PA reported.\par \par \uc2 JLR was forced to halt production on 31 August after discovering hackers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/sep/02/jaguar-land-rover-cyber-incident-manufacturing-retail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had infiltrated its systems}}}\uc2  a week ago.\par \par \uc2 The UK\u8217\'20\'19s biggest car manufacturer, owned by India\u8217\'20\'19s Tata group, revealed its production and sales had been \u8220\'20\'1Cseverely disrupted\u8221\'20\'1D, with factory staff told to work from home.\par \par \uc2 Production at JLR and dozens of its suppliers is to remain on hold for at least this week, with disruption from the crippling cyber-attack at the carmaker expected to last until October.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of production workers at the UK\u8217\'20\'19s biggest car manufacturing sites in Halewood on Merseyside, and Solihull and Wolverhampton in the West Midlands have been told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/sep/05/jaguar-land-rover-staff-stay-home-cyberattack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to stay away until at least today}}}\uc2 . They will continue to be paid as usual and \u8220\'20\'1Cbank\u8221\'20\'1D their hours to be picked up later on.\par \par \uc2 1.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 City regulator: will challenge lenders claiming to have lost car finance data\par \par \uc2 The City regulator has warned it will challenge lenders claiming to have lost data linked to the car finance scandal, helping ensure consumers get their fair share of a potential \u163\'00\'A318bn compensation scheme\par \par \uc2 Speaking to MPs on the Treasury Committee on Tuesday, Financial Conduct Authority (FCA) chief executive Nikhil Rathi confirmed that data retention had become a major sticking point, as the regulator weighed whether to open its redress scheme to contracts dating back to 2007.\par \par \uc2 The scheme is meant to draw a line under the car finance scandal, compensating millions of drivers who were overcharged as a result of controversial commission arrangements between lenders and car dealers. It follows a landmark supreme court ruling in August, which upheld one of three consumer complaints over commission.\par \par \uc2 But some lenders claim they may not be able to verify claims that are nearly 20 years old, with consumer data and contrast likely to have been lost or deleted. Most banks typically purge customer data after six years.\par \par \uc2 However, Rathi said that this would not be accepted as a blanket excuse. \u8220\'20\'1CWhere a firm says to us that they don\u8217\'20\'19t have the data, we\u8217\'20\'19re not just going to take that at face value, we will look at that very forensically.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The FCA ordered firms to stop deleting car finance documents when it launched its initial investigation in car finance commission payments in January 2024.\par \par \uc2 Sheree Howard, the FCA executive director in charge of authorisations, also told MPs that firms could end up retrieving data by working with other companies.\par \par \uc2 12.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Friedrich Merz , the German chancellor, has called for \u8220\'20\'1Cmore flexibility\u8221\'20\'1D from Brussels in relation to targets for the transition to electric vehicles \u8211\'20\'13 siding with German car manufacturers and opening up a divide with other European carmakers who want to stick to the deadline for phasing out combustion engines.\par \par \uc2 The bosses of Volvo and Polestar were among 150 car chiefs who wrote to the European Commission Ursula von der Leyen on Monday urging her to maintain the 2035 target for cars and vans and arguing that any change would hand an advantage to Chinese rivals.\par \par \uc2 Michael Lohscheller , Polestar\u8217\'20\'19s chief executive, said in a statement:\par \par \uc2 But on Tuesday, the German chancellor weighed in on Volkswagen \u8217\'20\'19s and Mercedes-Benz \u8217\'20\'19s side, calling for more regulatory flexibility from the EU. He threw his weight behind the German auto industry\u8217\'20\'19s push to soften rules that would effectively ban sales of new petrol vehicles in 10 years\u8217\'20\'19 time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are of course committed to the transition to e-mobility,\u8221\'20\'1D the conservative leader told the opening of a motor show in Munich, but added that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe need smart, reliable and flexible European regulation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Merz stopped short of calling for the 2035 deadline for selling only emission-free vehicles to be delayed or scrapped.\par \par \uc2 Polestar says it would be wrong to let the target date slip saying it would \u8220\'20\'1Cpunish the frontrunners and benefit those\u8221\'20\'1D like Volkswagen and Mercedes Benz who lagged behind.\par \par \uc2 Merz reiterated his coalition government\u8217\'20\'19s support for \u8220\'20\'1Ctechnology openness,\u8221\'20\'1D a reference to the auto sector\u8217\'20\'19s desire for hybrid and other vehicles to be exempted from the rules.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 12.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 12.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is Prof Dieter Helm \u8217\'20\'19s view on water minister Emma Hardy\u8217\'20\'19s remarks.\par \par \uc2 Helm, professor of economic policy at the University of Oxford , told the Efra committee that \u8220\'20\'1Cit would be a disaster\u8221\'20\'1D if a special administration was only used in extremis for Thames Water .\par \par \uc2 Updated at 12.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 11.55am BST\par \par \uc2 UK water minister: Thames Water has 'not met threshold' for special administration\par \par \uc2 More from the UK\u8217\'20\'19s water minister Emma Hardy.\par \par \uc2 She told MPs on the environment, food and rural affairs committee that beleaguered water company Thames Water has \u8220\'20\'1Cnot met the threshold\u8221\'20\'1D for special administration and suggested it would not do so until taps run dry.\par \par \uc2 Thames is racing to secure funding to avoid temporary nationalisation and recently secured a controversial, high-interest, \u163\'00\'A33bn loan to stave off collapse. The company recently secured a payment plan with the industry regulator for fines it owes worth \u163\'00\'A3123m.\par \par \uc2 The company has been trying to raise money for a turnaround plan for the past year, after building up a net debt pile worth \u163\'00\'A317.7bn under successive private owners.\par \par \uc2 Hardy claimed to the committee that it is not the government\u8217\'20\'19s decision whether a company goes into SAR. She said:\par \par \uc2 A water company goes into special administration when either the secretary of state applies to the court and makes the case for the water company to enter SAR, or if the water company says it can no longer operate and needs to go into SAR.\par \par \uc2 Hardy added:\par \par \uc2 Under further questioning she added that SAR can also be met when the company does not meet performance targets set by Ofwat , the regulator. Hardy added:\par \par \uc2 Asked by the committee if that was formal advice she\u8217\'20\'19s been given she said \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 Helena Dollimore, Efra committee member, said in response \u8220\'20\'1Cthe regulator is pretty useless, it does not want to bark, let alone bite.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ministers appear to be getting ready to place the company into SAR, and have appointed FTI Consulting as potential administrators.\par \par \uc2 Hardy confirmed the appointment, adding:\par \par \uc2 11.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Peter Kyle , the \u8216\'20\'18tech bro\u8217\'20\'19 minister charged with kickstarting UK growth\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve looked at the UK\u8217\'20\'19s new business minister, Peter Kyle , whose trip to China today coincides with his birthday.\par \par \uc2 When {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/peter-kyle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peter Kyle}}}\uc2  begins a 7,000-mile flight from Washington to Beijing this week, Britain\u8217\'20\'19s new business secretary could reflect on how far he has already come.\par \par \uc2 Kyle struggled at school due to dyslexia and left, in his own words, \u8220\'20\'1Cwithout any usable\u8221\'20\'1D qualifications. He made it to university in his 20s after several failed attempts.\par \par \uc2 Now, days after accepting his second ministerial brief in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/sep/05/who-will-replace-angela-rayner-the-role-changes-in-labours-reshuffle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reshuffle triggered by }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/sep/05/who-will-replace-angela-rayner-the-role-changes-in-labours-reshuffle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Angela Rayner}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/sep/05/who-will-replace-angela-rayner-the-role-changes-in-labours-reshuffle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  resignation, Kyle is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/sep/07/uk-business-secretary-peter-kyle-visit-beijing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leading talks with White House officials}}}\uc2  about the US-UK technology partnership. With no time to celebrate his 55th birthday on Tuesday, the business secretary will then jet off for tentative and delicate discussions with China about deeper economic cooperation.\par \par \uc2 The missions to the world\u8217\'20\'19s two largest economies are intended to help kickstart what Kyle told business leaders last week would be a \u8220\'20\'1Crelentless\u8221\'20\'1D pursuit of the growth that has so far eluded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/labour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Labour}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Those who have worked with Kyle, who was elected in 2015 as the MP for Hove in East Sussex, near where he grew up, say he will bring a sharp intellect and strong worth ethic to the role. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a very well-liked and hard-working guy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Theo Bertram, director of the Social Market Foundation thinktank and a former adviser to Tony Blair .\par \par \uc2 But in the year Kyle has spent as the minister for science and innovation, he has faced questions about whether he is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/may/14/minister-accused-of-being-too-close-to-big-tech-after-analysis-of-meetings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 far too close to big tech}}}\uc2 , in particular in the burgeoning artificial intelligence industry.\par \par \uc2 In the 1980s and 1990s, Kyle was mentored by the late Anita Roddick when he worked in the head office of her Body Shop empire. These days, he turns for advice not to a human mentor but to AI, a technology he has said is just a few years from matching \u8211\'20\'13 and even outstripping \u8211\'20\'13 human capability.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.27am BST\par \par \uc2 11.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Water minister: English water companies could transition to not-for-profit model\par \par \uc2 Water minister Emma Hardy has told MPs on the environment, food and rural affairs committee that English water companies could transition to a co-operative or not-for-profit model, similar to Welsh Water.\par \par \uc2 But she said no government money would be used for such a transition.\par \par \uc2 Asked if the sector could move from a for-profit model to a not-for-profit structure, she said:\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.07am BST\par \par \uc2 11.00am BST\par \par \uc2 A UK government bond auction has gone well.\par \par \uc2 The Debt Management Office sold \u163\'00\'A31.75bn of gilts maturing in 2043 that was covered 3.5 times, indicating good demand. The bonds were sold with a yield of 5.291%.\par \par \uc2 In bond markets, the yield on 30-year gilts has ticked up slightly to 5.46%.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.14am BST\par \par \uc2 10.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Gold hits fresh record high, silver also rises\par \par \uc2 Gold has continued to rise and hit a fresh record high earlier today.\par \par \uc2 Spot gold touched $3,659.10 an ounce and is now trading at $3,654 an ounce, up 0.5% on the day.\par \par \uc2 Gold prices have gained almost 39% so far this year, after rising by 27% in 2024, boosted by a weak dollar, central banks adding to their gold reserves, interest rate cuts and heightened global uncertainty. Gold is seen as a safe haven in times of turmoil.\par \par \uc2 The price of silver has also risen, as mounting expectations for interest rate cuts from the US Federal Reserve underpinned demand for precious metals. Spot silver edged 0.1% higher to $41.35 an ounce, near its highest level since 2011.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices are also up, with Brent crude, the global benchmark, trading nearly 1% higher at $66.61 a barrel. The Opec oil cartel and allies including Russia announced over the weekend that it would lift output at a slower pace than in previous.\par \par \uc2 Another factor underpinning oil prices is the prospect of fresh sanctions on Russia, a a major oil exporter. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/08/trump-says-he-is-ready-to-impose-new-sanctions-on-russia-what-does-this-mean-for-putins-war-in-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/08/trump-says-he-is-ready-to-impose-new-sanctions-on-russia-what-does-this-mean-for-putins-war-in-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  has threatened new sanctions on Russia}}}\uc2  after Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s heaviest strikes on Ukraine since its invasion in February 2022.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 10.43am BST\par \par \uc2 10.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s our full story on Anglo American \u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18merger of equals\u8217\'20\'19 with Canada\u8217\'20\'19s Teck Resources .\par \par \uc2 It comes after Anglo {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/oct/30/mining-firm-bhp-says-it-has-moved-on-from-failed-anglo-american-bid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fended off a series of takeover attempts}}}\uc2  by its larger rival BHP last year, pushing it to radically restructure its business.\par \par \uc2 Anglo has sought to streamline its focus on iron ore and copper. This year it spun off its platinum mining business, and it has been exploring {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/feb/20/anglo-american-writes-down-diamond-de-beers-29bn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the potential sale of its renowned diamond business De Beers}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Anglo owns the Collahuasi and Los Bronces copper mines in Chile while Teck owns the Quebrada Blanca copper mine in the Andes, 15 km west of Collahuasi.\par \par \uc2 Copper is demand around the world, as electric vehicles require a substantial amount of copper in batteries, electric motors, wiring and charging infrastructure. The metal is also used in artificial intelligence data centres.\par \par \uc2 A recent BloombergNEF report predicted that copper demand from AI-powered facilities will average about 400,000 tonnes a year over the next decade, peaking at 572,000 tonnes in 2028.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 10.38am BST\par \par \uc2 9.46am BST\par \par \uc2 France's industrial production falls in July\par \par \uc2 Russ Mould, investment director at AJ Bell , said:\par \par \uc2 The French stock market also shrugged off a decline in industry output. Manufacturing output fell by 1.7% in July after June\u8217\'20\'19s 3.5% increase, while wider industrial production fell by 1.1% following June\u8217\'20\'19s 3.7% gain, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.insee.fr/en/statistiques/8638013"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 official data from France\u8217\'20\'19s statistics office INSEE}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 June\u8217\'20\'19s sharp rise was driven by a surge in aerospace and aviation manufacturing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStill, the broader picture is more reassuring: production levels across all industrial sectors remain above those seen in May, said Charlotte de Montpellier, senior economist at ING.\par \par \uc2 9.02am BST\par \par \uc2 French stock market rises despite political crisis, bond yields creep higher\par \par \uc2 In the markets, the FTSE 100 index has edged 0.2% higher while Germany\u8217\'20\'19s Dax gained 0.15% and Italy\u8217\'20\'19s FTSE MiB rose by 0.5%.\par \par \uc2 France\u8217\'20\'19s CAC climbed by 0.7%, despite political turmoil in the country. French president Emmanuel Macron is seeking his fifth prime minister in less than two years, after centre-right PM {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/dec/13/from-farmer-to-premier-who-is-francois-bayrou-the-new-french-prime-minister"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fran\u231\'00\'E7ois Bayrou}}}\uc2  was ousted in a confidence vote on Monday, as expected. This toppled his minority government.\par \par \uc2 Bayrou had called the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/aug/27/french-prime-ministers-confidence-vote-and-its-possible-consequences"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vote}}}\uc2  himself as a last-ditch gamble for support, saying he needed backing from parliament for austerity measures to reduce the public debt.\par \par \uc2 The yield, or interest rate, on French government bonds is creeping higher, amid concerns over France\u8217\'20\'19s ability to get to grips with its high debt.\par \par \uc2 Asian stock markets were mixed, with Japan\u8217\'20\'19s Nikkei losing 0.4% and Hong Kong\u8217\'20\'19s Hang Seng up 1.1%.\par \par \uc2 Japan\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister Shigeru Ishiba resigned over the weekend, and Sanae Takaichi , a veteran of Japan\u8217\'20\'19s Liberal Democratic Party and a fiscal dove, has decided to run in the party\u8217\'20\'19s leadership race, the news agency Kydo reported.\par \par \uc2 The dollar has sunk to a seven-week low against other major currencies, with markets betting on an interest rate cut from the US Federal Reserve next week.\par \par \uc2 Hargreaves Lansdown analyst Britzman said:\par \par \uc2 8.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Matt Britzman, senior equity analyst at Hargreaves Lansdown , said:\par \par \uc2 Teck shares jumped by nearly 24% in after-hours trading as speculation swirled that the companies were close to a deal after a Bloomberg News article.\par \par \uc2 8.23am BST\par \par \uc2 The Anglo American share price has jumped by 5.2% in early trading in London, making it the biggest riser on the FTSE 100 index.\par \par \uc2 This gives the mining company a market value of \u163\'00\'A328.4bn.\par \par \uc2 Other miners such as Glencore and Antofagasta are also among the main risers, up by more than 2%.\par \par \uc2 M\u233\'00\'E9lanie Joly , Canada\u8217\'20\'19s industry minister, said on X:\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.26am BST\par \par \uc2 7.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Introduction: Anglo American agrees mining mega merger; Londoners face commuting struggles as tube strike enters second day\par \par \uc2 Good morning, and welcome to our rolling coverage of business, the financial markets and the world economy.\par \par \uc2 The London-listed miner {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/business/anglo-american"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anglo American}}}\uc2  is to merge with Canada\u8217\'20\'19s Teck Resources , in a deal that will create a $53bn (\u163\'00\'A339bn) giant but raises fears of job cuts.\par \par \uc2 It is the biggest mining deal in more than a decade. The FTSE 100 company said it had agreed a merger deal to create a \u8220\'20\'1Cglobal critical minerals champion\u8221\'20\'1D and one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest copper producers. The combined market value of both companies is more than $53bn.\par \par \uc2 Global demand for copper is expected to keep rising, driven by the electric vehicle boom and AI-powered data centres.\par \par \uc2 Billed as a \u8220\'20\'1Cmerger of equals\u8221\'20\'1D, the new mining group, called Anglo Teck, will be headquartered in Vancouver, Canada, and have corporate offices in London and Johannesburg. It will have its main listing on the London Stock Exchange , with secondary listings in Toronto, South Africa and New York.\par \par \uc2 Anglo shareholders will own 62.4% of the combined company and Teck the remaining 37.6%. The deal is expected to lead to annual pre-tax savings of $800m by the end of the fourth year.\par \par \uc2 Around $60m of savings will come from \u8220\'20\'1Cde-duplication and rationalisation of board, executive leadership and other costs associated with a listed company\u8221\'20\'1D and $150m from removing other overlapping functions, raising the prospect of job cuts. There won\u8217\'20\'19t be any net reduction in employees in Canada, the companies said.\par \par \uc2 Duncan Wanblad , the Anglo chief executive, who will move to Canada along with the rest of the leadership team, said:\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s more misery for London commuters today as tube strikes enter a second day, and unlike yesterday, the Docklands Light Railway isn\u8217\'20\'19t running today.\par \par \uc2 Industrial action by the RMT union has brought almost the entire tube network to a standstill, and buses and the Elizabeth line were taking the strain yesterday.\par \par \uc2 More congestion is expected today as more people still typically work from home on Mondays and Fridays.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/czew3z331dxt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A union organiser told the BBC}}}\uc2  yesterday that said there could be more industrial action after this week, but they hope to be in \u8216\'20\'18meaningful discussions\u8217\'20\'19 with Transport for London by the end of this week. Jared Wood said:\par \par \uc2 The union\u8217\'20\'19s demands include better pay and access to a travel card which gives holders ticket deals at Legoland, Thorpe Park and Chessington World of Adventures , as well as guided tours of Buckingham Palace, according to the Daily Telegraph. The rail staff leisure card gives 75% off all mainline train tickets outside London.\par \par \uc2 TfL has made a pay offer of 3.4%, which it urged the union to put to its members in a fresh ballot. It has said it cannot meet demands to cut hours below the current 35 a week.\par \par \uc2 Bike rental surged yesterday as Londoners took to two wheels. TfL \u8217\'20\'19s cycle hire scheme had more than 20,000 hires by 3pm, double the previous Monday\u8217\'20\'19s rate. The e-bike rental company Lime said it had 58% more users on Monday morning, while rival Forest said it had doubled its rush-hour usage.\par \par \uc2 The Agenda\par \par \uc2 * All day: TUC Congress in Brighton\par \par \uc2 * 9.15am BST: Treasury committee hearing on motor finance with FCA CEO Nikhil Rathi and chairman Ashley Adler\par \par \uc2 * 10am BST: EFRA hearing with water minister Emma Hardy\par \par \uc2 * 10am BST: UK Treasury gilt 2043 auction\par \par \uc2 * 10.30am BST: Germany 10-year Bund auction\par \par \uc2 * 3pm BST: US Non-farm Payrolls annual revision\par \par \uc2 * 4.15pm BST: Bank of England deputy governor Sarah Breeden speech\par \par \uc2 Updated at 9.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250909el99001jp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
