\par\par \b \uc2 US created 911,000 fewer jobs through March 2025 than initially reported\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 412 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 September 2025\par 16:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Revision highlights recent concerns about the health of the labor market, and follows a lackluster August jobs reportBusiness live \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates\par \par \uc2 The US added 911,000 fewer jobs than first estimated for the year to March 2025, the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  (\uc2 BLS\uc2 ) announced on Tuesday, highlighting recent concerns about the health of the labor market.\par \par \uc2 The revisions are 50% higher than last year\u8217\'20\'19s adjustment and were on the higher end of Wall Street {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/09/09/jobs-report-revisions-september-2025-.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimates}}}\uc2  between 600,000 and 1 million.\par \par \uc2 The revision comes after a lackluster {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/sep/05/us-jobs-report-august-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August jobs report}}}\uc2 , with only 22,000 jobs added in the US. That report too contained revisions and noted that 13,000 jobs were lost for the month of June 2025, the first negative jobs report survey since December 2020. The unemployment rate increased to 4.3%, the highest rate since 2021.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/01/trump-fires-erika-mcentarfer-labor-statistics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired}}}\uc2  Erika McEntarfer, commissioner of labor statistics, after a weak July job\u8217\'20\'19s report that he claimed \u8211\'20\'13 without evidence \u8211\'20\'13 was \u8220\'20\'1CRIGGED in order to make the Republicans, and ME, look bad\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But while these revisions to the jobs data are large, they are not unusual. During periods of economic change \u8211\'20\'13 such as the introduction of tariffs and the arrival of AI in the workplace \u8211\'20\'13 economists note businesses often take longer to reply to the \uc2 BLS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s surveys, leading to gaps in their data.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnnual revisions incorporate slow, administrative (non-survey) data that helps keep monthly estimates representative of broad labor-market trends,\u8221\'20\'1D stated Friends of Bureau of Labor Statistics in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.friendsofbls.org/updates/2025/9/4/background-information-for-jobs-day-sept-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FAQ on job statistics from the bureau}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The largest revisions were in leisure and hospitality (down 176,000), professional and business services (down 158,000) and retail trade (down 126,200). Government jobs were adjusted down by 31,000 jobs. The numbers released will face further revisions when \uc2 BLS\uc2  releases final benchmark figure in February 2026.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese numbers are likely to anger President Trump and the White House who incorrectly view revised data as political manipulation,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote \uc2 Elise Gould\uc2  and Ben Zipperer, economists at the \uc2 Economic Policy Institute\uc2 , in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/todays-bls-preliminary-benchmark-revisions-are-necessary-for-timely-and-accurate-data-not-fodder-for-trumps-attacks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post }}}\uc2 on the report.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump has already lashed out at \uc2 BLS\uc2 , including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/press/trumps-firing-of-bls-commissioner-is-undemocratic-and-economically-dangerous/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 firing the agency\u8217\'20\'19s commissioner}}}\uc2  because a jobs report showed a rapidly weakening labor market. But these \uc2 BLS\uc2  data revisions are not corrections of mistakes. Revisions are part of the regular, transparent process to update employment counts with the most comprehensive data possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250909el99004ee\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
