\par\par \b \uc2 Amazon fires 150 unionized third-party drivers, \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  says\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Aratani in New York \par \uc2 494 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 September 2025\par 13:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Union says \u8216\'20\'18Amazon is breaking the law\u8217\'20\'19 after drivers working for contractor Cornucopia were terminated\par \par \uc2 Amazon has fired more than 150 unionized drivers working for a third-party contractor in Queens, New York, according to the \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tdu.org/teamsters_take_on_amazon_union_busting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rallied}}}\uc2  at the company\u8217\'20\'19s DBK4 facility in Queens on Monday after the company fired the drivers, who worked for Cornucopia, a delivery service provider (DSP) that Amazon contracted with to make deliveries. Amazon works with more than 3,000 DSPs around the world who deliver the company\u8217\'20\'19s packages.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  said the firings were in retaliation for unionizing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmazon is breaking the law and we let the public know it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Antonio Rosario, a member of local 804 and a Teamster organizer, in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CAmazon workers will continue to organize and fight for what they deserve.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Amazon said the union was \u8220\'20\'1Cdeliberately spreading misinformation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Amazon has long claimed that drivers who are employed by third-party contractors are not employees of the company, and that firing a contractor does not amount to retaliation for unionizing.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, an Amazon spokesperson, Eileen Hards, called the move \u8220\'20\'1Ca recent change we made that\u8217\'20\'19s designed to allow DSPs to be more hands-on with their teams and support their operations at one delivery station\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur goal is to provide customers with fast delivery and great service \u8211\'20\'13 and we regularly review and make changes to the DSP program in support of this,\u8221\'20\'1D Hards said. \u8220\'20\'1CChanges like this not only benefit their employees, but also our customers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last August, a \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  official in Los Angeles ruled that Amazon had engaged in unfair labor practices after it terminated its contract with Battle-Tested Strategies (BTS), another DSP based in Palmdale, California, whose drivers had unionized with the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Although the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  said that Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s action did not amount to retaliation, the official said Amazon and BTS \u8220\'20\'1Cunlawfully failed and refused to bargain with the union over effects of the decision to terminate the BTS contract\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/08/24/nx-s1-5088580/amazon-delivery-drivers-nlrb-employees-teamsters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling}}}\uc2 , the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  deemed Amazon a joint employer of the drivers. Amazon has appealed against the ruling.\par \par \uc2 In the weeks leading up to Christmas, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  organized a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/dec/19/amazon-strike-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike}}}\uc2  among Amazon warehouse workers across eight facilities over what the union says were stalled contract negotiations for better pay and working conditions.\par \par \uc2 Last September, Amazon joined companies including \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  that argued the structure of the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  is unconstitutional because its board members cannot be removed by the president. Though a ruling on the case has not been issued, the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/07/court-ruling-trump-firing-cathy-harris-gwynne-wilcox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stayed}}}\uc2  Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s firing of Gwynne Wilcox, a member of the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 , despite being blocked by a lower court.\par \par \uc2 Since Wilcox\u8217\'20\'19s position remains unfilled, the labor board does not have a quorum to rule on labor disputes, meaning it is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/aug/31/trump-labor-watchdog-nlrb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unable to rule}}}\uc2  on major labor disputes.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250908el98005sd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
