\par\par \b \uc2 US union membership declining in \u8216\'20\'18right-to-work\u8217\'20\'19 states, report reveals\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 737 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 September 2025\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Growing divide across US as membership increasing \u8211\'20\'13 and wages higher \u8211\'20\'13 in states that protect workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights\par \par \uc2 Add another growing split to the increasingly divided United States: union membership.\par \par \uc2 US states that protect unions\u8217\'20\'19 collective bargaining rights have experienced an increase in new union members, while states with anti-union \u8220\'20\'1Cright to work\u8221\'20\'1D laws are responsible for declines in union members, a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://illinoisupdate.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/state-of-the-unions-2025-1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report }}}\uc2 reveals.\par \par \uc2 The report on the state of unions by the Illinois Economic Policy Institute and the Project for Middle Class Renewal at the \uc2 University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign\uc2  found significant discrepancies between the 26 states in the US with \u8220\'20\'1Cright to work\u8221\'20\'1D laws compared with the 24 states and Washington DC that protect collective bargaining rights.\par \par \uc2 The right-to-work states, concentrated in the south and central US, have a union density of 5.1%, compared with 14.2% for states with collective bargaining rights, concentrated on the coasts and in the north.\par \par \uc2 Workers in right-to-work states earn about 7% less in wages, accounting for local differences in the cost of living. According to the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest labor federation, states with right-to-work laws {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/issues/right-work"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received}}}\uc2  36% higher discrimination charges from the \uc2 Equal Employment Opportunity Commission\uc2  on average.\par \par \uc2 Right-to-work laws allow workers represented by unions to stop paying dues for the services and benefits they receive through union representation, depleting resources from labor unions. Public sector workers in all 50 states have also had their collective bargaining rights stripped through the imposition of right-to-work laws by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2018 decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/jun/27/supreme-court-unions-fair-share-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Janus v AFSCME.}}}\par \par \uc2 In 2024, states that protect collective bargaining saw an increase of nearly 10,000 union members, compared with the loss of 200,000 union members in states with right-to-work laws.\par \par \uc2 The report analyzed the impact of Illinois\u8217\'20\'19 2022 constitutional amendment that guarantees the right of collective bargaining and bans right-to-work laws. Illinois added 27,000 union members in 2024, increasing its unionization rate to 13.1%. Illinois organized more union members from 2022 through 2024, 18,300 members, than the previous seven years combined, the report states.\par \par \uc2 The report found union members in Illinois are also 8.3% more likely to own homes, 5.2% more likely to have health insurance coverage, and 1 to 4 percentage points less likely to rely on government assistance programs such as Medicaid and Snap food assistance benefits.\par \par \uc2 Similar results were found in Michigan in the wake of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/michigan-becomes-1st-state-in-decades-to-repeal-right-to-work-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repealing }}}\uc2 the state\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cright to work\u8221\'20\'1D law in 2023. Nearly 15,000 union members were added in Michigan from 2023 to 2024.\par \par \uc2 The report comes as the Massachusetts senator Elizabeth Warren and the California representative Brad Sherman have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.warren.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/bon25461.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reintroduced}}}\uc2  the nationwide right to unionize act last week, a bill to invalidate right-to-work laws that weaken unions\u8217\'20\'19 ability to organize workers.\par \par \uc2 Frank Manzo, co-author of the report and an economist at the Illinois Economic Policy Institute, noted that despite the headwinds facing labor unions in terms of the Janus decision, weak labor laws and overwhelmingly opposition to unionization from employers, unions have remained steadfast in states that protect collective bargaining while declining in those that do not.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s all occurring at a time when support for unions remains high and bipartisan, with seven in 10 Americans approving unions, and millions of workers reporting that they would join unions and would organize their workplaces if they could, per surveys,\u8221\'20\'1D said Manzo. \u8220\'20\'1CThe economy does better, workers do better and taxpayers do better when states and the federal government allows and, in fact, encourages workers to collectively bargain.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is very difficult to organize a union, and it is difficult to get a first contract. When the law, the politics and the infrastructure are intentionally designed to disincentivize and to keep, if not outright prevent, workers from having a collective voice, it shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be surprising to see some dilution, some reduction in density,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Robert Bruno, co-author of the report and director of the Project for Middle Class Renewal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe state of the labor movement is not only tied to economic prosperity for working people, but it\u8217\'20\'19s relevant to democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CAttacking a union, attacking the labor movement, is a way to restrain, limit and diminish democracy in society.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250908el98002ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
