\par\par \b \uc2 Revisions and rising unemployment: what to know about the US jobs report\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Aratani in New York \par \uc2 991 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 September 2025\par 19:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 August\u8217\'20\'19s report gave signs of a cooling labor market with negative job numbers for the first time since 2020 \u8211\'20\'13 here\u8217\'20\'19s what we learned\par \par \uc2 A closely watched {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/sep/05/us-jobs-report-august-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  on US jobs released on Friday gave signs of a cooling labor market.\par \par \uc2 The economy added just 22,000 new jobs in August, coming in below expectations, while the unemployment rate ticked slightly up to 4.3%, according to the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 . At the beginning of the year, more than 100,000 jobs were being added each month.\par \par \uc2 Amid \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s trade wars, tariffs have now been put on most foreign goods and prices have started going up. Uncertainty seems to have spooked businesses and this combination of a slowing jobs market and higher inflation paints a murky picture of the US economy.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we learned with Friday\u8217\'20\'19s report:\par \par \uc2 Negative job numbers for the first time since 2020\par \par \uc2 Friday\u8217\'20\'19s job report included revisions to initial reports for June and July. The pace of hiring in June was initially reported as 139,000 jobs added to the economy, but revisions now put the actual figure at -13,000. This is the first time the labor market lost jobs since December 2020, during the massive unemployment seen during the pandemic. July\u8217\'20\'19s numbers were revised up by 6,000, from 73,000 to 79,000.\par \par \uc2 Revisions, a standard part of the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 data collection, became a marked point of tension between the bureau and the White House after the bureau dramatically revised numbers in last month\u8217\'20\'19s report.\par \par \uc2 Initial figures overestimated the number of jobs in May and June by 258,000, which the bureau said was the result of receiving additional reports \u8211\'20\'13 the bureau collects its data by surveying employers \u8211\'20\'13 from businesses and government agencies. With the new revisions released on Friday, total revisions covering May, June and July revised figures down by a combined 279,000 for those three months.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/01/trump-fires-erika-mcentarfer-labor-statistics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired}}}\uc2  the bureau\u8217\'20\'19s commissioner, Erika McEntarfer, after the revision, saying the numbers were \u8220\'20\'1Crigged\u8221\'20\'1D to make him and Republicans look bad. But economists point out that the bureau is made up of career statisticians, many of whom have been with the bureau for many years.\par \par \uc2 Job losses were seen in federal employment and manufacturing\par \par \uc2 The impacts of the \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D are still being felt even though \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  has largely stepped away from his role in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s White House. In August, federal employment went down another 15,000 jobs, bringing the total number of federal job cuts to 97,000 since January.\par \par \uc2 Manufacturing jobs have also taken a hit this year, down 12,000 jobs in August and 78,000 over the last year.\par \par \uc2 Job growths were seen in healthcare and social assistance industries, which saw increases of 31,000 and 16,000 jobs, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Unemployment among Black Americans has jumped\par \par \uc2 In August, the unemployment rate for Black Americans jumped 0.3% over the last month to 7.5% \u8211\'20\'13 over double the unemployment rate for white and Asian Americans, which are just over 3.5%. The unemployment rate for Hispanic Americans was also higher, at 5.3%.\par \par \uc2 Though the overall unemployment rate went up just 0.1% over the last year, the Black unemployment rate jumped 1.4%. The unemployment rate for white and Asian Americans actually went down slightly compared with last year.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a longtime trend that Black Americans are the \u8220\'20\'1Clast hired, first fired\u8221\'20\'1D in an economic downturn, meaning they are the first to feel the impacts of a downturn and the last to recover from one. This was seen during the Great Recession, in which unemployment hit Black and Hispanic Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newamerica.org/pit/reports/unpacking-inequities-unemployment-insurance/last-hired-first-fired-black-latinx-workers-and-the-fight-for-jobs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disproportionately}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  will probably cut interest rates in September\par \par \uc2 Fed officials have been signaling that a rate cut could come at the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s next board meeting on 16 and 17 September, though it probably won\u8217\'20\'19t be a drastic cut. Investors seem to have found hope in last month\u8217\'20\'19s Jackson Hole {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/aug/22/jerome-powell-speech-jackson-hole"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speech}}}\uc2  by the Fed chair, \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , in which he implied that officials would probably ease interest rates amid concern about the labor market.\par \par \uc2 But the Fed cutting rates doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean it sees stability in the economy. Fed officials, including Powell, have raised concerns about higher prices due to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs. It remains unclear if inflation will keep going up, or if there will be a one-time price increase from the tariffs.\par \par \uc2 Powell noted that officials, for now, were more concerned about the labor market, which August\u8217\'20\'19s report confirmed has been experiencing turbulence this summer.\par \par \uc2 White House urges Americans to trust Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plan\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, before Friday\u8217\'20\'19s jobs report release, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/job-market-slumps-trump-administration-says-it-could-take-year-see-better-2025-09-05/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe real numbers\u8221\'20\'1D will be reported next year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe real numbers that I\u8217\'20\'19m talking about are going to be whatever it is, but will be in a year from now,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re going to see job numbers like our country has never seen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When asked about the hiring slump, the national economic council director, \uc2 Kevin Hassett\uc2 , told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/09/05/jobs-hassett-trump-rates.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNBC}}}\uc2  on Friday that \u8220\'20\'1Cyou are seeing that people are being hired\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMembers of my family have been hired,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CBoth of them started their new jobs about a week ago.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hassett called the jobs report \u8220\'20\'1Cdisappointing\u8221\'20\'1D but said that the numbers will eventually go back up.\par \par \uc2 In a separate interview on Friday, the US commerce secretary, \uc2 Howard Lutnick\uc2 , told CNBC that the jobs reports will be better once the administration makes changes to the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ll take out the people who are just trying to create noise against the president,\u8221\'20\'1D Lutnick said. He added that Americans will see \u8220\'20\'1Cthe greatest growth economy \u8230\'20\'26 starting six months from today to a year from today\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250905el95005sd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
