\par\par \b \uc2 US sheriffs decry White House effort to hire away local law enforcement for Ice\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levin in Los Angeles \par \uc2 1,360 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 September 2025\par 13:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 One sheriff calls surprise use of deputy email list offering $50,000 hiring bonus \u8216\'20\'18unprofessional and unethical\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The White House\u8217\'20\'19s aggressive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/sep/02/immigration-hiring-push-trump-private-army"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 push}}}\uc2  to hire federal immigration agents is causing friction with local sheriffs \u8211\'20\'13 even those who back {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s deportation agenda.\par \par \uc2 More than a dozen US sheriffs and law enforcement associations have complained that \uc2 US Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice) has tried to poach local deputies and officers as Ice rapidly expands.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is unprofessional and unethical,\u8221\'20\'1D Grady Judd, the sheriff in Polk county, Florida, told the Guardian last month after his deputies received recruitment emails from Ice.\par \par \uc2 Ice utilized an email list the sheriff had provided as part of his partnership supporting Trump\u8217\'20\'19s deportations; the messages noted recruits could receive a $50,000 hiring bonus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s tantamount to us going to police departments and putting up a recruiting booth in their lobby,\u8221\'20\'1D said Judd, a Republican who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theledger.com/story/news/local/2025/06/21/polk-county-sheriffs-office-has-sent-more-than-200-people-to-ice/84241065007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 authorized his deputies}}}\uc2  to carry out immigration arrests.\par \par \uc2 Judd and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fox13now.com/news/local-news/northern-utah/utah-sheriffs-call-ice-recruitment-of-deputies-classless-as-agency-offers-50-000-signing-bonuses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 other}}}\uc2  sheriffs have spoken out as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  has launched its massive recruitment effort to hire 10,000 new Ice officers and 3,000 border patrol agents, backed by an unprecedented $170bn in funding for immigration enforcement activities.\par \par \uc2 The anger from conservative sheriffs, generally Trump\u8217\'20\'19s close allies, underscores the challenges the White House is facing as it makes deportations and the expansion of Ice a top priority, sometimes at the expense of other law enforcement interests.\par \par \uc2 Federal agents who would normally handle child abuse, money laundering, fraud and other serious crimes have been diverted to immigration enforcement, targeting undocumented people with civil violations, Reuters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/thousands-agents-diverted-trump-immigration-crackdown-2025-03-22/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported in March}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last month, the administration moved to temporarily reassign more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/08/10/us/politics/trump-fbi-patrol-washington.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 100 FBI agents}}}\uc2  to conduct nighttime patrols in Washington DC, even though \uc2 FBI\uc2  officers generally have little experience or training in patrolling or immigration.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wesh.com/article/brevard-county-sheriff-criticizes-ice-recruitment-tactics/65641022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backlash}}}\uc2  from Judd and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theledger.com/story/news/local/2025/08/04/ices-recruitment-emails-to-polk-deputies-draw-grady-judds-wrath/85506309007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 other sheriffs}}}\uc2  in Florida was notable as the state has led the nation in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2025/apr/30/trump-local-police-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 287(g) agreements}}}\uc2 , which empower local law enforcement departments to directly assist Ice. Immigrant rights\u8217\'20\'19 groups have long criticized those partnerships as harmful to public safety, as they make immigrant communities less likely to report crimes or assist police in investigations.\par \par \uc2 Some of the most vocally Trump-supporting sheriffs have criticized Ice\u8217\'20\'19s recruitment. Wayne Ivey, the sheriff in Brevard county, Florida \u8211\'20\'13 who made headlines in June for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/video/florida-sheriff-wayne-ivey-threatens-to-kill-violent-protesters-241538117716"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatening}}}\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kgns.tv/2025/06/13/sheriff-issues-grave-warning-violent-anti-ice-protesters-we-will-kill-you/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hospitalize}}}\uc2  and \u8220\'20\'1Ckill\u8221\'20\'1D anti-Ice protesters \u8211\'20\'13 told WESH 2 News last month that Ice\u8217\'20\'19s targeting of local deputies was \u8220\'20\'1Cbackhanded\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cfrustrated every sheriff\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Judd said his department was paying for deputies to be trained as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.orlandosentinel.com/2025/07/28/ice-training-opens-door-to-central-florida-deputies-handling-immigration-arrests/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigration officers}}}\uc2 , allowing them to arrest and jail undocumented people for Ice. That arrangement gave Ice access to his deputies\u8217\'20\'19 contact information.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou took government documents that we filled out to help you, to recruit our people that we trained on our dime to support you. That\u8217\'20\'19s low-rent,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen that before.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Recruitment emails to sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s deputies were signed by Madison Sheahan, Ice\u8217\'20\'19s deputy director, who previously served as an aide to \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , homeland security secretary, when Noem was South Dakota governor, \uc2 ABC News{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/ice-recruitment-efforts-upset-local-law-enforcement-leaders/story?id=124259508"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 . Sheahan, 28, has no prior immigration enforcement experience and has alienated career officials within Ice, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2025/08/ice-recruitment-immigration-enforcement-billions/684000/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent Atlantic story}}}\uc2  delving into internal conflicts at the agency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs someone who is currently supporting Ice through the 287(g) program, you understand the unique responsibility we carry in protecting our communities and upholding federal law,\u8221\'20\'1D Sheahan\u8217\'20\'19s recruitment email said. \u8220\'20\'1CIce is actively recruiting officers like you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Judd said Ice representatives in Florida weren\u8217\'20\'19t involved in the recruitment and had apologized. He blamed Sheahan, saying she and her DC colleagues did not acknowledge the misstep: \u8220\'20\'1CThey doubled down. They didn\u8217\'20\'19t apologize. They didn\u8217\'20\'19t say it was bad form. That made me even more angry. It just shows her lack of maturity,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe illustration to me is they\u8217\'20\'19re probably sneaky and underhanded and not professional with the way they run the rest of the organization.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Still, Judd said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not going to back down on President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mission. We\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to help Ice, because we are professional, unlike the Ice deputy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the first five months of the year, Judd\u8217\'20\'19s office detained more than 200 undocumented people for Ice in the county\u8217\'20\'19s jails, according to the Ledger newspaper.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Sheriffs\u8217\'20\'19 Association\uc2 , which represents sheriffs across the country, also raised concerns about Ice recruitment. The association\u8217\'20\'19s executive director {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scrippsnews.com/politics/the-president/white-house-apologizes-to-sheriffs-over-controversial-ice-recruitment-tactics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  last month it would be hard for local departments to compete with the $50,000 bonus and other incentives, which could burden agencies already struggling with staffing.\par \par \uc2 Judd, however, said he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t concerned about his deputies joining Ice. He said he suspected ongoing anti-Ice protests were hampering recruitment: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a very difficult and dangerous job \u8230\'20\'26 and you\u8217\'20\'19ve got to be comfortable and sure that the community supports you. When people see the way that Ice is being unfairly targeted, even if they want to be in law enforcement, they don\u8217\'20\'19t want to be in that branch.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Scott Shuchart, a former senior Ice official under Biden, who has raised concerns about Trump recruitment spree, said it seemed \u8220\'20\'1Creally disrespectful\u8221\'20\'1D to poach from sheriffs who have invested their own funding to support Ice through 287(g) agreements: \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re already taking sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s deputies who are supposed to be keeping the community safe and instead are helping out Ice. To now do the double whammy of stealing those resources to be fully Ice\u8217\'20\'19s seems like no way to treat a partner.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the \uc2 US Department of Homeland Security\uc2  announced a program to reimburse local law enforcement agencies for the salaries of trained 287(g) officers and said departments would be \u8220\'20\'1Celigible for monetary performance awards based on the successful location of illegal aliens\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Tricia McLaughlin, DHS assistant secretary, said in a statement that Ice was recruiting \u8220\'20\'1Clocal law enforcement, veterans, and our 287(g) partners who have already been trained and have valuable law enforcement experience\u8221\'20\'1D. More than $500m from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/10/trump-bill-august-recess-democrats-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 major budget bill}}}\uc2  would go toward expanding 287(g) partnerships, she added.\par \par \uc2 McLaughlin also said Sheahan, the Ice deputy director, had law enforcement experience from her previous job as secretary of the Louisiana department of wildlife and fisheries, and had been \u8220\'20\'1Cinstrumental in leading negotiations\u8221\'20\'1D for more than 900 287(g) agreements: \u8220\'20\'1CThese attacks on Madison Sheahan\u8217\'20\'19s leadership style have no basis in reality and are rooted in sexism. [She] is a work horse, strong executor, and accountable leader who along with [acting Ice director] Todd Lyons is leading the men and women of Ice law enforcement to achieve the American people\u8217\'20\'19s mandate to target, arrest, and deport criminal illegal aliens.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The effort to recruit sheriffs \u8220\'20\'1Cshows how both cruel and reckless this administration is when it comes to law enforcement\u8221\'20\'1D, added Juan Cuba, executive director of Sheriff Accountability Action, a group that advocates for criminal justice reforms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a complete disregard for one of the biggest issues local law enforcement has, which is recruitment and retention. Those challenges are exacerbated by the administration\u8217\'20\'19s approach, but they don\u8217\'20\'19t care. What they care about is hitting these artificial quotas,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, noting Trump\u8217\'20\'19s demands for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/29/trump-ice-arrest-quota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 3,000 immigration arrests}}}\uc2  a day. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s less about public safety and more about just feeding this mass deportation machine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some sheriffs do {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.miamiherald.com/news/local/immigration/article309313260.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 oppose}}}\uc2  efforts to have their deputies act as immigration officers, because they already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://static1.squarespace.com/static/66b25013ab109f63b831f0f7/t/67e6de733048285411ed6c58/1743183475358/Report_+SHERIFF+OPPOSITION+SHOWS+CRACKS+IN+MASS+DEPORTATION+PLAN.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 feel stretched thin}}}\uc2  or are concerned about eroding public trust, Cuba noted. But publicly objecting can carry consequences, he said, noting that after Broward county\u8217\'20\'19s sheriff {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.local10.com/news/local/2025/06/05/broward-sheriff-says-bso-wont-be-involved-in-any-ice-raids/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he didn\u8217\'20\'19t want deputies arresting people for civil immigration violations, Florida\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://floridaphoenix.com/2025/06/09/broward-county-sheriff-doesnt-want-to-focus-on-immigration-crackdown-uthmeier-says-he-must/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened}}}\uc2  to take steps to have him removed from office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe see silence from police chiefs and sheriffs because of political threats,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is very alarming that public officials feel like they can\u8217\'20\'19t raise concerns.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250904el94003eb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
