\par\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18He\u8217\'20\'19s brazenly anti-worker\u8217\'20\'19: US marks the first Labor Day under Trump 2.0\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 1,753 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 September 2025\par 11:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Advocates say Trump has hurt workers in many ways, often by cutting their pay or making their jobs more dangerous\par \par \uc2 For this Labor Day, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump administration}}}\uc2  has draped an enormous banner outside the US labor department with his portrait and the words \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican Workers First.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump was elected on promises, since repeatedly pledged, that he would fight for workers and forgotten Americans. But many labor advocates say that Trump has consistently put corporate interests first in his second term as he has taken dozens of actions that hurt workers, often by cutting their pay or making their jobs more dangerous.\par \par \uc2 Despite his vow to help coal miners, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kffhealthnews.org/news/article/black-lung-coal-miners-silica-dust-federal-rule-rollback-enforcement-trump-staff-cuts-niosh-msha/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 halted enforcement of a regulation}}}\uc2  that protects miners from a debilitating, often deadly lung disease. He fired the chair of the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ), leaving the US\u8217\'20\'19s top labor watchdog without a quorum to protect workers from corporations\u8217\'20\'19 illegal anti-union tactics. Angering labor leaders, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/22/trump-federal-workers-union-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stripped one million federal workers}}}\uc2  of their right to bargain collectively and tore up their union contracts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a big betrayal,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Liz Shuler\uc2 , president of the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , the main US labor federation, said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe knew it would be bad, but we had no idea how rapidly he would be doing these things. He is stripping away regulations that protect workers. His attacks on unions are coming fast and furious. He talks a good game of being for working people, but he\u8217\'20\'19s doing the absolute opposite.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a government that is by, and for, the CEOs and billionaires,\u8221\'20\'1D Shuler added.\par \par \uc2 Trump has hurt construction workers by shutting down major wind turbine projects and ending Biden-era subsidies that encourage the construction of factories {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/power-switch/2025/07/08/trump-moves-fast-to-kill-green-energy-tax-breaks-00442256"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that make renewable-energy products}}}\uc2 . In moves that will harm some of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most vulnerable workers, the Trump administration has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/the-trump-administration-is-quietly-gutting-minimum-wage-protections-for-millions-of-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed ending minimum wage and overtime protections}}}\uc2  for 3.7 million home-care and domestic workers. It has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.disabilityscoop.com/2025/07/10/trump-administration-squashes-plan-to-end-subminimum-wage-employment-of-people-with-disabilities/31529/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed a Biden plan to prevent}}}\uc2  employers from paying disabled workers less than the $7.25-an-hour federal minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a huge disconnect between Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pro-worker rhetoric and the policies he\u8217\'20\'19s putting in place. The gulf is enormous,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Heidi Shierholz\uc2 , president of the \uc2 Economic Policy Institute\uc2 , a progressive thinktank. \u8220\'20\'1CIn his second term, he\u8217\'20\'19s been absolutely, brazenly anti-worker.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI keep thinking about his taking away the Biden-era increase in the minimum wage for federal contractors. It\u8217\'20\'19s unbelievably brazen,\u8221\'20\'1D Shierholz continued. ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/government/trump-nixes-1775-minimum-wage-federal-contractors-adopted-by-biden-2025-03-20/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump ended the requirement}}}\uc2  that federal contractors pay their workers at least $17.75 an hour.) \u8220\'20\'1CThe minimum wage is incredibly popular. He just took away the minimum wage from hundreds of thousands of workers. That blew my mind.\u8221\'20\'1D As a result, many full-time workers will see their pay drop {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/the-trump-administration-is-quietly-gutting-minimum-wage-protections-for-millions-of-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by more than $9,200 a year}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The administration disputes all these criticisms. \u8220\'20\'1CThe American worker has been left behind by the Democrat party for years, but President Trump has championed an agenda that puts the American worker first,\u8221\'20\'1D said Taylor Rogers, White House assistant press secretary.\par \par \uc2 Trump has \u8220\'20\'1Cunleashed an economic boom\u8221\'20\'1D, she said. Inflation is cooling, native-born Americans are benefiting from private-sector job gains and blue-collar wages are rising fast. \u8220\'20\'1CUnder President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s leadership, Republicans are once again the party of the American worker,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rogers.\par \par \uc2 Many labor experts say Trump is even more anti-union than \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 , often called the most anti-union president of modern times. Reagan fired 11,345 air traffic controllers who went on strike, but the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Shuler said that \u8220\'20\'1Cpales in comparison\u8221\'20\'1D to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ending collective bargaining for 1 million federal workers. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s the largest single act of union-busting in our history,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe is worse than Reagan when it comes to his approach to unions,\u8221\'20\'1D said Julie Su, who was acting labor secretary under Biden. \u8220\'20\'1CWe saw what Reagan did in the 1980s. That began a long decline in unionization. This president wants to make America non-union again. He\u8217\'20\'19s certainly trying to make the government non-union again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shierholz said the \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolute scale of crushing unions\u8221\'20\'1D under Trump is \u8220\'20\'1Con a whole different scale from what we saw under Reagan. Trump is saying it\u8217\'20\'19s absolutely open season on union folks. He took an absolute chainsaw to the federal workforce. He\u8217\'20\'19s giving the green light to the private sector and local government to do the same.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Justin Chen, president of an \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees\uc2  council representing 8,000 \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  (\uc2 EPA\uc2 ) workers across the US, is angry that Trump halted collective bargaining for \uc2 EPA\uc2  employees, voided most of their union contracts and fired probationary workers. \u8220\'20\'1CWhatever he said about fighting for workers was a complete lie,\u8221\'20\'1D Chen said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe treats federal employees with a great deal of disdain, not as civil servants valuable to make our government and economy run.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many labor advocates say Trump\u8217\'20\'19s signature policies, including tariffs and deportations, are hurting US workers. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs are pushing up prices and slowing economic growth, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.investopedia.com/economists-pan-trump-economic-agenda-11796051"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 economists say}}}\uc2 . Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbig, beautiful\u8221\'20\'1D tax cut will harm millions of working families by cutting food assistance and causing many to lose health coverage. As for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s deportation campaign, many workers say it\u8217\'20\'19s undermining their employers\u8217\'20\'19 businesses and forcing them to work harder because they have to do the work of their departed co-workers.\par \par \uc2 In her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/live/r4kDzpyVIKI?t=147s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 annual State of the Unions address}}}\uc2 , \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  president Shuler said on Wednesday: \u8220\'20\'1CThe state of working people in this country is they\u8217\'20\'19re under attack.\u8221\'20\'1D She added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe want cheaper groceries, and we get tanks on our streets. We want more affordable healthcare, and we get 16 million Americans about to be kicked off their coverage.\u8221\'20\'1D Shuler said unions will hold {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/29/workers-over-billionaires-trump-protest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 close to 1,000 rallies}}}\uc2  and other events this Labor Day across the US to kick off a year of mobilization.\par \par \uc2 Jenny Smith, a home-care worker in Champaign, Illinois, said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plan to end overtime and minimum-wage protections for home-care workers shows contempt for struggling, low-wage workers. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump doesn\u8217\'20\'19t know what it means to go to work day after day to earn a living,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you take away these wage protections, it will take money out of these workers\u8217\'20\'19 pockets. The majority of these workers are Black, brown and single mothers. You\u8217\'20\'19re taking from their children\u8217\'20\'19s mouths.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Smith voiced dismay that Trump hasn\u8217\'20\'19t made good on his promise to reduce prices. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very disappointed that prices aren\u8217\'20\'19t going down,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI just bought a dozen eggs for $6.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think he cares about us, but he does care about the billionaires.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has taken numerous steps that will weaken safety protections for workers. He is cutting staffing by 12% at the \uc2 Occupational Safety and Health Administration (Osha)\uc2 . His administration has proposed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.livenowfox.com/news/trump-labor-deregulation-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminating a requirement for adequate lighting}}}\uc2  on construction sites. It is reducing the fines that small businesses pay for violating safety rules. It has proposed blocking the government\u8217\'20\'19s mine-safety district managers from ordering upgrades in mine ventilation and safety. It has slowed action on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s effort to protect workers from high temperatures.\par \par \uc2 Trump also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kffhealthnews.org/news/article/black-lung-coal-miners-silica-dust-federal-rule-rollback-enforcement-trump-staff-cuts-niosh-msha/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 froze enforcement of a Biden-era regulation}}}\uc2  that protects miners from silicosis, a serious lung disease.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSilicosis has become a major killer among coal miners, but the Trump administration is trying to make silicosis great again,\u8221\'20\'1D said David Michaels, a professor of public health at \uc2 George Washington University\uc2  who headed Osha under \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe Trump administration has taken several steps that are devastating to the safety and health of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s workers. Osha, which is under-resourced and underpowered, has become significantly smaller as a result of the Trump and Doge [Trump\u8217\'20\'19s unofficial \u8216\'20\'18department of government efficiency\u8217\'20\'19] cuts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Michaels warned that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s cuts to Osha penalties will reduce incentives for companies to ensure safe conditions.\par \par \uc2 Administration officials point to the Trump-backed \u8220\'20\'1Cno tax on tips\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cno tax on overtime\u8221\'20\'1D as clearly pro-worker. But Yale\u8217\'20\'19s Budget Lab notes that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://budgetlab.yale.edu/news/240624/no-tax-tips-act-background-tipped-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only 4% of workers}}}\uc2  in the bottom half by income are in tipped jobs, while almost 40% of tipped workers earn so little they don\u8217\'20\'19t pay federal income taxes.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, the no-tax-on-overtime provision will reduce income taxes far less than most workers realize. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wthr.com/article/money/whats-the-deal/the-no-tax-on-overtime-law-comes-with-limits-one-big-beautiful-bill-act-why-income-hourly-wages-filing-time-how-much/531-bd0fd219-2736-4e68-85d3-eb78f82c4ff7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The deduction applies only to the \u8220\'20\'1Chalf\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  in \u8220\'20\'1Ctime-and-a-half\u8221\'20\'1D overtime pay. If a worker earns $20 an hour and their overtime rate is $30, that worker can deduct only the $10 premium for each overtime hour, not the full $30.\par \par \uc2 Shierholz said that if Trump were serious about helping workers, \u8220\'20\'1Che would raise the minimum wage, make overtime pay double pay and do away with the sub-minimum wage for tipped workers. That would truly help workers, but that\u8217\'20\'19s not what he\u8217\'20\'19s doing. He\u8217\'20\'19s doing as little as possible to help workers, while helping employers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While Trump says his deportations will create job opportunities for US-born workers, Shierholz\u8217\'20\'19s economic institute forecasts that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s effort to deport 1 million immigrants a year will result {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/trumps-deportation-agenda-will-destroy-millions-of-jobs-both-immigrants-and-u-s-born-workers-would-suffer-job-losses-particularly-in-construction-and-child-care/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in 5.9m lost jobs after four years}}}\uc2 : 3.3 million fewer employed immigrants and 2.6 million fewer employed US-born workers. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you don\u8217\'20\'19t have immigrant roofers and framers, you\u8217\'20\'19re not building houses, and that means electricians and plumbers lose their jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D Shierholz said. \u8220\'20\'1CPlus, you lose the consumer spending from those workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Corey Mahoney, a 35-year-old cargo handler at John F Kennedy international airport in New York, said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies have whipsawed workers at his warehouse. \u8220\'20\'1CThe tariff situation has slowed down work, and many people lost their jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. When Trump ended protected status for many Venezuelans and other immigrants, some of his Venezuelan co-workers left or were deported. \u8220\'20\'1CSome of the people I was working with tried to come to work, but they weren\u8217\'20\'19t allowed,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe were left with less people, and we had to work twice as hard. It\u8217\'20\'19s unfair.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is in an alternative universe thinking everything is good,\u8221\'20\'1D Mahoney said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe doesn\u8217\'20\'19t realize that normal people who are just trying to make a living aren\u8217\'20\'19t happy with what he\u8217\'20\'19s doing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250901el91002ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
