\par\par \b \uc2 More than 500 workers at Voice of America and other broadcasters to be laid off\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang and agencies \par \uc2 952 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 August 2025\par 12:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Acting CEO of parent agency makes announcement one day after judge blocks her from firing \uc2 VOA\uc2  director\par \par \uc2 The agency that oversees Voice of America and other government-funded international broadcasters is eliminating jobs for more than 500 employees, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  official said. The move could ratchet up a months-long legal challenge over the news outlets\u8217\'20\'19 fate.\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake, acting CEO of the US Agency for Global Media, announced the latest round of job cuts late Friday, one day after a federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.278809/gov.uscourts.dcd.278809.76.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked her}}}\uc2  from removing Michael Abramowitz as \uc2 VOA\uc2  director.\par \par \uc2 US district judge Royce Lamberth {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.278809/gov.uscourts.dcd.278809.72.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had ruled separately}}}\uc2  that the Republican administration had failed to show how it was complying with his orders to restore \uc2 VOA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s operations. His order Monday gave the administration \u8220\'20\'1Cone final opportunity, short of a contempt trial\u8221\'20\'1D to demonstrate its compliance. He ordered Lake to sit for a deposition by lawyers for agency employees by 15 September.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Lamberth said Abramowitz could not be removed without the approval of the majority of the International Broadcasting Advisory Board. Firing Abramowitz would be \u8220\'20\'1Cplainly contrary to law\u8221\'20\'1D, according to Lamberth, who was nominated to the bench by \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lake posted a statement on social media that said her agency had initiated a reduction in force, or RIF, eliminating 532 jobs for full-time government employees. She said the agency \u8220\'20\'1Cwill continue to fulfill its statutory mission after this RIF\u8211\'20\'13 and will likely improve its ability to function\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI look forward to taking additional steps in the coming months to improve the functioning of a very broken agency and make sure America\u8217\'20\'19s voice is heard abroad where it matters most,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote.\par \par \uc2 A group of agency employees who sued to block \uc2 VOA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s elimination said Lake\u8217\'20\'19s move would give their colleagues 30 days until their pay and benefits end.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe find Lake\u8217\'20\'19s continued attacks on our agency abhorrent,\u8221\'20\'1D they said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are looking forward to her deposition to hear whether her plan to dismantle \uc2 VOA\uc2  was done with the rigorous review process that Congress requires. So far we have not seen any evidence of that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe will continue to fight for what we believe to be our rights under the law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In June, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/voice-of-america-layoffs-trump-global-media-7a862bdc530dd3d48657c00d2df54539"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 layoff notices}}}\uc2  were sent to more than 600 agency employees. Abramowitz was placed on administrative leave along with almost the entire \uc2 VOA\uc2  staff. He was told he would be fired effective 31 August.\par \par \uc2 The administration said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.279211/gov.uscourts.dcd.279211.141.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court filing}}}\uc2  Thursday that it planned to send RIF notices to 486 employees of \uc2 VOA\uc2  and 46 other agency employees but intended to retain 158 agency employees and 108 \uc2 VOA\uc2  employees. The filing said the global media agency had 137 \u8220\'20\'1Cactive employees\u8221\'20\'1D and 62 other employees on administrative leave while \uc2 VOA\uc2  had 86 active employees and 512 others on administrative leave.\par \par \uc2 The agency also houses \uc2 Radio Free Europe/Radio Liberty\uc2 , \uc2 Radio Free Asia\uc2 , \uc2 Middle East Broadcasting Networks\uc2  and Radio Mart\u237\'00\'ED, which beams Spanish-language news into Cuba. The networks, which together reach an estimated 427 million people, date to the cold war and are part of a network of government-funded organizations trying to extend US influence and combat authoritarianism.\par \par \uc2 In March, Abramowitz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/voa-cuts-trump-director-michael-abramowitz-interview/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to dismantle the \uc2 VOA\uc2  would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cself-inflicted blow\u8221\'20\'1D to American national security, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CIf America pulls off the playing field and cedes it to our adversaries, then they\u8217\'20\'19re going to be telling the narratives that people around the world are going to be hearing, and that can\u8217\'20\'19t be good for America \u8230\'20\'26 They\u8217\'20\'19re going to be hearing an anti-America narrative. We need to fight that with truth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/20/alaska-radio-ksdp-trump-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Rural America costs a lot of money\u8217\'20\'19: Trump cuts are decimating a radio station at the edge of the world}}}\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe major challenge for the United States in general is this global information war in which countries like China and Russia are essentially really having our lunch. \u8230\'20\'26 So, I really feel that we need an organization that is accurate, unbiased, objective, and that tells the truth about America to the rest of the world in the languages that they understand.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This week, Trump also moved to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/08/29/us/politics/trump-federal-workers-union-protections.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remove union protections}}}\uc2  from a handful of federal employees, including those from the \uc2 VOA\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afscme.org/press/releases/2025/afscmes-saunders-stripping-voice-of-america-workers-of-their-union-is-a-clear-act-of-retaliation-but-we-will-not-back-down"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In response}}}\uc2 , the \uc2 American Federation of State, County and Municipal Employees\uc2 , the nation\u8217\'20\'19s largest trade union of public employees, said: \u8220\'20\'1CAFSCME members who fulfill the Congressionally mandated mission to broadcast Voice of America around the globe shine the beacon of freedom on the most oppressive of regimes. Now, because they have been fighting to keep Voice of America\u8217\'20\'19s mission alive, their own voice on the job has been stripped from them. \uc2 AFSCME\uc2  will fight this illegal action in court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, foreign staff at US-backed media outlets voiced concerns over their safety following Trump\u8217\'20\'19s shuttering of the global media agencies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/24/trump-shuttering-global-media-agency-endangers-reporters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Speaking to}}}\uc2  the Guardian in March, Jaewoo Park, a journalist for \uc2 Radio Free Asia\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have many co-workers in different services, several of whom came here and sought asylum visas. If their own government knew they worked for \uc2 RFA\uc2  [\uc2 Radio Free Asia\uc2 ] and they went back to their own country, their lives would be at risk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAuthoritarian governments have praised what Trump is doing right now \u8230\'20\'26 In Burma, Vietnam, Laos, Cambodia, there were people who fought for freedom and democracy, and they came to work at \uc2 RFA\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s very risky for them. Their lives are in danger if \uc2 Radio Free Asia\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t exist,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250831el8v0008i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
