\par\par \b \uc2 Nearly 1,000 \u8216\'20\'18worker over billionaire\u8217\'20\'19 actions planned for Labor Day in US\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 675 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 August 2025\par 11:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Rallies from Alaska to Hawaii will highlight cuts to wages, unions and social safety nets under Trump policies\par \par \uc2 Nearly 1,000 \u8220\'20\'1Cworker over billionaire\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://workerslaborday.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protests}}}\uc2  are being planned in all 50 states starting this weekend as part of a Labor Day week of action organized by labor unions and advocacy groups in opposition to the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s policies.\par \par \uc2 The actions include marches and rallies in cities such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/chicago-labor-day-rally-march-workers-over-billionaires/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chicago}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mobilize.us/aflcio/event/834688/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles}}}\uc2 , a Labor Day parade in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mobilize.us/aflcio/event/793169/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York City}}}\uc2 , rallies in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mobilize.us/aflcio/event/834949/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Palmer, Alaska}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mobilize.us/aflcio/event/831978/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Freeport, Maine}}}\uc2 , and a planned protest at the state capitol in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mobilize.us/aflcio/event/823900/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Honolulu}}}\uc2 , Hawaii.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/protest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protests}}}\uc2  are organized by the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , the largest federation of labor unions in the US, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://maydaystrong.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dozens}}}\uc2  of partner organizations, including \uc2 Public Citizen\uc2 , Indivisible, Democracy Forward, MoveOn and Patriotic Millionaires.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is about organic, grassroots organizing, and we intentionally wanted it to be outside of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/washington-dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington DC}}}\uc2 , because that\u8217\'20\'19s where the impacts are being felt,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Liz Shuler\uc2 , president of the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhether it\u8217\'20\'19s teachers or nurses or construction workers, they\u8217\'20\'19re all determined to stand up and fight back, because they\u8217\'20\'19re experiencing the cuts, they\u8217\'20\'19re experiencing the change in policies, they\u8217\'20\'19re experiencing the attacks of this White House on their unions, and so they\u8217\'20\'19re determined to make their voices heard and mobilize to fight forward regardless of what\u8217\'20\'19s happening around us, no matter the obstacles.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Among the policies being protested are the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  attempts to rescind {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/22/trump-federal-workers-union-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collective bargaining rights}}}\uc2  from 1 million federal workers, the largest single act of union busting in US history, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/trump-just-cut-the-minimum-wage-for-hundreds-of-thousands-of-private-sector-workers/?utm_medium=email&_hsenc=p2ANqtz---qKwsfLezXi3TyNtJnb8iowCtCgFb62tlFk7YqPa2mIS0u2wqridSBFxzEEczrbjbhEh8jdQnU2jvHWlO8ct-Gmb3IMpfsuyBBLxB-FmRqZA-F8Y&_hsmi=377805378&utm_content=377805378&utm_source=hs_email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut }}}\uc2 to minimum wage requirements for federal contractors from $17.75 an hour to $13.30 an hour, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/the-trump-administration-is-quietly-gutting-minimum-wage-protections-for-millions-of-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed rule }}}\uc2 to eliminate federal minimum wage and overtime protections for 3.7 million childcare and home care workers, and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.disabilityscoop.com/2025/07/10/trump-administration-squashes-plan-to-end-subminimum-wage-employment-of-people-with-disabilities/31529/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rescission}}}\uc2  of a minimum wage requirement for disabled workers.\par \par \uc2 The actions come as public support for labor unions remains strong. A national {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/sites/default/files/2025-08/DBR%20AFL-CIO%20Labor%20Day%20Survey%20Summary.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll }}}\uc2 conducted by the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  and David Binder Research found trust in labor unions is at 55% \u8211\'20\'13 larger than the 36% of respondents who said they trusted the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic party}}}\uc2  and the 35% of respondents who said they trusted the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican party}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are waking up to the fact we don\u8217\'20\'19t have to just sit back and take it and the labor movement is the place to go to channel that activism, to build what\u8217\'20\'19s next and we\u8217\'20\'19re putting forward a vision for what the economy can be,\u8221\'20\'1D added Shuler.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen people see tanks rolling into Washington DC, when we were promised lower costs, they\u8217\'20\'19re like, this makes no sense,\u8221\'20\'1D said Shuler. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re getting billionaires standing up at the front row of the inauguration, basically taking over agencies, our economy and our country. So I think that no matter what party you belong to, that is a unifying thing that everybody wants, the freedom, fairness and security that all working people deserve.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe billionaire agenda, the corruption we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing, is changing the way government is functioning. It\u8217\'20\'19s leading to real-time and impactful ramifications for regular people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lisa Gilbert, co-president of \uc2 Public Citizen\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe gutting of Medicaid, all the firings we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen of federal workers, the ravaging of families through Ice raids. It\u8217\'20\'19s just all coming together to cause people to stand up and say, \u8216\'20\'18we are the people of this country. It is workers over billionaires.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gilbert noted they currently have 984 events scheduled, with the aim to reach over 1,000 by Labor Day, a mass organizing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.citizen.org/news/workers-over-billionaires-labor-day-events-climb-to-500-across-all-50-states/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 effort}}}\uc2  that has been weeks in the making.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been standing together over and over again to talk about the authoritarian slide that this administration is ushering in in our country. We expect a lot of energy this weekend. This is really just the beginning of an ongoing fight against what\u8217\'20\'19s being taken away from regular people,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250829el8t002uw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
