\par\par \b \uc2 The Guardian view on Russia\u8217\'20\'19s strike on Kyiv: Putin is testing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s will and Europe\u8217\'20\'19s resolve\b0\par\par\uc2 Editorial \par \uc2 606 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 August 2025\par 22:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Kremlin sent a clear message with its lethal overnight raid on the Ukrainian capital. Will the US heed it?\par \par \uc2 Wednesday night brought a grim return to Russia\u8217\'20\'19s form: one of the heaviest air raids on Kyiv since the full-scale invasion began. Moscow eased off its strikes on major cities in the run-up to the Alaska summit, and it held off its attack on the Ukrainian capital until Keith Kellogg, the US special envoy, had finished his visit there. But within hours of his departure, at least 18 people, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/aug/28/russia-launches-kyiv-attack-ukraine-capital-deaths-injuries"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including several children}}}\uc2 , were dead in an attack on a residential block, and the \uc2 European Union\uc2  mission had been severely damaged.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  periodically suggests that he is drawing a line for \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 . Yet each time he appears toset a limit, the Russian president breezes through it. The Kyiv attack shows that it is MrPutin who is testing the US president. Mr Trump threatened \u8220\'20\'1Csevereconsequences\u8221\'20\'1D if Moscow did not immediately agree to a ceasefire \u8211\'20\'13 but in Anchorage was quickly persuaded by Mr Putin that there was no need for one prior to a peace deal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think in many ways he\u8217\'20\'19s there,\u8221\'20\'1D Mr Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/donald-trump-putin-zelensky-russia-ukraine-ceasefire-war-2119703"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters}}}\uc2  on Tuesday. But Russia\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brookings.edu/articles/beyond-the-alaska-summit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 diplomatic stalling}}}\uc2 , allowing it to continue to grind away on the battlefield, is transparent. The lethal strike on civilians in Kyiv shows exactly what it thinks of peace talks. As Mr Trump also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/International/trump-angry-putin-ukraine-strikes-continue-despite-peace/story?id=124977411"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remarked}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CEvery conversation I have with [Mr Putin] is a good conversation. And then unfortunately, a bomb is loaded up into Kyiv or someplace, and then I get very angry about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US president appears unable to draw the obvious conclusion, and his anger has yet to convert into action. He continues to cast blame on VolodymyrZelenskyy (\u8220\'20\'1Cnot exactly innocent either\u8221\'20\'1D) for Russia\u8217\'20\'19s unprovoked invasion. Mr Trump floated the idea of sanctions again, but only when pressed. His one concrete move \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/27/trump-tariff-india-russian-oil-purchase"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doubling the tariff on most Indian goods to 50%}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 was billed as punishment for NewDelhi\u8217\'20\'19s Russian oil imports.\par \par \uc2 In fact, those imports had been quietly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/exclusive-india-can-buy-much-russian-oil-it-wants-outside-price-cap-yellen-says-2022-11-11/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 encouraged}}}\uc2  by Washington to steady world markets, and European countries have bought oil from India once it has been refined. The real trigger was India\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/new-atlanticist/the-trump-administration-needs-a-strategic-reset-with-india/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refusal}}}\uc2  to scrap farm protections, an issue for Mr Trump\u8217\'20\'19s base. This was domestic politics rebadged as Russia policy, and a headache for NewDelhi, not for Moscow.\par \par \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , the president of the \uc2 European Commission\uc2 , accused Moscow of targeting the EU in its Wednesday night strike. That\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely to worry the White House. European leaders know that their ability to shape its worldview is restricted and intermittent. The result may last only until Mr Trump\u8217\'20\'19s next conversation, or next glimpse of a talking head on Fox News.\par \par \uc2 They continue to make maximal efforts and compromises for limitedreturns. The US has reportedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/gabbard-barred-sharing-intelligence-russia-ukraine-negotiations-five-eyes-partners/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stopped sharing information}}}\uc2  on any potential Ukraine-Russia deal even with the members of the anglophoneFiveEyes intelligence-sharingcommunity.\par \par \uc2 Given that, European governments are unlikely toget carried away by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/66ec25a0-4af8-467f-9fbe-cf42de890a7e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported willingness}}}\uc2  oftheUS to contribute intelligence and air supporttoa postwar force in Ukraine. Whether the posited reassurance force will actually materialise, and if so in what form, remains to be seen. But in theabsence of the ceasefire that would have to precede it, Europe must make clear that it will not waver in its support for Kyiv. In probing Mr Trump\u8217\'20\'19s intentions, Mr Putin is also probing Europe\u8217\'20\'19s resolve.It cannot afford to fail this test.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250828el8s004ez\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
