\par\par \b \uc2 Greater risk of toxic derailments if $85bn railroad merger is approved, warn unions\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,148 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 August 2025\par 14:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers sound alarm over proposed \uc2 Union Pacific\uc2  and \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2  deal and its risks to jobs, prices and power\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/29/union-pacific-norfolk-southern-railroad-merger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed mega-merger}}}\uc2  of two of the largest railroad companies in the US will hurt jobs, raise costs for consumers and increase the risk of more catastrophic train crashes, according to workers and unions.\par \par \uc2 Union Pacific\uc2  proposed a $85bn deal to buy \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2  last month, which would create the first transcontinental railroad network in the US.\par \par \uc2 As executives at \uc2 Union Pacific\uc2  seek approval from federal regulators the \uc2 Surface Transportation Board\uc2 , union leaders warn the deal heightens fears around safety \u8211\'20\'13 two years after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/23/norfolk-southern-settlement-east-palestine-ohio-derailment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 derailment}}}\uc2  of a \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2  train in East Palestine, Ohio, resulted in the release of plumes of toxic chemicals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe entirety of the workers\u8221\'20\'1D is against the merger, claimed \uc2 John Samuelsen\uc2 , the president of the Transport Workers Union. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re hoping that the stakeholders in DC that are making determinations are going to listen and understand that when something like East Palestine happens, the chances of that happening under a mammothly merged new entity become greater and greater,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnything that empowers the freight rail carriers makes them more profitable and just increases the levels of power that they can press is dangerous for workers, and actually dangerous for everybody,\u8221\'20\'1D Samuelsen added. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re already an incredibly difficult employer to deal with. And if they\u8217\'20\'19re twice as big, they\u8217\'20\'19ll be twice as difficult to deal with, and they\u8217\'20\'19re going to move to reduce headcount.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The two firms expect their merger to create an \u8220\'20\'1Cannualized synergy opportunity\u8221\'20\'1D worth $2.75bn. Samuelsen said such savings could not be achieved without reducing the workforce, a longstanding issue in the railroad industry.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have had nothing but bad experiences running the TWU in dealing with freight rail. They appear to be unchanged from the infamous rail bosses of the 1880s,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/11/books/review/iron-empires-michael-hiltzik.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 railroad tycoons}}}\uc2 , dubbed robber barons during the Gilded Age due to their business practices, amassed immense wealth and power through control of the railroad industry. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re extremely powerful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Smart Transportation Division, the largest rail labor organization in the US, has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.smart-union.org/statement-from-smart-td-on-the-proposed-union-pacific-and-norfolk-southern-merger/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposed}}}\uc2  the merger over \uc2 Union Pacific\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s safety record and labor practices.\par \par \uc2 Since the East Palestine derailment, a railroad safety bill has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/senate-bill/576/all-info"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stalled}}}\uc2  in Congress, despite JD Vance supporting it as a US senator, and the Trump administration has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pymnts.com/cpi-posts/trump-administration-clears-63-billion-in-mergers-marking-sharp-shift-from-biden-era-antitrust-policy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already demonstrated}}}\uc2  a strikingly more lax approach toward approving corporate mergers compared with the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 Six class I railroads currently control the majority of the rail network in the US: \uc2 BNSF Railway\uc2 , Union Pacific, \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2 , \uc2 CSX\uc2 , \uc2 Canadian National Railway\uc2  and CPKC, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://investor.cpkcr.com/news/press-release-details/2023/Canadian-Pacific-and-Kansas-City-Southern-combine-to-create-CPKC/default.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 merged}}}\uc2  from two separate railroad companies in 2023. The number of class I railroads in the US has dwindled from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cato.org/regulation/spring-2023/understanding-railroads-unions-fight"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 39}}}\uc2  in 1980.\par \par \uc2 Nick Wurst, the general secretary of Railroad Workers United and a railroad freight conductor in Massachusetts, expressed concern with the power a merger of two class I railroad firms would yield to an already powerful industry \u8211\'20\'13 and prompt executives to try to \u8220\'20\'1Ctrim the fat\u8221\'20\'1D in their workforces.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to let them massively expand their negotiating power, not just with the shippers, with the customers, but also it\u8217\'20\'19s going to expand their power in terms of negotiations with workers, and lobbying in Washington,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wurst. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s reasonable to anticipate that there\u8217\'20\'19s going to be sort \u8211\'20\'13 of a hunt for redundancies. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s just going to affect union employees; it\u8217\'20\'19s also going to affect management, too.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The news of a proposed merger has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/union-pacific-norfolk-southern-merger-transcontinental-railroad/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sparked}}}\uc2  concerns that other operators, such as \uc2 BNSF\uc2  and \uc2 CSX\uc2 , would move to merge in response.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I heard about this merger, I was horrified for the simple fact that everything that\u8217\'20\'19s happened in East Palestine points to the fact that these rail carriers have way too much power the way it is,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jeff Kurtz, a retired railroad worker at \uc2 BNSF\uc2  who had served as the legislative and safety director at the \uc2 Brotherhood of Locomotive Engineers and Trainmen\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The merger would make \uc2 Union Pacific\uc2  and \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot more powerful\u8221\'20\'1D, he added, pointing to the 1996 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.trains.com/trn/railroads/history/bnsf-railway-merger-family-tree/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 merger}}}\uc2  between the \uc2 Burlington Northern Railroad\uc2  and the Santa Fe Railway, which formed \uc2 BNSF\uc2 . Benefits in existing union contracts were eliminated if they weren\u8217\'20\'19t included in both, Kurtz recalled, or the lesser benefit was adopted and applied to the merged workforce.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThings will get worse,\u8221\'20\'1D he warned. \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, you\u8217\'20\'19ve got these long trains, blocking crossings, cutting towns in half. Another thing that you might get with this merger is them moving terminals around, and moving people out of these small towns. There\u8217\'20\'19s not going to be a lot of recourse for towns to handle this stuff.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Matt Weaver, a railroad worker, expressed concern that the merger would force workers to travel even further away from home.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow do you raise a family on that? What\u8217\'20\'19s in the land of opportunity? It\u8217\'20\'19s about being a father, being a mother and being there to raise your kids,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CHow can you do that when you\u8217\'20\'19re at this point, it could be 2,000 miles away from home? How are they going to do that? It wears you out to think of the stress on the employee when they expect the same amount of production and they\u8217\'20\'19ve cut since World War One, they\u8217\'20\'19ve cut 95% of rail labor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The class I railroad labor force has declined from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.stb.gov/wp-content/uploads/files/docs/competitionStudy/Volume%201.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 450,000}}}\uc2  in 1980 to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.progressiverailroading.com/rail_industry_trends/news/US-Class-I-employment-dipped-in-March--71760"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 122,000 workers }}}\uc2 in 2024, he noted. \u8220\'20\'1CNone of these mergers have ever been good for the workers,\u8221\'20\'1D said Weaver. \u8220\'20\'1CThat doesn\u8217\'20\'19t serve the people. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t serve the shippers. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t serve the consumer because it drives prices up. We\u8217\'20\'19re playing Monopoly here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Seven industry groups {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/c948bbb5-3ed0-4886-b8e6-646f63bb98ba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 representing}}}\uc2  shippers, including the National Industrial Transportation League, the \uc2 American Chemistry Council\uc2 , and the Freight Rail Customer Alliance have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freightwaves.com/news/shippers-line-up-against-railroad-mergers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposed}}}\uc2  any further railroad mergers, claiming the companies already have too much market power.\par \par \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2  deferred comment to \uc2 Union Pacific\uc2 . A spokesperson for \uc2 Union Pacific\uc2  declined to comment but referred to claims on the company\u8217\'20\'19s website that the merger would be \u8220\'20\'1Ca win\u8221\'20\'1D for the US economy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a win for our customers; it\u8217\'20\'19s a win for the workforce and it\u8217\'20\'19s a win for shareholders,\u8221\'20\'1D the firm has argued. \u8220\'20\'1CThis combination will transform the US supply chain, unleash the industrial strength of American manufacturing and create new sources of economic growth, safe, resilient communities and workforce opportunity that preserves union jobs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They also noted that Transload Group, a rail transloading and logistic service provider that has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://norfolksouthern.mediaroom.com/2024-04-02-Norfolk-Southern-to-purchase-Chicago-transload-and-warehouse-facility"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously partnered}}}\uc2  with \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2 , expressed support for the deal.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250825el8p002e5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
