\par\par \b \uc2 White House cancels union contracts for hundreds of thousands of federal workers\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,037 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 August 2025\par 22:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Government workers are \u8216\'20\'18canary in coalmine\u8217\'20\'19 for Trump bid to gut union rights, leaders warn\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has unilaterally stripped hundreds of thousands of federal workers of their union contracts after a federal appeals court overruled an injunction which halted the plans. It is just getting started, according to the White House.\par \par \uc2 An executive order {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/policywatch/executive-order-on-exclusions-from-federal-labor-management-relations-programs/#:~:text=On%20March%2027%2C%20President%20Trump,have%20found%20to%20be%20illegal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued}}}\uc2  in March sought to cancel all collective bargaining agreements for most federal employees, citing national security concerns \u8211\'20\'13 and remove collective bargaining rights from more than a million workers.\par \par \uc2 While unions including the \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees\uc2  launched legal action as they challenged the move, obtaining an injunction, this was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://talkingpointsmemo.com/news/trump-federal-workers-unions-terminate-contracts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in effect overruled}}}\uc2  earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Union contracts at the Department of Veterans Affairs, \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/litigation/usda-moves-end-employee-union-contracts-documents-show-2025-08-13/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Department of Agriculture}}}\uc2  have since been terminated. An estimated 400,000 have been affected, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hamiltonnolan.com/p/fragile-movements-crumble"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 2.6% of unionized workers}}}\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that what this administration is doing is trying us as a test bed. If they are successful, I do believe that they\u8217\'20\'19ll be coming after every labor organization in the US,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Everett Kelley\uc2 , president of the \uc2 AFGE\uc2 , the largest federal labor union in the US, told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a fight for the very democracy of this country. This is a fight for every worker in America.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Trump is successful in dismantling \uc2 AFGE\uc2 , there\u8217\'20\'19s nothing to stop him from coming after every labor organization in the country, and we believe he will.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Taylor Rogers, White House assistant press secretary, said the recent appeals court decision \u8220\'20\'1Creaffirms that President Trump has the lawful executive authority to protect America\u8217\'20\'19s interests, and may eliminate collective bargaining agreements in agencies engaged in national security functions\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Trump administration looks forward to continued victory on the issue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 AFGE\uc2 , which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afge.org/publication/largest-veteran-affairs-employee-union-outraged-after-secretary-collins-terminates-afge-collective-bargaining-agreement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 represents}}}\uc2  320,000 employees at the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA), received notice on 6 August \u8211\'20\'13 five days after the appeals court ruling \u8211\'20\'13 that union contracts would be terminated as a result.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.va.gov/press-room/va-terminates-union-contracts-for-most-bargaining-unit-employees/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on the move, Doug Collins, secretary of veteran affairs, did not cite national security, but claimed cancelling the contracts would free up time and resources across the department.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere has not been a cancellation of union contracts on this scale in US history,\u8221\'20\'1D said Naveed Shah, political director of the veterans group Common Defense and a \uc2 US Army\uc2  veteran. \u8220\'20\'1CIf the workers and veterans at the VA are not sacred enough to protect, then \u8230\'20\'26 every worker in the public and private sector should be concerned.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shah warned that cancelling union contracts at the VA would make it harder for workers to advocate for their patients and have a safe workplace, thereby degrading the care veterans receive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey have created division, anxiety and uncertainty in your daily life as a government employee,\u8221\'20\'1D said a nurse at the Department of Veterans Affairs in Queens, New York, who requested anonymity for fear of retaliation. \u8220\'20\'1CThis attack on the working class in the government is just the first step.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers have won benefits and rights including the eight-hour workday, sick leave, workers\u8217\'20\'19 compensation, fairness in promotions and the ability to raise concerns through labor unions, the nurse said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith the administration\u8217\'20\'19s actions, they\u8217\'20\'19ve taken that away,\u8221\'20\'1D they added. \u8220\'20\'1CWith this administration coming in and politicizing the workforce and demonizing the work and the employee, it has taken away from our ability to really give the best to our veterans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The VA has long faced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.veteransforpeace.org/take-action/stop-privatization-veterans-health-administration#:~:text=Save%20Our%20VA%20seeks%20justice%20for%20veterans,veterans%2C%20their%20families%2C%20and%20to%20the%20larger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threats}}}\uc2  of cuts and services being contracted out to privatization, the nurse argued. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve taken away the one entity that stood in front of the agency and held them to the standard, held them to the law, held them to the contract, and was also the whistleblower on all of the things that were wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D they added. \u8220\'20\'1CThis administration has made a major step towards diminishing the care that the vets get. The vets deserve a certain level of care. That\u8217\'20\'19s why the VA was created.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Canary in the coalmine\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 On 8 August \u8211\'20\'13 seven days after the appeals court ruling \u8211\'20\'13 workers at the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  (\uc2 EPA\uc2 ) received notice the agency was terminating all collective bargaining agreements with unions representing workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the greatest attack on labor rights since the Patco strike,\u8221\'20\'1D when about 12,000 air traffic controllers walked out in 1981, and \uc2 Ronald Reagan{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://libraries.uta.edu/news/1981-patco-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 responded}}}\uc2  by firing them and dissolving the union, said Justin Chen, president of the AFGE Council 238, which represents about 8,000 workers at the \uc2 EPA\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAnd this is quite a bit worse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re just the canary in the coalmine for the rest of the working class essentially.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union is looking into additional legal avenues to protect their members, Chen said, as its lawsuit against the executive order is ongoing after the appeals court lifted the injunction.\par \par \uc2 AFGE\uc2  is currently backing a bill in Congress, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/2550/cosponsors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Protect America\u8217\'20\'19s Workforce Act}}}\uc2 , that would restore collective bargaining rights to federal workers. The bill has 222 cosponsors in the House, including seven Republicans.\par \par \uc2 In an April {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afge.org/globalassets/documents/2025-docs/faqs-for-eo14251-exclusions-from-federal-labor-manage.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 memo}}}\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://beta.chcoc.gov/mission"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chief Human Capital Officers Council}}}\uc2  ( stated that collective bargaining agreements should not be terminated until the conclusion of litigation, or the agency provided further guidance. Attorneys representing the Trump administration had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.govexec.com/workforce/2025/08/va-terminates-most-its-union-contracts-appearing-disregard-opm-guidance/407274/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited }}}\uc2 the memo to judges that agencies would wait to terminate the contracts.\par \par \uc2 The office of management and budget did not respond to requests for comment on why union contracts were cancelled while the litigation over the executive order is ongoing. The Office of Personnel Management {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opm.gov/news/secrets-of-opm/building-momentum-through-legal-wins/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deferred}}}\uc2  to their director\u8217\'20\'19s blog post.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe administration, they know us as a threat to their authoritarianism essentially, they know we are the ones who represent workers who are civil servants who pledge to both uphold the constitution and serve the mission of their agencies, which is supposed to be politically agnostic and serve the public,\u8221\'20\'1D added Chen. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very obvious that this administration, despite them trying to portray themselves as some sort of defender of the working man, they attack popular programs like Medicaid, they attack popular agencies like the \uc2 EPA\uc2  and the VA.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250822el8m002s7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
