\par\par \b \uc2 CEO-to-worker pay gap surges to 632 to 1 at US\u8217\'20\'19s lowest-paying large firms, study shows\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 704 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 August 2025\par 11:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 At 100 firms in S&P 500 with lowest median pay, executives\u8217\'20\'19 comp increased by average of nearly 35% over five years\par \par \uc2 Some of the US\u8217\'20\'19s lowest-paying large firms increased their CEOs\u8217\'20\'19 compensation by an average of almost 35% over five years, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ips-dc.org/report-executive-excess-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new research}}}\uc2 . Their workers\u8217\'20\'19 salaries did not keep up.\par \par \uc2 As executive remuneration ballooned, the average CEO-to-worker pay gap across the 100 companies in the S&P 500 with lowest median worker pay \u8211\'20\'13 dubbed the Low-Wage 100 by the Institute for Policy Studies \u8211\'20\'13 widened by 12.9% between 2019 and 2024, from 560 to 1 to 632 to 1.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMedian pay increased only modestly, whereas CEO pay really skyrocketed,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Sarah Anderson\uc2 , director of the Global Economy Project at the Institute for Policy Studies, and author of the report.\par \par \uc2 Between 2019 to 2024, CEO pay at these companies increased by 34.7%, unadjusted for inflation, compared with a 16.3% increase in these firms\u8217\'20\'19 average median worker pay during the same period \u8211\'20\'13 short of inflation, which came to 22.6% over the same period.\par \par \uc2 By last year, average CEO compensation in the Low-Wage 100 stood at $17.2m. Average median worker pay was $35,570.\par \par \uc2 Of the 100 firms, median worker pay fell at 22 between 2019 and 2024. Ulta Beauty reported a 46% drop in median worker pay to $11,078 as the company significantly expanded its part-time workforce.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 CEO pay was the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/24/trump-bill-ceo-pay-starbucks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largest gap in 2024}}}\uc2 , with its CEO, \uc2 Brian Niccol\uc2 , receiving total compensation worth $95.8m, 6,666 times as much as the company\u8217\'20\'19s $14,674 median pay.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a stunning message for \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  management to send to their workers who\u8217\'20\'19ve organized unions at 570 stores in recent years, and they\u8217\'20\'19re still waiting for the company to negotiate a contract. It says a lot about who they really value at that company and who they don\u8217\'20\'19t,\u8221\'20\'1D said Anderson.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  did not respond to multiple requests for comment on the report.\par \par \uc2 The IPS report cites a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/newsroom/meetings-events/sec-roundtable-executive-compensation-disclosure-requirements"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June roundtable}}}\uc2  hosted by the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 , the US markets regulator, on executive compensation disclosure requirements, where Drew Hambly, investment director at \uc2 CalPers\uc2 , the largest public pension fund in the US, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hFAA7EqLZDE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described}}}\uc2  the negative impacts overcompensation of executives has on low-wage workforces.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/24/trump-bill-ceo-pay-starbucks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starbucks\u8217\'20\'19 CEO made 6,666 times more than his workers in 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do want our boards to think more about the bottom 50% of people who work for them,\u8221\'20\'1D Hambly said. \u8220\'20\'1CBecause when I go into a business, I\u8217\'20\'19m probably interacting with a lower-wage worker. And if you\u8217\'20\'19re going to drive value over time, that\u8217\'20\'19s the face of your company.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In recent years US families have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/aug/01/trump-inflation-cost-of-living-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struggled }}}\uc2 with high costs for groceries and housing, and layoffs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fastcompany.com/91386050/layoffs-2025-companies-have-announced-over-800000-jobs-cuts-so-far-there-are-3-big-reasons-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have been on the rise}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIn the midst of all of this, CEOs are focused on making themselves even richer, instead of thinking about the welfare of their employees or even the long-term growth of their company,\u8221\'20\'1D said Anderson. \u8220\'20\'1CI think if they continue on this path, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a trend that is bad, not just for workers, but for these companies and our economy as a whole.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Between 2019 to 2024, Low-Wage 100 firms spent $644bn on stock buybacks. More than half spent more on buybacks than on capital improvements at their firms.\par \par \uc2 Lowe\u8217\'20\'19s spent $46.6bn on stock buybacks: $28,456 per each of the retailer\u8217\'20\'19s 273,000 employees, according to the report. \uc2 Home Depot\uc2  ranked second in stock buybacks during this period, spending $37.9bn.\par \par \uc2 The report also noted 32 billionaires owe their wealth to Low-Wage 100 corporations, including eight billionaires from \uc2 Walmart\uc2 , four from \uc2 Estee Lauder\uc2  and three from \uc2 DoorDash\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As policy solutions, the report highlighted support for a tax hike on corporations that pay their CEO at least 50 times more what they pay employees. It also urged policymakers to increase taxes on stock buybacks.\par \par \uc2 Ulta Beauty, Lowe\u8217\'20\'19s and \uc2 Home Depot\uc2  did not respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250821el8l0035y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
