\par\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18An existential threat\u8217\'20\'19: US health workers call \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  a risk to public health\b0\par\par\uc2 Melody Schreiber \par \uc2 1,197 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 August 2025\par 11:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than 750 health workers say Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s misinformation fuels violence and endangers lives\par \par \uc2 Current and former employees at US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 health}}}\uc2  agencies released a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://savehhs.org"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  on Wednesday outlining how misinformation spread by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/robert-f-kennedy-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr}}}\uc2  is endangering the lives of federal employees and the American people.\par \par \uc2 Experts emphasized to the Guardian that he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Can existential threat to public health\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On 8 August, a gunman killed a police officer, David Rose, and fired nearly 500 bullets, shattering 150 windows, at the Atlanta headquarters of the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC). The man, who was killed on the scene, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/19/father-cdc-shooter-covid-vaccine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 believed}}}\uc2  the Covid-19 vaccine caused his depression.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy, secretary of the US Department of Health and Human Services (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ), has been \u8220\'20\'1Ccomplicit in dismantling America\u8217\'20\'19s public health infrastructure and endangering the nation\u8217\'20\'19s health by repeatedly spreading inaccurate health information\u8221\'20\'1D, said the letter, which was signed by more than 750 current and former employees from \uc2 HHS\uc2  agencies, including the CDC and the \uc2 National Institutes of Health\uc2  (\uc2 NIH\uc2 ), and addressed to Kennedy and the \uc2 US Congress\uc2 . The employees drafted the letter in their personal capacity, they said.\par \par \uc2 Pressure against Kennedy is mounting in public health.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/19/maga-cow-products-beef-tallow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Raging bulls: why Maga is pushing cow products on to America }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen your own leadership peddles falsehoods, it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t just erode the public trust, it creates the conditions for the kind of violence that we saw on Friday,\u8221\'20\'1D Yolanda Jacobs, president of \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees (AFGE)\uc2  local 2883 and a CDC employee, told reporters last week. \u8220\'20\'1CThis was a targeted attack. It was a targeted act of violence against not just CDC, but CDC\u8217\'20\'19s employees.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The shooting was \u8220\'20\'1Cpublic health\u8217\'20\'19s Jan 6,\u8221\'20\'1D Colin Carlson, an assistant professor of epidemiology at Yale University\u8217\'20\'19s School of Public Health, co-wrote in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.statnews.com/2025/08/15/cdc-shooting-january-6th-for-public-health/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 op-ed}}}\uc2  calling for the resignation of health officials, including Kennedy, who have spread dangerous misinformation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo me, the worst case scenario is, and has always been, that someone shows up with a gun,\u8221\'20\'1D Carlson said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really important that we do something now, while we can, before the shooting that kills more people. Because this will keep happening. It will spread, and it will get worse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kennedy, a prominent anti-vaccine advocate for two decades, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gbnews.com/politics/us/rfk-promises-clean-cesspool-corruption-cdc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  the CDC a \u8220\'20\'1Ccesspool of corruption\u8221\'20\'1D. He has made numerous false claims about mRNA vaccines, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2021/dec/10/robert-f-kennedy-jr/no-covid-19-vaccine-not-deadliest-vaccine-ever-mad/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling}}}\uc2  Covid vaccines the \u8220\'20\'1Cdeadliest vaccine ever made\u8221\'20\'1D. He replaced members of the CDC\u8217\'20\'19s vaccine advisory committee with largely inexperienced advisers, some of whom have histories of anti-vaccine activism.\par \par \uc2 One of the advisers, Robert Malone, posted violent images directed at scientists in the hours before and soon after the CDC shooting, prompting the Democratic senator Richard Blumenthal, of Connecticut, to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hsgac.senate.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025-08-13-Letter-from-Sen-Blumenthal-to-HHS.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demand}}}\uc2  his removal and the restoration of the original experts to the committee.\par \par \uc2 The letter on Wednesday decried the \u8220\'20\'1Cdeliberate destruction of trust in America\u8217\'20\'19s public health workforce\u8221\'20\'1D, which puts employees at risk of violence and keeps them from working to protect the health of Americans.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous and deceitful statements and actions have contributed to the harassment and violence experienced by CDC staff\u8221\'20\'1D, the letter read.\par \par \uc2 Matthew Buckham, Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s acting chief of staff, was co-founder of the group that maintains a \u8220\'20\'1CDEI Watch List\u8221\'20\'1D targeting \uc2 HHS\uc2  employees.\par \par \uc2 Watch lists like these have published the photos and personal home addresses of federal workers, who have been threatened in their homes, said Vi Le, an expert on preventing gun violence.\par \par \uc2 When Le heard about the shooting, she scrambled to pull together resources for CDC employees.\par \par \uc2 But she didn\u8217\'20\'19t do it on behalf of the CDC; she did it as a volunteer with the \uc2 AFGE\uc2 . That\u8217\'20\'19s because in April, her entire department on preventing gun violence in the US was let go.\par \par \uc2 Yet when asked how he would address misinformation leading to violence in the wake of the CDC shooting, Kennedy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scrippsnews.com/health/rfk-jr-in-interview-with-scripps-news-trusting-the-experts-is-not-science"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pointed}}}\uc2  to past public health officials who he said \u8220\'20\'1Chave not been honest\u8221\'20\'1D about Covid vaccines.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAn attack on a \uc2 US government\uc2  agency should be a moment in time when we come together,\u8221\'20\'1D Dr \uc2 Anne Schuchat\uc2 , former principal deputy director of the CDC, said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://static1.squarespace.com/static/689f5612fc63c95dc6488b44/t/68a5574c8da0a82c770d2953/1755666253003/HHS+Letter+Press+Release_8amMediaBlast.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  about the letter. \u8220\'20\'1CInstead, Secretary Kennedy continues to spread misinformation at the risk of American lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 HHS\uc2  did not respond by press time to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s media inquiries about the role of health officials in promoting misinformation that may lead to violence.\par \par \uc2 Employees also called on the \uc2 NIH\uc2  director, Jay Bhattacharya, to \u8220\'20\'1Crefrain from his dangerous politicization of mRNA vaccine technology\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The day after the CDC shooting, Bhattacharya {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?app=desktop&v=IB0H2lJPGIk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared}}}\uc2  on Steve Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s podcast to push back on what he characterized as health officials\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1Crelentless propaganda and pressure\u8221\'20\'1D to take the mRNA Covid vaccines.\par \par \uc2 Bhattacharya spoke about how the former director of the CDC, \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , was \u8220\'20\'1Cblinded\u8221\'20\'1D to the \u8220\'20\'1Cfacts\u8221\'20\'1D of the vaccine, which he said had harmful side effects.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs far as public health goes, for vaccines the mRNA platform is no longer viable,\u8221\'20\'1D Bhattacharya said.\par \par \uc2 It echoed previous statements of his putting the blame for anti-vaccine sentiment on US officials. In July 2024, Bhattacharya {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?app=desktop&v=2LlfSLKKy-k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that people who claimed to be injured by vaccines became \u8220\'20\'1Cpublic enemy number one in 2021\u8221\'20\'1D, adding they were seen as a \u8220\'20\'1Cthreat\u8221\'20\'1D to officials\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to distribute vaccines.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Bhattacharya published an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2025/08/12/nih-mrna-vaccines-jay-bhattacharya/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 op-ed}}}\uc2  arguing that \u8220\'20\'1CmRNA technology has failed to earn the public\u8217\'20\'19s trust\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWithin days of the shooting, all of these guys were back out there immediately talking about how dangerous vaccines are,\u8221\'20\'1D Carlson said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe see them condemn the violence and act like they had nothing to do with it, and then we also see them repeat the messaging that the shooter believed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rhetoric about the harms of vaccines, and the alleged dangers posed by health officials, is circulated and amplified in anti-vaccine circles, especially online.\par \par \uc2 The man arrested for killing Minnesota lawmaker Melissa Hortman and her husband, Mark, in June {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theblaze.com/news/exclusive-assassination-suspect-vance-boelter-tells-stunning-inside-story-about-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  the conservative blog the Blaze that he confronted the couple because he believed the mRNA shots were killing people.\par \par \uc2 Violence is the point of decades of anti-vaccine and anti-scientific disinformation \u8211\'20\'13 not a byproduct but a tool, Carlson said. Stochastic terrorism, in which public figures use mass media to inspire political violence, has been used to harm trans people and abortion providers, for example, in the past.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve learned the comfortable distance between incitement and violence,\u8221\'20\'1D Carlson said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Maga movement is incredibly good at saying just enough and distributing the burden of incitement within its ecosystem, letting the people at the top set the messaging and then having places like rightwing news outlets and social media sites do the work of amplifying and accelerating and putting violence to the messaging.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Removing officials like Kennedy and preventing future violence is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe only path\u8221\'20\'1D to restoring trust in public health, Carlson said.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an existential threat to public health. If we fight and lose, that\u8217\'20\'19s OK, but I would rather fight and lose than lie down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250821el8l002mi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
