\par\par \b \uc2 US health agency workers accuse RFK Jr of fueling violence against them\b0\par\par\uc2 Marina Dunbar \par \uc2 582 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 August 2025\par 20:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than 750 workers in letter say \uc2 HHS\uc2  secretary\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric played a role in recent attack at CDC\u8217\'20\'19s Atlanta headquarters\par \par \uc2 More than 750 current and former federal health employees on Wednesday accused the health and human services (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ) secretary, Robert F Kennedy Jr, of fueling harassment and violence directed at government healthcare staff.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.savehhs.org/read-the-letter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a letter}}}\uc2  sent to Kennedy and members of Congress, the group accuses RFK Jr of contributing to \u8220\'20\'1Cthe harassment and violence experienced by \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) staff\u8221\'20\'1D, citing decisions such as removing members from a CDC vaccine advisory panel, questioning the safety of the measles vaccine, and firing key CDC staff as actions that sow distrust in federal medical professionals.\par \par \uc2 The group says Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric played a role in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/09/police-officer-david-rose-atlanta-cdc-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 8 August attack}}}\uc2  at the CDC\u8217\'20\'19s headquarters in Atlanta, where a Georgia man opened fire on four CDC buildings, firing dozens of shots and killing a police officer. Law enforcement officials said the gunman blamed a Covid-19 vaccine for making him feel depressed and suicidal.\par \par \uc2 After the attack, Kennedy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/health/after-the-shooting-at-cdc-rfk-jr-criticizes-agencys-pandemic-response"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to confirm}}}\uc2  the motive of the shooter in an interview. He described political violence as \u8220\'20\'1Cwrong\u8221\'20\'1D but neither he nor Donald Trump have spoken publicly about the motive, despite law enforcement officials making clear the shooter targeted the CDC over the vaccine.\par \par \uc2 The health workers are now asking Kennedy to \u8220\'20\'1Ccease and publicly disavow the ongoing dissemination of false and misleading claims about vaccines, infectious disease transmission, and America\u8217\'20\'19s public health institutions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The workers further accused Kennedy of being \u8220\'20\'1Ccomplicit in dismantling America\u8217\'20\'19s public health infrastructure and endangering the nation\u8217\'20\'19s health by repeatedly spreading inaccurate health information\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The letter urged the \uc2 HHS\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cacknowledge and affirm that CDC\u8217\'20\'19s work is rooted in scientific, non-partisan evidence focused on improving the health of every American\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Censure that the \uc2 HHS\uc2  workforce can carry out its duties in an environment free from imminent threats of harm\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, it asks Kennedy to take \u8220\'20\'1Cvigorous action\u8221\'20\'1D to eliminate online content that targets federal employees, including \u8220\'20\'1CDEI watchlists\u8221\'20\'1D. The workers asked for a response from the health secretary by 2 September.\par \par \uc2 In response to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s request for comment, the \uc2 HHS\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CSecretary Kennedy is standing firmly with CDC employees \u8211\'20\'13 both on the ground and across every center \u8211\'20\'13 ensuring their safety and wellbeing remain a top priority. In the wake of this heartbreaking shooting, he traveled to Atlanta to offer his support and reaffirm his deep respect, calling the CDC \u8216\'20\'18a shining star among global health agencies\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The statement continues: \u8220\'20\'1CFor the first time in its 70-year history, the mission of \uc2 HHS\uc2  is truly resonating with the American people \u8211\'20\'13 driven by President Trump and Secretary Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s bold commitment to Make America Healthy Again. Any attempt to conflate widely supported public health reforms with the violence of a suicidal mass shooter is an attempt to politicize a tragedy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The letter comes a day after the \uc2 American Academy of Pediatrics\uc2  (AAP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/19/pediatrics-academy-covid-19-vaccine-recommendation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took a stance}}}\uc2  against the \uc2 HHS\uc2 , urging that children as young as six months and up to 23 months receive the Covid-19 vaccine, a position that diverges from the current federal guidance given by the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s health agencies.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy responded to the AAP\u8217\'20\'19s updated guidelines on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SecKennedy/status/1957914911415153107"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social media}}}\uc2  by accusing the organization of failing to sufficiently disclose conflicts of interest.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250820el8k004v4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
