\par\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A literal gut punch\u8217\'20\'19: Missouri workers devastated by Republican repeal of paid sick leave\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,429 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 August 2025\par 14:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Voters approved sick leave mandate by 58% but lawmakers are caving to lobbying by the state\u8217\'20\'19s chamber of commerce\par \par \uc2 Being sick is a costly business for Bill Thompson, who worked in the fast-food industry in Independence, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/missouri"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Missouri}}}\uc2 , for more than 30 years, and recently worked at \uc2 Guitar Center\uc2  until early July, when he was laid off.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs an older worker, I have health issues from working on my feet and with my hands for many years with no breaks for eight to 10 hours a day. I have done it for 38 years now, living paycheck to paycheck,\u8221\'20\'1D 54-year-old Thompson said, noting in Missouri workers are not {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://labor.mo.gov/dls/general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mandated}}}\uc2  breaks of any kind during work.\par \par \uc2 So when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  in Missouri repealed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/11/missouri-repeal-paid-sick-leave-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paid sick leave mandate}}}\uc2  that the state\u8217\'20\'19s voters approved by 58% after an aggressive lobbying campaign by the Missouri chamber of commerce and industry and other business industry groups, he said, \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a literal gut punch.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re not paid for missed days, it literally means food off your table, bills unpaid, rent unpaid, then that can lead towards homelessness. Some of the people I know in the movement are currently homeless but still are fighting back against this,\u8221\'20\'1D said Thompson. \u8220\'20\'1CI was very disappointed and disgusted that hard-working taxpayers this would have helped matter so little to them.\u8221\'20\'1D Thompson helped gather signatures for the paid-sick-leave and minimum-wage-increase ballot initiative because of his experiences of working through illnesses and losing income when he had to take time off to care for his ailing mother.\par \par \uc2 Workers and labor groups in Missouri strongly criticized the repeal, arguing elected officials chose to side with \u8220\'20\'1Cgreed\u8221\'20\'1D over workers, as efforts to re-enact the law and prevent legislators from overturning voter ballot initiatives in Missouri are under way.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s house and senate passed HB567, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://governor.mo.gov/press-releases/archive/governor-kehoe-signs-bold-tax-cuts-and-pro-business-legislation-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed}}}\uc2  into law on 10 July by the governor, \uc2 Mike Kehoe\uc2 , which repealed the paid sick leave mandate and annual minimum wage increases tied to the consumer price index beyond the increase to $15 an hour in 2016 that voters also approved.\par \par \uc2 Voters in Nebraska, by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Nebraska_Initiative_436,_Paid_Sick_Leave_Initiative_(2024)"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 74.5%}}}\uc2 , and Alaska, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ogletree.com/insights-resources/blog-posts/2024-election-results-states-decide-key-ballot-measures-on-paid-sick-leave-minimum-wage-hikes-and-tipped-worker-pay/#:~:text=Beyond%20the%20federal%20elections%2C%20several,result%20has%20not%20been%20called."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly 57%}}}\uc2  approval, also passed paid sick leave mandates in November 2024. As of December 2024, 18 states and Washington DC had enacted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/WB/StatePaidSickLeaveLaws.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paid sick leave laws}}}\uc2  covering private employers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey chose to side with greed over the health of Missouri workers,\u8221\'20\'1D said Richard Eiker, a McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s worker in the Kansas City, Missouri, area for more than 20 years who supported the paid sick leave mandate. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we\u8217\'20\'19re not going anywhere, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to stay in this and keep fighting until we win better treatment for Missouri workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Eiker said the issue of paid sick leave was a public {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 health}}}\uc2  issue, especially for food service workers, and that he has often had to go into work sick or injured because he couldn\u8217\'20\'19t afford to take the unpaid time off from work.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhether it\u8217\'20\'19s been an injury I\u8217\'20\'19ve sustained at work or been an illness I\u8217\'20\'19ve had, I\u8217\'20\'19ve often found myself having to go into work regardless of whether I recovered fully or not, simply because I can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to take the time off of work in order to take care of my bills and everything,\u8221\'20\'1D Eiker said.\par \par \uc2 For 10 years, Eiker was the primary caregiver for his mother and he recounted that on a day that she wasn\u8217\'20\'19t feeling well, he had to go to work. He came home to find her unconscious and unresponsive after she suffered a stroke.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the time I was caring for her, her expenses, my expenses, and we were trying to keep the apartment we were in, all these pressures on me, if I had paid sick time off and I had been able to stay with her that day, I wonder if things could have been different,\u8221\'20\'1D Eiker added.\par \par \uc2 Though voters all approved paid sick leave in states where Republicans have dominated in statewide elections, only Republicans in Missouri have pushed to entirely repeal paid sick leave approved by voters.\par \par \uc2 The repeal law in Missouri goes into effect on 28 August, just weeks after the paid sick leave mandate took effect in May 2025.\par \par \uc2 Proponents of paid sick leave criticized the repeal given the strong support for it and that negotiations were under way to reach a compromise.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think we were 95% of the way on a negotiated agreement, one that I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have been happy with, because it would have been different than what the voters had passed. But at the end of the day, elected officials, I think, weren\u8217\'20\'19t so much concerned with paid sick days. I think they were more concerned with the idea that working people have power over our lives,\u8221\'20\'1D said Richard von Glahn, policy director at Missouri Jobs With Justice, a worker advocacy group based in St Louis that worked on the paid sick leave ballot initiative.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that was the more important issue for the chamber of commerce and elected officials to try to push back on, because I think they\u8217\'20\'19re really terrified that working people have a sense of our own agency in a state like this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He argued the paid sick leave campaign to gather signatures and speak with voters \u8220\'20\'1Cwere easy because paid sick days are such common sense to most people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven on a day where Missourians sort of overwhelmingly voted for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  and Governor Kehoe, they also overwhelmingly voted for an increase in paid sick days,\u8221\'20\'1D Von Glahn said. \u8220\'20\'1CAny notion that there\u8217\'20\'19s really a Republican party, that is a party of workers, Missouri shows just how much of a stranglehold corporate interests still have on the Republican establishment. I think that\u8217\'20\'19s a cautionary tale for working-class people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Groups in Missouri are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://missouriindependent.com/2025/07/28/kicked-a-hornets-nest-missouri-gop-repeal-of-voter-approved-laws-inspires-backlash/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weighing}}}\uc2  a new ballot initiative to enshrine the law in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution, and a 2026 ballot initiative has been filed to require at least 80% of the state legislature to repeal all or parts of a voter-approved measure.\par \par \uc2 The paid sick leave mandate was repealed as the Missouri chamber of commerce and industry {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mochamber.com/news-archive/gov-kehoe-signs-proposition-a-relief-bill-protecting-missouri-jobs-and-businesses/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  the bill to do so its \u8220\'20\'1Ctop priority\u8221\'20\'1D during the 2025 legislative session, though repealing the law through the legislature was initially seen as challenging given the strong public support for it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome legislators may look at this and go, we don\u8217\'20\'19t want to goof with it at all because the percentage was so high in support of it,\u8221\'20\'1D Ray McCarty, CEO of Associated Industries of Missouri, said in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://missouriindependent.com/2024/11/07/missouri-business-groups-weigh-challenge-to-voter-approved-minimum-wage-hike-sick-leave/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  with the Missouri Independent in November 2024.\par \par \uc2 Opponents of the paid sick leave bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mochamber.com/news-archive/gov-kehoe-signs-proposition-a-relief-bill-protecting-missouri-jobs-and-businesses/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2  it was \u8220\'20\'1Ca job killer\u8221\'20\'1D, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/paid-sick-days-and-paid-family-and-medical-leave-are-not-job-killers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 common refrain}}}\uc2  in opposition to paid sick leave policies for years, though data and research have shown paid sick leave improves workforce participation and lowers employee turnover, especially of women, in addition to adding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/paid-sick-leave-improves-workers-health-and-the-economy/%20https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=3953523"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 health benefits}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The authors of the bill to repeal the paid sick leave mandate in the state house and senate did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 In an email, a spokesperson for Kehoe claimed \u8220\'20\'1Cout of state special interests\u8221\'20\'1D played a significant role in passing the voter-approved Proposition A, though they did not name who they believe those were.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHB567 protects families, job creators, and small businesses by rolling back government overreach, cutting red tape, and eliminating costly mandates,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson added. \u8220\'20\'1CThis law promotes freedom for workers to find jobs that fit their needs and for businesses to offer the benefits that work best for them \u8211\'20\'13 ensuring Missouri\u8217\'20\'19s future is driven by its own people and economy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Thompson could not disagree more. In 2020, when he worked at \uc2 Burger King\uc2 , he said, he had to take eight weeks off work, all unpaid, because his mother\u8217\'20\'19s cancer had reached an inoperable stage and she was put on palliative care through hospice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI moved in with her and cared for her, cooked meals, made sure she took her meds,\u8221\'20\'1D explained Thompson. \u8220\'20\'1CI had to go to food pantries and rely on the charity of family and neighbors to feed us. She was in hospice care for eight weeks and passed away. I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t paid for that time away from work. No one should go through this working in the richest country in the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250812el8c002xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
