\par\par \b \uc2 I was the US labor secretary. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s latest firing undermines a key agency\b0\par\par\uc2 Robert Reich \par \uc2 657 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 August 2025\par 10:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The firing of Erika McEntarfer, head of the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 , destroys the credibility of essential information\par \par \uc2 I spent much of the 1990s as the secretary of labor. One unit of the labor department is the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I was instructed by my predecessors as well as by the White House, and by every labor economist and statistician I came in contact with, that one of my cardinal responsibilities was to guard the independence of the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Otherwise, this crown jewel of knowledge about jobs and the economy would be compromised. If politicized, it would no longer be trusted as a source of information.\par \par \uc2 So what does {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  do? In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/01/trump-fires-erika-mcentarfer-labor-statistics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one fell swoop}}}\uc2  on Friday, he essentially destroyed the credibility of the \uc2 BLS\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump didn\u8217\'20\'19t like the fact that the \uc2 BLS\uc2  revised downward its jobs reports for April and May.\par \par \uc2 Well, that\u8217\'20\'19s too bad. Revisions in monthly jobs reports are nothing new. They\u8217\'20\'19re made when the bureau gets more or better information over time, which it often does.\par \par \uc2 Yet with no basis in fact, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114955222046259464"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged}}}\uc2  that Erika McEntarfer, the commissioner of labor statistics, \u8220\'20\'1Crigged\u8221\'20\'1D the data \u8220\'20\'1Cto make the Republicans, and ME, look bad\u8221\'20\'1D. Then he ordered her fired and replaced with someone else \u8211\'20\'13 presumably someone whose data Trump will approve of.\par \par \uc2 How can anyone in the future trust the information that emerges from the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  when the person in charge of the agency has to come up with data to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s liking in order to stay in the job? Answer: they cannot.\par \par \uc2 Trump has destroyed the credibility of this extraordinarily important source of information.\par \par \uc2 When Trump doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like the message, he shoots the messenger and replaces the messenger with someone who will come up with messages that he approves. So we\u8217\'20\'19re left without credible sources of information about what is really occurring.\par \par \uc2 Trump is in the process of trying to do the same with the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 demanding that \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s chair, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/aug/01/trump-jerome-powell-tariffs-federal-reserve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut interest rates}}}\uc2  or lose control of the agency.\par \par \uc2 What happens to the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s credibility if Powell gives in to Trump? It loses it.\par \par \uc2 In the future, we wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have confidence that the Fed is fighting inflation as rigorously as it should. And without that confidence, longer-term interest rates will spike because investors will assume that there\u8217\'20\'19s no inflation cop on the beat, and therefore will demand a higher risk premium.\par \par \uc2 Trump hates facts that he disagrees with. That\u8217\'20\'19s why {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/19/trump-epa-layoffs-research-development"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he\u8217\'20\'19s}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/06/trump-epa-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismembering}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2 , which has repeatedly shown that the climate crisis isn\u8217\'20\'19t a \u8220\'20\'1Choax\u8221\'20\'1D, as Trump claims, but more like a national emergency.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s why Trump is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/01/university-commencement-speeches-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacking}}}\uc2  American universities, whose scientists are developing wind and solar energy, and whose historians have revealed America\u8217\'20\'19s tragic history of racism and genocide of indigenous people.\par \par \uc2 He is killing off the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control\uc2  and the \uc2 National Institutes of Health\uc2 , which are showing the sources of sickness and disease and how we can guard against them.\par \par \uc2 This is a man and a regime that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want the public to know the truth. He is turning the US into George Orwell\u8217\'20\'19s dystopian 1984.\par \par \uc2 The Trumping of America is happening so fast and in so many places that it\u8217\'20\'19s hard to see the whole. Which partly explains why he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want the facts out. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want us to know how bad it really is.\par \par \uc2 * Robert Reich, a former US secretary of labor, is a professor of public policy emeritus at the \uc2 University of California, Berkeley\uc2 . He is a Guardian US columnist. His newsletter is at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://robertreich.substack.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 robertreich.substack.com}}}\uc2 . His next book, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/763803/coming-up-short-by-robert-b-reich/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coming Up Short: A Memoir of My America}}}\uc2 , will be out on 5 August\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250805el85002s3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
