\par\par \b \uc2 Now is the time for Democrats to hammer Trump on the economy\b0\par\par\uc2 Lloyd Green \par \uc2 807 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 August 2025\par 14:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 With inflation and unemployment rising, Democrats must speak out \u8211\'20\'13 and show they care about the average voter\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEconomic Growth Shatters Expectations as President Trump Fuels America\u8217\'20\'19s Golden Age,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/articles/2025/07/economic-growth-shatters-expectations-as-president-trump-fuels-americas-golden-age/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  on Wednesday. But within 48 hours, the data told a very different story, giving the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  a badly needed opening if they can muster the competence and focus to seize upon it.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the US commerce department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bea.gov/news/2025/personal-income-and-outlays-june-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that inflation had ticked up to 2.6%. A day later, the labor department reported that unemployment had risen to 4.2% in July, and that the US had actually gained {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.nr0.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 258,000 }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.nr0.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fewer }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.nr0.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jobs}}}\uc2  than previously reported.\par \par \uc2 From the looks of things, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tariffs}}}\uc2  are damaging the economy. Suddenly, things aren\u8217\'20\'19t looking so hot.\par \par \uc2 Rather than copping to a screw-up, however, the president immediately laid blame elsewhere. In a barrage of posts on social media, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/aug/01/trump-jerome-powell-tariffs-federal-reserve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lambasted}}}\uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , the chair of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 , attacked his intelligence and again threatened his tenure at the Fed.\par \par \uc2 The president trashed Powell, who he appointed, as \u8220\'20\'1Ca stubborn MORON\u8221\'20\'1D. Adding insult to injury, Trump brayed: \u8220\'20\'1CIF HE CONTINUES TO REFUSE, THE BOARD SHOULD ASSUME CONTROL, AND DO WHAT EVERYONE KNOWS HAS TO BE DONE!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But things didn\u8217\'20\'19t end there. The tantrum continued unabated.\par \par \uc2 Hours later, Trump grabbed another page from the strongman playbook and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/01/trump-fires-erika-mcentarfer-labor-statistics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired}}}\uc2  Erika McEntarfer, the head of the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 . He suggested that she had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114954846612623858"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cooked the books}}}\uc2  and was essentially giving aid and comfort to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the man who first appointed her.\par \par \uc2 As we know, there is reality and then there is Trump\u8217\'20\'19s version of reality.\par \par \uc2 At Friday\u8217\'20\'19s final bell, the Dow had dropped more than 540 points and the Nasdaq was down 2.24%. The ghost of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cliberation day\u8221\'20\'1D had returned to haunt the markets, giving the Democrats ample material to work with.\par \par \uc2 Already, the One Big Beautiful Bill Act places Trump and the Republicans at odds with their base and with swing voters. According to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/trump-wsj-poll-tax-bill-support-ee51c67e?gaa_at=eafs&gaa_n=ASWzDAjV8bA8QJdrqhBPPo2-2g6Q-vEql8eq7s76ZMTlYjem88VgzuuxXfOHitgY6c4%3D&gaa_ts=688d2a20&gaa_sig=vq9NAwPaIrKA1e_67Ry0cbi_2VByamPEeVCxz7fJW7cifEpOsZz2rdg0n4_ZVsvhA_MYCH8PasM0LTCMLb6FzQ%3D%3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Journal poll}}}\uc2 , 70% of the US believes the act {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/24/trump-tax-bill-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 benefits the rich}}}\uc2 . Beyond that, the tax plan is underwater with the public, 42-52, and is disfavored by a majority of independents.\par \par \uc2 Practically speaking, the \uc2 Congressional Budget Office{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbo.gov/system/files/2025-06/Arrington-Guthrie-Letter-Medicaid.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 projected}}}\uc2  in June that nearly 8 million people would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/24/trump-medicaid-funding-budget-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lose their insurance}}}\uc2  under the Trump-backed bill. For the current iteration of the GOP, that\u8217\'20\'19s a problem. These days, Republican voters tilt working class. Many of them break economically liberal and socially conservative.\par \par \uc2 This why House Republicans danced around the issue of coming Medicaid cuts. They stand to harm their own voters. And they know it.\par \par \uc2 Take Mike Lawler, a representative from New York\u8217\'20\'19s Hudson Valley. More than 200,000 of his constituents receive Medicaid benefits. Town halls in his district have become rowdy events, with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2025/05/05/mike-lawler-gop-lawmaker-rowdy-town-hall/83453935007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 police hauling out a constituent}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lawler claims to have \u8220\'20\'1Cfought extensively to make sure that there were not draconian changes to Medicaid\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the end of the day, this is about strengthening the program,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2025/07/06/republican-medicaid-cuts-midterms-big-beautiful-bill-00440023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lawler added}}}\uc2 . Uh, that\u8217\'20\'19s why he needed the cops.\par \par \uc2 More than 64 Republican House members represent districts where Medicaid rates exceed the national average, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2025/05/07/politics/enrollment-medicaid-republican-representatives-dg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to CNN}}}\uc2 . In those seats, five incumbents won last November by five points or fewer.\par \par \uc2 But the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s problems don\u8217\'20\'19t end with Medicaid. These days, social security, the most sacrosanct legacy of the New Deal, may be in the crosshairs of Team Trump.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Scott Bessent, the treasury secretary, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/07/30/business/bessent-trump-social-security.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 acknowledged}}}\uc2  the so-called \u8220\'20\'1CTrump accounts\u8221\'20\'1D created for kids by the One Big Beautiful Bill Act were actually a \u8220\'20\'1Cback door for privatizing social security\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The accounts are designed as a vehicle for Americans to build and accumulate wealth as soon as they are born. Under the new law, newborns will be eligible to receive $1,000 from Uncle Sam.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSocial security is a defined benefit plan paid out,\u8221\'20\'1D Bessent explained. \u8220\'20\'1CTo the extent that if all of a sudden these accounts grow, and you have in the hundreds of thousands of dollars for your retirement, then that\u8217\'20\'19s a gamechanger.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As a candidate and then again in office, Trump had pledged to leave social security untouched. Now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/20/social-security-disruptions-doge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that pledge is in doubt}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In 2024, the Republicans made the economic failures of the Biden-Harris administration central to their campaigns. The Trump-Vance campaign raked the Democrats over the coals over inflation. In politics, turnabout is fair play. It is time for the Democrats to show that they actually care about the average voter.\par \par \uc2 * Lloyd Green is an attorney in New York and served in the \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  from 1990 to 1992\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250804el84003xq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
