\par\par \b \uc2 Trump fires labor statistics chief hours after data showed jobs growth slowed\b0\par\par\uc2 Callum Jones in New York and Michael Sainato \par \uc2 675 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 August 2025\par 02:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US president accused of \u8216\'20\'18firing the messenger\u8217\'20\'19 as he makes claims without evidence about Erika McEntarfer\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  fired the federal government official in charge of labor statistics, hours after data revealed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/aug/01/jobs-report-july-trump-tariffs-trade-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jobs growth stalled}}}\uc2  this summer, prompting accusations that he is \u8220\'20\'1Cfiring the messenger\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US president claimed that Erika McEntarfer, commissioner of labor statistics, had \u8220\'20\'1Cfaked\u8221\'20\'1D employment figures in the run-up to last year\u8217\'20\'19s election, in an effort to boost \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chances of victory.\par \par \uc2 Trump later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114955222046259464"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s Jobs Numbers were RIGGED in order to make the Republicans, and ME, look bad\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He produced no evidence for these allegations, and insisted that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/useconomy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy}}}\uc2  was, in fact, \u8220\'20\'1CBOOMING\u8221\'20\'1D on his watch.\par \par \uc2 But Friday\u8217\'20\'19s employment figures told a very different story, and raised questions about the state of the labor market since Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need accurate Jobs Numbers,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote on Truth Social. \u8220\'20\'1CI have directed my Team to fire this Biden Political Appointee, IMMEDIATELY. She will be replaced with someone much more competent and qualified.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McEntarfer was contacted for comment. The \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  (\uc2 BLS\uc2 ) confirmed in a brief statement that she had been dismissed. William Wiatrowski, the agency\u8217\'20\'19s deputy commissioner, will serve as acting commissioner.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s abrupt announcement came as administration officials scrambled to explain a lackluster employment report. Not only did jobs growth fail to meet expectations in July, but previous estimates for May and June were revised significantly lower.\par \par \uc2 The president was promptly accused of trying to hide accurate statistics. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is firing the messenger because he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem to like jobs numbers that reflect how badly he\u8217\'20\'19s damaged the economy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lily Roberts, managing director for inclusive growth at the \uc2 Center for American Progress\uc2 , a thinktank.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPoliticizing our country\u8217\'20\'19s collection of data on what\u8217\'20\'19s going on in the economy \u8230\'20\'26 will make it harder to create an economy that makes sure everyone has a good job,\u8221\'20\'1D added Roberts. \u8220\'20\'1CBorrowing from the authoritarian playbook fuels more uncertainty that will cost Americans for years to come.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Paul Schroeder, executive director of the Council of Professional Associations on Federal Statistics, described the president\u8217\'20\'19s allegation as \u8220\'20\'1Cvery damaging and outrageous\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CNot only does it undermine the integrity of federal economic statistics but it also politicizes data which need to remain independent and trustworthy. This action is a grave error by the administration and one that will have ramifications for years to come.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McEntarfer is a widely respected economist and veteran employee of the federal government. She previously worked at the \uc2 US Census Bureau\uc2  under \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  and at the US census bureau under \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , Trump and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In January 2024, before McEntarfer\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation for her current post by the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , her nomination was backed by four former \uc2 BLS\uc2  commissioners.\par \par \uc2 In a letter also signed by organizations including the American Statistics Association and a string of senior economists, they said there were \u8220\'20\'1Cmany reasons\u8221\'20\'1D to confirm McEntarfer as commissioner of labor statistics, citing her \u8220\'20\'1Cwealth of research and statistical experience\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She was ultimately confirmed by a vote in the Senate, with 86 votes cast in favor and eight against.\par \par \uc2 Gene Sperling, chair of the national economic council under \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  and Obama, and who worked as an official under Biden, said he expected Trump to \u8220\'20\'1Cdestroy the credibility\u8221\'20\'1D of economic data when his administration suffered its first bad jobs report. \u8220\'20\'1CNow: first bad job report, and he just fired \uc2 BLS\uc2  head over absurd claims of bias,\u8221\'20\'1D Sperling wrote on X, formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s decision to fire McEntarfer was \u8220\'20\'1Coutrageous but not surprising\u8221\'20\'1D, said Julie Su, former acting US labor secretary under Biden. \u8220\'20\'1CHe hates facts, so he blames truth-tellers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US \u8220\'20\'1Cneeds and deserves trustworthy economic data\u8221\'20\'1D, added Su. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a pathetic attempt by the president to gaslight everyone about the consequences of his disastrous economic policies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250801el81006bv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
