\par\par \b \uc2 US adds just 73,000 jobs in July amid pressure from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s trade war\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 659 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 August 2025\par 23:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 July jobs growth slowed amid rising signs that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs are weighing on trade, prices and hiringUS politics live \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/useconomy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy}}}\uc2  added 73,000 jobs in July, far lower than expected, amid ongoing concerns with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/31/trump-extends-deadline-tariff-deal-mexico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 escalating}}}\uc2  trade war.\par \par \uc2 Forecasters surveyed by \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  had predicted the July jobs report would show a drop in added jobs to about 109,000. The unemployment rate rose to 4.2% from 4.1% in June.\par \par \uc2 The Bureau of Labor also slashed the number of jobs added in recent months. May\u8217\'20\'19s jobs figure was revised down by 125,000, from 144,000 to 19,000, and June was revised down by 133,000, from 147,000 to 14,000 \u8211\'20\'13 a combined 258,000 fewer jobs than previously reported.\par \par \uc2 Hours after the data was released, Trump announced that he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/aug/01/trump-fires-erika-mcentarfer-labor-statistics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 firing the federal government official}}}\uc2  in charge of labor statistics, claiming, without evidence, that Erika McEntarfer, commissioner of labor statistics, had \u8220\'20\'1Cfaked\u8221\'20\'1D employment figures ahead of last year\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 Healthcare and social assistance added 73,300 jobs over the month but growth was dragged down by more cuts to federal workers. Twelve thousand federal jobs were lost in July and federal employment is down by 84,000 since reaching a peak in January.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere was little to celebrate in the July Employment Report,\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas Ryan, North America economist for \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2 , wrote in a note to investors. He noted that the three-month average employment gain had now fallen to \u8220\'20\'1Ca troublingly low 35,000 \u8211\'20\'13 a figure that is difficult to interpret as anything other than a sign of hiring stalling, even as population growth slows.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shortly before the latest official jobs data was published, two Federal Reserve policymakers who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/jul/30/federal-reserve-interest-rates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broke ranks with its other officials on interest rates earlier this week}}}\uc2  released statements explaining their respective decisions.\par \par \uc2 The labor market \u8220\'20\'1Chas become less dynamic and shows increasing signs of fragility\u8221\'20\'1D, said \uc2 Michelle W Bowman\uc2 , Fed vice-chair for supervision and a Trump appointee. Putting off a rate cut \u8220\'20\'1Ccould result in a deterioration in the labor market and a further slowing in economic growth\u8221\'20\'1D, she added.\par \par \uc2 Christopher Waller\uc2 , another Trump appointee, said waiting before cutting rates was \u8220\'20\'1Coverly cautious\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI see no reason that we should hold the policy rate at its current level and risk a sudden decline in the labor market.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump, who has lambasted the Fed for months after it repeatedly opted to hold rates steady, welcomed the pair\u8217\'20\'19s official interventions \u8211\'20\'13 and called on the central bank\u8217\'20\'19s board to \u8220\'20\'1Cassume control\u8221\'20\'1D of policy if \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , the central bank\u8217\'20\'19s chair, refuses to cut rates.\par \par \uc2 The jobs report comes in a week packed with economic news. On Wednesday, the \uc2 Bureau of Economic Analysis\uc2  reported that gross domestic product, a broad measure of the US\u8217\'20\'19s economic health, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bea.gov/data/gdp/gross-domestic-product"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 grew at 3%}}}\uc2  in the last three months, up from a 0.5% decline in the first quarter.\par \par \uc2 The first quarter fall and second quarter bounceback were driven by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariff}}}\uc2  policies as businesses stocked up on imports ahead of the levies at the start of the year \u8211\'20\'13 which cut growth \u8211\'20\'13 and cut back on imports in the second \u8211\'20\'13 which boosted growth.\par \par \uc2 Taken together, the US economy grew at a sluggish 1.2% in the first six months of the year, down from the 2.5% average pace in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Also on Wednesday, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/federal-reserve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal Reserve}}}\uc2  announced it would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/jul/30/federal-reserve-interest-rates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not cut interest rates.}}}\uc2  The Fed is under {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/jul/24/trump-jerome-powell-federal-reserve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 intense pressure}}}\uc2  from Trump to cut rates but its chair said the central bank was still waiting to see what impact Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs will have on prices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHigher tariffs have begun to show through more clearly to prices of some goods, but their overall effects on economic activity and inflation remain to be seen,\u8221\'20\'1D Powell said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250801el810040i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
