\par\par \b \uc2 White House freezes $108m in funds to \uc2 Duke University\uc2  over affirmative action\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agency \par \uc2 776 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 July 2025\par 02:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Trump administration says North Carolina school violated Civil Rights Act by using racial preferences in hiring\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  has frozen $108m in federal research funding to \uc2 Duke University\uc2  after the federal government announced this week that it was investigating allegations that the school engaged in racial discrimination in the form of affirmative action, according to a person familiar with the matter and media reports.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Institutes of Health\uc2  reportedly halted the funding to the private university in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/northcarolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina}}}\uc2 , said the person who spoke to the Associated Press on Wednesday on the condition of anonymity to discuss internal deliberations. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2025/07/29/politics/trump-duke-freeze-funding-health-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc11.com/post/duke-university-being-investigated-us-department-education-law-journal-practices/17355992/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC News}}}\uc2  also reported the funding freeze.\par \par \uc2 The development came as, earlier this week, the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  and the Department of Education issued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hhs.gov/sites/default/files/duke-health-joint-letter.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a joint letter}}}\uc2  to Duke, stating that it had been made aware of allegations of what it called racial preferences in Duke\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Chiring, student admissions, governance, patient care, and other operations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Duke\uc2  is the latest institution to have its federal funding held up as the government investigates allegations of antisemitism and policies that support greater diversity, equity and inclusion that the Trump administration alleges are unlawful. It follows other investigations by the administration into top-flight private universities, including the Ivy League\u8217\'20\'19s Harvard, Columbia and Cornell.\par \par \uc2 Duke did not immediately comment on the reported funding freeze.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hhs.gov/sites/default/files/duke-health-joint-letter.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Monday\u8217\'20\'19s letter to Duke}}}\uc2 , the Trump administration states that it has been made aware of allegations that \uc2 Duke University\uc2  and Duke Health are engaged in practices that, \u8220\'20\'1Cif true, would violate Titles VI of the Civil Rights Act and Section 1557 of the Affordable Care Act, and render Duke Health unfit for any further financial relationship with the federal government\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese practices allegedly include illegal and wrongful racial preferences and discriminatory activity in recruitment, student admissions, scholarships and financial aid, mentoring and enrichment programs, hiring, promotion, and more,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter from the government states.\par \par \uc2 The letter does not provide any specific examples.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRacism is a scourge when practiced by individuals, but it is especially corrosive when enshrined in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most eminent and respected institutions,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter, signed by the US health secretary, Robert F Kennedy Jr, and the education secretary, Linda McMahon, adds.\par \par \uc2 The letter orders Duke to end any practices at its health system that give \u8220\'20\'1Cbenefits or advantages\u8221\'20\'1D based on race.\par \par \uc2 Saying Duke is unlikely to be capable of an \u8220\'20\'1Chonest and trustworthy review\u8221\'20\'1D, the letter takes the unusual step of requesting a new merit and civil rights committee that would be approved by the government and authorized by the school\u8217\'20\'19s board of trustees.\par \par \uc2 The panel would be tasked with identifying and ending any racial preferences. If problems remained after six months, the administration would pursue legal enforcement, the letter said.\par \par \uc2 The education department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ed.gov/about/news/press-release/us-department-of-education-initiates-investigation-duke-university-and-duke-law-journal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 separately opened an investigation into the Duke Law Journal on Monday}}}\uc2  over allegations that it gave advantages to prospective editors from underrepresented groups.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has used federal research funding as leverage in its unprecedented effort to reshape universities that Trump has described as hotbeds of liberalism.\par \par \uc2 It has presented a crisis for universities that rely on federal grants as a major source of revenue, spurring some to take on debt and find other ways to self-fund research.\par \par \uc2 Duke University\uc2  spent $1.5bn on research last year, with nearly 60% coming from federal sources, according to the university\u8217\'20\'19s website.\par \par \uc2 Even before the latest funding freeze, Duke faced financial turmoil. Last week, university leaders said almost 600 employees had accepted voluntary buyouts but that layoffs would still be needed. Officials said they needed to reduce costs amid uncertainty around federal research funding and a hike to the university\u8217\'20\'19s federal endowment tax.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has been ratcheting up pressure on universities in hopes of striking deals such as one that \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  signed last week.\par \par \uc2 The Ivy League school {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/23/columbia-university-220m-trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed to pay a $200m settlement }}}\uc2 over three years to the federal government and make changes to admissions, hiring, student discipline and more in exchange for regaining access to federal funding, among other things.\par \par \uc2 In exchange for Columbia\u8217\'20\'19s concessions, the White House will reinstate $400m in federal funding it had stripped from the university earlier this year over allegations that it allowed antisemitism to fester on campus.\par \par \uc2 The Columbia deal was met with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/24/columbia-university-deal-white-house-reactions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mixed reactions}}}\uc2  from students, faculty and alumni.\par \par \uc2 The administration has described it as a template for other universities including Harvard, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/2025/jul/21/harvard-trump-administrations-26bn-cuts-illegal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which has been in talks with the administration}}}\uc2  even as it battles the White House in court.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250730el7u006bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
