\par\par \b \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 CEO made 6,666 times more than his workers in 2024\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 478 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 July 2025\par 17:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 CEO pay climbs ahead of Trump tax windfall for wealthy, says report\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/starbucks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starbucks}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 CEO, \uc2 Brian Niccol\uc2 , made 6,666 times more than his average worker last year, according to a report on the growing gap between top executives and their workers.\par \par \uc2 The inequality gap between CEOs\u8217\'20\'19 pay and that of their median workers rose in 2024 to 285 to 1 from 268 to 1 in 2023, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/paywatch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  released this week by the largest federation of labor unions in the US, the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CEO pay rose {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/press/releases/new-afl-cio-report-nations-top-ceos-made-285-times-workers-pay-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 7%}}}\uc2  in 2024 among S&P 500 companies, an increase of $1.24m from 2023.\par \par \uc2 Niccol, who joined the company in September 2024, received more than $97.8m in total compensation in 2024. The typical \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  worker\u8217\'20\'19s pay was less than $15,000.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe median \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  worker would have had to start working for \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in 4643 BC (during the Stone Age!) just to earn what \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 CEO earned in 2024 alone,\u8221\'20\'1D the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/paywatch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  stated.\par \par \uc2 The report notes Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/01/senate-passes-big-beautiful-bill-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cbig, beautiful\u8221\'20\'1D reconciliation bill}}}\uc2  passed this year will hand the average CEO of an S&P 500 company a $489,118 tax cut, 639 times more than the median US worker.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCorporate CEOs are raking in millions, and now they\u8217\'20\'19ll get another kickback from President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  tax cut gift and anti-worker agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fred Redmond, secretary treasurer of the AFL-CIO.\u8220\'20\'1CTrump is paying for this handout to CEOs by cutting healthcare, food assistance and hundreds of thousands of jobs that depend on government investments.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://itep.org/top-1-to-receive-1-trillion-tax-cut-from-trump-megabill-over-next-decade/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysis}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Institute on Taxation and Economic Policy\uc2  found the top 1% of US families, by income, will collectively receive a tax cut of $1.02tn over the next decade as a result of the reconciliation bill.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  first ran for president criticizing exorbitant CEO pay, claiming he was going to raise taxes on them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou see these guys making these enormous amounts of money, and it\u8217\'20\'19s a total and complete joke,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in 2015 during an interview during his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/story/2015/09/trump-ceo-213584"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first presidential campaign}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThey pay very little tax, and that\u8217\'20\'19s going to end when I come out with my plan in about three weeks, could be sooner than that \u8230\'20\'26 We\u8217\'20\'19re going to be reducing taxes for the middle class. But for the hedge fund guys, they\u8217\'20\'19re going to be paying up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the wake of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2017 tax cuts, corporations saw {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://itep.org/corporate-taxes-before-and-after-the-trump-tax-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their tax rates fall}}}\uc2  from an average of 22% to 12.8% after the law went into effect.\par \par \uc2 Under his first presidential term, average CEO pay rose from $13.1m in December 2016 to $15.5m in December 2020. Corporate income tax collections {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/press/releases/afl-cio-releases-2019-executive-paywatch-report#:~:text=The%20AFL%2DCIO%20today%20released,Activision%20Blizzard%20and%20Delta%20Airlines."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropped}}}\uc2  in the wake of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2017 tax cuts by $93bn in 2018.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250724el7o004ee\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
