\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s a madhouse\u8217\'20\'19: US state department workers reeling after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s firings\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,418 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 July 2025\par 10:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 About 3,000 workers have left the agency through firings and buyouts in a move Democrats and staff call \u8216\'20\'18unlawful\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Workers at the US state department say firings, resignation buyouts, a proposed budget cut of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://federalnewsnetwork.com/workforce/2025/07/state-dept-layoffs-necessary-for-higher-quality-workforce-deputy-secretary-tells-lawmakers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 48%}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.state.gov/building-an-america-first-state-department"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reorganization }}}\uc2 under the Trump administration has left staff with low morale and will likely have long-term impacts.\par \par \uc2 Foreign programs and services aimed towards {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/nbc-out/out-politics-and-policy/government-agencies-scrub-lgbtq-web-pages-remove-info-trans-intersex-p-rcna190519"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LGBTQ+ communities}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/global-health-policy/fact-sheet/the-trump-administrations-foreign-aid-review-status-of-u-s-global-maternal-and-child-health-efforts/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 maternal and reproductive health}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/statedeptdeia?lang=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 minority groups}}}\uc2  have been removed or cut in place of far-right ideological policies being pursued by a 26-year-old senior adviser and Trump appointee at the agency.\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats and workers have criticized recent firings at the department, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/07/16/us/politics/senate-state-department-firings.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 characterizing}}}\uc2  them as \u8220\'20\'1Cunlawful\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Csloppy\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Crushed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 More than 1,350 employees at the state department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/11/state-department-layoffs-rif"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received}}}\uc2  Reduction In Force (Rif) notices on 11 July after the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/08/supreme-court-trump-federal-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lifted injunctions}}}\uc2  blocking the Trump administration from moving forward with them, about 15% of the domestic workforce.\par \par \uc2 Approximately 3,000 employees in total {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/11/state-department-layoffs-rif"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have left the agency}}}\uc2  through the Rif and early retirement or resignation buyouts.\par \par \uc2 During a Senate committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6OzJDAMr6j8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hearing}}}\uc2  on 16 July about the cuts, deputy secretary of state for management and resources, Michael Rigas, claimed: \u8220\'20\'1CThe 15% number that you referenced came from our initial assessment after consulting with the under secretaries,\u8221\'20\'1D and claimed \u8220\'20\'1Ccertainly\u8221\'20\'1D that there was an analysis done on the costs and benefits of the cuts.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/08/supreme-court-trump-federal-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court clears way for Trump officials to resume mass government firings}}}\par \par \uc2 Jose Mercado, who was recently laid off after working at the state department for 29 years, pushed back. \u8220\'20\'1CThere was no consulting. There was no analyzing. He is absolutely incorrect in the information that he provided, especially when answering Representative Meeks\u8217\'20\'19 last questioning. It was the least transparent process that you can ever imagine, and it was directed. It was not up to the undersecretaries. It was very directed from top down,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy law and by practice, this is why it\u8217\'20\'19s not supposed to happen this way,\u8221\'20\'1D added Mercado, who served as deputy director of the Bureau of Democracy, Human Rights and Labor\u8217\'20\'19s office of the western hemisphere affairs. \u8220\'20\'1CThis was not done within the confines of the law. The procedures were rewritten so they could do this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees\uc2 , the union for federal workers, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afge.org/article/layoffs-loom-at-the-state-department-raising-concerns-among-employees-and-diplomats/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  it is preparing legal challenges to the Reduction In Force at the state department.\par \par \uc2 A policy adviser at the state department, who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation, claimed veterans and employees with seniority or disabilities would not be terminated without being offered other positions, in addition to personnel who were set up to complete trainings with the \uc2 Department of Defense\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the \uc2 US Department of State\uc2  cited the supremecourt decision to permit Reduction In Forces by the Trump administration to move forward in arguing the reduction in force was lawful, though the court did not {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afge.org/article/supreme-court-clears-path-for-trump-administration-rifs-afge-vows-continued-fight/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 address the legality}}}\uc2  of the efforts.\par \par \uc2 They claimed the layoffs were in accordance with applicable law. They had no comment on any additional layoffs or the proposed budget cut.\par \par \uc2 Low morale and shifting policies to far-right ideologies\par \par \uc2 The policy adviser noted in recent months the morale at the department has sunk and a culture of \u8220\'20\'1Ckeeping your head down\u8221\'20\'1D has prevailed in anticipation of cuts. They also cited staffers were limited to what organizations or embassies they could meet with.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey were asking that any meetings we had were approved by senior leadership in the bureau, which was unheard of,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CBecause of the political sensitivities of this administration.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They said the cuts affect national security, given human rights and the diplomatic corps have been sidelined in favor of pushing far-right ideologies.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/may/14/trump-federal-layoffs-ripple-effect-us-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18So many are devastated\u8217\'20\'19: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s federal firings and their ripple effect}}}\par \par \uc2 They explained the annual human rights reports compiled by staffers and submitted to Congress by February had sections removed by Trump administration officials on anything related to maternal and reproductive health, LGBTQ+ rights, or minority groups because they don\u8217\'20\'19t fall into the administration\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica first\u8221\'20\'1D priority.\par \par \uc2 The advisor also cited a Trump political appointee as an example, Samuel Samson, 27, who wrote a recent \uc2 Substack{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/on-the-right-newsletter/415360/state-department-substack-samuel-samson-adrian-vermeule-integralism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 article}}}\uc2  published by the state department criticizing Europe for \u8220\'20\'1Cmass migration\u8221\'20\'1D and criticizing criminal investigations into far-right factions in the UK and Germany.\par \par \uc2 Samson has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.eu/article/us-state-department-adviser-proposed-funding-french-far-right-marine-le-pen-appeal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed}}}\uc2  the state department directly fund French far-right leader \uc2 Marine Le Pen\uc2 , who is currently facing embezzlement charges in France. And he recently went on a trip to South Africa, which the adviser said was also used as a family vacation.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the state department said the trip was to meet with government leaders and civil society about the Expropriation Act, which has been criticized as unfair to white landowners, the rights of white minorities in South Africa, and Trump administration priorities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re getting rid of people who are defending human rights across the world, and those are being cut to promote the type of ideology that is completely out of line with mainstream political and foreign policy thought,\u8221\'20\'1D the adviser said. \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2025/05/remigration-trump-state-department-removal-ethnic-cleansing/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re talking about \u8216\'20\'18remigration\u8217\'20\'19}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19, a far-right European concept of cleansing via mass deportations or promoting voluntary return of non white immigrants and their descendants. It\u8217\'20\'19s a madhouse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Long-term impacts of cuts\par \par \uc2 Mercado explained that after the 2024 presidential election, employees anticipated changes that are typical with changing presidential administrations, but were surprised when no guidance was being given to employees even once \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  assumed office in January 2025.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were not receiving any guidance whatsoever on what they wanted us to work on, which was, at the time, kind of strange, because we\u8217\'20\'19re used to getting that information relatively quickly,\u8221\'20\'1D Mercado said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe were getting excluded from a lot of the decision making and policy writing, action memos, information memos, so that the regular workflow that we were in, that started getting less and less brought into the fold.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Then when the administration came in, \uc2 USAID\uc2  was dismantled and rumors began swirling around on cuts at the US state department.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a hard pill to swallow once we found out that we were gone, but all of this time, it was understood that this was going to affect the civil service. A lot of folks did not think that the Foreign Service would get touched,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CWe served as a check and balance, we provided an outsider\u8217\'20\'19s view to an extent within the department. We understand you want to do x and y with nation z, but here are the things that you need to consider before you do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/19/trump-epa-layoffs-research-development"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s EPA eliminates research and development office and begins layoffs}}}\par \par \uc2 Mercado noted his department provided information and served as a counterbalance when the National Security Council and other high-level policymakers were looking into making decisions, especially in regard to nations with human rights issues to help improve those in order to facilitate \uc2 US government\uc2  and businesses and organizations from doing business with that country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe institutional knowledge that\u8217\'20\'19s lost in that, in the end, will affect the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D he said on the impacts of the cuts. \u8220\'20\'1CDiminished capabilities, weaker foreign policy and by getting rid of their watchdog, which you could consider us that when it comes to human rights and democracy, it now leaves the door open for unsavory business practices.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The policy adviser argued the national security risks posed by defunding and cutting staff at the state department, that have also been previously claimed by former Trump officials at the \uc2 Department of Defense\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re essentially destroying people\u8217\'20\'19s lives based on some capricious nature of this administration to impose and create some political ideology,\u8221\'20\'1D the advisor said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the \uc2 Department of Defense\uc2  has actually been the biggest critic of cuts at the State Department. \uc2 Gen Jim Mattis\uc2 , the former secretary of defense under Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/clip/senate-committee/user-clip-mattis-ammunition/4658822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said}}}\uc2  if you\u8217\'20\'19re not going to fund the state department, you need to buy me more bullets.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In 2013, during a Senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/clip/senate-committee/user-clip-mattis-ammunition/4658822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hearing}}}\uc2 , Mattis, as commander of the US Central Command, told senators: \u8220\'20\'1CThe more that we put into the state department\u8217\'20\'19s diplomacy, hopefully the less we have to put into a military budget.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the \uc2 US Department of State\uc2  claimed the layoffs and cuts preserved critical functions.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250721el7l001e4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
