\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Colleagues rally round California professor arrested during Ice raid on cannabis farm\b0\par\par\uc2 Victoria Clayton in Los Angeles \par \uc2 1,019 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 July 2025\par 20:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Witnesses dispute police account that John Caravello threw teargas canister at agent during raid that resulted in farm worker\u8217\'20\'19s death\par \par \uc2 Academics and colleagues are rallying around a California university professor who was arrested and charged with assaulting a federal officer during a chaotic immigration raid at a cannabis farm that resulted in a worker\u8217\'20\'19s death.\par \par \uc2 John Caravello, a math and philosophy professor at California State University Channel Islands, joined a crowd of protesters who confronted immigration agents when they arrived at Glass House cannabis farm in Camarillo, a community about 50 miles north of Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 He was among hundreds of people who were arrested at the Glass House facilities in Camarillo and nearby Carpinteria. Those swept up in the raids include protesters such as Caravello, approximately 360 farm workers, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/us-army-veteran-immigration-raid-53cb22251a01599a0c4d1a8d5650d050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a US military veteran}}}\uc2  who worked as a security guard. The sweeping operation has since attracted widespread scrutiny, particularly{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/14/jaime-alanis-california-ice-raid-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  after the death of a farm worker}}}\uc2  who fell from a greenhouse roof while attempting to hide from agents. The action is thought to be the largest raid in terms of arrests and the first death linked to the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s immigration crackdown in California.\par \par \uc2 Caravello, who volunteered as an organizer and immigrant advocate alongside his teaching work, is accused of throwing a teargas canister at law enforcement agents and \u8220\'20\'1Cassaulting, resisting, or impeding\u8221\'20\'1D officers, according to an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://keyt.b-cdn.net/2025/07/USA-v-Caravello-COMPLAINT.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 affidavit}}}\uc2 . But witnesses on the scene tell a different story.\par \par \uc2 Genevieve Flores-Haro, associate director of Oxnard-based Micop (Mixteco Indigena Community Organizing Project), knows Caravello and was among the demonstrators present when he was arrested. On Thursday morning, Flores-Haro said the phones of her team of immigrant rights activists began blowing up with reports from family and friends that agents with \uc2 US Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice) were at Glass House farms.\par \par \uc2 When they arrived on scene at the Camarillo farm just after 11am, Ice agents had already set up cones and yellow tape emblazoned with \u8220\'20\'1CCustoms and Border Protection\u8221\'20\'1D to block off the street. According to Flores-Haro, a crowd of demonstrators that eventually grew to around 200 people began chanting \u8220\'20\'1CChinga La Migra\u8221\'20\'1D, which loosely translates to \u8220\'20\'1CFuck Ice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Demonstrators also attempted to use their bodies to block the passage of Ice vans trying to leave with farm worker detainees. Instead of employing non-violent methods, says Flores-Haro, Ice agents brought out military-style vehicles and launched teargas into the crowd. Later, agents used additional teargas and rubber bullets against the demonstrators.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only teargas canisters that I saw thrown were by Ice agents and the national guard,\u8221\'20\'1D said Flores-Haro, who watched Caravello\u8217\'20\'19s arrest. Flores-Haro said Caravello appeared to be helping a fellow demonstrator who uses a wheelchair. She said she did not see him touch a canister, but some reports say Caravello attempted to remove a canister stuck beneath the demonstrator\u8217\'20\'19s wheelchair.\par \par \uc2 Flores-Haro said the demonstration was largely peaceful and described use of teargas by officers as unnecessary. \u8220\'20\'1CThere may have been a few people acting out, but it did not merit this show of force. I\u8217\'20\'19m an American citizen. I was born here. I\u8217\'20\'19m a taxpayer, I\u8217\'20\'19m a USC graduate. My taxpayer dollars were used by the federal government to shoot at me.\u8221\'20\'1D After being teargassed, Flores-Haro had difficulty breathing and is still experiencing a cough.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  (DHS) and Ice did not respond to multiple Guardian requests for comment about Caravello\u8217\'20\'19s arrest and witness accounts of what happened at the farm. Bill Essayli, the recently appointed 39-year-old US attorney for California\u8217\'20\'19s central district, who is known as Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s enforcer in the immigration battle in Los Angeles, posted on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/usattyessayli"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 X}}}\uc2  that Caravello was arrested for \u8220\'20\'1Cthrowing a teargas canister at law enforcement\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Flores-Haro said she and Caravello had spoken out at a Camarillo city council meeting the night before the raid took place. During {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=90VhVob-tns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 public comments}}}\uc2 , Caravello identified himself as a CSUCI professor and a longtime organizer with Ventura County Tenants Union and, more recently, a volunteer with VC Defensa, a coalition of local organizations dedicated to protecting immigrant and refugee populations in Ventura and Santa Barbara counties. He asked council members to stand up against Ice\u8217\'20\'19s presence in the community, noting that many of his students and their families were undocumented.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s my responsibility to protect them, and so I\u8217\'20\'19ve been patrolling the city streets following armed, masked thugs trying to kidnap my neighbors,\u8221\'20\'1D Caravello told the council.\par \par \uc2 Caravello was released on a $15,000 bond on Monday but still faces criminal charges, and is scheduled to be arraigned on 1 August.\par \par \uc2 When he walked free from the Los Angeles Metropolitan detention center earlier this week, a small crowd of supporters cheered, \u8220\'20\'1CJohn Caravello, you deserve a medal for standing up for the community\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a chant that brought tears to the professor\u8217\'20\'19s eyes.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Cal State Channel Islands said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are currently gathering additional information to fully understand the circumstances of the incident. At this time, it is our understanding that Professor Caravello was peacefully participating in a protest \u8211\'20\'13 an act protected under the first amendment and a right guaranteed to all Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Because his case is still pending, Caravello declined to comment, but a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.calfac.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California Faculty Association}}}\uc2  colleague, Theresa Monta\u241\'00\'F1o, said her friend was relieved to be released, yet still worries for other detainees. Families are still searching for the whereabouts of some farm workers and others have shown up in facilities as far away as El Paso, Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJohn is part of a labor union and activist organization,\u8221\'20\'1D said Monta\u241\'00\'F1o. \u8220\'20\'1CNot everyone has those networks to fight for them.\u8221\'20\'1D Monta\u241\'00\'F1o also said she was confident Caravello, who she described as \u8220\'20\'1Cbig-hearted\u8221\'20\'1D, will ultimately be cleared.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJohn is not guilty, and we have witnesses to attest to that,\u8221\'20\'1D says Monta\u241\'00\'F1o. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a seasoned organizer. He would never throw anything at a federal agent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250717el7h0030f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
