\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US undocumented farm workers feel \u8216\'20\'18hunted like animals\u8217\'20\'19 amid Trump\u8217\'20\'19s immigration raids\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,384 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2025\par 20:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ice raids have caused workers to lose hours and income, and forced them into hiding at home, according to interviews\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 <a href="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/09/construction-workers-builders-immigration-trump">Undocumented"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/09/construction-workers-builders-immigration-trump">Undocumented}}}\uc2  builders face exploitation amid Trump raids</a>\par \par \uc2 Undocumented farm workers feel they\u8217\'20\'19re being \u8220\'20\'1Chunted like animals\u8221\'20\'1D, they told the Guardian, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration ramps up its crackdown on immigration.\par \par \uc2 Raids by \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice) have caused workers to lose hours and income, and forced them into hiding at home, according to interviews.\par \par \uc2 With many US farms reliant on undocumented workers to function, the US president and his administration have sought to reassure their owners in recent months. But Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/5385223-trump-farmers-immigration-undocumented-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pledge}}}\uc2  to put farmers \u8220\'20\'1Cin charge\u8221\'20\'1D of immigration enforcement alarmed workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights advocates, who suggested they were being asked to surrender \u8220\'20\'1Ctheir freedom to their employer\u8221\'20\'1D just to stay in the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe really feel like we\u8217\'20\'19re being hunted, we\u8217\'20\'19re being hunted like animals,\u8221\'20\'1D said an undocumented farm worker in Ventura county, California, who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation.\par \par \uc2 An Ice raid at a cannabis farm in the county last week resulted in a worker suffering severe injuries after falling from a greenhouse and later dying. The raids sparked protests, with federal agents using smoke canisters in a bid to disperse a crowd of hundreds of protesters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t go out peacefully to do things, or go to work with any peace of mind anymore. We\u8217\'20\'19re stressed out and our kids are stressed out. No one is the same since these raids started,\u8221\'20\'1D the worker added. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are stressed and worrying if it continues like this, what are we going to do because the rent here is very expensive and it has affected us a lot. How are we going to make ends meet if this continues?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Abigail Jackson, a White House spokesperson, said: \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump is a tireless advocate for American farmers \u8211\'20\'13 they keep our families fed and our country prosperous. He trusts farmers and is committed to ensuring they have the workforce needed to remain successful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Department of Agriculture and Ice did not respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Most of the{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/racial-equity-and-health-policy/issue-brief/potential-implications-of-immigration-restrictions-on-the-u-s-agricultural-workforce/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  more than 2.6 million}}}\uc2  farm workers in the US are Hispanic, non-citizen immigrants. Around 40% of US farm workers are estimated to be undocumented.\par \par \uc2 Last month, the Trump administration called for Ice arrest quotas of 3,000 per day, up from 1,000. Following criticism of the raids, Trump claimed that changes were coming to how raids were conducted in agriculture, hospitality and food service, though a directive issued by Ice to stop targeting such sites was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/policywatch/trump-decides-to-pause-ice-raids-in-agriculture-meatpacking-and-hospitality-then-quickly-reverses-course/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reversed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump recently{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/5385223-trump-farmers-immigration-undocumented-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  claimed}}}\uc2  the administration is looking into legislation to defer immigration enforcement on farms to farmers. \u8220\'20\'1CFarmers, look, they know better. They work with them for years,\u8221\'20\'1D he said at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/5385223-trump-farmers-immigration-undocumented-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rally}}}\uc2  in Iowa on 3 July.\par \par \uc2 The US president is \u8220\'20\'1Cclearly\u8221\'20\'1D trying to give corporate leaders \u8220\'20\'1Cas close to slavery \u8230\'20\'26 that he can give to them,\u8221\'20\'1D claimed Rosalinda Guillen, a farm worker from Washington, community organizer and founder of the non-profit Community to Community. \u8220\'20\'1CGiving workers an opportunity who are already here in this country the ability to work and support their families and stay in this country by giving up their dignity and their freedom to their employer? If that isn\u8217\'20\'19t a definition of slavery, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know what is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has indicated that his administration could{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2025/07/03/politics/trump-migrant-farmworkers-deportations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  issue}}}\uc2  temporary passes to immigrant workers. \u8220\'20\'1CEven Trump consumes products being produced by farm workers, without realizing who produced these for him,\u8221\'20\'1D L\u225\'00\'E1zaro \u193\'00\'C1lvarez, a member of the Workers\u8217\'20\'19 Center of Central New York and Alianza Agr\u237\'00\'EDcola, who has worked on a farm for more than a decade, said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey have really demonized us with the word \u8216\'20\'18criminals\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D \u193\'00\'C1lvarez said. \u8220\'20\'1CDespite the fact we are undocumented, we pay taxes. We are invisible to the government until we pay taxes, and we don\u8217\'20\'19t receive any benefits.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Teresa Romero, president of \uc2 United Farm Workers\uc2 , a labor union representing farm workers, said: \u8220\'20\'1CEverything that he\u8217\'20\'19s doing to detain these workers is unconstitutional. They don\u8217\'20\'19t have a document signed by a judge. They don\u8217\'20\'19t have a court order. They want to just eliminate protections of farm workers who are currently here and have been working in the field for 20 to 30 years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese workers who have not committed any crime are being taken by people who are masked, are not wearing a uniform and don\u8217\'20\'19t have a marked vehicle, so they are essentially being kidnapped.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The impacts of these raids on farm workers will reverberate, Romero warned, from the communities being affected to consumers who rely on the work of farm workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of fear of going to work,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Sarait Martinez, executive director of Centro Binacional para el Desarrollo Ind\u237\'00\'EDgena Oaxaque\u241\'00\'F1o (CBDIO), which works in the Central valley and on the central coast of California with Indigenous farmworkers. She added that family dynamics among farm workers have been changing due to the Ice raids, as parents will alternate between who goes to work and who stays home with the children, to ensure they aren\u8217\'20\'19t both arrested, and separated from their children.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis administration is targeting and just racially profiling anyone at this point that is brown, and it\u8217\'20\'19s intimidating workers,\u8221\'20\'1D said Martinez. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a broader agenda of this administration, who and how they want workers to be employed in the country, and I think we need to be aware of that, and we need to be organizing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Luis Jim\u233\'00\'E9nez, an undocumented farm worker in central New York for 21 years, said the raids have affected the mental health of many undocumented farm workers. ea05a110-2f0f-41ea-ba0a-8d9189dbddb7\par \par \uc2 The best public interest journalism relies on first-hand accounts from people in the know.\par \par \uc2 If you have something to share on this subject you can contact us confidentially using the following methods.\par \par \uc2 Secure Messaging in the Guardian app\par \par \uc2 The Guardian app has a tool to send tips about stories. Messages are end to end encrypted and concealed within the routine activity that every Guardian mobile app performs. This prevents an observer from knowing that you are communicating with us at all, let alone what is being said.\par \par \uc2 If you don't already have the Guardian app, download it ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.apple.com/app/the-guardian-live-world-news/id409128287"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 iOS}}}\uc2 /{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.guardian"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Android}}}\uc2 ) and go to the menu. Select \u8216\'20\'18Secure Messaging\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 SecureDrop, instant messengers, email, telephone and post\par \par \uc2 See our guide at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tips"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 theguardian.com/tips}}}\uc2  for alternative methods and the pros and cons of each.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of people come here to work and their families back home depend on the work and the support of them, so it would be a tragedy if they were arrested and deported,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t know who is going to report us or at what moment if we go out we will be reported to Ice because of the propaganda the federal government has been carrying out against the immigrant community.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are many people who are racist but do not realize it affects them, too,\u8221\'20\'1D added Jim\u233\'00\'E9nez. \u8220\'20\'1CThe immigrant community and migrant labor supports the agricultural industry and makes the economy grow. And if the economy is good, then those people are better off financially.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd there are people who don\u8217\'20\'19t care about that because of the simple fact of wanting to get immigrants out of this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Back in Ventura county, the undocumented farm worker warned of far-reaching consequences should Trump press ahead with his crackdown. \u8220\'20\'1CIf there are no immigrants, there is no food, there are no houses, no hotels, no people who do the work in restaurants,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CWithout us, food is going to be more expensive. We\u8217\'20\'19re essential.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe worked through Covid. We worked through the wildfires in Los Angeles. We get up at 4am every day. No one else is willing to work the eight-, 10-hour days the way we do. We\u8217\'20\'19re not criminals. We\u8217\'20\'19re hardworking people trying to give our kids a better life. And we contribute a lot to this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250714el7e0018p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
