\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump news at a glance: state department plans mass layoffs in line with president\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18America First\u8217\'20\'19 policy\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff \par \uc2 860 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 July 2025\par 03:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Nearly 15% of domestic workforce to be let go in major restructuring of diplomatic corps \u8211\'20\'13 key US politics stories from Thursday 10 July\par \par \uc2 The state department has announced that it plans to move forward with mass layoffs as part of the most significant restructuring of America\u8217\'20\'19s diplomatic corps in decades. Officials say the cuts will align their mission with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica First\u8221\'20\'1D vision.\par \par \uc2 The layoffs, which are commonly called reductions in force (or RIFs), along with voluntary redundancies, will affect nearly 15% of the state department\u8217\'20\'19s domestic staff. A senior department official said that was close to 1,800 people. The restructuring will also see several hundred bureaus merged or eliminated entirely.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in the courts, a judge has blocked Trump\u8217\'20\'19s birthright citizenship order and certified a class-action lawsuit, one of many challenging the order.\par \par \uc2 Here are the key {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  stories at a glance:\par \par \uc2 State department to push ahead with mass layoffs\par \par \uc2 The state department has gone forward with the layoffs, which were long expected, after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/08/supreme-court-trump-federal-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court sided}}}\uc2  this week with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  against a federal judge\u8217\'20\'19s hold on plans for mass government firings that could affect hundreds of thousands of federal employees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the coming days, the department will be communicating to individuals affected by the reduction in force,\u8221\'20\'1D read a memo attributed to Michael Rigas, the deputy secretary for management and resources, announcing the layoffs. \u8220\'20\'1CFirst and foremost, we want to thank them for their dedication and service to the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/10/birthright-citizenship-trump-order-paused"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story}}}\par \par \uc2 Judge blocks Trump\u8217\'20\'19s birthright citizenship order\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempt to end {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/15/what-is-birthright-citizenship-supreme-court-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 birthright citizenship}}}\uc2  suffered a courtroom defeat on Thursday as a federal judge in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-hampshire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Hampshire}}}\uc2  blocked the controversial executive order nationwide and certified a sweeping class-action lawsuit that could protect tens of thousands of children.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/10/birthright-citizenship-trump-order-paused"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story}}}\par \par \uc2 Brazil to retaliate against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 50% tariff threat\par \par \uc2 Brazil is drawing up plans to hit back against 50% US tariffs on the country\u8217\'20\'19s exports, setting the stage for further escalation in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s trade war with Latin America\u8217\'20\'19s largest economy.\par \par \uc2 The US president vowed to impose steep duties on Brazilian goods on Wednesday, accusing the country of conducting a \u8220\'20\'1Cwitch hunt\u8221\'20\'1D against its previous president, \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2 , who is facing a trial over his attempt to overturn his 2022 election defeat.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/10/brazil-trump-tariff-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story}}}\par \par \uc2 US will impose 35% blanket tariffs on Canadian imports, Trump says in letter\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said on Thursday the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/10/us-canada-tariffs-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US would impose a 35% tariff on imports from Canada }}}\uc2 next month and planned to impose blanket tariffs of 15% or 20% on most other trade partners.\par \par \uc2 In a letter released on his social media platform, Trump told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/mark-carney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Carney}}}\uc2 , the Canadian prime minister, the new rate would go into effect on 1 August and would go up if Canada retaliated.\par \par \uc2 Mahmoud Khalil files $20m claim against Trump officials\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mahmoud-khalil"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mahmoud Khalil}}}\uc2 , the \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  graduate and Palestinian activist who was detained by the Trump administration for months, have filed a claim for $20m in damages, alleging Khalil was falsely imprisoned, maliciously prosecuted and smeared as an antisemite as the government sought to deport him over his prominent role in campus protests.\par \par \uc2 The filing \u8211\'20\'13 a precursor to a lawsuit \u8211\'20\'13 names the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , \uc2 US Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  and the state department. \u8220\'20\'1CThey are abusing their power because they think they are untouchable,\u8221\'20\'1D Khalil said. \u8220\'20\'1CUnless they feel there is some sort of accountability, it will continue to go unchecked.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/10/mahmoud-khalil-trump-ice-damages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s inaugural fund received $19m from fossil fuel industry\par \par \uc2 The fossil fuel sector poured more than $19m into the president\u8217\'20\'19s inaugural fund, accounting for nearly 8% of all donations it raised, a new analysis shows, raising concerns about the White House\u8217\'20\'19s relationship with big oil.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/10/trump-inaugural-fund-fossil-fuel-industry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story}}}\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  offices begin rejecting Medicaid\par \par \uc2 At least two regional {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/planned-parenthood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planned Parenthood}}}\uc2  affiliates have notices on their websites telling patients that, due to a provision in Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 new tax-and-spending bill that \u8220\'20\'1Cdefunds\u8221\'20\'1D the reproductive healthcare giant, they can no longer accept Medicaid.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/10/planned-parenthood-medicaid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story}}}\par \par \uc2 What else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Six Secret Service agents {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/10/trump-assassination-attempt-secret-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have been suspended}}}\uc2  without pay after the assassination attempt against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at a Pennsylvania rally last July.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Federal immigration officials carrying out raids on two southern California cannabis farms {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/10/federal-agents-raid-farms-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clashed with protesters}}}\uc2  , firing chemical munitions to disperse the crowd.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/10/sean-duffy-nasa-trump-appointment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appointed his transportation secretary}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Sean Duffy\uc2 , as interim administrator of \uc2 Nasa\uc2 , six weeks after withdrawing the nomination of an \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  ally for the role.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Explained: why is Trump going after Brazil? Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/10/trump-lula-tariffs-brazil-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what you need to know}}}\uc2  about the tariff spat.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2  special rapporteur investigating abuses in Gaza, Francesca Albanese, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jul/11/francesca-albanese-un-gaza-investigator-us-sanctions-guilt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has responded}}}\uc2  to being sanctioned by the Trump administration, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cthe powerful punishing those who speak for the powerless, it is not a sign of strength, but of guilt\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Catching up? Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/10/trump-administration-news-today-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 9 July 2025}}}\uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250711el7b000b8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
