\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US agriculture secretary says Medicaid recipients can replace deported farm workers\b0\par\par\uc2 Joseph Gedeon in Washington \par \uc2 470 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 July 2025\par 20:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Brooke Rollins\uc2  also claimed automation can replace the immigrant labor force despite repeated evidence of failure\par \par \uc2 The US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/agriculture"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agriculture}}}\uc2  secretary has suggested that increased automation and forcing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/medicaid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Medicaid}}}\uc2  recipients to work could replace the migrant farm workers being swept up in Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mass deportation campaign, despite years of evidence and policy failures that those kinds of measures are not substitutes for the immigrant labor force underpinning American agriculture.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a news conference with Republican governors on Tuesday, \uc2 Brooke Rollins\uc2  said the administration would rely on \u8220\'20\'1Cautomation, also some reform within the current governing structure\u8221\'20\'1D, and pointed to \u8220\'20\'1C34 million able-bodied adults in our Medicaid program\u8221\'20\'1D as potential workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s been a lot of noise in the last few days and a lot of questions about where the president stands and his vision for farm labor,\u8221\'20\'1D Rollins said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are plenty of workers in America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump signed legislation on Friday creating the first federally mandated work requirements for Medicaid recipients, set to take effect by the end of 2026. Medicaid is a healthcare safety net program that currently covers pregnant women, mothers, young children and the disabled, with 40 states having expanded coverage to working poor families earning up to 138% of the federal poverty level.\par \par \uc2 However, agricultural experts and economists have repeatedly warned that neither automation nor welfare reforms can realistically replace the migrant workforce that dominates American farming.\par \par \uc2 According {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ers.usda.gov/topics/farm-economy/farm-labor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to USDA data}}}\uc2 , 42% of US farm workers are undocumented immigrants, and just under 70% are foreign-born.\par \par \uc2 And a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.urban.org/research/publication/assessing-potential-coverage-losses-among-medicaid-expansion-enrollees-under"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March report}}}\uc2  from the Urban Institute found that most Medicaid recipients are either already working, exempt or face some sort of instability.\par \par \uc2 Previous state-level immigration crackdowns are also evidence of the challenges facing Rollins\u8217\'20\'19s proposed solution. Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s 2011 immigration law resulted in a shortage of more than 5,200 farm workers and projected losses of hundreds of millions of dollars at the time, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.farmprogress.com/management/studies-surveys-confirm-georgia-farm-labor-losses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 University of Georgia study}}}\uc2 . Alabama farmers reported similar struggles, with locals {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tucson.com/news/national/article_d8c03670-96da-5508-8dec-972087beffb8.html?utm_source=tucson.com&utm_medium=js_redirect&utm_campaign=invalid_source"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 telling the Associated Press}}}\uc2  in 2011 that American workers lasted about a day at their new farm jobs.\par \par \uc2 While agricultural automation is advancing fast, it still {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/automation-tractors-robots-agriculture-labor-workforce-farming-df6087837925c14cfdd7ad2f80410a54"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears to remain years away}}}\uc2  from replacing manual labor in fruit and vegetable harvesting.\par \par \uc2 Rollins acknowledged the administration must be \u8220\'20\'1Cstrategic\u8221\'20\'1D in implementing deportations \u8220\'20\'1Cso as not to compromise our food supply\u8221\'20\'1D, but held that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s promise of a \u8220\'20\'1C100% American workforce stands.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump himself appeared to soften his stance last week, telling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/trump-urges-temporary-pass-from-immigration-crackdown-key-industries-i-cherish-our-farmers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News}}}\uc2  he was considering exemptions for undocumented farm workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19re going to do is we\u8217\'20\'19re going to do something for farmers where we can let the farmer sort of be in charge,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250709el79002gy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
FF
