\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Undocumented builders face unchecked exploitation amid Trump raids: \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s more work, less pay\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,159 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 July 2025\par 19:11 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In a new series on undocumented workers, construction laborers talk about how fear is fueling wage theft and workplace abuse\par \par \uc2 As the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  ramps up its crackdown on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/usimmigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigration}}}\uc2 , undocumented workers in the construction industry claim raids and arrests have emboldened some contractors to cut pay and increase hours.\par \par \uc2 Rogelio, a tile setter, works for various contractors in the the Tucson, Arizona, region. He is undocumented, and did not provide his full name.\par \par \uc2 When {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  returned to office in January, Rogelio said his employers cut their rates by 30% to 40%. Other laborers told him they had endured similar treatment.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/16/home-depot-ice-raids-los-angeles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 At Home Depot, Ice raids terrorize the workers who helped build LA: \u8216\'20\'18They just come and grab you\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey decreased the pay by piece because they know most of the tile setters don\u8217\'20\'19t have social security numbers, so they take advantage of that. We are in their hands,\u8221\'20\'1D Rogelio told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s more work, less pay. We have no choice right now.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re struggling with bills. We\u8217\'20\'19re struggling with food. We\u8217\'20\'19re struggling with everything because we don\u8217\'20\'19t get enough money to pay whatever we need to pay.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many of the undocumented immigrants Rogelio knows are only leaving home to work, Rogelio said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a lot of fear,\u8221\'20\'1D he told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CWe look for news in the morning to see if we\u8217\'20\'19re able to go to work or not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With approximately 2.9 million US construction workers \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/17/immigrant-workers-trump-deportation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 34% of the workforce}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 foreign-born, construction sector lobbyists have publicly urged the Trump administration to soften their hardline stance on immigration. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the need for safe and secure borders is paramount, mass deportation is not the answer,\u8221\'20\'1D Buddy Hughes, chairperson of the \uc2 National Association of Home Builders\uc2 , said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Advocates for workers rights say some operators in the sector are using Trump\u8217\'20\'19s crackdown to abuse undocumented workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEspecially in construction, there\u8217\'20\'19re a lot of subcontractors that take advantage of this situation by not paying them the fair wage or not even paying them at all,\u8221\'20\'1D said Laura Becerra, movement politics director of the non-profit Workers Defense Project based in Texas.\par \par \uc2 Undocumented workers are unlikely to lodge an official complaint, she added. \u8220\'20\'1CSince people don\u8217\'20\'19t want to say anything because they don\u8217\'20\'19t want to be put on the radar, and they\u8217\'20\'19re also getting retaliated against if they do say something.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The administration is pushing ahead with public raids on undocumented immigrant workers. The \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice) agency is arresting an increasing number of immigrants without any criminal history, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/24/trump-immigrants-ice-arrests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian analysis of federal government data}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s an attack,\u8221\'20\'1D Becerra said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s taking a toll on families, families that need to make ends meet, that are already suffering from low wages and doing work no one wants to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Tucson, undocumented workers are avoiding freeways, according to Rogelio. \u8220\'20\'1CFreeways are one of the worst places to drive right now because of all the police and border patrol and they look for mostly hispanic people to stop,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are living day by day and not knowing what\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen tomorrow.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In some areas \u8220\'20\'1Cthere are spots where you can work with no problem,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut others, there are racist people living there and they don\u8217\'20\'19t want us. They want our work, they want cheap labor, but they don\u8217\'20\'19t want us.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe came here because we want to work and provide for our families. The only reason I\u8217\'20\'19m here, personally, I have two kids who are American citizens. I\u8217\'20\'19m not asking for any benefits from the government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reports from across the US suggest undocumented workers are facing unprecedented pressure.\par \par \uc2 Savannah Palmira, director of organizing for the \uc2 International Union of Painters and Allied Trades\uc2  district council 5, which covers workers in states around the Pacific north-west, said the threat of raids is making it harder for workers to organize.\par \par \uc2 A roofing company in Washington was raided by \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice) earlier this year after workers filed safety complaints, Palmira claimed, with the fear of retaliation stemming from that case spreading to other job sites, and leaving workers reluctant to speak out and file complaints against abusive work practices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat contractors are doing is taking an opportunity to not be held accountable for their bad practices,\u8221\'20\'1D said Palmira. \u8220\'20\'1CThe more and more people are starting to talk about workers getting taken advantage of, Ice is getting called on them. They\u8217\'20\'19re taking a tool away from us to be able to put bad contractors on notice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Washington, another undocumented construction worker \u8211\'20\'13 who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation \u8211\'20\'13 said many of his coworkers were \u8220\'20\'1Cthinking about going back to their countries\u8221\'20\'1D due to the reality of life in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe last company I worked for took advantage of people in every situation,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, from dissuading injured workers from getting medical attention to denying overtime and breaks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey say, you are undocumented, so they will pay you $10 an hour because you have no work permit,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd if not, they will tell Ice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Washington state, immigrants make up 25% of the trades workforce in construction. With a consistent labor shortage and demand for housing constantly growing, residential construction needs all the skilled workers available,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesperson for the Building Industry Association of Washington said in an email. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve provided our members with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.biaw.com/news/be-prepared-when-ice-visits-your-jobsite"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guidance on how to legally employ immigrants}}}\uc2 , including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ice.gov/sites/default/files/documents/Document/2015/i9-guidance.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 verifying the identity and US employment authorization}}}\uc2  of all employees. We also generally support improving US Immigration policy to allow responsible and law-abiding undocumented worker a pathway to achieving citizenship.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Arizona Builders Alliance did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 On a national level the construction industry has repeatedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nahb.org/advocacy/industry-issues/labor-and-employment/immigration-reform-is-key-to-building-a-skilled-workforce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  of the negative impacts of immigration raids on what they claim has already been a severe labor shortage in US construction.\par \par \uc2 Asked about contractors allegedly using the ramp up in immigration enforcement to cut pay and increase workloads, the \uc2 National Association of Home Builders\uc2  issued a statement from Hughes, its chairperson, which did not directly address the claims.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith the construction industry facing a deficit of more than 200,000 workers, policymakers must consider that any disruption to the labor force would raise housing costs, limit supply and worsen the nation\u8217\'20\'19s housing affordability crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D Hughes said. \u8220\'20\'1CTo address this pressing national issue, \uc2 NAHB\uc2  is urging Congress to support meaningful investments in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s education system to encourage students to pursue careers in the skilled trades.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPolicymakers should also support sensible immigration policies that preserve and expand existing temporary work visa programs while also creating new market-based visa programs that will accurately match demand with available labor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250709el79001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
