ries tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 The president said seven countries would be named in the morning, with others coming in the afternoon.\par \par \uc2 The news comes after the president published tariff letters directed to 14 other countries on his social media account yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-09T01:22:56.753Z">at 2.22am BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-09T00:36:50.087Z">1.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Though overall inflation has not hit the predicted heights, the prices of used cars are ticking up across the US amid tariff-driven market volatility, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/autos-transportation/us-used-car-prices-surge-tariffs-drive-market-volatility-2025-07-09/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to the news outlet:\par \par \uc2 The Manheim Used Vehicle Value Index rose 1.6% in June from May on a seasonally adjusted basis and surged 6.3% from a year earlier, the largest year-over-year increase since August 2022, according to data released on Tuesday. At 208.5, the index has been trending upward for a year and is now at its highest since October 2023.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-09T01:32:36.908Z">at 2.32am BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-09T00:15:25.040Z">1.15am BST\par \par \uc2 A federal judge in Colorado has dismissed a case filed by survivors and family members of people killed during a November 2022 mass shooting at Club Q in Colorado Springs.\par \par \uc2 The 12 plaintiffs claimed that El Paso county and its former sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s failure to enforce the state red flag law allowed the shooter, who\u8217\'20\'19d had run-ins with the law and talked about aspiring to be a mass shooter, to carry out the attack that killed five people and injured another 19.\par \par \uc2 The judge said that though the sheriff and county commissioner are not being found legally liable: \u8220\'20\'1CTheir collective role in refusing to at least try to thwart what most likely was a horrific but preventable tragedy should weigh heavily on their individual consciences, and most certainly will not be forgotten by the people of Colorado.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more background on the shooting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courthousenews.com/sheriff-skirts-suit-over-failing-to-use-red-flag-law-before-club-q-attack/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-09T01:30:40.190Z">at 2.30am BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T23:58:42.164Z">12.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump administration officials met with their Qatari counterparts at the White House ahead of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s meeting with Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , the Associated Press reports, citing an anonymous White House official.\par \par \uc2 The teams discussed ceasefire and hostage negotiations in the war on Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-09T00:02:15.155Z">at 1.02am BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T23:51:57.656Z">12.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Despite receiving permission from the Trump administration to hire more employees, the National Weather Service never posted 126 vacancies to the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s hiring website, Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2025/07/08/national-weather-service-help-wanted-ads-not-posted-00442033"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The news comes in the wake of catastrophic flooding of the Guadalupe River in Texas. Although the National Weather Service accurately forecast the flood, staffing shortages may impact the agency\u8217\'20\'19s ability to respond to future disasters, officials told Politico.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CConsidering that there are critical staff shortages at NWS weather forecast offices across the country and the president of the United States has given NWS leadership permission to hire 126 replacements, it begs the question why the Department of Commerce has not implemented a presidential directive,\u8221\'20\'1D Tom Fahy, the legislative director for the National Weather Service employees organization, the union that represents many NWS staffers, told Politico.\par \par \uc2 Almost 600 employees have left the agency in recent months, following \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to shrink the federal government.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-09T00:00:40.344Z">at 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T23:32:37.197Z">12.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Despite trying to pay his bond, Atlanta-based Spanish-language journalist Mario Guevara remains in federal custody.\par \par \uc2 Guevara was arrested while covering a protest in mid-June, and detained by Immigrations and Customs Enforcement. Last week, an immigration judge granted him bond, which would have allowed him to leave the George immigration detention facility where he was being held.\par \par \uc2 Despite trying to pay the $7,500 bond, Guevara\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer says Ice did not accept Guevara\u8217\'20\'19s payment.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/08/journalist-ice-custody-mario-guevara-atlanta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Spanish-language journalist still in Ice custody despite being granted bond}}}\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T23:07:44.166Z">12.07am BST\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration will continue phasing out the last type of asbestos legally allowed in US manufacturing, the Associated Press reports, citing an \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  court filing today.\par \par \uc2 The administration had previously planned to allow manufacturers to continue using chrysotile asbestos, despite a Biden-era ban on the chemical. In a court filing last month, it had said parts of the ban went \u8220\'20\'1Cbeyond what is necessary to eliminate the unreasonable risk\u8221\'20\'1D. Following outcry from asbestos opponents, however, the administration has shifted course.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T23:53:08.999Z">at 12.53am BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T22:44:36.851Z">11.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Eight men have been deported to South Sudan from the United States, following a supreme court ruling last month allowing the Trump administration to deport migrants to countries not their own, the Associated Press reports. Only one is from South Sudan.\par \par \uc2 Apuk Ayuel, a spokesperson for the \uc2 South Sudanese foreign ministry\uc2 , confirmed that the men are now in Sudan and said that they are \u8220\'20\'1Cunder the care of the relevant authorities who are screening them and ensuring their safety and well-being\u8221\'20\'1D. He did not share where the men are being held.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s my colleague Maanvi Singh with more on the case:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/03/us-supreme-court-south-sudan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court clears way for deportations of eight men to South Sudan}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T22:46:18.126Z">at 11.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T22:27:40.183Z">11.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York City mayor \uc2 Eric Adams\uc2  accused of corruption by four ex-officers\par \par \uc2 New York City mayor \uc2 Eric Adams\uc2  faces lawsuits filed today by four former high-ranking police officers accusing the embattled Democrat of promoting corruption in the police department, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/07/08/nyregion/nypd-corruption-lawsuits-adams.html?smid=nytcore-ios-share&referringSource=articleShare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In his lawsuit, one of the former officers, former chief of detectives and 40-year force veteran James Essig , claims that the former commissioner of the \uc2 NYPD\uc2  sold promotions to the tune of $15,000. Essig says he was forced to resign after objecting to the practice.\par \par \uc2 Essig\u8217\'20\'19s suit adds that senior \uc2 NYPD\uc2  leadership