 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Joseph Gedeon with the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/08/court-click-to-cancel-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US court strikes down \u8216\'20\'18click-to-cancel\u8217\'20\'19 rule designed to make unsubscribing easier}}}\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, a federal judge ruled against five non-profit organizations that sued the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  over the rescinding of hundreds of millions of dollars meant to prevent and respond to issues such as gun violence, substance abuse and hate crimes.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton with more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/08/judge-trump-cuts-court-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge says Trump cuts to anti-violence groups \u8216\'20\'18shameful\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 but can\u8217\'20\'19t stop them}}}\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T21:48:55.823Z">10.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling today will allow the Trump administration to proceed with its plans to layoff vast swaths of federal workers. The impacted agencies will include: the US Departments of Agriculture, Commerce, Health and Human Services, State, Treasury and Veterans Affairs.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T21:55:15.830Z">at 10.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T21:31:59.733Z">10.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pam Bondi, the attorney general, applauded the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling today allowing the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s mass federal layoffs to proceed.\par \par \uc2 Writing on social media, Bondi said: \u8220\'20\'1CToday, the Supreme Court stopped lawless lower courts from restricting President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s authority over federal personnel.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow, federal agencies can become more efficient than ever before,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T21:43:36.134Z">at 10.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T21:20:58.217Z">10.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling to allow \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s mass federal layoffs to continue \u8220\'20\'1Cdealt a serious blow to our democracy and puts services that the American people rely on in grave jeopardy \u8221\'20\'1D, the unions, non-profits and local governments that filed the lawsuit said in a statement today.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs added that the court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not change the simple and clear fact that reorganizing government functions and laying off federal workers en masse haphazardly without any congressional approval is not allowed by our constitution\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T21:42:59.098Z">at 10.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T21:11:02.833Z">10.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 It appears that Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  has arrived at the White House for his closed-door meeting with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A White House pool reporter says that Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s motorcade has arrived, though press did not see Netanyahu enter the White House as he used a different entrance.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T21:08:33.232Z">10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Travelers will soon be able to keep their shoes on while traversing US airport security, the Homeland Security secretary \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  announced today, in a reversal of a nearly two decades old policy.\par \par \uc2 In a press conference at Reagan airport today, Noem announced the new \uc2 Transportation Security Administration\uc2  policy, which she said she hoped would make travel to the United States easier ahead of the Olympics, World Cup and 250th anniversary of the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Golden Age of America is here,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re so excited that we can make the experience for those individuals traveling throughout our airports in the United States more hospitable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The TSA policy requiring travelers to remove their footwear dates back to 2006.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T21:44:46.397Z">at 10.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T20:53:16.704Z">9.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s scheduled meeting with Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  is starting later than the announced 4 .30pm ET start time. We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you the top lines once it begins.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T21:44:56.021Z">at 10.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T20:40:18.533Z">9.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Liberal Justice \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2  was the sole member of the Supreme Court to dissent in the court\u8217\'20\'19s recent ruling clearing the way for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration to resume mass job cuts and the restructuring of federal agencies.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/24A1174"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her dissent}}}\uc2 , Jackson criticized the court\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Centhusiasm for greenlighting this President\u8217\'20\'19s legally dubious actions in an emergency posture\u8221\'20\'1D and called the decision \u8220\'20\'1Chubristic and senseless\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She warned that the administration\u8217\'20\'19s actions \u8220\'20\'1Cpromises mass employee terminations, widespread cancellation of federal programs and services, and the dismantling of much of the Federal Government as Congress has created it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T21:45:20.036Z">at 10.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T20:26:45.017Z">9.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  is headed to Malaysia this week, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reports. The trip will mark the secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s first visit to Asia, which comes as the White House has just announced steep tariffs on goods imported from many other Asian nations.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  announced 25% tariffs on goods from Malaysia, and equal or higher tariffs on goods from Japan, South Korea, Indonesia, Bangladesh, Cambodia, Thailand, Laos and Myanmar.\par \par \uc2 Relatedly, Howard Lutnick, the commerce secretary, told CNBC today that US officials will meet with their Chinese counterparts to discuss trade between the two countries next month.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T20:38:23.921Z">at 9.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T19:53:27.355Z">8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court lifts order blocking Trump's mass federal layoffs\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has cleared the way for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration to resume carrying out mass job cuts and the restructuring of agencies, key elements of his campaign to downsize and reshape the federal government.\par \par \uc2 The justices lifted San Francisco-based US district judge Susan Illston\u8217\'20\'19s 22 May order that had blocked large-scale federal layoffs called \u8220\'20\'1Creductions in force\u8221\'20\'1D affecting potentially hundreds of thousands of jobs, while litigation in the case proceeds.\par \par \uc2 Workforce reductions were planned at the US departments of agriculture, commerce, health and human services, state, treasury, veterans affairs and more than a dozen other agencies.\par \par \uc2 Illston wrote in her ruling that Trump had exceeded his authority in ordering the downsizing, siding with a group of unions, non-profits and local governments that challenged the administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs history demonstrates, the president may broadly restructure federal agencies only when authorized by Congress,\u8221\'20\'1D Illston wrote.\par \par \uc2 The judge blocked the agencies from carrying out mass layoffs and limited their ability to cut or overhaul federal programs. She also ordered the reinstatement of workers who had lost their jobs, though she delayed implementing this portion of her ruling while the appeals process plays out.\par \par \uc2 Illston\u8217\'20\'19s ruling was the broadest of its kind against the government overhaul being pursued by Trump and Doge .\par \par \uc2 The San Francisco-based ninth US circuit court of appeals in a 2-1 ruling on 30 May denied the administration\u8217\'20\'19s request to halt the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling.\par \par \uc2 It said the administration had not shown that it would suffer an irreparable injury if the judge\u8217\'20\'19s order remained in place and that the plaintiffs were likely to prevail in their lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 The ruling prompted the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s 2 June emergency request to the supreme court to halt Illston\u8217\'20\'19s order.\par \par \uc2 Controlling the personnel of federal agencies \u8220\'20\'1Clies at the heartland\u8221\'20\'1D of the president\u8217\'20\'19s executive branch authority, the justice department said in its filing to the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe constitution does not erect a presumption against presidential control of agency staffing, and the president does not need special permission from Congress to exercise core Article II powers,\u8221\'20\'1D the filing said, referring to the constitution\u8217\'20\'19s section delineating presidential authority.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs urged the supreme court to deny the request. Allowing the Trump administration to move forward with its \u8220\'20\'1Cbreakneck reorganization\u8221\'20\'1D, they wrote, would mean that \u8220\'20\'1Cprograms, offices and functions across the federal government will be abolished, agencies will be radically downsized from what Congress authorized, critical government services will be lost and hundreds of thousands of federal employees will lose their jobs\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T20:41:56.688Z">at 9.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T19:18:29.130Z">8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says he will meet again with Netanyahu this evening\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  will meet again on Tuesday evening to discuss Gaza, a day after they met for hours while officials conducted indirect negotiations on a US-brokered ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 Trump and Netanyahu dined together on Monday at the White House during the Israeli leader\u8217\'20\'19s third US visit since the president began his second term on 20 January.\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu spent much of Tuesday at the Capitol, telling reporters after a meeting with House speaker Mike Johnson that while he did not think Israel\u8217\'20\'19s campaign in the Palestinian territory was done, negotiators are \u8220\'20\'1Ccertainly working\u8221\'20\'1D on a ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have still to finish the job in Gaza , release all our hostages, eliminate and destroy \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 military and government capabilities,\u8221\'20\'1D Netanyahu said.\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s plan to return to the White House at 4.30pm ET pushed back his meeting with Senate leaders to Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after Netanyahu spoke, Trump envoy \uc2 Steve Witkoff\uc2  said he hoped to reach a temporary ceasefire agreement this week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are hopeful that by the end of this week, we\u8217\'20\'19ll have an agreement that will bring us into a 60-day ceasefire. Ten live hostages will be released. Nine deceased will be released,\u8221\'20\'1D Witkoff told reporters at a meeting of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet earlier.\par \par \uc2 In his remarks to reporters at Congress, Netanyahu praised Trump, saying there has never been closer coordination between the US and Israel in his country\u8217\'20\'19s history.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T19:55:16.756Z">at 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T18:51:06.034Z">7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pentagon provided $2.4tn to private arms firms to \u8216\'20\'18fund war and weapons\u8217\'20\'19, report finds\par \par \uc2 A new study of defense department spending previewed exclusively to the Guardian shows that most of the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s discretionary spending from 2020 to 2024 has gone to outside military contractors, providing a $2.4tn boon in public funds to private firms in what was described as a \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinuing and massive transfer of wealth from taxpayers to fund war and weapons manufacturing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://watson.brown.edu/costsofwar/papers/2025/MilitaryContractors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report from the Quincy Institute for Responsible Statecraft and Costs of War}}}\uc2  program at Brown University said that the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s new Pentagon budget will push annual US military spending past the $1tn mark.\par \par \uc2 That will deliver a projected windfall of more than half a trillion dollars that will be shared among top arms firms such as \uc2 Lockheed Martin\uc2  and \uc2 Raytheon\uc2  as well as a growing military tech sector with close allies in the administration such as JD Vance , the report said.\par \par \uc2 The report is compiled of statistics of Pentagon spending and contracts from 2020 to 2024, during which time the top five Pentagon contractors (\uc2 Lockheed Martin\uc2 , \uc2 Raytheon\uc2 , \uc2 Boeing\uc2  , \uc2 General Dynamics\uc2  and \uc2 Northrop Grumman\uc2 ) received $771bn in contract awards. Overall, private firms received approximately 54% of the department\u8217\'20\'19s discretionary spending of $4.4tn over that period.\par \par \uc2 Taking into account supplemental funding for the Pentagon passed by Congress under Trump\u8217\'20\'19s flagship sweeping tax and spending bill, the report said, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-military"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US military}}}\uc2  budget will have nearly doubled this century, increasing 99% since 2000.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe US withdrawal from Afghanistan in September 2021 did not result in a peace dividend,\u8221\'20\'1D the authors of the report wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CInstead, President Biden requested, and Congress authorized, even higher annual budgets for the Pentagon, and President Trump is continuing that same trajectory of escalating military budgets.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That contradicts early indications from Trump in February that he could cut military spending in half, adding that he would tell China and Russia that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s no reason for us to be spending almost $1tn on the military \u8230\'20\'26 and I\u8217\'20\'19m going to say we can spend this on other things\u8221\'20\'1D. Instead, the spending bill pushed by Trump through Congress included a $157bn spending boost for the Pentagon.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/08/pentagon-military-spending"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pentagon provided $2.4tn to private arms firms to \u8216\'20\'18fund war and weapons\u8217\'20\'19, report finds}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T18:58:39.238Z">at 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T18:31:44.893Z">7.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Migrants deported from US to El Salvador prison remain under US control, Salvadorian officials tell \uc2 UN\par \par \uc2 The government of El Salvador has acknowledged to United Nations investigators that the Trump administration maintains control of the Venezuelan men who were deported from the US to a notorious Salvadoran prison, contradicting past public statements by officials from both countries.\par \par \uc2 The revelation was contained in court filings on Monday by lawyers for more than 100 migrants who are seeking to challenge their deportations to El Salvador\u8217\'20\'19s mega-prison known as Cecot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn this context, the jurisdiction and legal responsibility for these persons lie exclusively with the competent foreign authorities,\u8221\'20\'1D Salvadorian officials wrote in response to queries from the unit of the \uc2 UN Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2  group has been looking into the fate of the men who were sent to El Salvador from the US in mid-March, even after a federal judge had ordered the planes that were carrying them to be turned around.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has argued that it is powerless to return the men, as they are beyond the reach of US courts and no longer have access to due process rights or other US constitutional guarantees.\par \par \uc2 But lawyers for the migrants said the \uc2 UN\uc2  report shows otherwise. \uc2 American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  lawyer \uc2 Lee Gelernt\uc2  said in an email:\par \par \uc2 El Salvador has confirmed what we and everyone else understood: it is the United States that controls what happens to the Venezuelans languishing at Cecot. Remarkably the \uc2 US government\uc2  didn\u8217\'20\'19t provide this information to us or the court .\par \par \uc2 Skye Perryman\uc2  , CEO and president of Democracy Forward , said the documents show \u8220\'20\'1Cthat the administration has not been honest with the court or the American people\u8221\'20\'1D. The \uc2 ACLU\uc2  and Democracy Forward are both representing the migrants.\par \par \uc2 A justice department spokesperson declined to comment. White House and homeland security department officials did not immediately respond to requests for comment from the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T18:40:03.604Z">at 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T18:00:46.951Z">7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US education secretary, Linda McMahon , yesterday threatened the state of California with legal action after the state refused to ban transgender girls from participating in girls\u8217\'20\'19 sports as demanded by the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C@CAgovernor, you\u8217\'20\'19ll be hearing from @AGPamBondi,\u8221\'20\'1D McMahon wrote on X, using the handles for California\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , and the US attorney general, Pam Bondi .\par \par \uc2 McMahon\u8217\'20\'19s statement was the latest salvo in the culture wars over transgender youth and ratchets up the personal rivalry between Trump and Newsom. Trump has made reversing advances in transgender rights a priority since returning to office on 20 January, while California law has allowed student athletes to participate in sports in alignment with their gender identity since 2013.\par \par \uc2 The justice department declined to comment and the education department did not immediately respond to a Reuters request for clarification on the meaning of McMahon\u8217\'20\'19s comment.\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s state education department did not immediately respond to a request for comment. Newsom\u8217\'20\'19s office and the \uc2 California Interscholastic Federation\uc2  (CIF), the governing body for high school sports, declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 The US education department issued a statement in June declaring California in violation of the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s interpretation of Title IV, the education law banning sex-based discrimination, and demanding the state alter its policy. The state rejected the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s directive, and in June filed a pre-enforcement lawsuit against the US justice department in anticipation of legal action.\par \par \uc2 With controversy brewing ahead of the state high school track and field championship in June, the CIF allowed girls displaced from the finals by a transgender athlete to also be granted space to compete. The CIF also allowed girls to appear on the winners\u8217\'20\'19 podium if they would have won a medal without a transgender athlete competing.\par \par \uc2 As a result, the CIF crowned two champions in the girls\u8217\'20\'19 high jump and triple jump after transgender girl AB Hernandez won both events.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T18:08:09.099Z">at 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T17:39:08.422Z">6.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump again floats federal takeover of Washington, DC\par \par \uc2 During his cabinet meeting, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also suggested his administration was looking into taking over governance of Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Trump said his chief of staff, Susie Wiles, was in close touch with the city\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, Muriel Bowser, a Democrat.\par \par \uc2 It is not the first time the president floated a federal takeover of the city, home to the White House, Congress and the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Trump told reporters in February: \u8220\'20\'1CI think we should take over Washington DC \u8211\'20\'13 make it safe. I think that we should govern District of Columbia.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Under home rule, Congress already vets all laws in the city and federal lawmakers can overturn some of them. However, it would take an act of Congress to make federal rule a reality.\par \par \uc2 Both houses would have to vote to repeal the 1973 Home Rule Act. It would be a controversial move and unlikely to make it through.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T17:53:22.379Z">at 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T17:27:05.877Z">6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he would announce a 50% tariff on imported copper on Tuesday. The Trump administration announced a so-called Section 232 investigation into US imports of the red metal in February.\par \par \uc2 Trump had ordered the investigation into possible tariffs on copper imports to rebuild US production of a metal critical to electric vehicles, military hardware, semiconductors and a wide range of consumer goods.\par \par \uc2 Trump signed an order directing the commerce secretary, Howard Lutnick, to start a new national security investigation under Section 232 of the Trade Expansion Act of 1962, the same law that Trump used in his first term to impose 25% global tariffs on steel and aluminum.\par \par \uc2 A White House official said any potential tariff rate would be determined by the investigation, adding that Trump preferred tariffs over quotas.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T17:17:21.545Z">6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 The homeland security secretary, \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  , said first responders in Texas are \u8220\'20\'1Cstill looking for a lot of little girls\u8221\'20\'1D who remain missing after a devastating flood in Texas.\par \par \uc2 Noem described the scene in Texas as Trump met with his cabinet at the White House on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Noem visited Camp Mystic in Kerrville on Saturday after the catastrophic flood on Friday.\par \par \uc2 You can read our Texas live coverage here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jul/08/texas-floods-search-efforts-fifth-day-death-toll-latest-news-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas flooding: at least 107 people have died as questions intensify over handling of disaster \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T17:22:22.958Z">at 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T17:03:10.906Z">6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump's Middle East envoy says 60-day Gaza ceasefire could be finalized by end of week\par \par \uc2 A temporary ceasefire agreement in Gaza could be finalized by the end of the week, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Middle East envoy, \uc2 Steve Witkoff\uc2 , said at the cabinet meeting.\par \par \uc2 Witkoff added that proximity talks had reduced outstanding issues from \u8220\'20\'1Cfour issues \u8230\'20\'26 to one\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are hopeful that by the end of this week, we will have an agreement that will bring us into a 60-day ceasefire,\u8221\'20\'1D Witkoff said. \u8220\'20\'1CTen live hostages will be released. Nine deceased will be released.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump added that he would meet with the Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , later to discuss Gaza \u8220\'20\'1Calmost exclusively\u8221\'20\'1D, describing the situation as \u8220\'20\'1Ca tragedy\u8221\'20\'1D while claiming that the prime minister has been \u8220\'20\'1Cvery unfairly treated\u8221\'20\'1D because of his corruption trial.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s been very unfairly treated. I think what they\u8217\'20\'19ve done to him in Israel is very unfair. Having to do with this trial, he\u8217\'20\'19s a wartime prime minister, had an unbelievable outcome, and I think he\u8217\'20\'19s been treated very unfairly,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said of Netanyahu.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T17:23:17.979Z">at 6.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T16:36:38.946Z">5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some more on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments about Putin. Talking about the Russian invasion of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2 , he said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat was a war that should have never happened. A lot of people are dying and it should end.\par \par \uc2 We get a lot of bullshit thrown at us by Putin , if you want to know the truth. He\u8217\'20\'19s very nice all the time, but it turns out to be meaningless. \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked if he wants to see further sanctions against Russia, he says: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m looking at it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T17:23:54.378Z">at 6.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T16:35:08.269Z">5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 When asked about the latest on the \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2  case \u8211\'20\'13 in which the Department of Justice concluded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/07/jeffrey-epstein-suicide-justice-department-fbi-review-confirms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 there was no secret client list}}}\uc2  and it lacked evidence to prosecute \u8211\'20\'13 Pam Bondi brought up her Fox News interview comments from earlier this year that has gone viral this week about Epstein\u8217\'20\'19s client list, explaining that when she said files were \u8220\'20\'1Csitting on my desk to be reviewed\u8221\'20\'1D, she meant the Epstein file along with JFK and MLK assassination files.\par \par \uc2 The US attorney general explained that investigators found \u8220\'20\'1Ctens of thousands\u8221\'20\'1D of child sexual abuse videos downloaded by Epstein, which she said would \u8220\'20\'1Cnever be released, never going to see the light of day\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Regarding Epstein\u8217\'20\'19s death, Bondi said prison video showed he committed suicide, though she noted a technical issue with the recording system based on the prison\u8217\'20\'19s outdated video system.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Trump was clearly irritated by the question, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CYou still talking about \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2 ? This guy has been talked about for years \u8230\'20\'26 And are people still talking about this guy, this creep? That is unbelievable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T16:46:47.710Z">at 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T16:24:25.945Z">5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump 'not happy' with Putin but says any potential action would come as 'a little surprise'\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters, Trump said that he is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot happy\u8221\'20\'1D with Russian leader \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , and noted that weekly casualties in Ukraine are now at 7,000 a week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not happy with Putin. I can tell you that much right now, because he\u8217\'20\'19s killing a lot of people, and a lot of them are his soldiers, his soldiers and their soldiers mostly. And it\u8217\'20\'19s now up to 7,000 a week,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 When pressed by reporters about potential action, Trump declined to elaborate, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be telling you, we want to have a little surprise.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump praised Ukrainian resistance while crediting US military aid: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Ukrainians were brave, but we gave them the best equipment ever made.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T16:36:01.312Z">at 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T16:05:17.823Z">5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Opening his full cabinet meeting just before noon, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  again targeted his predecessors\u8217\'20\'19 trade policies, claiming the US was previously \u8220\'20\'1Cled by stupid people\u8221\'20\'1D who lacked business acumen.\par \par \uc2 Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe only adhered to the rules of other nations who charge us tremendous tariffs because we were led by stupid people, or people without any business sense.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T15:50:03.203Z">4.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is set to attend Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s Club World Cup final at MetLife Stadium in New Jersey, a senior administration official {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/GarrettHaake/status/1942601751778988203"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tells }}}\uc2 NBC News senior White House correspondent Garrett Haake.\par \par \uc2 The Club World Cup final would conclude Fifa\u8217\'20\'19s newly expanded 32-team global tournament.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T16:05:07.776Z">at 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T15:19:55.825Z">4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump confirms new tariffs to take effect 1 August: 'there will be no change'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has issued an ultimatum to the US\u8217\'20\'19s trading partners, confirming that new tariffs will take effect on 1 August with no possibility of delays.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114818149310161097"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Truth Social post}}}\uc2  on Tuesday, Trump said:\par \par \uc2 As per letters sent to various countries yesterday, in addition to letters that will be sent today, tomorrow, and for the next short period of time, TARIFFS WILL START BEING PAID ON AUGUST 1, 2025. There has been no change to this date, and there will be no change. In other words, all money will be due and payable starting AUGUST 1, 2025 \u8211\'20\'13 No extensions will be granted. Thank you for your attention to this matter!\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T15:24:47.035Z">at 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T15:08:39.676Z">4.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US government\uc2  will ban sales of US farmland to Chinese buyers and other foreign adversaries, the agriculture secretary, \uc2 Brooke Rollins\uc2 , announced at a joint press conference on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Speaking alongside defense secretary \uc2 Pete Hegseth\uc2  and homeland security secretary \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , Rollins said the administration would pursue executive actions and work with states to halt such purchases, citing national security and food security concerns.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo longer can foreign adversaries assume we\u8217\'20\'19re not watching,\u8221\'20\'1D Hegseth {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qF5T0oB9zfM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 , adding that the Pentagon would block farmland sales near military installations to protect food supplies for troops \u8220\'20\'1Cespecially in a contingency\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The move includes plans for increased monitoring of existing farmland owned by entities from China, Russia and Iran. Chinese investors currently control 265,000 acres of US land, according to government data, with roughly half connected to \uc2 Smithfield Foods\uc2 , which was bought by Chinese conglomerate \uc2 WH Group\uc2  in 2013.\par \par \uc2 Chinese ownership of US farmland has already fallen significantly, dropping from 384,000 acres in 2021 to current levels.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T15:11:21.909Z">at 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T14:59:14.045Z">3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , and some of his top officials met with JD Vance at Blair House on Tuesday, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/kann_news/status/1942591006710587423"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israeli media reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Blair House, directly across from the White House, serves as the official presidential guest house and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://time.com/archive/6913913/blair-house-worlds-most-exclusive-hotel/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been called}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe world\u8217\'20\'19s most exclusive hotel\u8221\'20\'1D. Only the most important foreign dignitaries get invited to stay there.\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s accommodation at the historic residence signals the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to maintaining the special US-Israel relationship, even as the prime minister faces an arrest warrant from the international criminal court over war crime allegations stemming from Israel\u8217\'20\'19s devastating conduct in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/netanyahu-meets-with-vance-in-washington-along-with-top-aides/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was joined}}}\uc2  by strategic affairs minister Ron Dermer, national security adviser Tzachi Hanegbi, ambassador to Washington Yechiel Leiter and military secretary Maj Gen Roman Gofman.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T15:12:16.106Z">at 4.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T14:21:23.390Z">3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rightwing influencers in the US who are often aligned with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  are angry that a joint justice department and \uc2 FBI{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/25992101/epstein.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 memo}}}\uc2  has dismissed the existence of a \u8220\'20\'1Cclient list\u8221\'20\'1D in the case against late sex offender {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The disgraced financier killed himself in a jail cell at the Metropolitan Detention Center in New York City in 2019 while awaiting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-sdny/pr/jeffrey-epstein-charged-manhattan-federal-court-sex-trafficking-minors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prosecution}}}\uc2  on child sex-trafficking and conspiracy charges.\par \par \uc2 Almost ever since, Epstein\u8217\'20\'19s death has been the subject of conspiracy theories on the right, including a supposed \u8220\'20\'1Cclient list\u8221\'20\'1D that he purportedly used to blackmail wealthy co-conspirators.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidential administration then created anticipation that the alleged list would be publicly disclosed, including the US attorney general, Pam Bondi, who had told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/attorney-general-bondi-under-siege-after-doj-reveals-no-epstein-client-list"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News}}}\uc2  in an interview: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s sitting on my desk right now to review.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/08/rightwing-jeffrey-epstein-client-list"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rightwing influencers indignant over FBI claim that Jeffrey Epstein\u8217\'20\'19s client list doesn\u8217\'20\'19t exist}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T14:32:45.480Z">at 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T13:35:37.121Z">2.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 A split Wisconsin supreme court is paving the way for a statewide \u8220\'20\'1Cconversion therapy\u8221\'20\'1D ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/wisconsin-supreme-court-conversion-therapy-ban-16fc23a14e15f1cfcf9c2dbb89cc0e9a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by striking down}}}\uc2  a Republican committee\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional challenge to the proposed rule.\par \par \uc2 The 4-3 decision from the liberal-majority court overturned the GOP-controlled joint committee for the review of administrative rules, which had twice rejected a state agency regulation banning the scientifically discredited practice aimed at \u8220\'20\'1Cconverting\u8221\'20\'1D LGBTQ+ people to heterosexuality.\par \par \uc2 The ruling is yet another brush up between the Democratic governor, \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2 , and the Republican-controlled legislature over LGBTQ+ rights. Evers has previously vetoed GOP bills targeting transgender high school athletes and has sought to limit the legislature\u8217\'20\'19s power.\par \par \uc2 Conversion therapy is already banned in 23 states and Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T13:49:40.220Z">at 2.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T13:21:51.268Z">2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dan Osborn, the independent candidate who came surprisingly close to defeating Republican senator \uc2 Deb Fischer\uc2  in Nebraska last year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/osbornforne/status/1942557787013407203"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced on Tuesday}}}\uc2  he will run for the state\u8217\'20\'19s other Senate seat in 2026 against GOP senator \uc2 Pete Ricketts\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The industrial mechanic and former \uc2 Kellogg\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s strike leader lost to Fischer by less than seven points in 2024 \u8211\'20\'13 a remarkable result in deep-red Nebraska. Osborn received 66,000 more votes than \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who lost the state to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  by 20 points in the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 Osborn ran on a populist platform combining conservative stances on border security and gun rights with liberal views on abortion and campaign finance reform, while distancing himself from Democrats. He has said he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t caucus with Democrats if elected.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T13:24:50.556Z">at 2.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T12:39:50.408Z">1.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Obama adviser warns of AI threat after Rubio impostor reported\par \par \uc2 David Axelrod, who served as senior adviser to \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , said the AI scam using Rubio was \u8220\'20\'1Conly a matter of time\u8221\'20\'1D and urged urgent action to defend against such attacks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  impostor is using AI voice to call high-level officials,\u8221\'20\'1D Axelrod wrote on X. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the new world in which we live and we\u8217\'20\'19d better figure out how to defend against it because of its implications for our democracy and the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rollcall.com/factbase/trump/topic/calendar/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is scheduled}}}\uc2  to have a meeting with his cabinet officials at 11 am.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T12:42:21.471Z">at 1.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T12:26:09.015Z">1.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  impostor using AI to contact multiple senior officials \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 An unknown fraudster has used artificial intelligence to impersonate the US secretary of state, \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , contacting at least five senior officials.\par \par \uc2 According to a state department cable {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2025/07/08/marco-rubio-ai-imposter-signal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seen by the Washington Post}}}\uc2 , the impostor sent fake voice messages and texts that mimicked Rubio\u8217\'20\'19s voice and writing style to those targets including three foreign ministers, a US governor and a member of Congress.\par \par \uc2 The cable, dated 3 July, said the impostor \u8220\'20\'1Cleft voicemails on Signal for at least two targeted individuals\u8221\'20\'1D and sent text messages inviting others to communicate on the platform.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s still a mystery who is behind the scam, but the cable reportedly reads that the goal had been \u8220\'20\'1Cgaining access to information or accounts\u8221\'20\'1D of powerful government officials.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T12:38:29.466Z">at 1.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T11:49:59.257Z">12.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 A pediatrician for a chain of clinics affiliated with a prominent Houston hospital system is \u8220\'20\'1Cno longer employed\u8221\'20\'1D there, according to officials, after a social media account associated with her published a post wishing the \u8220\'20\'1CMaga\u8221\'20\'1D voters of a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 -supporting county in Texas to \u8220\'20\'1Cget what they voted for\u8221\'20\'1D amid flash flooding that killed more than 100 people, including many children.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were made aware of a social media comment from one of our physicians,\u8221\'20\'1D read a statement from Blue Fish Pediatrics circulated late on Sunday. \u8220\'20\'1CThe individual is no longer employed by Blue Fish Pediatrics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The statement also said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe strongly condemn the comments that were made in that post. That post does not reflect the values, standards or mission of Blue Fish Pediatrics. We do not support or condone any statement that politicizes tragedy, diminishes human dignity, or fails to clearly uphold compassion for every child and family, regardless of background or beliefs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Blue Fish Pediatrics\u8217\'20\'19 statement neither named the physician in question nor specified whether she had resigned or was dismissed. But multiple publicly accessible social media posts identified her as Dr Christina Propst. A Guardian source familiar with the situation confirmed the accuracy of the posts naming Propst. And, at the time it issued the statement, Blue Fish Pediatrics had recently unpublished Propst\u8217\'20\'19s biographical page from its website.\par \par \uc2 Attempts to contact Propst weren\u8217\'20\'19t immediately successful.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/08/texas-floods-pediatrician-maga"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas pediatrician \u8216\'20\'18no longer employed\u8217\'20\'19 after post about pro-Trump flood victims}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T12:36:59.526Z">at 1.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T11:28:19.361Z">12.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 A pregnant physician who was denied a Covid-19 vaccine is suing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  alongside a group of leading doctors associations, charging that the administration sought to \u8220\'20\'1Cdesensitize the public to anti-vaccine and anti-science rhetoric\u8221\'20\'1D, according to their attorney.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit specifically takes aim at health secretary Robert F Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s unilateral decision to recommend against Covid-19 vaccines for pregnant women and healthy children.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s announcement circumvented expert scientific review panels and flouted studies showing pregnant women are at heightened risk from the virus, and made it more difficult for some to get the vaccine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis administration is an existential threat to vaccination in America, and those in charge are only just getting started,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Richard H Hughes IV\uc2 , partner at Epstein Becker Green and lead counsel for the plaintiffs in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American Academy of Pediatrics\uc2 , American College of Physicians and American Public Health Association are among a list of leading physicians associations named as plaintiffs in the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf left unchecked, secretary Kennedy will accomplish his goal of ridding the United States of vaccines, which would unleash a wave of preventable harm on our nation\u8217\'20\'19s children,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hughes. \u8220\'20\'1CThe professional associations for pediatricians, internal medicine physicians, infectious disease physicians, high-risk pregnancy physicians, and public health professionals will not stand idly by as our system of prevention is dismantled. This ends now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In late May, Kennedy announced that the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/27/rfk-jr-covid-vaccine-kids-pregnant-women"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no longer recommend}}}\uc2  Covid-19 vaccines for healthy children or pregnant women. The announcement, made on social media, contradicted a raft of evidence showing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMsb2506929"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pregnant women}}}\uc2  and infants are at especially high-risk from the disease, including from the administration\u8217\'20\'19s own scientific leaders.\par \par \uc2 In June, Kennedy went further by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/10/rfk-jr-cdc-vaccine-panel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 firing}}}\uc2  all 17 sitting members of a key vaccine advisory panel to the CDC. The advisory panel is a key link in the vaccine distribution pipeline, helping to develop recommendations insurers use when determining which vaccines to cover.\par \par \uc2 That panel met for the first time in late June. Members {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/25/cdc-vaccine-panel-rfk-acip"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced they would review}}}\uc2  both the childhood vaccine schedule and any vaccines that had not been formally reviewed in seven years. They also recommended against a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/26/rfk-flu-shot-vaccines-panel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long-vilified}}}\uc2  vaccine preservative, in spite of a lack of evidence of harm.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/07/pregnant-doctor-covid-19-vaccine-rfk-jr-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pregnant doctor denied Covid-19 vaccine sues Trump administration}}}\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T11:09:34.587Z">12.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans toe Trump line even in aftermath of deadly Texas floods\par \par \uc2 The US is reeling after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas-floods-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catastrophic floods}}}\uc2  killed more than 100 people in Texas, including 27 children and counsellors from an all-girls Christian camp. On Monday, Democrats asked a government watchdog to investigate whether cuts at the National Weather Service (NWS) affected the forecasting agency\u8217\'20\'19s performance.\par \par \uc2 But Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 default response has been to express fealty to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . They lavished praise on the president for providing federal assistance while studiously avoiding questions around the effect of his \u8220\'20\'1C{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/may/05/elon-musk-doge-federal-government"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 department of government efficiency}}}\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D (Doge) or threats to dismantle the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  (Fema).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a sign of the sickness and dysfunction of what was the Republican party that they have almost no thoughts about their constituents,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/27/rick-wilson-lincoln-project-dismiss-trump-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rick Wilson}}}\uc2 , a cofounder of the Lincoln Project, an anti-Trump group. \u8220\'20\'1CTheir thoughts are, how do I avoid making sure that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t look at me as an enemy or a critic?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite the fact that the Doge cuts and the reductions in force and the early buyouts have savaged the workforce of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.weather.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 National Weather Service}}}\uc2 , they can\u8217\'20\'19t even utter the slightest vague, elliptical critique of the administration that is now engaged in these cuts that have cost the lives of the people they supposedly represent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The raging flash floods \u8211\'20\'13 among the US\u8217\'20\'19s worst in decades \u8211\'20\'13 slammed into riverside camps and homes in central Texas before daybreak on Friday, pulling sleeping people out of their cabins, tents and trailers and dragging them for miles past floating tree trunks and cars. Some survivors were found clinging to trees. Authorities say the death toll is sure to rise as crews look for the many who are still missing.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/08/texas-floods-republicans-response-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans toe Trump line even in aftermath of deadly Texas floods}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T11:58:19.154Z">at 12.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T10:49:50.616Z">11.49am BST\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  has ended temporary protections for people from Honduras and Nicaragua in the latest phase of its effort to expel undocumented people from the US.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  (DHS) announced it would end temporary protected status (TPS) for an estimated 72,000 Hondurans and 4,000 Nicaraguans in moves that will come into effect in about 60 days.\par \par \uc2 Citizens of the two Central American nations were accorded the status after Hurricane Mitch in 1998, which left 10,000 dead after it ripped through the region.\par \par \uc2 Honduras and Nicaragua are the latest in a series of countries to have their US-based citizens stripped of temporary protections since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s return to the White House. Similar moves have been made to end TPS for those from Venezuela, Haiti, Afghanistan, Cameroon and Nepal.\par \par \uc2 Not all of those being stripped of the protection will necessarily be at risk of being forced to leave. Roughly 21,000 Hondurans and 1,100 Nicaraguans have obtained green cards, giving them legal permanent residence status.\par \par \uc2 Those without such status will be urged to arrange their departure through a Customs and Border Protection app, which would offer complimentary plane tickets and a $1,000 exit bonus, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/dhs-terminates-temporary-protected-status-around-76k-honduran-nicaraguan-migrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Fox News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/07/trump-tps-honduras-nicaragua"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump ends deportation protections for people from Honduras and Nicaragua}}}\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T10:25:35.937Z">11.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Exclusive: US only has 25% of all Patriot missile interceptors needed for Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s military plans\par \par \uc2 The United States only has about 25% of the Patriot missile interceptors it needs for all of the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s military plans after burning through stockpiles in the Middle East in recent months, an alarming depletion that led to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  freezing the latest transfer of munitions to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The stockpile of the Patriot missiles has fallen so low that it raised concern inside the Pentagon that it could jeopardize potential US military operations, and deputy defense secretary, \uc2 Stephen Feinberg\uc2 , authorized the transfer to be halted while they reviewed where weapons were being sent.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appeared to reverse at least part of that decision on Monday when he told reporters in advance of a dinner at the White House with Israeli prime minister {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/benjamin-netanyahu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu}}}\uc2  that he would \u8220\'20\'1Csend some more weapons\u8221\'20\'1D to Ukraine, although he did not disclose whether that would include Patriot systems.\par \par \uc2 Trump also told Ukrainian president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/volodymyr-zelenskiy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy}}}\uc2 , in a phone call that he was not responsible for the halt in weapons shipments and that he had directed a review of US weapons stockpiles but didn\u8217\'20\'19t order the freeze, according to people briefed on the conversation.\par \par \uc2 But the determination last month to halt the transfer, as described by four people directly familiar with the matter, was based in large part on the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s global munitions tracker, which is used to generate the minimum level of munitions required to carry out the US military\u8217\'20\'19s operations plans.\par \par \uc2 According to the tracker, which is managed by the joint chiefs of staff and the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s defense security cooperation agency, the stockpiles of a number of critical munitions have been below that floor for several years since the Biden administration started sending military aid to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/08/us-pentagon-military-plans-patriot-missile-interceptor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US only has 25% of all Patriot missile interceptors needed for Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s military plans}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T11:54:26.643Z">at 12.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T10:12:07.206Z">11.12am BST\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin said on Tuesday that it would take time to clarify what weapons the United States is supplying and will supply to Ukraine after president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said Washington would have to send more arms to Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 Trump said on Monday that the United States would send more weapons to Ukraine, primarily defensive ones, to help the war-torn country defend itself against intensifying Russian advances.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T10:00:06.300Z">11.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  to meet JD Vance and Mike Johnson today\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome to the US politics live blog. I\u8217\'20\'19m Tom Ambrose and I will be bringing you all the latest news lines over the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 We start with news that Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  will meet US vice-president \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  at 9.15am local time at the Blair House, The Times of Israel has reported .\par \par \uc2 He will then meet \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2  speaker Mike Johnson at Capitol House, before returning to Blair House for meetings.\par \par \uc2 Then at 4pm, Netanyahu will head to the Senate for meeting with majority leader \uc2 John Thune\uc2 , Democratic senator \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  and other lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 It comes as Netanyahu told \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that he would nominate him for the Nobel peace prize on Monday, as the two leaders met for the first time since the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jun/21/trump-us-nuclear-strikes-iran"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US launched strikes on Iran\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear program}}}\uc2  as part of a short-lived war between Israel and Iran.\par \par \uc2 Trump was expected to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jul/07/indirect-talks-gaza-ceasefire-netanyahu-washington-visit-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 press Netanyahu to agree to a ceasefire}}}\uc2  in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in Gaza amid an outcry over the humanitarian cost of an offensive that has led to nearly 60,000 deaths.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/08/trump-nominated-nobel-peace-prize-netanyahu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Netanyahu nominates Trump for Nobel peace prize at White House meeting}}}\par \par \uc2 In other developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House published letters to 14 countries detailing new tariff rates on imported goods to the United States. He also signed an executive order on Monday extending a 90-day pause for a slate of so-called \u8220\'20\'1Creciprocal\u8221\'20\'1D tariffs first introduced in April \u8211\'20\'13 in effect pushing back the deadline of trade talks back to 1 August. The tariffs include:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Japan , South Korea , Malaysia , Kazakhstan, and Tunisia: 25%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Indonesia: 32%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Bangladesh and Serbia: 35%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Bosnia: 30%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Cambodia and Thailand: 36%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 South Africa: 30%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Laos and Myanm ar: 40%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump signed two other executive orders today: one directs his administration to \u8220\'20\'1Cstrictly enforce the termination of the clean electricity production and investment tax credits\u8221\'20\'1D, Biden-era subsidies for wind and solar projects. The other extends a federal hiring freeze through 15 October 15.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Los Angeles mayor, \uc2 Karen Bass\uc2  , confronted immigration agents after US Customs and Border Patrol conducted a raid on the city\u8217\'20\'19s MacArthur Park today, she said in a social media post.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  will deport Kilmar \u193\'00\'C1brego Garc\u237\'00\'EDa if he is released from custody, a justice department attorney said in court this morning, according to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Department of Veterans Affairs will no longer need to cut 80,000 jobs, as ordered by the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D, because it has already cut staff by 30,000 through retirements, buyouts and hiring freezes, the agency said today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A judge has ordered the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  to continue disbursing Medicaid payments to \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  , despite a provision in the president\u8217\'20\'19s recently signed tax and spending bill.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250708el78001h4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
