\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump and Netanyahu meet at White House amid indirect ceasefire talks \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Cecilia Nowell (now); Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton, Fran Lawther, Chris Stein, Lucy Campbell and Yohannes Lowe (earlier) \par \uc2 9,971 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 July 2025\par 09:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can find all of our live US politics coverage <a href="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news">here</a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.theguardian.com/us-news">here</a}}}\uc2 >\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T02:03:40.821Z">3.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Our live coverage is ending now. In the meantime, you can find all of our live US politics coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 . Here is a summary of the key developments from today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hosted the Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , at the White House today. The visit comes as indirect talks between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  over a ceasefire and hostage deal in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jul/06/gaza-mood-ceasefire-talks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2  continued for a second day on Monday. Speaking to reporters, Netanyahu said he has sent a letter to the Nobel committee nominating Trump for a Nobel peace prize. Earlier in the day, Netanyahu met with US secretary of state, \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , and Middle East envoy, \uc2 Steve Witkoff\uc2 . He will meet House speaker Mike Johnson tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 During his meeting with Netanyahu, Trump told reporters the United States will resume weapons shipments to Ukraine. Last week, the Pentagon halted shipments of US Patriot air defence systems and other precision weapons to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  after concern that US stockpiles were running too low. Earlier in the day, White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt denied that Trump had ordered weapons shipments to Ukraine paused, instead saying the decision was made as part of a normal review of such shipments by the defense secretary, \uc2 Pete Hegseth\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House published letters to 14 countries detailing new tariff rates on imported goods to the United States. He also signed an executive order on Monday extending a 90-day pause for a slate of so-called \u8220\'20\'1Creciprocal\u8221\'20\'1D tariffs first introduced in April \u8211\'20\'13 in effect pushing back the deadline of trade talks back to 1 August. The tariffs include:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Japan , South Korea , Malaysia , Kazakhstan, and Tunisia: 25%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Indonesia: 32%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Bangladesh and Serbia: 35%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Bosnia: 30%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Cambodia and Thailand: 36%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 South Africa: 30%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Laos and Myanm ar: 40%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump signed two other executive orders today: one directs his administration to \u8220\'20\'1Cstrictly enforce the termination of the clean electricity production and investment tax credits\u8221\'20\'1D, Biden-era subsidies for wind and solar projects. The other extends a federal hiring freeze through 15 October 15.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Los Angeles mayor, \uc2 Karen Bass\uc2  , confronted immigration agents after US Customs and Border Patrol conducted a raid on the city\u8217\'20\'19s MacArthur Park today, she said in a social media post.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  will deport Kilmar \u193\'00\'C1brego Garc\u237\'00\'EDa if he is released from custody, a justice department attorney said in court this morning, according to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Department of Veterans Affairs will no longer need to cut 80,000 jobs, as ordered by the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D, because it has already cut staff by 30,000 through retirements, buyouts and hiring freezes, the agency said today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A judge has ordered the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  to continue disbursing Medicaid payments to \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  , despite a provision in the president\u8217\'20\'19s recently signed tax and spending bill.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T02:09:15.781Z">at 3.09am BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T01:50:48.564Z">2.50am BST\par \par \uc2 In a break from decades-old policy, the \uc2 IRS\uc2  said in a court filing today that churches and other religious groups should be allowed to endorse political candidates, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 In a lawsuit, two Texas churches and an association of Christian broadcasters asked the \uc2 IRS\uc2  to exempt all nonprofits, which many churches are, from endorsing political candidates to their members. The \uc2 IRS\uc2  agreed to a narrower exemption, saying that it would view a church\u8217\'20\'19s decision to endorse a candidate not as campaigning but as a private matter, like \u8220\'20\'1Ca family discussion\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T01:14:31.017Z">2.14am BST\par \par \uc2 A judge has ordered the Trump administration to continue disbursing Medicaid payments to \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , despite a provision in the president\u8217\'20\'19s recently signed tax and spending bill.\par \par \uc2 US district judge Indira Talwani issued a temporary restraining order in response to a lawsuit filed earlier today by the \uc2 Planned Parenthood Federation of America\uc2 . The lawsuit argues that the ban on Medicaid funding, which targets \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  for providing abortion care, will see increased rates of untreated sexually transmitted diseases and cancer, as well as unplanned pregnancies, nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T01:19:18.932Z">at 2.19am BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T00:55:10.604Z">1.55am BST\par \par \uc2 The Department of Veterans Affairs will no longer need to cut 80,000 jobs, as ordered by the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Department of Government Efficiency\uc2 , because it has already cut staff by 30,000 through retirements, buyouts and hiring freezes, the agency said today.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.va.gov/press-room/va-to-reduce-staff-by-nearly-30k-by-end-of-fy2025/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a news release}}}\uc2 , veterans affairs secretary \uc2 Doug Collins\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CSince March, we\u8217\'20\'19ve been conducting a holistic review of the department centered on reducing bureaucracy and improving services to Veterans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA department-wide RIF\u8221\'20\'1D or, reduction in force, \u8220\'20\'1Cis off the table, but that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean we\u8217\'20\'19re done improving VA. Our review has resulted in a host of new ideas for better serving Veterans that we will continue to pursue,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T00:44:20.325Z">1.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Ahead of Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s arrival in Washington DC today, demonstrators gathered outside of the US Embassy branch office in Tel Aviv to call for the release of the 7 October attack hostages and urge a ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 Here are images from the rally:\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T09:13:07.675Z">at 10.13am BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T00:23:21.342Z">1.23am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he lifted the United States\u8217\'20\'19s sanctions on Syria at the request of Middle Eastern leaders, including \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 . The Israeli prime minister added that Syria\u8217\'20\'19s new leadership gives Israel a chance at a new relationship with Syria.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T00:11:35.751Z">1.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says the United States will resume weapons shipments to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey have to be able to defend themselves. They\u8217\'20\'19re getting hit very hard now,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The president did not add any additional details.\par \par \uc2 Last wee, the Pentagon halted shipments of US Patriot air defence systems and other precision weapons to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  after concern that US stockpiles were running too low.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-08T00:09:42.491Z">1.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump and Netanyahu are answering questions about Zohran Mamdani, the democratic socialist who won New York City\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic mayoral primary.\par \par \uc2 In response to a question about Mamdani, who has said he would enforce the \uc2 International Criminal Court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s arrest order if Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  visited New York city, Netanyahu said \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not concerned about that\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who has threatened to deport Mamdani, who is a US citizen, said \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll get him out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Later Trump called Mamdani a \u8220\'20\'1Ccommunist and said \u8220\'20\'1Che\u8217\'20\'19s said some really bad things about Jewish people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T23:58:06.179Z">12.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  passed on a question about a two-state solution to the Israeli-Palestinian conflict, asking Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  to answer instead.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think Palestinians should have all of the power to govern themselves, but none of the power to threaten us,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T00:02:11.707Z">at 1.02am BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T23:54:13.377Z">12.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says Iran has approached the White House for talks following the United State\u8217\'20\'19s strike on the country\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear facilities. He also compared the US\u8217\'20\'19s strikes to the country\u8217\'20\'19s decision to drop atomic bombs on Japan during World War II.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want to say what it reminded me of but if you go back a long time ago, it reminded people of a certain other event. And \uc2 Harry Truman\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s picture is now in the lobby, in a nice location, not in the lobby where it should have been, but that stopped a lot of fighting, and this stopped a lot of fighting,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to have to\u8221\'20\'1D strike Iran again, he added.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T23:54:58.946Z">at 12.54am BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T23:51:25.717Z">12.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine is a \u8220\'20\'1Chorrible thing\u8221\'20\'1D and that he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cnot happy\u8221\'20\'1D with Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He added that it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter that it\u8217\'20\'19s not Americans who are being killed. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m disappointed frankly that President Putin hasn\u8217\'20\'19t stopped,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T23:48:56.752Z">12.48am BST\par \par \uc2 In response to a question about the future of Gaza, Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s called free choice: if people want to stay, they can stay, but if they want to leave, they should be able to leave.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T23:45:52.607Z">12.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Also at the Trump-Netanyahu dinner, Trump confirmed his plans to visit victims of the floods in Texas on Friday.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T23:45:22.757Z">12.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking at his dinner with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  said he has sent a letter to the Nobel committee nominating Trump for a Nobel Peace Prize.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-08T00:53:13.831Z">at 1.53am BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T23:36:18.774Z">12.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Demonstrators gathered in Washington DC today to protest the arrival of Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , who is currently meeting with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for talks many hope will lead to a ceasefire agreement in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war with Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Here are a few images from the scenes outside the White House and Blair House, where Netanyahu met Secretary of State \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  and Middle East envoy \uc2 Steve Witkoff\uc2  earlier.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T23:17:44.632Z">12.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  signed two other executive orders today, amid his tariff announcements.\par \par \uc2 One directs his administration to \u8220\'20\'1Cstrictly enforce the termination of the clean electricity production and investment tax credits\u8221\'20\'1D, Biden-era subsidies for wind and solar projects.\par \par \uc2 The other extends a federal hiring freeze through October 15. That order, which states \u8220\'20\'1Cno Federal civilian position that is presently vacant may be filled, and no new position may be created,\u8221\'20\'1D does not apply to military personnel, immigration enforcement, national security, public safety or the Executive Office of the President.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T22:54:51.049Z">11.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu arrives at White House\par \par \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  has arrived at the White House for his scheduled talks with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  this evening.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli prime minister met with Secretary of State \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  and Middle East envoy \uc2 Steve Witkoff\uc2  earlier this afternoon, the Associated Press reports, citing the prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 The visit comes as indirect talks between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  over a ceasefire and hostage deal in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jul/06/gaza-mood-ceasefire-talks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2  continued for a second day on Monday.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/world/middle-east/israel-hamas-ceasefire-gaza-trump-netanyahu-white-house-qatar-rcna217167"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump has increased pressure}}}\uc2  for a deal in Gaza in recent weeks and raised the possibility that a ceasefire could be declared in a matter of hours or days.\par \par \uc2 Hamas\uc2  demands an Israeli withdrawal, while Netanyahu insists on \uc2 Hamas\uc2  disarming. The meeting between Trump and Netanyahu could give new urgency to the US ceasefire proposal, but whether it leads to a deal that ends the war is unclear.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T22:57:18.524Z">at 11.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T22:03:49.556Z">11.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump signs executive order pushing tariff deadline to 1 August\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has set new 25% tariffs on Japan and South Korea, as well as new tariff rates on a dozen other countries, including Bangladesh and South Africa. The announcement was made via a post on Truth social that included letters sent to the nations\u8217\'20\'19 leaders.\par \par \uc2 He also signed an executive order on Monday extending a 90-day pause for a slate of so-called \u8220\'20\'1Creciprocal\u8221\'20\'1D tariffs first introduced in April \u8211\'20\'13 in effect pushing back the deadline of trade talks back to 1 August.\par \par \uc2 Read the details of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s most recent moves {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/07/trump-tariffs-japan-south-korea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T22:26:53.318Z">at 11.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T21:43:29.326Z">10.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration will deport Kilmar \u193\'00\'C1brego Garc\u237\'00\'EDa if he is released from custody, a Justice Department attorney said in court this morning, according to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Maryland father, who was wrongfully deported to El Salvador in March, is currently detained on smuggling charges the Trump administration filed after he was returned to the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u193\'00\'C1brego Garc\u237\'00\'EDa\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have asked the Federal District Court hearing the smuggling case to keep him in custody so that the federal government does not deport \u193\'00\'C1brego Garc\u237\'00\'EDa before the criminal case is concluded.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T21:43:42.910Z">at 10.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T21:35:01.609Z">10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 California has rejected the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s guidelines on transgender athletes, education secretary Linda McMahon said in a social media post.\par \par \uc2 Since taking office in January, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has directed his Education Department to enforce Title IX, a civil rights law preventing sex discrimination, to prevent transgender athletes from competing on teams that align with their gender identity. In June, the Education Department found that California had violated civil rights law by allowing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/hub/gender-in-sports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 transgender girls}}}\uc2  to compete on girls sports teams.\par \par \uc2 In her post, McMahon included email screenshots showing that the California Department of Education and Interscholastic Federation had opted not to comply with the Trump administration proposal, which would have required the state to apologize to athletes who had lost competitions to trans athletes.\par \par \uc2 In a screenshot of an email, California Education Department general counsel Len Garfinkel wrote that the state \u8220\'20\'1Crespectfully disagrees\u8221\'20\'1D with the Trump Administration\u8217\'20\'19s analysis.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/25/california-title-ix-violation-trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California violated Title IX by allowing trans athletes on girls\u8217\'20\'19 teams, Trump administration says}}}\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T21:15:34.250Z">10.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Los Angeles mayor \uc2 Karen Bass\uc2  confronted immigration agents after US Customs and Border Patrol conducted a raid on the city\u8217\'20\'19s MacArthur Park today, she said in a social media post.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe SECOND I heard about this, I went to the park to speak to the person in charge to tell them it needed to end NOW. Absolutely outrageous,\u8221\'20\'1D Bass wrote in the post.\par \par \uc2 On Monday morning, heavily armed immigration officials swept MacArthur Park, located in the city\u8217\'20\'19s Westlake neighborhood, on horseback and aboard armored vehicles.\par \par \uc2 Bass, who was scheduled to attend a news conference with California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , diverted to the park, where she confronted customs officials. The mayor\u8217\'20\'19s show of force against immigration agents comes after weeks of mounting tension between Los Angeles residents and customs officials.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T20:56:50.668Z">9.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Israel\u8217\'20\'19s defence minister has laid out plans to force all Palestinians in Gaza into a camp on the ruins of Rafah, in a scheme which legal experts and academics described as a blueprint for crimes against humanity.\par \par \uc2 Israel Katz\uc2  said he has ordered Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military to prepare for establishing a camp, which he called a \u8220\'20\'1Chumanitarian city\u8221\'20\'1D, on the ruins of the city of Rafah, Haaretz newspaper reported.\par \par \uc2 Palestinians would go through \u8220\'20\'1Csecurity screening\u8221\'20\'1D before entering, and once inside would not be allowed to leave, Katz said at a briefing for Israeli journalists.\par \par \uc2 Israeli forces would control the perimeter of the site and initially \u8220\'20\'1Cmove\u8221\'20\'1D 600,000 Palestinians into the area, Katz said, mostly people currently displaced in the al-Mawasi area.\par \par \uc2 Eventually the entire population of Gaza would be housed there, and Israel aims to implement \u8220\'20\'1Cthe emigration plan, which will happen\u8221\'20\'1D, Haaretz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2025-07-07/ty-article/.premium/defense-minister-israel-to-concentrate-all-gaza-population-in-rafah-humanitarian-zone/00000197-e56a-d1ad-ab97-e5ef764e0000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quoted him}}}\uc2  saying.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jul/07/israeli-minister-reveals-plan-to-force-population-of-gaza-into-camp-on-ruins-of-rafah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israeli plan for forced transfer of Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s population \u8216\'20\'18a blueprint for crimes against humanity\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T20:40:39.875Z">9.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump posts more tariff letters, with highest rate at 40%\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has posted more tariff letters addressing a number of countries on his Truth Social platform.\par \par \uc2 They include:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tunisia will face a 25% tariff on goods imported to the US.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Indonesia \u8211\'20\'13 32%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Bangladesh and Serbia \u8211\'20\'13 35%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Bosnia \u8211\'20\'13 30%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Cambodia and Thailand \u8211\'20\'13 36%\par \par \uc2 The latest round of letters brings the total number on Monday to 14. Earlier in the day, Trump announced the following tariff rates:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 25% US tariffs on goods from Japan , South Korea , Malaysia and Kazakhstan\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 30% US tariffs on South Africa\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 40% US tariffs on Laos and Myanmar\par \par \uc2 Myanmar and Laos have so far been worst hit. The south-east Asian nation of Laos, a country heavily bombed by the US during the cold war, has a poverty rate of 18.3%, according to the ADB. Myanmar is still {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/apr/01/myanmar-earthquake-death-toll-unmarked-graves"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reeling from a devastating earthquake}}}\uc2  and years of civil war following a 2021 military coup.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T21:31:43.072Z">at 10.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T20:30:56.403Z">9.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Away from tariffs, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is hosting the Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , at the White House later today.\par \par \uc2 The visit comes as indirect talks between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  over a ceasefire and hostage deal in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jul/06/gaza-mood-ceasefire-talks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2  continued for a second day on Monday.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/world/middle-east/israel-hamas-ceasefire-gaza-trump-netanyahu-white-house-qatar-rcna217167"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump has increased pressure}}}\uc2  for a deal in Gaza in recent weeks and raised the possibility that a ceasefire could be declared in a matter of hours or days.\par \par \uc2 Hamas\uc2  demands an Israeli withdrawal, while Netanyahu insists on \uc2 Hamas\uc2  disarming. The meeting between Trump and Netanyahu could give new urgency to the US ceasefire proposal, but whether it leads to a deal that ends the war is unclear.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe utmost priority for the president right now in the Middle East is to end the war in Gaza and to return all of the hostages,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt told reporters hours before the two leaders meet for a private dinner.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T19:48:43.333Z">8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt blasted the top Democrat in the Senate \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  for questioning the federal response to the Texas floods.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about what Schumer is asking. According to his office, the Senate minority leader has asked the Commerce Department\u8217\'20\'19s acting inspector general Duane Townsend \u8220\'20\'1Cto immediately to open an investigation into the scope, breadth, and ramifications of whether staffing shortages at key local National Weather Service (NWS) stations contributed to the catastrophic loss of life and property during the deadly flooding.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The full letter is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.democrats.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/nws_staffing_letter_to_noaa_oig.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T19:24:21.901Z">8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Three-week reprieve from tariffs little comfort for \uc2 European Union\par \par \uc2 There was cold comfort for the \uc2 EU\uc2  on Monday night as it emerged the bloc has only been given a three-week reprieve from the United States\u8217\'20\'19s threatened 50% tariffs.\par \par \uc2 Revealing the details of negotiations for the first time, the Irish deputy prime minister Simon Harris said he expects the status quo and its temporary pause on punitive tariffs to be extended until 1 August. That would be in line with an executive order the White House said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will soon sign.\par \par \uc2 Even then it was time to reach what he called \u8220\'20\'1Can agreement in principle\u8221\'20\'1D on a \u8220\'20\'1Cframework agreement\u8221\'20\'1D. It is not clear whether the car industry will be spared the 25% hike in tariffs as part of that framework agreement, an elementary aspect of Germany\u8217\'20\'19s demands for a quick deal.\par \par \uc2 Ireland, Germany and Italy are the members of the bloc that export more to the US than import but Ireland is considered most vulnerable per capita because of the numbers employed by pharmaceutical companies, many of them US multinationals.\par \par \uc2 Harris conceded that some of tariff would be permanent during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s regime, likely to be 10% and there was as yet no sign of any stay on sectoral tariffs including pharma, currently threatened by a \u8220\'20\'1Csection 232 investigation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris said:\par \par \uc2 I want to be clear that while it is likely there will be some form of tariffs going forward, their imposition even at a lower rate is bad for consumers, jobs, economic growth and investment. We have consistently called for zero-for-zero tariffs in as many areas as possible and I know the \uc2 EU\uc2  has advocated this course of action.\par \par \uc2 Uncertainty continues around the outcomes of the existing 232 investigations including on Pharma. This is obviously an area of significant concern to Ireland. However, my hope is that in the coming days and weeks both sides can work intensively and constructively to bring about an agreement.\par \par \uc2 This post has been updated to say that the comments came from Irish deputy prime minister Simon Harris, not taoiseach \uc2 Miche\u225\'00\'E1l Martin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T20:33:16.840Z">at 9.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T19:08:00.704Z">8.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson to meet \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  on Tuesday\par \par \uc2 Speaker of the House Mike Johnson will meet with Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  tomorrow, his office confirmed.\par \par \uc2 The meeting will take place at the Capitol, where only the Senate is in session this week, after congressional Republicans last week pulled multiple all-nighters to pass \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s One Big Beautiful Bill Act in time for his signature last Friday.\par \par \uc2 Most Republicans in Congress are supportive of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s defense, though some questioned the wisdom of supporting its hostilities with Iran. Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s visit to Washington will begin this evening when he stops by the White House to have dinner with Trump.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T19:33:16.288Z">at 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T18:38:53.283Z">7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump posts letters for Malaysia, Kazakhstan, South Africa, Laos and Myanmar\par \par \uc2 Trump has been posting more letters to world leaders on Truth Social, announcing new tariffs set to kick in from August.\par \par \uc2 These include:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 25% US tariffs on goods from Japan, South Korea, Malaysia and Kazakhstan\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 30% US tariffs on South Africa\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 40% US tariffs on Laos and Myanmar\par \par \uc2 More letters are expected over the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T18:43:22.450Z">at 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T18:23:34.746Z">7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 A formal \uc2 US government\uc2  review concluded that \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2  died by suicide, contradicting conspiracy theories that hold otherwise. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 A review of files held by the \uc2 US government\uc2  on the financier {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein}}}\uc2  has said there is no secret client list to be released, and confirmed his August 2019 death by suicide while in federal custody, both of which contradict conspiracy theories.\par \par \uc2 A memo said that a Department of Justice (DOJ) and \uc2 Federal Bureau of Investigation\uc2  (\uc2 FBI\uc2 ) review of the files \u8211\'20\'13 which has for years been teased as a treasure trove of information about a larger network of wrongdoing \u8211\'20\'13 concluded that no further charges are expected, as investigators \u8220\'20\'1Cdid not uncover evidence that could predicate an investigation against uncharged third parties\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The justice department also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/video-files/video2.mp4?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released hours of footage}}}\uc2  taken from Manhattan\u8217\'20\'19s metropolitan correctional center, showing that no one entered or left the area where Epstein was held during, before or after the time medical examiners concluded he took his life.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs part of our commitment to transparency, the Department of Justice and the \uc2 Federal Bureau of Investigation\uc2  have conducted an exhaustive review of investigative holdings relating to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D the DOJ said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/07/jeffrey-epstein-suicide-justice-department-fbi-review-confirms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein died by suicide, justice department and FBI review confirms}}}\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T18:12:18.639Z">7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the brewing controversy over whether there was enough warning of the Texas flash floods from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/07/texas-flood-survivor-reactions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2 , who is in Kerrville, Texas:\par \par \uc2 As Texas marshals a formidable response to the flash floods that have already killed dozens, questions are now being posed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/06/texas-floods-forecast-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about warnings that were given}}}\uc2  on Thursday and early Friday about the severity of the approaching storm and the coordination between local officials and the National Weather Service.\par \par \uc2 New flood alerts were issued for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Chill country\u8221\'20\'1D on Sunday, prompting rescue services to suspend the search for missing people, including at least 11 from Camp Mystic, the summer camp on the banks of the Guadalupe River hard hit by Friday\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas-floods-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flash flood}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At an early evening press briefing, Kerr county authorities said they were suspending the search and evacuating first responders from the river valley. They confirmed that 68 had died there, including 28 children. Not all have been identified, with officials still examining the bodies of 18 adults and 10 children.\par \par \uc2 Extraordinary tales of resilience have also emerged alongside videos of the destruction and loss that are circulating on social media. On Sunday, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/breaking911/status/1941958164749971970?s=46&t=qSYF7mcg_QrF3-bJ06OKCg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video was posted}}}\uc2  on X of girls from Camp Mystic being evacuated from the camp and singing the hymns Pass It On and Amazing Grace as they crossed a bridge over the still torrential Guadalupe River.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/07/texas-flood-survivor-reactions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18No warning at all\u8217\'20\'19: Texas flood survivors question safety planning and officials\u8217\'20\'19 response}}}\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T18:02:28.945Z">7.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Karoline Leavitt denied that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had ordered weapons shipments to Ukraine paused, instead saying the decision was made as part of a normal review of such shipments by the defense secretary, \uc2 Pete Hegseth\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was a standard review by the Pentagon of all weapons and all aid and all support that the United States is providing [to] all countries and all regions around the world, not just Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House press secretary said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo, it\u8217\'20\'19s a pause to review to ensure that everything the Pentagon is pushing out there is in the best interest of our military and our men and women in uniform.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pentagon officials have said the pause was needed to ensure the US has enough weapons for its own needs, but Democrats have accused them of lying:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/05/hegseth-weapons-shipments-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hegseth falsely cited weapon shortages in halting shipments to Ukraine, Democrats say}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T18:13:33.457Z">at 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T17:48:44.936Z">6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump will send more tariff letters to foreign leaders 'in the coming days', White House says\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will send foreign leaders more letters notifying them of new tariffs in the days to come, said Karoline Leavitt .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere will be additional letters in the coming days,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House press secretary said, in addition to the 12 he plans to send today and the two already made public, which were to South Korea and Japan\u8217\'20\'19s leaders,\par \par \uc2 As for why Trump decided to start with the two Asian allies, Leavitt said:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the president\u8217\'20\'19s prerogative and those are the countries he chose.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T18:11:01.072Z">at 7.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T17:39:04.561Z">6.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to send tariff letters to 12 more countries, formally delay reciprocal tariffs\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt said that in addition to Japan and South Korea, the leaders of 12 more countries will receive letters from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  announcing the imposition of new tariffs beginning next month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere will be approximately 12 other countries that will receive notifications and letters directly from the president of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Leavitt said. She added that Trump still planned to \u8220\'20\'1Ccreate tailor made trade plans for each and every country on this planet\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She also confirmed that Trump would formally extend his deadline for the imposition of reciprocal tariffs to 1 August from 9 July, with the intention of giving countries more time to negotiate deals:\par \par \uc2 The President will also sign an executive order today, delaying the July 9 deadline to August 1. So the reciprocal tariff rate, or these new rates that will be provided in this correspondence to these foreign leaders will be going out the door within the next month, or deals will be made, and those countries continue to negotiate with the United States. We\u8217\'20\'19ve seen a lot of positive developments in the right direction, but the administration, the president and his trade team, want to cut the best deals for the American people and the American worker. That\u8217\'20\'19s what they\u8217\'20\'19re focused on.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T17:39:30.123Z">at 6.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T17:34:30.033Z">6.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary says critics of flood warnings should be 'deeply ashamed'\par \par \uc2 Karoline Leavitt just kicked off the White House briefing for the day, beginning with an attack on those who have questioned whether the National Weather Service was adequately prepared to warn of the deadly flash floods in Texas.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary cited \u8220\'20\'1Csome members of the media\u8221\'20\'1D as well as \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  , the Democratic Senate minority leader who has reportedly called for an investigation from the commerce department inspector general into whether the National Weather Service had enough staff in offices that would have forecast the storms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBlaming President Trump for these floods is a depraved lie, and it serves no purpose during this time of national mourning. Here are the facts: in the lead-up to this tragic natural disaster, the National Weather Service did its job despite unprecedented rainfall,\u8221\'20\'1D Leavitt said.\par \par \uc2 She continued:\par \par \uc2 To any person who has deliberately lied about these facts surrounding this catastrophic event, you should be deeply ashamed. At this time, the administration\u8217\'20\'19s focus will be \u8230\'20\'26 on giving the victims in their communities the support they deserve during these recovery efforts in this tragic time. May God bless the great people of Texas, especially the parents who have lost their children. President Trump loves you. We are praying for you, and he will be traveling to see you later this week.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T18:12:03.834Z">at 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T17:28:25.153Z">6.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jul/07/donald-trump-elon-musk-new-party-us-politics-live-latest-news?page=with%3Ablock-686bf44b8f08aadc85ad0169#block-686bf44b8f08aadc85ad0169"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired a new tariff barrage}}}\uc2 , this time at Japan and South Korea, which will face 25% levies beginning 1 August unless it inks some kind of deal with Washington. The president broke the news in letters to the countries\u8217\'20\'19 leaders, and has said that more letters will be released today. We\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know if any of those materialize. Meanwhile, in Brussels, \uc2 European Union\uc2  ambassadors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jul/07/donald-trump-elon-musk-new-party-us-politics-live-latest-news?page=with%3Ablock-686bfd668f0833eb85210451#block-686bfd668f0833eb85210451"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have been briefed}}}\uc2  on a new trade framework with the United States that will prevent some \u8211\'20\'13 but not all \u8211\'20\'13 tariffs.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has been going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cideological deportation policy\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jul/07/donald-trump-elon-musk-new-party-us-politics-live-latest-news?page=with%3Ablock-686bdb138f08aadc85acffab#block-686bdb138f08aadc85acffab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 goes on trial}}}\uc2  today in Massachusetts.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  , a top trade adviser to Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jul/07/donald-trump-elon-musk-new-party-us-politics-live-latest-news?page=with%3Ablock-686bd0398f0833eb85210142#block-686bd0398f0833eb85210142"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hailed \u8220\'20\'1Cprogress\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  in tariff negotiations, even as the administration is set to blow its \u8220\'20\'1C90 deals in 90 days deadline\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jul/07/donald-trump-elon-musk-new-party-us-politics-live-latest-news?page=with%3Ablock-686bc5c08f08aadc85acfebd#block-686bc5c08f08aadc85acfebd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set to sign}}}\uc2  executive orders in the Oval Office at 4pm today, though the press is not set to attend. After that, he\u8217\'20\'19ll welcome \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  back to the White House.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T17:11:32.732Z">6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 European ambassadors briefed on draft US trade deal\par \par \uc2 EU\uc2  ambassadors are currently being briefed about the draft framework deal that seems to have been agreed over the weekend with the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 It will extend the period of negotiation, avoiding the threatened 50% tariffs on exports, but mean Trump\u8217\'20\'19s blanket 10% tariff will stay.\par \par \uc2 Ireland\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister says the deal is about creating a \u8220\'20\'1Cstable space\u8221\'20\'1D for further negotiations.\par \par \uc2 The taoiseach \uc2 Miche\u225\'00\'E1l Martin\uc2  said such a high level agreement would avoid retaliatory measures and escalation of a trade war.\par \par \uc2 It \u8220\'20\'1Cwould leave space for further discussions\u8221\'20\'1D he said adding it would create \u8220\'20\'1Ca deal of clarity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The prime minister was speaking after a call with \uc2 European Commission\uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  on Monday morning, European time.\par \par \uc2 A diplomatic source said the deal is \u8220\'20\'1Cfar from ideal\u8221\'20\'1D, but it means that the \uc2 EU\uc2  can now try and \u8220\'20\'1Ccontrol the controllable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T16:56:58.490Z">5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 In addition to announcing new tariffs on South Korea and Japan, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also threatened both countries with higher levies if they retaliate with their own trade measures.\par \par \uc2 From his letter to South Korea\u8217\'20\'19s president Lee Jae Myung :\par \par \uc2 If for any reason you decide to raise your Tariffs, then, whatever the number you choose to raise them by, will be added onto the 25% that we charge. Please understand that these Tariffs are necessary to correct the many years of Korea\u8217\'20\'19s Tariff, and Non Tariff, Policies and Trade Barriers, causing these unsustainable Trade Deficits against the United States. This Deficit is a major threat to our Economy and, indeed, our National Security!\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a certain tone to his letters, one that indicates a deal can be done if both countries accede to his trade demands. From his letter to Lee:\par \par \uc2 We look forward to working with you as your Trading Partner for many years to come. If you wish to open your heretofore closed Trading Markets to the United States, and eliminate your Tariff, and Non Tariff, Policies and Trade Barriers, we will, perhaps, consider an adjustment to this letter. These Tariffs may be modified, upward or downward, depending on our relationship with your Country. You will never be disappointed with The United States of America.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for your attention to this matter!\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T16:42:10.560Z">5.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said that starting today, he\u8217\'20\'19ll send \u8220\'20\'1C12, maybe 15\u8221\'20\'1D letters to major trading partners announcing new tariffs.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve now seen two letters, to the leaders of Japan and South Korea. We\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know what else Trump announces.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T16:28:10.615Z">5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump announces 25% tariffs on Japan, South Korea\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has released letters to the leaders of Japan and South Korea, announcing new 25% tariffs on both nations\u8217\'20\'19 exports to the United States and higher levies on goods transshipped through the countries.\par \par \uc2 The letters appear to be the first that administration officials planned to release today outlining new tariffs on major trading partners.\par \par \uc2 The letters to Japan\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister Ishiba Shigeru and South Korean president Lee Jae Myung are very similar. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Trump wrote to Shigeru and posted on Truth Social:\par \par \uc2 We have had years to discuss our Trading Relationship with Japan, and have concluded that we must move away from these longterm, and very persistent, Trade Deficits engendered by Japan\u8217\'20\'19s Tariff, and Non Tariff, Policies and Trade Barriers. Our relationship has been, unfortunately, far from Reciprocal. Starting on August 1, 2025, we will charge Japan a Tariff of only 25% on any and all Japanese products sent into the United States, separate from all Sectoral Tariffs. Goods transshipped to evade a higher Tariff will be subject to that higher Tariff. Please understand that the 25% number is far less than what is needed to eliminate the Trade Deficit disparity we have with your Country. As you are aware, there will be no Tariff if Japan, or companies within your Country, decide to build or manufacture product within the United States and, in fact, we will do everything possible to get approvals quickly, professionally, and routinely - In other words, in a matter of weeks.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T16:09:34.015Z">5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has made a last-minute addition to its schedule in the form of a briefing set for 1pm by press secretary Karoline Leavitt.\par \par \uc2 Leavitt will field questions from reporters in attendance, and we can only guess at what she\u8217\'20\'19ll try to focus their attention on. Expect questions about Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s visit today, if federal job cuts made the disaster in Texas worse and what to make of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s latest tariff threats.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T15:47:48.262Z">4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has openly mused about investigating the citizenship of Zohran Mamdani, the Democratic nominee for mayor of New York City. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  reports, the threat is part of a new trend that has seen the president question the immigration status of his detractors:\par \par \uc2 Threats of retribution from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  are hardly a novelty, but even by his standards, the US president\u8217\'20\'19s warnings of wrathful vengeance in recent days have represented a dramatic escalation.\par \par \uc2 In the past week, Trump has threatened deportation, loss of US citizenship or arrest against, respectively, the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest person, the prospective future mayor of New York and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former homeland security secretary.\par \par \uc2 The head-spinning catalogue of warnings may have been aimed at distracting from the increasing unpopularity, according to opinion surveys, of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda, some analysts say. But they also served as further alarm bells for the state of US democracy five and a half months into a presidency that has seen a relentless assault on constitutional norms, institutions and freedom of speech.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Trump turned his sights on none other than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 , the tech billionaire who, before a recent spectacular fallout, had been his closest ally in ramming through a radical agenda of upending and remaking the \uc2 US government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But when the \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  founder vowed to form a new party if Congress passed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s signature \u8220\'20\'1Cone big beautiful bill\u8221\'20\'1D into law, Trump swung into the retribution mode that is now familiar to his Democratic opponents.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWithout subsidies, Elon would probably have to close up shop and head back home to South Africa,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114776149269773065"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump posted on his Truth Social platform}}}\uc2 , menacing both the billions of dollars in federal subsidies received by Musk\u8217\'20\'19s companies, and \u8211\'20\'13 it seemed \u8211\'20\'13 his US citizenship, which the entrepreneur received in 2002 but which Trump supporters such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/05/us/steve-bannon-trump-elon-musk.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon have questioned}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/05/trump-threats-freedoms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 If the US president threatens to take away freedoms, are we no longer free?}}}\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T15:25:39.826Z">4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tom Homan, the official who \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has named \u8220\'20\'1Cborder czar\u8221\'20\'1D and put in charge of his mass deportation plans, spoke briefly to reporters at the White House earlier today.\par \par \uc2 He was asked what he thought of comments from Zohran Mamdani , who won the Democratic primary in the New York City mayor\u8217\'20\'19s race, that he would not cooperate with Homan\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to arrest and deport undocumented immigrants living in the city.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGood luck on that. We\u8217\'20\'19re gonna be in New York City,\u8221\'20\'1D Homan replied.\par \par \uc2 Trump has threatened Mamdani since he emerged as the frontrunner to become mayor of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s largest city. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/29/trump-zohran-mamdani-nyc-funds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump threatens to cut off New York City funds if Mamdani \u8216\'20\'18doesn\u8217\'20\'19t behave\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T15:00:37.075Z">4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  logged on to Truth Social this morning to, randomly enough, post words of support for \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2 , the former Brazilian president who is on trial over an alleged coup plot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBrazil is doing a terrible thing on their treatment of former President \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2 . I have watched, as has the World, as they have done nothing but come after him, day after day, night after night, month after month, year after year! He is not guilty of anything, except having fought for THE PEOPLE,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump wrote, adding \u8220\'20\'1CLEAVE BOLSONARO ALONE!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bolsonaro took the stand to deny the allegations about a month ago:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jun/10/brazil-jair-bolsonaro-coup-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bolsonaro denies coup plot but admits discussing \u8216\'20\'18alternative ways\u8217\'20\'19 to remain president}}}\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T14:37:46.575Z">3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trial set to begin over Trump administration's \u8216\'20\'18ideological-deportation policy\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 One of the first major trials of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s policies is set to begin today, over his administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to deport foreign students who take part in pro-Palestinian activism. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on what we can expect from the case, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alice-speri"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alice Speri}}}\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 A lawsuit challenging the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s effort to deport foreign students over pro-Palestinian views goes to trial in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/massachusetts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Massachusetts}}}\uc2  federal court on Monday, where the government for the first time will need to defend its extraordinary position that it can deport noncitizens over their political speech.\par \par \uc2 The case was brought by the national \uc2 American Association of University Professors\uc2  (AAUP); its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/harvard-university"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harvard}}}\uc2 , Rutgers and \uc2 New York University\uc2  chapters; and the Middle East Studies Association (Mesa) following the arrest and detention of several noncitizen students and scholars who have spoken out on Palestinian rights. The government has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/10/mahmoud-khalil-memo-marco-rubio-deport-beliefs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed the authority}}}\uc2  to deport noncitizens who have committed no crimes but whose presence it deems poses a threat to US foreign policy.\par \par \uc2 The case is the first of half-dozen legal challenges to the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s sweeping crackdown on universities to make it to trial, with civil rights and education advocates asking the judge to declare the \u8220\'20\'1Cideological-deportation policy\u8221\'20\'1D unconstitutional and unlawful.\par \par \uc2 Those arrested as part of the government\u8217\'20\'19s promised campaign against pro-Palestinian foreign students have all been released from immigration detention, with the last of them \u8211\'20\'13 Mahmoud Khalil \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/20/mahmoud-khalil-release-federal-judge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 freed on 20 June}}}\uc2 . But they all continue to fight against efforts to deport them. Other students left the US or went into hiding to avoid arrest.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/07/trial-trump-ideological-deportation-policy-pro-palestinian-students"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trial to consider Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18ideological-deportation policy\u8217\'20\'19 targeting pro-Palestinian students }}}\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T14:16:54.233Z">3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 European leaders are meanwhile bracing for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s next move on tariffs, which may come as soon as today in the form of letters sent to countries letting them know how much they\u8217\'20\'19ll have to pay to access the US market.\par \par \uc2 Our Business live blog is covering that side of the story, and you can read it here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/jul/07/donald-trump-threatens-10-tariff-brics-trade-war-deadline-deals-letters-business-live-news-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 EU\u8217\'20\'19s von der Leyen has \u8216\'20\'18good exchange\u8217\'20\'19 on trade with Trump, as US threatens Brics group with extra 10% tariff \u8211\'20\'13 business live}}}\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T13:55:09.721Z">2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump trade advisor hails 'progress' as administration set to blow '90 deals in 90 days' deadline\par \par \uc2 Shortly after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  paused his disruptive \u8220\'20\'1Cliberation day\u8221\'20\'1D tariffs last April, his top trade adviser, \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  , went on \uc2 Fox Business Network\uc2  to promise \u8220\'20\'1C90 deals in 90 days\u8221\'20\'1D with major trading partners.\par \par \uc2 It seemed a wildly unrealistic goal, considering such agreements can take months or years to hammer out. The 9 July deadline for those deals is nigh, and Washington has just two new trade deals \u8211\'20\'13 with the UK and Vietnam \u8211\'20\'13 to show for its efforts, and other White House officials have since downplayed the seriousness of that deadline.\par \par \uc2 Navarro appeared on CNBC this morning and was asked whether he was disappointed that the barrage of deals did not come to be. He replied:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m happy with with the progress we\u8217\'20\'19ve had, because every country that we run a major deficit with is fully engaged. I think what we\u8217\'20\'19re learning from the negotiations is simply \u8230\'20\'26 how difficult it is for these countries to give up the advantage they have over us.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T13:30:38.615Z">2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re also live blogging the latest tragic news out of flood-stricken Texas, where confirmation arrived this morning of the deaths of 27 girls and counsellors at a summer camp.\par \par \uc2 You can follow along here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jul/07/texas-floods-rescue-teams-search-missing-more-heavy-rains-forecast-latest-news-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas flooding live updates: Girls summer camp confirms 27 campers and counsellors dead}}}\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T13:06:32.600Z">2.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 We expect to get our first glimpse of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at 4pm ET today, when he signs unspecified executive orders in the Oval Office, according to the White House schedule.\par \par \uc2 Reporters won\u8217\'20\'19t be invited to that one, but that could always change \u8211\'20\'13 he often uses such occasions to hold forth to the press. After that, Trump is scheduled to greet \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  at the White House, then have dinner with him, beginning at 6:30pm.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T12:14:33.236Z">1.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 US to make several trade announcements in next 48 hours, treasury secretary says\par \par \uc2 The United States will make several trade announcements in the next 48 hours, treasury secretary Scott Bessent has said this morning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve had a lot of people change their tune in terms of negotiations. So my mailbox was full last night with a lot of new offers, a lot of new proposals,\u8221\'20\'1D Bessent told CNBC. \u8220\'20\'1CSo it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a busy couple of days.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It comes amid confusion over when the administration\u8217\'20\'19s new tariff rates will come into effect. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said the US would start delivering tariff letters from 12:00pm ET today, but they will apparently be delayed, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/06/trump-tariff-delay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 going into effect on 1 August}}}\uc2  and not 9 July as previously expected.\par \par \uc2 Asked if the tariffs were coming into effect on 1 August or this week, Trump \u8211\'20\'13 helpfully \u8211\'20\'13 replied: \u8220\'20\'1CNo, there are going to be tariffs, the tariffs, the tariffs are going to be, the tariffs. I think we\u8217\'20\'19ll have most countries done by July 9, yeah. Either a letter or a deal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The letters would not necessarily provide an ultimatum, according to Bessent . \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just \u8216\'20\'18thank you for wanting to trade with the United States of America. We welcome you as a trading partner, and here\u8217\'20\'19s the rate, unless you want to come back and try to negotiate,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Bessent declined to comment on whether negotiations on new ownership of the TikTok short video app, which Trump also said would start this week, would be linked to trade talks with China .\par \par \uc2 He said he would meet with his Chinese counterpart in the next couple of weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think there are things for us to do together if the Chinese want to do it, so we will discuss whether we are able to move beyond trade into other areas,\u8221\'20\'1D he told CNBC.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T12:45:32.775Z">at 1.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T11:47:23.439Z">12.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trial to consider Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18ideological-deportation policy\u8217\'20\'19 targeting pro-Palestinian students\par \par \uc2 Alice Speri is a journalist covering foreign policy, conflict and human rights\par \par \uc2 A lawsuit challenging the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s effort to deport foreign students over pro-Palestinian views goes to trial in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/massachusetts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Massachusetts}}}\uc2  federal court on Monday, where the government for the first time will need to defend its extraordinary position that it can deport noncitizens over their political speech.\par \par \uc2 The case was brought by the national \uc2 American Association of University Professors\uc2  (AAUP); its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/harvard-university"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harvard}}}\uc2 , Rutgers and \uc2 New York University\uc2  chapters; and the Middle East Studies Association (Mesa) following the arrest and detention of several noncitizen students and scholars who have spoken out on Palestinian rights. The government has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/10/mahmoud-khalil-memo-marco-rubio-deport-beliefs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed the authority}}}\uc2  to deport noncitizens who have committed no crimes but whose presence it deems poses a threat to US foreign policy.\par \par \uc2 The case is the first of half-dozen legal challenges to the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s sweeping crackdown on universities to make it to trial, with civil rights and education advocates asking the judge to declare the \u8220\'20\'1Cideological-deportation policy\u8221\'20\'1D unconstitutional and unlawful.\par \par \uc2 Those arrested as part of the government\u8217\'20\'19s promised campaign against pro-Palestinian foreign students have all been released from immigration detention, with the last of them \u8211\'20\'13 Mahmoud Khalil \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/20/mahmoud-khalil-release-federal-judge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 freed on 20 June}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But they all continue to fight against efforts to deport them. Other students left the US or went into hiding to avoid arrest.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/07/trial-trump-ideological-deportation-policy-pro-palestinian-students"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trial to consider Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18ideological-deportation policy\u8217\'20\'19 targeting pro-Palestinian students }}}\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T11:48:12.306Z">at 12.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T11:23:40.557Z">12.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 The president of the \uc2 European Commission\uc2 , \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  , said she had a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood exchange\u8221\'20\'1D with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Sunday, a Commission spokesperson told reporters during a daily press briefing this morning.\par \par \uc2 The spokesperson said:\par \par \uc2 We want to reach a deal with the US (by 9 July). We want to avoid tariffs. We believe they cause pain. We want to achieve win-win outcomes, not lose-lose outcomes.\par \par \uc2 Trump imposed a 20% import tax on all EU-made products in early April as part of a set of tariffs targeting countries with which the US has a trade imbalance. Hours after the nation-specific duties took effect, he put them on hold until 9 July at a standard rate of 10% to quiet financial markets and allow time for negotiations.\par \par \uc2 US officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/06/trump-tariff-delay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have now indicated}}}\uc2  that tariffs will begin on 1 August, with countries \u8211\'20\'13 and blocs like the EU - scrambling to make last minute trade deals as the deadline nears.\par \par \uc2 Von der Leyen\uc2  has conceded there is insufficient time to agree on a comprehensive agreement due to the volume and complexity of EU-US trade, but could strike a trade deal in principle.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T11:27:30.258Z">at 12.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T10:46:08.031Z">11.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Texas floods: rescue teams continue search for missing with more heavy rains forecast\par \par \uc2 We can now bring you the latest updates from the devastating Texas floods that have killed at least 82 people. Rescuers are working around the clock to find survivors but their efforts may be hampered by more heavy rain that is expected to fall today.\par \par \uc2 Most of the fatalities were in Kerr County , where Camp Mystic , a Christian girls\u8217\'20\'19 camp, was deluged.\par \par \uc2 Kerr county\u8217\'20\'19s sheriff, Larry Leitha, said at a briefing on Sunday afternoon that 68 people had been confirmed dead in the county, including 28 children, with the search continuing for the missing girls and their counselor from Camp Mystic, along the Guadalupe river .\par \par \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19s governor, Greg Abbott, said in an earlier briefing that another 10 fatalities had been confirmed in neighboring counties. Abbott said that officials were still searching for 41 known missing persons across the state.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  signed a major disaster declaration on Sunday for Kerr county and said he would likely visit on Friday. You can read more in our Texas floods live blog {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jul/07/texas-floods-rescue-teams-search-missing-more-heavy-rains-forecast-latest-news-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T10:20:55.481Z">11.20am BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s global affairs correspondent, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roth-andrew"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Roth}}}\uc2 , has written up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jul/07/netanyahu-israel-iran-gaza-white-house-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this analysis}}}\uc2  exploring the complicated relationship between Netanyahu and Trump and the prospects of a Gaza ceasefire deal. Here is a snippet:\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu and Trump have a complex personal relationship \u8211\'20\'13 and Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2025/jun/24/trump-swears-in-outburst-at-israel-and-iran-over-ceasefire-violations-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 openly vented frustration}}}\uc2  at him last month during efforts to negotiate a truce with Iran \u8211\'20\'13 but the two have appeared in lockstep since the US launched a bombing run against Iran\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear programme, fulfilling a key goal for Israeli war planners.\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu arrives in Washington in a strong political position, observers have said, potentially giving him the diplomatic cover he would need to end the war in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2  without facing a revolt from his rightwing supporters that could lead to the collapse of his government\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 As Netanyahu comes to Washington on Monday for the third time since Trump\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration, he appears to know exactly what he is doing. And while Trump has touted his bona fides as a dealmaker, the decision for when and how a ceasefire is implemented in Gaza appears ultimately out of his hands.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T10:00:38.401Z">11.00am BST\par \par \uc2 You can read more about the Israeli prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s visit in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/jul/07/middle-east-crisis-live-trump-gaza-hostages-release-netanyahu-meeting-israel-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our Middle East live blog}}}\uc2  being helmed by the excellent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/charlie-moloney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Charlie Moloney}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T09:58:31.898Z">10.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Cautious hopes for a Gaza ceasefire breakthrough as Netanyahu arrives in Washington\par \par \uc2 Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  is arriving in Washington today to meet his closest ally, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who has pushed for a \u8220\'20\'1Cdeal this week\u8221\'20\'1D between \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and Israel.\par \par \uc2 Trump is not scheduled to meet Netanyahu until 6:30 pm (2230 GMT) Monday, the White House said, without the usual presence of journalists.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli leader, who has relied on US weapons to fuel his country\u8217\'20\'19s assault on Gaza, said he believed his discussions with Trump on Monday would help advance talks on a hostage release and ceasefire deal that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jul/05/israel-airstrikes-gaza-hamas-ceasefire-talks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israeli negotiators resumed in Qatar on Sunday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ahead of Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s third visit since Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to office this year, Trump said there was a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood chance\u8221\'20\'1D of reaching an agreement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve gotten a lot of the hostages out, but pertaining to the remaining hostages, quite a few of them will be coming out,\u8221\'20\'1D he told journalists.\par \par \uc2 About 1,200 people were killed and 251 taken hostage in the \uc2 Hamas\uc2 -led 7 October attack on southern Israel in 2023, triggering Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war on Gaza, which, according to the territory\u8217\'20\'19s health ministry, has killed over 57,000 Palestinian people to date.\par \par \uc2 Around 20 of the remaining hostages are believed to be still alive. A majority of the original hostages have been freed through diplomatic negotiations, though the Israeli military has also recovered some.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T10:01:38.263Z">at 11.01am BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T09:44:13.735Z">10.44am BST\par \par \uc2 US to start sending letters to US trade partners dictating new tariffs, Trump says\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said his administration plans to start sending letters on Monday to US trade partners dictating new tariffs, amid confusion over when the new rates will come into effect.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt could be 12, maybe 15 [letters],\u8221\'20\'1D the president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtu.be/ZSNB8E6ckJM?si=WvB0qgYGOja9V6cV&t=49"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cand we\u8217\'20\'19ve made deals also, so we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have a combination of letters and some deals have been made.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/05/trump-tariff-pause-inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously announced}}}\uc2  90-day pause on tariffs set to end on 9 July, the president was asked if the new rates would come into effect this week or on 1 August, as some officials had suggested.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo, there are going to be tariffs, the tariffs, the tariffs are going to be, the tariffs,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtu.be/ZSNB8E6ckJM?si=n3RJVkEKNGOW484q&t=212"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the president began}}}\uc2  uncertainly. \u8220\'20\'1CI think we\u8217\'20\'19ll have most countries done by July 9, yeah. Either a letter or a deal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sensing the confusion, his commerce secretary, Howard Lutnick, jumped in to add: \u8220\'20\'1CBut they go into effect on August 1. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tariffs}}}\uc2  go into effect August 1, but the president is setting the rates and the deals right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story, by my colleagues {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/robert-mackey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Mackey}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-almeida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Almeida}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lisaocarroll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lisa O\u8217\'20\'19Carroll}}}\uc2 , here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/06/trump-tariff-delay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump and US commerce secretary say tariffs are delayed until 1 August, sparking confusion}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T09:57:18.907Z">at 10.57am BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T09:20:03.528Z">10.20am BST\par \par \uc2 The US is extremely mindful of \uc2 BRICS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 economic might and its growing influence on the diplomatic stage. The group, often described as the developing world\u8217\'20\'19s alternative to the G7 group of nations, has undergone a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/aug/24/five-brics-nations-announce-admission-of-six-new-countries-to-bloc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent rapid expansion}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BRICS\uc2  was founded by Brazil, Russia, India, China and South Africa, but the group last year expanded to include Indonesia, Iran, Egypt, Ethiopia and the UAE.\par \par \uc2 Some of its members have denounced US tariff policies and have suggested reforms to how major currencies are valued.\par \par \uc2 The group pushes for greater representation for emerging economies and thinks western countries have a disproportionate influence on global organisations like the World Bank and International Monetary Fund.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T09:20:57.442Z">at 10.20am BST\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T09:16:30.350Z">10.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  threatens extra 10% tariff for \u8216\'20\'18anti-American\u8217\'20\'19 Brics policies\par \par \uc2 In other news, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has widened his trade war after saying the US will impose an additional 10% tariff on any countries aligning themselves with the \u8220\'20\'1Canti-American policies\u8221\'20\'1D of the \uc2 BRICS\uc2  group of developing nations that include China and Russia.\par \par \uc2 Trump wrote on social media:\par \par \uc2 Any country aligning themselves with the Anti-American policies of \uc2 BRICS\uc2 , will be charged an ADDITIONAL 10% tariff. There will be no exceptions to this policy.\par \par \uc2 His comments came after a joint Sunday statement from the opening of the \uc2 BRICS\uc2  summit in Rio de Janeiro in which the group warned the rise in tariffs threatened global trade, continuing its veiled criticism of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s erratic tariff policies.\par \par \uc2 Since his return to the White House, Trump has announced a series of steep import taxes on foreign goods, arguing they will protect American jobs and the US manufacturing industry.\par \par \uc2 In April, in line with this protectionist view, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/02/trump-new-tariffs-liberation-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  a 10% base tariff rate on most countries and additional duties ranging up to 50%, although he later delayed the effective date for all but 10% duties until 9 July.\par \par \uc2 The negotiating window until 9 July has led to announced deals only with the UK and Vietnam. You can read more on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariff threat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/jul/07/donald-trump-threatens-10-tariff-brics-trade-war-deadline-deals-letters-business-live-news-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in our business live blog}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T08:56:20.158Z">9.56am BST\par \par \uc2 My colleagues {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/robert-mackey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Mackey}}}\uc2  have a little more detail about how the feud between the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man and the world\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful man has recently escalated. Here is an extract {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/06/elon-musk-america-party-scott-bessent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from their story}}}\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 When the pair fell out earlier in the summer, Musk lashed out during an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/05/trump-elon-musk-fallout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 astonishing social media duel}}}\uc2  in which he stated Trump\u8217\'20\'19s name was in the files relating to associates of the late pedophile and sex trafficker \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Musk later deleted the post and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/jun/11/elon-musk-trump-regret-posts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apologized to the president}}}\uc2  as they embarked on an uneasy truce. On Sunday, however, Musk returned to the subject, reposting a photo of the jailed Epstein facilitator Ghislaine Maxwell that questioned why she was the only person in prison while men who engaged in sex with underage girls \u8211\'20\'13 a crime colloquially known in the US as statutory rape \u8211\'20\'13 were not.\par \par \uc2 In other posts he said it would be \u8220\'20\'1Cnot hard\u8221\'20\'1D to break the two-party stranglehold in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  enjoyed by Democrats and Republicans\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Trump has made clear his feelings about his former friend in recent days after criticism of the bill. In response to Musk\u8217\'20\'19s posts calling the bill \u8220\'20\'1Cinsane\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump said he might {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/01/trump-musk-feud-doge-deportation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Clook into\u8221\'20\'1D deporting}}}\uc2  the South African-born, naturalized US citizen billionaire.\par \par \uc2 2025-07-07T08:50:10.756Z">9.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump calls Musk's new political party 'ridiculous' and says \uc2 Tesla\uc2  owner is 'off the rails'\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our live coverage of US politics and the second {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  has hit out at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to start and bankroll a new US political party that the tech billionaire believes can offer a viable alternative to the Democrats and Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters before boarding Air Force One yesterday, the US president said:\par \par \uc2 I think it\u8217\'20\'19s ridiculous to start a third party. It\u8217\'20\'19s always been a two-party system and I think starting a third party just adds to the confusion.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after speaking about his former ally, Trump posted further comments on his Truth Social platform, writing:\par \par \uc2 I am saddened to watch \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  go completely \u8216\'20\'18off the rails,\u8217\'20\'19 essentially becoming a TRAIN WRECK over the past five weeks.\par \par \uc2 Trump and Musk were formerly close allies, with the \uc2 Tesla\uc2  boss and X owner appointed to slash federal spending through the unofficial \uc2 Department of Government Efficiency\uc2  (Doge) from January through May.\par \par \uc2 Musk fell out with the Republican president over his sprawling tax and spending plan, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jul/01/what-is-in-big-beautiful-bill-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed into law on Friday}}}\uc2 , which is expected to add at least $3 trillion (\u163\'00\'A32.2 trillion) to the US\u8217\'20\'19s already huge $37tn (\u163\'00\'A327tn) debt pile. Musk has argued that the bill, which he has described as \u8220\'20\'1Cutterly insane and destructive\u8221\'20\'1D, would irresponsibly add to the US national debt.\par \par \uc2 Musk, the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest person, posted on X over the weekend that he had set up the America Party to challenge the Republican and Democratic \u8220\'20\'1CUniparty\u8221\'20\'1D. The details of the structure of the new venture or a timeline for its creation are still unclear.\par \par \uc2 But some of his social media posts suggests the new political party would focus on two or three Senate seats, and eight to 10 House districts.\par \par \uc2 We will have more on this and other US politics stories throughout the day so stick with us.\par \par \uc2 Updated 2025-07-07T09:28:57.615Z">at 10.28am BST \par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250707el770015r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
