\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Ice \u8216\'20\'18politically targeted\u8217\'20\'19 farm worker activist Juarez Zeferino, colleagues say\b0\par\par\uc2 Dharna Noor \par \uc2 1,939 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 July 2025\par 14:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Detention comes amid Trump crackdown against perceived political enemies, including immigrants and labor leaders\par \par \uc2 Farm worker activist Alfredo \u8220\'20\'1CLelo\u8221\'20\'1D Juarez Zeferino, 25, was driving his partner to her job on a tulip farm north of Seattle one March morning when they were pulled over by an unmarked car. A plainclothes agent for \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice) emerged and shattered Juarez Zeferino\u8217\'20\'19s front window before handcuffing him, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cascadiadaily.com/2025/apr/24/skagit-farmworker-leaders-implore-sen-murray-to-help-hold-ice-accountable/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his partner said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The officer drove Juarez Zeferino to a nondescript warehouse \u8211\'20\'13 the same one he and other activists had years ago {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cascadiadaily.com/2022/jan/28/unmarked-dhs-facilities-uncovered-in-ferndale/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discovered is an unmarked Ice holding facility}}}\uc2 . After his 25 March detention, dozens gathered outside to demand his release.\par \par \uc2 Instead, he was transferred to the Northwest Ice Processing Center in Tacoma, Washington, where he has been held ever since.\par \par \uc2 Officially, Juarez Zeferino\u8217\'20\'19s arrest was based on a deportation order. But the activist\u8217\'20\'19s detention comes as the Trump administration has launched an aggressive crackdown against its perceived political enemies, including both immigrants and labor organizers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe, no question, that he was a target,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rosalinda Guillen, veteran farm worker organizer and founder of Community to Community Development, where Juarez Zeferino volunteered.\par \par \uc2 The young organizer has played an instrumental role in securing protections for Washington farm workers, including strengthened statewide heat protections for outdoor laborers mandating water breaks when temperatures top 80F, enshrined in 2023. In 2021, he and other activists also won a law guaranteeing farm workers overtime pay. And in 2019, advocacy from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/nov/14/domestic-farm-workers-h-2a-trump-deportation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Juarez Zeferino and other campaigners}}}\uc2  about exploitation in the H-2A guest worker program prompted Washington to create the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.yakimaherald.com/news/local/new-state-committee-examining-h2-a-and-agricultural-workforce-meets-monday/article_05b91dc2-3e36-5fe8-bb44-5a7826a98bab.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nation\u8217\'20\'19s first-ever oversight committee}}}\uc2  for foreign workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a very humble person, very quiet but yet very determined and willing to go to whatever extent to get victory for his people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Edgar Franks, political director of Familias Unidas por la Justicia, an independent farm worker union which Juarez Zeferino helped found.\par \par \uc2 His successful track record has earned him renown in labor and immigrant justice circles across the country. Franks believes it also made him a \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical target\u8221\'20\'1D for Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe just have to look at the record of everybody that has been targeted by the Trump administration, from the students at Columbia to [the detention of immigration activist Jeanette Vizguerra] in Colorado,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s already a track of people that have been targeted to silence them and to make sure that the people that look up to them get silenced.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reached for comment, the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  spokesperson, Tricia McLaughlin, said that allegations of Ice politically targeting Juarez Zeferino were \u8220\'20\'1Ccategorically FALSE\u8221\'20\'1D, calling him \u8220\'20\'1Can illegal alien from Mexico with a final order of removal from a judge\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only thing that makes someone a target of Ice is if they are in the United States illegally,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 She said the activist, whom she called \u8220\'20\'1CJuan Juarez-Ceferino,\u8221\'20\'1D refused to comply with Ice during his arrest, and that officers used the \u8220\'20\'1Cminimum amount of force necessary to resolve the situation\u8221\'20\'1D and protect themselves.\par \par \uc2 In court, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cascadiadaily.com/2025/may/08/bond-for-farmworker-activist-alfredo-juarez-zeferino-deferred-at-hearing/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DHS attorney also said Juarez Zeferino was noncompliant during his arrest,}}}\uc2  and claimed he was a flight risk because he had previously missed a court hearing.\par \par \uc2 His lawyer Larkin VanDerhoef denied that his client was a flight risk, saying he was unaware of his missed court date. In court, he noted that Juarez Zeferino had received dozens of letters, demonstrating that he is a \u8220\'20\'1Cpositive force\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said Juarez Zeferino complied with the officers who arrested him. \u8220\'20\'1CLelo had opened his window to talk to officers and was asking to see their warrant for his arrest when they smashed his window,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that a group of officers from not only Ice, but also border patrol, homeland security investigations, and the \uc2 Drug Enforcement Administration\uc2  worked together to arrest him.\par \par \uc2 Juarez Zeferino\u8217\'20\'19s detention has sparked concern among other immigrant workers fighting for better labor conditions, and since his arrest, others have also been detained. In April armed Customs and Border Protection agents {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.burlingtonfreepress.com/story/news/2025/04/22/vermont-migrants-arrested-dairy-farm-workers/83220821007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raided a Vermont dairy farm}}}\uc2  and arrested eight immigrant laborers who were involved with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://migrantjustice.net/milk-with-dignity-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 labor rights campaign}}}\uc2 . Last month, Ice also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.1199seiu.org/magazine/members-rally-solidarity-detained-farm-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ufw.org/ufw-to-hold-rallies-for-ufw-farm-worker-leaders-detained-by-ice-in-ny/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 farm worker leaders}}}\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a good strategy to squelch union organizing as well as farm worker advocacy, but it is horrifying to us that some of the people who make the lowest salaries in our country are being deported even as they provide the necessary workforce to keep our country fed,\u8221\'20\'1D said Julie Taylor, executive director of the National Farm Worker Ministry, a faith-based organization which supports farm worker organizing.\par \par \uc2 From a traffic stop to a deportation order\par \par \uc2 Juarez Zeferino was arrested on the grounds of a 2018 deportation order. It stemmed from a 2015 traffic stop by Bellingham, Washington, police officers who then turned him over to Ice.\par \par \uc2 After the stop, Juarez Zeferino \u8211\'20\'13 then a minor \u8211\'20\'13 was detained for less than 24 hours. He later sued Bellingham and its police department saying that his arrest was the result of racial profiling; the city settled for $100,000.\par \par \uc2 The farm worker activist\u8217\'20\'19s friends and legal counsel said he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cascadiadaily.com/2025/may/08/bond-for-farmworker-activist-alfredo-juarez-zeferino-deferred-at-hearing/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unaware of the deportation order}}}\uc2 , which was mailed to an address Juarez Zeferino provided but then bounced back to the government.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe wasn\u8217\'20\'19t in hiding,\u8221\'20\'1D said Franks. \u8220\'20\'1CHe was out in the open, doing media and serving on city commissions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 His lawyer VanDerhoef successfully had the order reopened in April this year \u8211\'20\'13 just one day before Juarez Zeferino was due to be placed on a deportation flight.\par \par \uc2 But in May, an immigration court judge ruled that she had no jurisdiction to grant bond to Juarez Zeferino \u8211\'20\'13 a decision VanDerhoef quickly appealed.\par \par \uc2 VanDerhoef said the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling was based on an unusual legal interpretation by Tacoma judges, who routinely argue that they lack jurisdiction to issue bonds to immigrants who entered the country without a visa. He signed his client on to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seattletimes.com/seattle-news/tacoma-immigration-judges-are-toughest-in-u-s-on-bond-suit-says/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 class-action lawsuit}}}\uc2  focused on the issue.\par \par \uc2 He also filed a motion to terminate the case against his client. In June, a court denied the motion, so the next step will probably be to apply for asylum in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re basically weighing what other options he has, what he can apply for,\u8221\'20\'1D VanDerhoef said.\par \par \uc2 Aaron Korthuis, an attorney at the Northwest Immigrant Rights Project, who is representing Juarez Zeferino in the class-action lawsuit, said he did not doubt the activist was a political target.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of what this administration is doing is attempting to send a message through its arrests [and] through its removals,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t shock anyone that who they are targeting for arrest is part and parcel of the larger effort to intimidate, exact retribution, and send a message.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 VanDerhoef declined to comment on whether or not his client\u8217\'20\'19s arrest was politically motivated, but said it was unsurprising that it had sparked concern about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s immigration policies among other farm workers. \u8220\'20\'1CThe last thing I want to do is cause any more fear or panic that is already high among immigrant communities,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I do think this administration has shown that nothing is off the table when it comes to who they will target and also the tactics they use.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Experts say the Trump administration has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/13/trump-immigration-due-process-legal-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 violated court norms and ignored court orders }}}\uc2 in its attacks on immigrants. The president has also made life harder for immigration attorneys, including in a memorandum claiming they engage in \u8220\'20\'1Cunscrupulous behavior\u8221\'20\'1D. And the sheer number of Ice raids conducted under his administration also makes it harder for such lawyers to do their jobs, said VanDerhoef.\par \par \uc2 In the north-east US, Ice arrests have increased so much that officials are \u8220\'20\'1Crunning into space issues\u8221\'20\'1D, said VanDerhoef. The immigration prison where Juarez Zeferino is being held has so far exceeded its capacity that some people have been transferred without warning to facilities in Los Angeles and Alaska.\par \par \uc2 The overcrowding also creates challenges when it comes to representation, VanDerhoef said. These days, visitation rooms are often so overbooked that he and other attorneys are facing \u8220\'20\'1Chalf a day waits\u8221\'20\'1D to meet with their clients.\par \par \uc2 He worries that attorneys cannot keep up with the increase in Ice arrests. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are not significantly more lawyers doing this work even though there are significantly more people being detained,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Back to the struggle\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Guillen, the veteran farm worker organizer, first met Juarez Zeferino in 2013, when he he was a 13-year-old who had recently arrived in the US from Mexico. He was so small that he looked more like he was 11, she said, but he was \u8220\'20\'1Ca hard worker\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cfierce\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That year, Juarez Zeferino and about 200 workers on a Washington berry farm walked off the job demanding better working conditions and pay. Over the next four years, they organized work stoppages and boycotts, with Juarez Zeferino \u8211\'20\'13 who speaks English, Spanish and his native Mixteco \u8211\'20\'13 often serving as a spokesperson.\par \par \uc2 In 2017, the workers were granted a union election, resulting in the formation of Familias Unidas por la Justicia, an independent farm worker union representing hundreds of Indigenous farm workers.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a \u8220\'20\'1Cnightmare\u8221\'20\'1D organization for Trump, who doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want to see immigrant laborers organized, said Guillen. \u8220\'20\'1CThese are communities that normally are marginalized, fighting for their rights and winning,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. ea05a110-2f0f-41ea-ba0a-8d9189dbddb7\par \par \uc2 The best public interest journalism relies on first-hand accounts from people in the know.\par \par \uc2 If you have something to share on this subject you can contact us confidentially using the following methods.\par \par \uc2 Secure Messaging in the Guardian app\par \par \uc2 The Guardian app has a tool to send tips about stories. Messages are end to end encrypted and concealed within the routine activity that every Guardian mobile app performs. This prevents an observer from knowing that you are communicating with us at all, let alone what is being said.\par \par \uc2 If you don't already have the Guardian app, download it ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.apple.com/app/the-guardian-live-world-news/id409128287"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 iOS}}}\uc2 /{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.guardian"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Android}}}\uc2 ) and go to the menu. Select 'Secure Messaging'.\par \par \uc2 SecureDrop, instant messengers, email, telephone and post\par \par \uc2 See our guide at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tips"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 theguardian.com/tips}}}\uc2  for alternative methods and the pros and cons of each.\par \par \uc2 Since Juarez Zeferino\u8217\'20\'19s arrest, calls for his freedom have met with an outpouring of support, Guillen said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll the legislators know him, and there was immediate support for him in letters and calls,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 But she wishes Democrats would do more to fight for workers like him, including by trying to stop Ice arrests within Washington. \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats need to be bolder,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Franks agreed, and said workers like Juarez Zeferino should obtain amnesty from Ice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust a couple years ago we were essential workers and the heroes but now we\u8217\'20\'19re the terrorists and the criminals,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Asked if she had visited Juarez Zeferino, Guillen said, \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t do it.\u8221\'20\'1D She worries about his health and wellbeing in the facility.\par \par \uc2 Franks, too, said he was concerned that the \u8220\'20\'1Calready skinny\u8221\'20\'1D Juarez Zeferino will become malnourished while in detention. But when he has visited the young activist, he said he was \u8220\'20\'1Ctrying to keep his spirits up\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s still messing around and joking around,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd he\u8217\'20\'19s like, \u8216\'20\'18when I get out, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to do this, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to do that.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked what is on that to-do list, Franks said Juarez Zeferino wants to be reunited with his family. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd he wants to get back to the struggle,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250707el77001mi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
