\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Dating app \uc2 Bumble\uc2  to lay off hundreds of staff amid turnaround bid\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 368 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2025\par 16:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Company is cutting 30% of its global workforce as part of an effort to return to a \u8216\'20\'18start-up mentality\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Dating app \uc2 Bumble\uc2  announced plans to lay off almost a third of its workforce as part of a bid to return to a \u8220\'20\'1Cstart-up mentality\u8221\'20\'1D as it fights to revive growth.\par \par \uc2 The Austin, Texas-based company is cutting about 240 roles, or 30% of its global staff, amid a turnaround effort. Its stock has tumbled since the firm went public in 2021.\par \par \uc2 Founder \uc2 Whitney Wolfe Herd\uc2 , who stepped down as CEO in 2024 but returned earlier this year, said \uc2 Bumble\uc2  needed to take \u8220\'20\'1Cdecisive action\u8221\'20\'1D in order \u8220\'20\'1Cto restructure to build a company that\u8217\'20\'19s resilient, intentional, and ready for the next decade\u8221\'20\'1D in an email to staff.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve reset our strategy, and are going back to a start-up mentality \u8211\'20\'13 rooted in an ownership mindset and team structures designed for faster, more meaningful execution,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote.\par \par \uc2 Shares in \uc2 Bumble\uc2  rallied some 24% during early trading in New York on Wednesday. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2025/apr/27/dating-apps-user-decline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dating apps face a reckoning as users log off: \u8216\'20\'18There\u8217\'20\'19s no actual human connection\u8217\'20\'19}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Bumble\uc2  said it will incur non-recurring charges of between $13m and $18m for employee severance, benefits and related charges, primarily during the third and fourth quarters of 2025.\par \par \uc2 The company expects to generate \u8220\'20\'1Cup to\u8221\'20\'1D $40m in annual cost savings, which it plans to reinvest in initiatives such as product and technology development, according to a stock market filing.\par \par \uc2 The company also raised its second-quarter revenue forecast to a range of $244m to $249m, up from the prior view of $235m to $243m.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn recent months, we\u8217\'20\'19ve been rebuilding \u8211\'20\'13 returning to what makes us trusted, unique, and deeply human,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Herd. \u8220\'20\'1CBut intentional rebuilding requires hard decisions. Today, we are marking one of the most difficult: we are reducing the size of our team. This decision is not a reflection of any individual but rather where we are going as a company and what we are building for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reuters contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250625el6p0028n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
