\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump officials cutting $1bn in \uc2 NIH\uc2  grants is \u8216\'20\'18void and illegal\u8217\'20\'19, judge rules\b0\par\par\uc2 Cecilia Nowell and agencies \par \uc2 471 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 June 2025\par 15:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Judge says cuts represent unlawful \u8216\'20\'18racial discrimination\u8217\'20\'19 and orders grants given to those that filed suit be reinstated\par \par \uc2 A federal judge ruled on Monday that the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s termination of more than $1bn in research grants at the \uc2 National Institutes of Health\uc2  (\uc2 NIH\uc2 ) was \u8220\'20\'1Cvoid and illegal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 US district judge William Young added that the cuts, which targeted research with a perceived connection to diversity, equity and inclusion (DEI) programs, represented unlawful \u8220\'20\'1Cracial discrimination and discrimination against America\u8217\'20\'19s LGBTQ community\u8221\'20\'1D, Reuters reported. Young, who was appointed to the bench by then president \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 , added that he had \u8220\'20\'1Cnever seen a record where racial discrimination was so palpable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Young ordered that grants previously awarded to the organizations and 16 Democratic-led states that filed the lawsuit against the Trump administration be reinstated.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ) director of communications, Andrew Nixon, said that the agency \u8220\'20\'1Cstands by its decision to end funding for research that prioritized ideological agendas over scientific rigor and meaningful outcomes for the American people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder the leadership of Secretary Kennedy and the Trump administration, \uc2 HHS\uc2  is committed to ensuring that taxpayer dollars support programs rooted in evidence-based practices and gold standard science \u8211\'20\'13 not driven by divisive DEI mandates or gender ideology. \uc2 HHS\uc2  is exploring all legal options, including filing an appeal and moving to stay the order.\u8221\'20\'1D <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/09/nih-scientists-letter-health-research-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NIH scientists go public to denounce Trump\u8217\'20\'19s deep cuts in health research}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 In February, the Trump administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/08/trump-administration-medical-research-funding-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slashed}}}\uc2  billions of dollars in \uc2 NIH\uc2  funding, in an attempt to shrink the federal government and national debt led by then presidential adviser \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and his so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D. The move came amid efforts to cut 10,000 jobs from federal health agencies.\par \par \uc2 In April, the \uc2 American Public Health Association\uc2 ; the \uc2 United Automobile, Aerospace and Agricultural Implement Workers of America\uc2 ; and other health experts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/02/nih-funding-trump-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed suit}}}\uc2 , saying the cuts had targeted research with any connection to race, gender identity, vaccines or equity. The legal complaint claimed that the \uc2 NIH\uc2  broke from its science-based review process in preference of \u8220\'20\'1Cvague\u8221\'20\'1D new priorities.\par \par \uc2 According to a letter signed by dozens of \uc2 NIH\uc2  employees, the \uc2 NIH\uc2  has cut 2,100 research grants {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/09/nih-scientists-letter-health-research-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 valued at more than $12bn}}}\uc2  since Donald Trump took office.\par \par \uc2 During a Senate committee hearing last week, the \uc2 NIH\uc2  director, Jay Bhattacharya, said he \u8220\'20\'1Cdidn\u8217\'20\'19t take this job to terminate grants\u8221\'20\'1D, and was evaluating ways to restore some funding.\par \par \uc2 Young\u8217\'20\'19s ruling on Monday only applies to some of the grants mentioned in the lawsuit. The federal judge will rule on further claims after both sides present additional evidence.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250618el6i002ke\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
