\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Vital\u8217\'20\'19 that British steel gets Trump tariff deal after UK-US trade pact, say unions\b0\par\par\uc2 Julia Kollewe and Jasper Jolly \par \uc2 876 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 June 2025\par 09:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Starmer should secure deal as soon as possible to exempt UK steel from US levies, says Community union\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 <a href="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/jun/17/fuel-oil-tanker-rates-surge-middle-east-crisis-worries-markets-israel-iran-business-live">Business"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2025/jun/17/fuel-oil-tanker-rates-surge-middle-east-crisis-worries-markets-israel-iran-business-live">Business}}}\uc2  live \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates</a>\par \par \uc2 Steel trade unions have said it is \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely vital\u8221\'20\'1D that the UK rapidly secures a deal to protect the sector from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tariffs, after the industry was excluded from an initial UK-US pact signed on Monday night.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/jun/16/starmer-and-trump-finalise-uk-us-trade-deal-at-g7-but-steel-tariffs-still-on-hold"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Keir Starmer and Trump signed off a UK-US trade deal}}}\uc2  at the G7 summit in Canada, with the US president saying Britain would have protection against future tariffs \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause I like them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The car industry was relieved that tariffs on the sector will be reduced to 10% from 27.5%. The UK aerospace sector will face no tariffs at all from the US after deal, which followed an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/may/08/trump-and-starmer-confirm-breakthrough-us-uk-trade-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 initial agreement made in May}}}\uc2 . <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/jun/16/starmer-and-trump-finalise-uk-us-trade-deal-at-g7-but-steel-tariffs-still-on-hold"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump says UK is protected from tariffs \u8216\'20\'18because I like them\u8217\'20\'19 as trade deal is signed off}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 However, the announcement of the deal did not include the removal of tariffs on steel imports. UK steelmakers still face 25% tariffs, although this is lower than the global tariff of 50% imposed by the Trump administration on other nations.\par \par \uc2 The UK business department said the two leaders had pledged to \u8220\'20\'1Cmake progress towards 0% tariffs on core steel products as agreed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Alasdair McDiarmid, the assistant general secretary of the steel union Community, welcomed the progress that has been made on reaching a deal on steel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHowever, it\u8217\'20\'19s now absolutely vital that a deal for steel is secured as soon as possible,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1COur steel producers and their US customers need an end to the current state of uncertainty to allow normal business to resume.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCrucially, we must see a full exemption for all UK steel exports to the US \u8211\'20\'13 without that guarantee some of our leading steel businesses could be left behind, with a threat to jobs and livelihoods.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A steel industry source said the automotive deal had been widely expected to be completed before steel and aluminium. However, the person said \u8220\'20\'1Cwe now need steel to happen pretty quickly\u8221\'20\'1D to avoid the risk of 50% tariffs kicking in on 9 July, under the terms of the UK\u8217\'20\'19s temporary exemption.\par \par \uc2 Gareth Stace\uc2 , the director general of the trade body \uc2 UK Steel\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe look forward to imminently benefiting from a tariff rate cut similar to that which the automotive and aerospace industries will enjoy in seven days. The UK steel industry badly needs clarification over the \u8216\'20\'18melted and poured\u8217\'20\'19 requirement, and the level of quotas available to UK steelmakers so that we can restore the historical trade routes that have served both the UK and the US economies for many years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ministers have been working to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2025/jun/05/fears-tata-steel-could-be-excluded-from-starmer-trump-tariff-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ensure the UK\u8217\'20\'19s biggest steelmaker, Tata Steel, is included}}}\uc2  in tariff-free access to the US. Its bosses fear the deal could end up excluding Indian-owned \uc2 Tata Steel\uc2 , which runs the vast Port Talbot steelworks in south Wales, because of the origin of some of its products. The company exports more than $100m (\u163\'00\'A374m) worth of goods to the US every year.\par \par \uc2 The Chinese ownership of \uc2 British Steel\uc2 , which is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/jun/16/british-steel-debts-jingye-group-pwc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 under government control}}}\uc2 , could be a sticking point in a deal for the industry as the executive order signed by Trump suggests the US wants assurances that the metal originates in the UK.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe UK also committed to working to meet American requirements on the security of the supply chains of steel and aluminium products intended for export to the US and on the nature of ownership of relevant production facilities,\u8221\'20\'1D the order states.\par \par \uc2 Separately, \uc2 British Steel\uc2  has secured a new five-year supply contract with \uc2 Network Rail\uc2  worth more than \u163\'00\'A3500m, under which \uc2 British Steel\uc2  will supply between 70,000 and 80,000 tonnes of rail a year. McDiarmid welcomed the extension but expressed concern that \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 British Steel\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s share of the \uc2 Network Rail\uc2  contract is set to reduce significantly\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Mike Hawes\uc2 , the chief executive of the \uc2 Society of Motor Manufacturers and Traders\uc2 , told BBC Radio 4\u8217\'20\'19s Today programme he hoped the new 10% tariff rate for UK carmakers would start \u8220\'20\'1Cin the next few days\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The UK-US trade pact had been negotiated in early May, \u8220\'20\'1Cbut we\u8217\'20\'19ve been waiting for it to be implemented so manufacturers can start shipping without being subject to those punitive tariffs\u8221\'20\'1D, he said.\par \par \uc2 He added that \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot less\u8221\'20\'1D had been exported to the US in the meantime, and some UK manufacturers had halted shipments. The British luxury carmakers \uc2 Jaguar Land Rover\uc2  and Bentley are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/jun/16/jaguar-land-rover-trump-tariffs-profits-tata-motors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 among those that paused shipments}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve been pausing because their customers \u8211\'20\'13 we\u8217\'20\'19ve got shrewd customers \u8211\'20\'13 were going to wait and see what was going to happen,\u8221\'20\'1D Hawes said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou could see that the cost to the ultimate consumer was going to come down because of the reduction in the tariff, but you just didn\u8217\'20\'19t know when.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250617el6h0018i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
FF
