\par\par \uc2 Film\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18People didn\u8217\'20\'19t like women in space\u8217\'20\'19: how Sally Ride made history and paid the price\b0\par\par\uc2 Radheyan Simonpillai \par \uc2 1,270 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 June 2025\par 09:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ride was the first US woman in space \u8211\'20\'13 but a National Geographic documentary looks at how she was forced to hide her queerness to succeed\par \par \uc2 A week before Sally \u8211\'20\'13 a documentary about the first American woman to fly into space \u8211\'20\'13 landed at the Sundance film festival in January, \uc2 Nasa\uc2  employees {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/feb/11/trump-dei-nasa-executive-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received emails}}}\uc2  informing them how Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s diversity, equity and inclusion (DEI) rollbacks would take effect.\par \par \uc2 Contracts and offices associated with DEI programs were to be terminated. Staff were given Orwellian instruction to inform the government of any attempt to disguise inclusion efforts in \u8220\'20\'1Ccoded or imprecise language\u8221\'20\'1D. In the weeks to follow, \uc2 Nasa\uc2  would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/mar/21/nasa-drops-plan-first-woman-moon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 take back its promise}}}\uc2  to send the first woman and person of color to the moon\u8217\'20\'19s surface. Meanwhile, employees are reported to be hiding their rainbow flags and any other expressions of solidarity with the LGBTQ+ community, allegedly because they were instructed to do so though \uc2 Nasa\uc2  denies those claims.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe pride flag flew in space a couple years ago,\u8221\'20\'1D says Cristina Costantini, the director of Sally, on a \uc2 Zoom\uc2  call with the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CNow all \uc2 Nasa\uc2  employees are being asked to take down any representations of pride.\u8221\'20\'1D <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2025/jun/11/titan-sub-disaster-netflix-documentary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Absolutely shocking\u8217\'20\'19: Netflix documentary examines how the Titan sub disaster happened}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Costantini calls the developments sad, especially because such harmful silencing contributes to the very atmosphere that made her film\u8217\'20\'19s subject hide her own queer identity throughout her celebrated career. Sally Ride, who made history when she rode the space shuttle Challenger into the stars on 18 June 1983, was a lesbian. The public, and so many who knew Ride personally, only found out that part of her legacy after she died of cancer in 2012. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2012/jul/24/sally-ride"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ride\u8217\'20\'19s obituary}}}\uc2  identified Tam O\u8217\'20\'19Shaughnessy as her partner of 27 years.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Shaughnessy is a key voice in Sally, a National Geographic documentary revisiting everything we thought we knew about Ride \u8211\'20\'13 from her astronomic accomplishments to the infuriating sexism she confronted at \uc2 Nasa\uc2  and in the media, with reporters questioning how she would dress, whether space travel would affect her ovaries and if she would buckle and cry in the face of daunting challenges. But now there\u8217\'20\'19s the extra dimension, the part of Ride kept tragically buried because of the institutionalized homophobia we see resurfacing today. \u8220\'20\'1CWe made this movie not thinking it was particularly controversial,\u8221\'20\'1D says Costantini. \u8220\'20\'1CWe had no idea it would be this relevant.\u8221\'20\'1D <figure class="element element-video" data-canonical-url="{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C67rl6MNGe0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C67rl6MNGe0}}}\uc2 " > </figure>\par \par \uc2 Costantini is speaking from her Los Angeles office in Atwater Village, a photo of a space shuttle and another of Ride on the Challenger mission hovering just behind her. The investigative reporter turned film-maker \u8211\'20\'13 who grew up wanting to be a scientist and made her feature debut co-directing the Sundance audience award winner {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2018/oct/17/science-fair-review-international-science-and-engineering-fair-documentary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Science Fair}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 describes Ride as a major influence on her life. She remembers researching the astronaut as a young child on an old Encarta Encyclopedia CD-Rom for a book report. In grade three, Costantini contributed to a class mural where the students in her Milwaukee school painted their heroes on a wall. Ride is drawn standing alongside Brett Favre and Michael Jordan \u8211\'20\'13 a small sampling of the heroes that fed childhood aspirations in the mid-90s, says Costantini.\par \par \uc2 With Sally, Costantini is returning to her icon\u8217\'20\'19s story with a canvas bigger than either a book report or mural, but an even more challenging story to tell.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe film is really two stories interwoven,\u8221\'20\'1D says Costantini. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the public and the private Sally. The public Sally is so well-documented that it\u8217\'20\'19s a problem. We had to bring in 5,000 reels from the Nasa archive and sort through and sound sync all of them. That was a monumental task.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd then the other task is the private story, maybe the more interesting story, which has no documentation at all. There are only five really good pictures of [Sally and her partner, Tam] together that we had. You can\u8217\'20\'19t build a love story out of showing people the same five pictures over and over again. For that we had to kind of invent our own cinematic romantic language.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Costantini\u8217\'20\'19s doc pairs narrations from O\u8217\'20\'19Shaughnessy and others who were close to Ride with animation and 16mm visuals. They express the love, the excitement of first relationships, the heavy toll from keeping these feelings secret and the sting when Ride \u8211\'20\'13 whose noted emotional reserve is making more and more sense \u8211\'20\'13 would behave inexplicably.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSally is a very confusing central subject in some ways,\u8221\'20\'1D says Costantini, remarking on how Ride didn\u8217\'20\'19t always make for a picture-perfect feminist hero, the uneasiness going a long way to make her even more compelling. The director refers to a story recounted by fellow astronaut Kathryn Sullivan. During the race to become the first American woman to go to space, Ride sabotaged a \uc2 Nasa\uc2  exercise Sullivan was working on. Talking heads mull whether that was an example of Ride\u8217\'20\'19s prankster sense of humour, or a cutthroat competitive nature that flew in the face of female solidarity and sisterhood. \u8220\'20\'1CShe didn\u8217\'20\'19t leave tell all diaries or an audio journal of how she was feeling in every single moment. So we\u8217\'20\'19re left to interpret later on what her choices were, and why she did what she did.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Costantini also points to Ride\u8217\'20\'19s five-year marriage to fellow astronaut Steve Hawley. The union in retrospect can be seen as a betrayal of who she was, and the LGTBQ+ movement that she never publicly aligned with. But it was also a necessary and sacrificial career move to make her dream possible, deflecting any suspicions about sexual orientation while making Ride a more ideal candidate to make history and inspire young women. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople didn\u8217\'20\'19t like women in space,\u8221\'20\'1D says Costantini. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd they especially didn\u8217\'20\'19t like single women in space. Some of the male astronauts were, like: \u8216\'20\'18Well, it was a good look for her not to be single and in space.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When Ride does climb above the atmosphere on her historic mission, there\u8217\'20\'19s a cathartic moment where the tense conflicts within her \u8211\'20\'13 or put upon her \u8211\'20\'13 are either resolved or abandoned, if only temporarily. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2025/jun/13/liza-a-truly-terrific-absolutely-true-story-review-dazzling-glamour-and-true-grit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liza: A Truly Terrific Absolutely True Story review \u8211\'20\'13 dazzling glamour and true grit }}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI loved being weightless,\u8221\'20\'1D says Ride, while in space, her recorded words packing new mean considering all the burdens we now understand. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a feeling of freedom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe escaped Earth\u8217\'20\'19s orbit \u8211\'20\'13 Earth\u8217\'20\'19s gravity \u8211\'20\'13 metaphorically too,\u8221\'20\'1D says Costantini, on that pivotal moment in American history and Ride\u8217\'20\'19s personal life. \u8220\'20\'1CLooking at the Earth from space, she started to, for the first time, really think about the imaginary lines that we have. She was struck by the fact that all these countries have known borders around them. These are human constructions. As Tam says in the film, the lines between genders, the lines between race, the lines between countries, who we\u8217\'20\'19re allowed to love, those are meaningless constructs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSpace was transformative for her. When she came back to Earth, she finally allowed herself to be who she really is, and love who she really loved.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sally premieres on National Geographic on 16 June and is available on \uc2 Hulu\uc2  and \uc2 Disney\uc2 + on 17 June\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250615el6f0010a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
