\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Labor unions around US demand release of union leader arrested in LA protest\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato and Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 1,030 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 June 2025\par 12:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 David Huerta, serving as observer during an Ice raid, was held over allegations of interfering before release on Friday\par \par \uc2 Labor unions around the US rallied together on Monday to demand the release of a labor leader arrested and injured during \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice) raids in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 David Huerta, president of Service Employees International Union California and SEIU United Service Workers West, was serving as a community observer during an Ice raid in Los Angeles on Friday when federal agents arrested him over allegations of interfering.\par \par \uc2 He was initially hospitalized and released later on Friday for injuries sustained during the arrest. Videos circulating online show officers shoving Huerta to the ground during the arrest before handcuffing him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat happened to me is not about me; this is about something much bigger. This is about how we as a community stand together and resist the injustice that\u8217\'20\'19s happening,\u8221\'20\'1D Huerta said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://seiuca.org/press-releases/2025/06/06/seiu-california-president-david-huerta-injured-detained-at-ice-raid-in-los-angeles/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  after his release from the hospital. \u8220\'20\'1CHard-working people, and members of our family and our community, are being treated like criminals. We all collectively have to object to this madness because this is not justice. This is injustice. And we all have to stand on the right side of justice.\u8221\'20\'1D <figure class="element element-atom"> <gu-atom data-atom-id="d1c3d669-14a8-4712-afd4-75846049aa1a" data-atom-type="media"> </gu-atom> </figure>\par \par \uc2 Huerta was eventually {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/immigration-los-angeles-protest-huerta-union-arrest-68a8fa6d5c931062d34e1e33a94f2b47"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged}}}\uc2  with conspiring to impede an officer and released from federal custody on Monday on a $50,000 bond, following a hearing in Los Angeles. But his detention has become a rallying cry for labor leaders around the US, who had called for an end to the immigration enforcement raids and use of the national guard to suppress protests in Los Angeles. California has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/jun/09/los-angeles-protests-live-tensions-flare-trump-deploys-national-guard-troops"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued}}}\uc2  the Trump administration over its decision to federalize the national guard. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/09/los-angeles-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles gears up for fourth day of protests against immigration raids}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 Leaders of major unions convened hundreds of protesters on Monday outside justice department headquarters in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDavid was the first one to say this isn\u8217\'20\'19t just about him,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Becky Pringle\uc2 , president of the \uc2 National Education Association\uc2 , the largest labor union in the country. \u8220\'20\'1CWe know what this administration is doing, so we are saying to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and all of his allies: we will not, we will not, scapegoat immigrants.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jaime Contreras, an executive vice-president at the \uc2 SEIU\uc2  32BJ, representing workers across the north-eastern United States, said Huerta\u8217\'20\'19s case would serve as a rallying cry for his members and supporters, because \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot more people that agree with us than agree with them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDavid for us is \u8230\'20\'26 he\u8217\'20\'19s a labor leader, he\u8217\'20\'19s a brother, he\u8217\'20\'19s a union member, he\u8217\'20\'19s a respected leader in California, and we\u8217\'20\'19re here to let him know that he\u8217\'20\'19s not alone,\u8221\'20\'1D Contreras said.\par \par \uc2 He compared Huerta\u8217\'20\'19s arrest to the saga of Kilmar \u193\'00\'C1brego Garc\u237\'00\'EDa, a Maryland resident who was deported to El Salvador in violation of a court order, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/06/kilmar-abrego-garcia-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last week brought back to the United States}}}\uc2  to answer allegations of human smuggling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not gonna stand by that,\u8221\'20\'1D Contreras said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s always a next election, so we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna make everybody pay at the voting booth when it comes to election time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In New York City, \uc2 SEIU\uc2  32BJ\u8217\'20\'19s president, Manny Pastreich, told union members and protesters: \u8220\'20\'1CEverything we hold dear is under attack. Unions, workers, freedom, immigrant communities, healthcare, the constitution, our union brothers and sisters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must fight back. We reject these attacks on our communities and demand the immediate release of our union brother David Huerta,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Huerta, well-known among Democrats in California given his long record as a union leader in the state, received support from governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  and other Democratic officials across the US, including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jeffries.house.gov/2025/06/07/leader-jeffries-statement-on-arrest-of-david-huerta/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House minority leader, Hakeem Jeffries}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 SEIU\uc2  refuses to be silent in the face of these horrific attacks on working communities. Standing in solidarity as a movement of working people is not new to us,\u8221\'20\'1D said April Verrett, international president of theSEIU.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 SEIU\uc2  protects the rights and dignity of hard-working people, and the safety of workers in the workplace. Imagine what it feels like for thousands of workers around the country to be attacked by masked men with weapons, or to bear witness to their co-workers getting dragged away, knowing their kids may not see them again. We demand David Huerta\u8217\'20\'19s immediate release and an end to these abusive workplace raids.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In addition to New York and Washington DC, the union is on Monday leading or participating in rallies in Atlanta, Boston, Charlotte, Chicago, Denver, Harrisburg, Philadelphia, Pittsburgh, Portland, Oregon, Raleigh-Durham, Sacramento, San Francisco, Seattle and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bsky.app/profile/seiumn.bsky.social/post/3lr6i6wge422f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 St Paul, Minnesota}}}\uc2 , to call for Huerta\u8217\'20\'19s release, for the California national guard to stand down and for an end to the Ice raids.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American Federation of Labor and Congress of Industrial Organizations\uc2 , the largest federation of labor unions in the US, has also called for Huerta\u8217\'20\'19s release.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s mass deportation agenda has unnecessarily targeted our hard-working immigrant brothers and sisters, David was exercising his constitutional rights and conducting legal observation of Ice activity in his community,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Liz Shuler\uc2 , president of the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/press/releases/afl-cio-demands-immediate-release-seiu-california-president-david-huerta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe labor movement stands with David and we will continue to demand justice for our union brother until he is released.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lee Saunders\uc2 , president of the \uc2 American Federation of State, County and Municipal Employees\uc2 , the largest public employee union in the US, also called for Huerta\u8217\'20\'19s release.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmericans have a constitutional right to free speech. That right was violated when Ice agents violently arrested and injured Huerta as he peacefully observed immigration enforcement activity in his community,\u8221\'20\'1D Saunders said. \u8220\'20\'1CHuerta was exercising his legal right to speak out and bear witness. In response, Ice used force, caused harm, and continues to hold him in unjust detention.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250609el6900337\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
