\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 US jobs market slows down as businesses cope with Trump trade war uncertainty\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Aratani in New York \par \uc2 481 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 June 2025\par 14:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 May\u8217\'20\'19s jobs report was dragged down by loss of 22,000 federal workers\u8217\'20\'19 jobs as Doge cut positions\par \par \uc2 The US economy added 139,000 jobs in May, a slowdown compared with recent months as American businesses cope with uncertainty around {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  continuing trade war.\par \par \uc2 After signs of a strong labor market in April \u8211\'20\'13 which was largely seen as resiliency against teetering trade policy from the White House \u8211\'20\'13 May saw a drop in new jobs added to the labor market, according to new data from the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 . The unemployment rate remained steady at 4.2%, unchanged from last month.\par \par \uc2 May\u8217\'20\'19s jobs report was dragged down by the loss of 22,000 federal workers\u8217\'20\'19 jobs as the Trump administration used the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdepartment of government efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D (Doge) to cut government positions. Since January, 59,000 Federal jobs have been cut.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  also cut the numbers of jobs created in March and April. In an update, the bureau said a total of 95,000 fewer jobs had been created over the two months.\par \par \uc2 After the report was released, Trump once again called on the Federal Reserve chair, \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  (whom he has nicknamed \u8220\'20\'1CToo Late\u8221\'20\'1D), to cut interest rates. <aside class="element element-rich-link element--thumbnail">\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/jun/05/donald-trump-xi-jinping-china-phone-call-invitation-trade-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump to meet Xi Jinping in China after \u8216\'20\'18very good\u8217\'20\'19 call on trade}}}\uc2  </aside>\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18Too Late\u8217\'20\'19 at the Fed is a disaster! Europe has had 10 rate cuts, we have had none. Despite him, our Country is doing great. Go for a full point, \uc2 Rocket Fuel\uc2 !\u8221\'20\'1D the president wrote on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/114636703372425608"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Truth Social.}}}\par \par \uc2 Economists expected a downward slump after data earlier in the week suggested a cooling job market. Payroll firm ADP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adpemploymentreport.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that private-sector payrolls increased by just 37,000 in May, the lowest gain in more than two years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter a strong start to the year, hiring is losing momentum,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Nela Richardson\uc2 , chief economist at ADP, in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Institute for Supply Management\uc2  also released its latest purchasing mangers\u8217\'20\'19 index figure, which measures the general landscape for manufacturers and showed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/us-private-payrolls-growth-slows-sharply-may-2025-06-04/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reading}}}\uc2  of 49.9 in April \u8211\'20\'13 the lowest since June 2024.\par \par \uc2 In the most recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sca.isr.umich.edu/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 results}}}\uc2  of the \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s survey of consumers, released at the end of May, consumer sentiment had stayed relatively stable from April to May, with the caveat that April\u8217\'20\'19s reading was the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/apr/25/trump-tariffs-trade-war-consumer-sentiment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lowest}}}\uc2  drop in consumer sentiment since 1990.\par \par \uc2 The impact of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s trade war has yet to be seen in inflation readings. In April, the annual inflation rate was at 2.3%, a slight decrease from March, though economists said that the impact of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-tariffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs}}}\uc2  will be gradual and probably will not impact data until the summer.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250606el66001xl\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/2021 to 06/10/2026\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trl